0, "avg_logprob": -0.1041539770657899, "compression_ratio": 1.6460481099656357, "no_speech_prob": 1.3672472442410877e-12}, {"id": 13, "seek": 5264, "start": 67.72, "end": 68.68, "text": " Like a barcode or something.", "tokens": [51119, 1743, 257, 2159, 22332, 420, 746, 13, 51167], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1041539770657899, "compression_ratio": 1.6460481099656357, "no_speech_prob": 1.3672472442410877e-12}, {"id": 14, "seek": 5264, "start": 68.68, "end": 69.38, "text": " Yeah, like a barcode.", "tokens": [51167, 865, 11, 411, 257, 2159, 22332, 13, 51202], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1041539770657899, "compression_ratio": 1.6460481099656357, "no_speech_prob": 1.3672472442410877e-12}, {"id": 15, "seek": 5264, "start": 69.78, "end": 77.58, "text": " But the reality, as this incredibly dense text we are exploring today argues, is that a coordinate system is purely a choice.", "tokens": [51222, 583, 264, 4103, 11, 382, 341, 6252, 18011, 2487, 321, 366, 12736, 965, 38218, 11, 307, 300, 257, 15670, 1185, 307, 17491, 257, 3922, 13, 51612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1041539770657899, "compression_ratio": 1.6460481099656357, "no_speech_prob": 1.3672472442410877e-12}, {"id": 16, "seek": 5264, "start": 77.74000000000001, "end": 78.48, "text": " It is a lens.", "tokens": [51620, 467, 307, 257, 6765, 13, 51657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1041539770657899, "compression_ratio": 1.6460481099656357, "no_speech_prob": 1.3672472442410877e-12}, {"id": 17, "seek": 7848, "start": 78.48, "end": 88.42, "text": " And depending on which lens you pick, entirely different features of reality come into this sharp, brilliant focus, while others just become hopelessly mathematically distorted.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 5413, 322, 597, 6765, 291, 1888, 11, 7696, 819, 4122, 295, 4103, 808, 666, 341, 8199, 11, 10248, 1879, 11, 1339, 2357, 445, 1813, 27317, 356, 44003, 33431, 13, 50862], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10581890596162288, "compression_ratio": 1.5530546623794212, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832356484180797e-12}, {"id": 18, "seek": 7848, "start": 88.74000000000001, "end": 91.42, "text": " Which brings us to the actual source material.", "tokens": [50878, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 3539, 4009, 2527, 13, 51012], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10581890596162288, "compression_ratio": 1.5530546623794212, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832356484180797e-12}, {"id": 19, "seek": 7848, "start": 91.60000000000001, "end": 94.22, "text": " Yes. So to you, our resident learner, welcome back.", "tokens": [51021, 1079, 13, 407, 281, 291, 11, 527, 10832, 33347, 11, 2928, 646, 13, 51152], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10581890596162288, "compression_ratio": 1.5530546623794212, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832356484180797e-12}, {"id": 20, "seek": 7848, "start": 94.32000000000001, "end": 101.42, "text": " Today we are immersing ourselves in a truly mind-bending deep dive into this 2026 undergraduate textbook.", "tokens": [51157, 2692, 321, 366, 16787, 278, 4175, 294, 257, 4908, 1575, 12, 65, 2029, 2452, 9192, 666, 341, 945, 10880, 19113, 25591, 13, 51512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10581890596162288, "compression_ratio": 1.5530546623794212, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832356484180797e-12}, {"id": 21, "seek": 7848, "start": 101.78, "end": 105.16, "text": " It's titled Geometry as Computational Infrastructure.", "tokens": [51530, 467, 311, 19841, 2876, 34730, 382, 37804, 1478, 38425, 2885, 13, 51699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10581890596162288, "compression_ratio": 1.5530546623794212, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832356484180797e-12}, {"id": 22, "seek": 7848, "start": 105.22, "end": 107.48, "text": " Written by the independent researcher Flixion.", "tokens": [51702, 10159, 2987, 538, 264, 6695, 21751, 3235, 970, 313, 13, 51815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10581890596162288, "compression_ratio": 1.5530546623794212, "no_speech_prob": 1.3832356484180797e-12}, {"id": 23, "seek": 10748, "start": 107.48, "end": 113.26, "text": " Right, Flixion. And our goal today is we are going to extract Flixion's grand unified theory.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 11, 3235, 970, 313, 13, 400, 527, 3387, 965, 307, 321, 366, 516, 281, 8947, 3235, 970, 313, 311, 2697, 26787, 5261, 13, 50654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09414529378435253, "compression_ratio": 1.599290780141844, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947614102022501e-12}, {"id": 24, "seek": 10748, "start": 113.44, "end": 114.46000000000001, "text": " And it is grand.", "tokens": [50663, 400, 309, 307, 2697, 13, 50714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09414529378435253, "compression_ratio": 1.599290780141844, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947614102022501e-12}, {"id": 25, "seek": 10748, "start": 114.62, "end": 122.60000000000001, "text": " It really is. Because what this book proposes is that a single geometric shape, the sphere, and a single mathematical tool called the Laplacian,", "tokens": [50722, 467, 534, 307, 13, 1436, 437, 341, 1446, 2365, 4201, 307, 300, 257, 2167, 33246, 3909, 11, 264, 16687, 11, 293, 257, 2167, 18894, 2290, 1219, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 11, 51121], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09414529378435253, "compression_ratio": 1.599290780141844, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947614102022501e-12}, {"id": 26, "seek": 10748, "start": 123.08, "end": 126.30000000000001, "text": " they secretly govern entirely disconnected fields of science.", "tokens": [51145, 436, 22611, 1980, 7696, 29426, 7909, 295, 3497, 13, 51306], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09414529378435253, "compression_ratio": 1.599290780141844, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947614102022501e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 10748, "start": 126.42, "end": 129.94, "text": " We are talking about the bioelectricity of regenerating flatworms.", "tokens": [51312, 492, 366, 1417, 466, 264, 12198, 33243, 507, 295, 26358, 990, 4962, 30917, 82, 13, 51488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09414529378435253, "compression_ratio": 1.599290780141844, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947614102022501e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 10748, "start": 129.94, "end": 133.66, "text": " Which is wild. And the architecture of irreversible computer code.", "tokens": [51488, 3013, 307, 4868, 13, 400, 264, 9482, 295, 16014, 840, 964, 3820, 3089, 13, 51674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09414529378435253, "compression_ratio": 1.599290780141844, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947614102022501e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 13366, "start": 133.66, "end": 139.78, "text": " And even the literal mathematical geometry of how human beings distinguish between different ideas.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 754, 264, 20411, 18894, 18426, 295, 577, 1952, 8958, 20206, 1296, 819, 3487, 13, 50671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09885546056235708, "compression_ratio": 1.5208333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.76917139792232e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 13366, "start": 139.9, "end": 142.98, "text": " It is just a sweeping, almost audacious claim.", "tokens": [50677, 467, 307, 445, 257, 33285, 11, 1920, 2379, 22641, 3932, 13, 50831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09885546056235708, "compression_ratio": 1.5208333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.76917139792232e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 13366, "start": 143.12, "end": 148.6, "text": " But what is truly fascinating here is how methodically Flixion builds the case from the ground up.", "tokens": [50838, 583, 437, 307, 4908, 10343, 510, 307, 577, 3170, 984, 3235, 970, 313, 15182, 264, 1389, 490, 264, 2727, 493, 13, 51112], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09885546056235708, "compression_ratio": 1.5208333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.76917139792232e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 13366, "start": 148.8, "end": 153.62, "text": " You know, they don't just throw out a poetic metaphor about everything being a circle and expect you to just nod along.", "tokens": [51122, 509, 458, 11, 436, 500, 380, 445, 3507, 484, 257, 41080, 19157, 466, 1203, 885, 257, 6329, 293, 2066, 291, 281, 445, 15224, 2051, 13, 51363], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09885546056235708, "compression_ratio": 1.5208333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.76917139792232e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 15362, "start": 153.62, "end": 155.46, "text": " No, they really bring the receipts.", "tokens": [50365, 883, 11, 436, 534, 1565, 264, 2268, 48908, 13, 50457], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1681659361895393, "compression_ratio": 1.6255506607929515, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346884562466358e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 15362, "start": 155.66, "end": 162.62, "text": " They provide a rigorous mathematical framework, starting from the very foundation of what a coordinate system actually is.", "tokens": [50467, 814, 2893, 257, 29882, 18894, 8388, 11, 2891, 490, 264, 588, 7030, 295, 437, 257, 15670, 1185, 767, 307, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1681659361895393, "compression_ratio": 1.6255506607929515, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346884562466358e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 15362, "start": 162.84, "end": 169.48000000000002, "text": " And they prove how the mathematics of a spherical shell reappears organically in all these distinct domains.", "tokens": [50826, 400, 436, 7081, 577, 264, 18666, 295, 257, 37300, 8720, 35638, 68, 685, 1798, 984, 294, 439, 613, 10644, 25514, 13, 51158], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1681659361895393, "compression_ratio": 1.6255506607929515, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346884562466358e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 15362, "start": 169.72, "end": 170.68, "text": " Okay, let's unpack this.", "tokens": [51170, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 26699, 341, 13, 51218], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1681659361895393, "compression_ratio": 1.6255506607929515, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346884562466358e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 15362, "start": 171.08, "end": 173.24, "text": " Let's start right at that foundational premise.", "tokens": [51238, 961, 311, 722, 558, 412, 300, 32195, 22045, 13, 51346], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1681659361895393, "compression_ratio": 1.6255506607929515, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346884562466358e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 15362, "start": 173.62, "end": 174.86, "text": " The illusion of coordinates.", "tokens": [51365, 440, 18854, 295, 21056, 13, 51427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1681659361895393, "compression_ratio": 1.6255506607929515, "no_speech_prob": 1.7346884562466358e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 17486, "start": 174.86, "end": 178.9, "text": " Because Flixion hits this incredibly hard in chapter one.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 3235, 970, 313, 8664, 341, 6252, 1152, 294, 7187, 472, 13, 50567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15348981927942346, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612905933382049e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 17486, "start": 179.42000000000002, "end": 186.58, "text": " They state that a coordinate chart is an interface between an observer and a space, not a commitment to the space's true shape.", "tokens": [50593, 814, 1785, 300, 257, 15670, 6927, 307, 364, 9226, 1296, 364, 27878, 293, 257, 1901, 11, 406, 257, 8371, 281, 264, 1901, 311, 2074, 3909, 13, 50951], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15348981927942346, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612905933382049e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 17486, "start": 186.76000000000002, "end": 191.64000000000001, "text": " So to make this concrete, let's talk about something as simple as a 2D circle on a piece of paper.", "tokens": [50960, 407, 281, 652, 341, 9859, 11, 718, 311, 751, 466, 746, 382, 2199, 382, 257, 568, 35, 6329, 322, 257, 2522, 295, 3035, 13, 51204], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15348981927942346, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612905933382049e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 17486, "start": 192.38000000000002, "end": 194.58, "text": " How does that prove the whole interface concept?", "tokens": [51241, 1012, 775, 300, 7081, 264, 1379, 9226, 3410, 30, 51351], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15348981927942346, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612905933382049e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 17486, "start": 194.8, "end": 195.28000000000003, "text": " Gladly.", "tokens": [51362, 28301, 356, 13, 51386], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15348981927942346, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612905933382049e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 17486, "start": 195.54000000000002, "end": 199.34, "text": " So let's visualize that standard circle drawn on a blank piece of paper.", "tokens": [51399, 407, 718, 311, 23273, 300, 3832, 6329, 10117, 322, 257, 8247, 2522, 295, 3035, 13, 51589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15348981927942346, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612905933382049e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 17486, "start": 199.46, "end": 199.74, "text": " Got it.", "tokens": [51595, 5803, 309, 13, 51609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15348981927942346, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612905933382049e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 19974, "start": 199.74, "end": 206.68, "text": " Now, if you want to describe a specific point on the edge of that circle mathematically, you generally have two common choices.", "tokens": [50365, 823, 11, 498, 291, 528, 281, 6786, 257, 2685, 935, 322, 264, 4691, 295, 300, 6329, 44003, 11, 291, 5101, 362, 732, 2689, 7994, 13, 50712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16498856625314487, "compression_ratio": 1.6931818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556523946970048e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 19974, "start": 207.84, "end": 209.76000000000002, "text": " You could use a Cartesian chart.", "tokens": [50770, 509, 727, 764, 257, 22478, 42434, 6927, 13, 50866], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16498856625314487, "compression_ratio": 1.6931818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556523946970048e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 19974, "start": 209.9, "end": 212.20000000000002, "text": " Which is the standard X and Y grid right.", "tokens": [50873, 3013, 307, 264, 3832, 1783, 293, 398, 10748, 558, 13, 50988], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16498856625314487, "compression_ratio": 1.6931818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556523946970048e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 19974, "start": 212.32000000000002, "end": 212.58, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50994, 1779, 13, 51007], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16498856625314487, "compression_ratio": 1.6931818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556523946970048e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 19974, "start": 213.02, "end": 216.04000000000002, "text": " Measuring the horizontal and vertical distance from the center.", "tokens": [51029, 1923, 296, 1345, 264, 12750, 293, 9429, 4560, 490, 264, 3056, 13, 51180], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16498856625314487, "compression_ratio": 1.6931818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556523946970048e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 19974, "start": 216.68, "end": 218.36, "text": " Or you could use a polar chart.", "tokens": [51212, 1610, 291, 727, 764, 257, 12367, 6927, 13, 51296], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16498856625314487, "compression_ratio": 1.6931818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556523946970048e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 19974, "start": 218.62, "end": 220.96, "text": " And polar throws out X and Y entirely right.", "tokens": [51309, 400, 12367, 19251, 484, 1783, 293, 398, 7696, 558, 13, 51426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16498856625314487, "compression_ratio": 1.6931818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556523946970048e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 19974, "start": 220.96, "end": 221.68, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [51426, 467, 775, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16498856625314487, "compression_ratio": 1.6931818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556523946970048e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 19974, "start": 221.86, "end": 226.68, "text": " Instead, it assigns a radius, the straight line distance from the center, and an angle.", "tokens": [51471, 7156, 11, 309, 6269, 82, 257, 15845, 11, 264, 2997, 1622, 4560, 490, 264, 3056, 11, 293, 364, 5802, 13, 51712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16498856625314487, "compression_ratio": 1.6931818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556523946970048e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 22668, "start": 226.68, "end": 229.70000000000002, "text": " Basically, how far you've rotated around the center point.", "tokens": [50365, 8537, 11, 577, 1400, 291, 600, 42146, 926, 264, 3056, 935, 13, 50516], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13821545453138753, "compression_ratio": 1.6180758017492711, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272739891005304e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 22668, "start": 229.88, "end": 229.96, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50525, 1779, 13, 50529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13821545453138753, "compression_ratio": 1.6180758017492711, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272739891005304e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 22668, "start": 230.12, "end": 235.94, "text": " And I remember in school, you just sort of switch between them based on whatever the textbook tells you to do for that specific problem.", "tokens": [50537, 400, 286, 1604, 294, 1395, 11, 291, 445, 1333, 295, 3679, 1296, 552, 2361, 322, 2035, 264, 25591, 5112, 291, 281, 360, 337, 300, 2685, 1154, 13, 50828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13821545453138753, "compression_ratio": 1.6180758017492711, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272739891005304e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 22668, "start": 236.18, "end": 238.74, "text": " It just felt like two different languages for the exact same thing.", "tokens": [50840, 467, 445, 2762, 411, 732, 819, 8650, 337, 264, 1900, 912, 551, 13, 50968], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13821545453138753, "compression_ratio": 1.6180758017492711, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272739891005304e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 22668, "start": 238.8, "end": 239.16, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50971, 7587, 13, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13821545453138753, "compression_ratio": 1.6180758017492711, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272739891005304e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 22668, "start": 239.42000000000002, "end": 241.8, "text": " But the crucial insight is why we switch languages.", "tokens": [51002, 583, 264, 11462, 11269, 307, 983, 321, 3679, 8650, 13, 51121], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13821545453138753, "compression_ratio": 1.6180758017492711, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272739891005304e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 22668, "start": 242.56, "end": 243.74, "text": " Why do both exist?", "tokens": [51159, 1545, 360, 1293, 2514, 30, 51218], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13821545453138753, "compression_ratio": 1.6180758017492711, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272739891005304e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 22668, "start": 244.02, "end": 245.26000000000002, "text": " To make the math easier.", "tokens": [51232, 1407, 652, 264, 5221, 3571, 13, 51294], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13821545453138753, "compression_ratio": 1.6180758017492711, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272739891005304e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 22668, "start": 245.4, "end": 245.76000000000002, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51301, 1079, 13, 51319], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13821545453138753, "compression_ratio": 1.6180758017492711, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272739891005304e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 22668, "start": 246.18, "end": 249.98000000000002, "text": " Suppose you want to physically slide that circle across the paper.", "tokens": [51340, 21360, 291, 528, 281, 9762, 4137, 300, 6329, 2108, 264, 3035, 13, 51530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13821545453138753, "compression_ratio": 1.6180758017492711, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272739891005304e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 22668, "start": 250.44, "end": 250.94, "text": " A translation.", "tokens": [51553, 316, 12853, 13, 51578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13821545453138753, "compression_ratio": 1.6180758017492711, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272739891005304e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 22668, "start": 251.5, "end": 255.20000000000002, "text": " In Cartesian coordinates, the math for sliding is incredibly simple.", "tokens": [51606, 682, 22478, 42434, 21056, 11, 264, 5221, 337, 21169, 307, 6252, 2199, 13, 51791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13821545453138753, "compression_ratio": 1.6180758017492711, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272739891005304e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 22668, "start": 255.20000000000002, "end": 256.58, "text": " You just add to X or Y.", "tokens": [51791, 509, 445, 909, 281, 1783, 420, 398, 13, 51860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13821545453138753, "compression_ratio": 1.6180758017492711, "no_speech_prob": 1.4272739891005304e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 25668, "start": 257.0, "end": 257.44, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50381, 7587, 13, 50403], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1756155428679093, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582738208789863e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 25668, "start": 257.7, "end": 260.74, "text": " If you want to move it right, you just add a number to the X value.", "tokens": [50416, 759, 291, 528, 281, 1286, 309, 558, 11, 291, 445, 909, 257, 1230, 281, 264, 1783, 2158, 13, 50568], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1756155428679093, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582738208789863e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 25668, "start": 260.86, "end": 262.52, "text": " You want to move it, you add to the Y value.", "tokens": [50574, 509, 528, 281, 1286, 309, 11, 291, 909, 281, 264, 398, 2158, 13, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1756155428679093, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582738208789863e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 25668, "start": 262.98, "end": 265.6, "text": " The whole shape moves neatly and linearly.", "tokens": [50680, 440, 1379, 3909, 6067, 36634, 293, 43586, 13, 50811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1756155428679093, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582738208789863e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 25668, "start": 266.38, "end": 271.64, "text": " But what happens if you try to describe that exact same sliding motion using polar coordinates?", "tokens": [50850, 583, 437, 2314, 498, 291, 853, 281, 6786, 300, 1900, 912, 21169, 5394, 1228, 12367, 21056, 30, 51113], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1756155428679093, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582738208789863e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 25668, "start": 272.18, "end": 272.8, "text": " Oh, man.", "tokens": [51140, 876, 11, 587, 13, 51171], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1756155428679093, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582738208789863e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 25668, "start": 273.32, "end": 274.32, "text": " I'm trying to picture it.", "tokens": [51197, 286, 478, 1382, 281, 3036, 309, 13, 51247], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1756155428679093, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582738208789863e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 25668, "start": 274.56, "end": 281.2, "text": " If I just slide the circle to the right, the distance from the original center to my point changes, and the angle changes, too.", "tokens": [51259, 759, 286, 445, 4137, 264, 6329, 281, 264, 558, 11, 264, 4560, 490, 264, 3380, 3056, 281, 452, 935, 2962, 11, 293, 264, 5802, 2962, 11, 886, 13, 51591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1756155428679093, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582738208789863e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 28120, "start": 281.2, "end": 283.2, "text": " It becomes a trigonometric nightmare.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 3643, 257, 35386, 266, 29470, 18724, 13, 50465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17916714228116548, "compression_ratio": 1.375, "no_speech_prob": 1.2738313008575641e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 28120, "start": 283.78, "end": 291.46, "text": " The radius and the angle warp in incredibly complex, nonlinear ways, just to describe a simple slide across a desk.", "tokens": [50494, 440, 15845, 293, 264, 5802, 36030, 294, 6252, 3997, 11, 2107, 28263, 2098, 11, 445, 281, 6786, 257, 2199, 4137, 2108, 257, 10026, 13, 50878], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17916714228116548, "compression_ratio": 1.375, "no_speech_prob": 1.2738313008575641e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 28120, "start": 291.5, "end": 293.03999999999996, "text": " It's just computationally exhausting.", "tokens": [50880, 467, 311, 445, 24903, 379, 34076, 13, 50957], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17916714228116548, "compression_ratio": 1.375, "no_speech_prob": 1.2738313008575641e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 28120, "start": 293.46, "end": 293.96, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [50978, 467, 307, 13, 51003], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17916714228116548, "compression_ratio": 1.375, "no_speech_prob": 1.2738313008575641e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 29396, "start": 293.96, "end": 295.97999999999996, "text": " But if you want to spin the circle...", "tokens": [50365, 583, 498, 291, 528, 281, 6060, 264, 6329, 485, 50466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16627743509080675, "compression_ratio": 1.4046242774566473, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043164638626425e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 29396, "start": 295.97999999999996, "end": 296.15999999999997, "text": " Oh, right.", "tokens": [50466, 876, 11, 558, 13, 50475], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16627743509080675, "compression_ratio": 1.4046242774566473, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043164638626425e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 29396, "start": 296.23999999999995, "end": 297.71999999999997, "text": " Then the script flips entirely.", "tokens": [50479, 1396, 264, 5755, 40249, 7696, 13, 50553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16627743509080675, "compression_ratio": 1.4046242774566473, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043164638626425e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 29396, "start": 297.91999999999996, "end": 298.4, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50563, 48746, 736, 13, 50587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16627743509080675, "compression_ratio": 1.4046242774566473, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043164638626425e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 29396, "start": 298.71999999999997, "end": 300.4, "text": " Polar coordinates are perfect for rotation.", "tokens": [50603, 3635, 289, 21056, 366, 2176, 337, 12447, 13, 50687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16627743509080675, "compression_ratio": 1.4046242774566473, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043164638626425e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 29396, "start": 300.65999999999997, "end": 305.52, "text": " You just add a value to the angle, say, 45 degrees, and the radius stays exactly the same.", "tokens": [50700, 509, 445, 909, 257, 2158, 281, 264, 5802, 11, 584, 11, 6905, 5310, 11, 293, 264, 15845, 10834, 2293, 264, 912, 13, 50943], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16627743509080675, "compression_ratio": 1.4046242774566473, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043164638626425e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 29396, "start": 305.59999999999997, "end": 306.35999999999996, "text": " Math is trivial.", "tokens": [50947, 15776, 307, 26703, 13, 50985], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16627743509080675, "compression_ratio": 1.4046242774566473, "no_speech_prob": 1.3043164638626425e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 30636, "start": 306.36, "end": 313.46000000000004, "text": " Meanwhile, spinning a circle in Cartesian coordinates requires applying sines and cosines to both the X and Y values simultaneously.", "tokens": [50365, 13879, 11, 15640, 257, 6329, 294, 22478, 42434, 21056, 7029, 9275, 262, 1652, 293, 3792, 1652, 281, 1293, 264, 1783, 293, 398, 4190, 16561, 13, 50720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14571962551194795, "compression_ratio": 1.6139705882352942, "no_speech_prob": 1.3354408724686184e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 30636, "start": 313.78000000000003, "end": 315.36, "text": " It is messy and prone to error.", "tokens": [50736, 467, 307, 16191, 293, 25806, 281, 6713, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14571962551194795, "compression_ratio": 1.6139705882352942, "no_speech_prob": 1.3354408724686184e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 30636, "start": 315.86, "end": 321.98, "text": " So the question Fliction asks us to consider is, which coordinate system is the true description of the circle?", "tokens": [50840, 407, 264, 1168, 3235, 4105, 8962, 505, 281, 1949, 307, 11, 597, 15670, 1185, 307, 264, 2074, 3855, 295, 264, 6329, 30, 51146], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14571962551194795, "compression_ratio": 1.6139705882352942, "no_speech_prob": 1.3354408724686184e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 30636, "start": 322.40000000000003, "end": 326.36, "text": " And the answer has to be neither right, because they're just tools.", "tokens": [51167, 400, 264, 1867, 575, 281, 312, 9662, 558, 11, 570, 436, 434, 445, 3873, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14571962551194795, "compression_ratio": 1.6139705882352942, "no_speech_prob": 1.3354408724686184e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 30636, "start": 326.98, "end": 327.16, "text": " Neither.", "tokens": [51396, 23956, 13, 51405], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14571962551194795, "compression_ratio": 1.6139705882352942, "no_speech_prob": 1.3354408724686184e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 30636, "start": 327.78000000000003, "end": 332.56, "text": " They are both just computational interfaces optimized for completely different tasks.", "tokens": [51436, 814, 366, 1293, 445, 28270, 28416, 26941, 337, 2584, 819, 9608, 13, 51675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14571962551194795, "compression_ratio": 1.6139705882352942, "no_speech_prob": 1.3354408724686184e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 33256, "start": 332.56, "end": 336.78000000000003, "text": " The Cartesian chart is a software tool built to make translation easy.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 22478, 42434, 6927, 307, 257, 4722, 2290, 3094, 281, 652, 12853, 1858, 13, 50576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599536559161018, "compression_ratio": 1.665137614678899, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283280263710957e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 33256, "start": 337.14, "end": 340.2, "text": " And the polar chart is a tool built to make rotation easy.", "tokens": [50594, 400, 264, 12367, 6927, 307, 257, 2290, 3094, 281, 652, 12447, 1858, 13, 50747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599536559161018, "compression_ratio": 1.665137614678899, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283280263710957e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 33256, "start": 340.34, "end": 340.82, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50754, 7587, 13, 50778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599536559161018, "compression_ratio": 1.665137614678899, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283280263710957e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 33256, "start": 341.38, "end": 347.86, "text": " Two charts assigning different numerical labels to the same physical point are not disagreeing about the nature of reality.", "tokens": [50806, 4453, 17767, 49602, 819, 29054, 16949, 281, 264, 912, 4001, 935, 366, 406, 14091, 278, 466, 264, 3687, 295, 4103, 13, 51130], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599536559161018, "compression_ratio": 1.665137614678899, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283280263710957e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 33256, "start": 348.26, "end": 350.78, "text": " They are just prioritizing different kinds of work.", "tokens": [51150, 814, 366, 445, 14846, 3319, 819, 3685, 295, 589, 13, 51276], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599536559161018, "compression_ratio": 1.665137614678899, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283280263710957e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 33256, "start": 350.98, "end": 353.44, "text": " Which leads to a really dangerous trap, I think.", "tokens": [51286, 3013, 6689, 281, 257, 534, 5795, 11487, 11, 286, 519, 13, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599536559161018, "compression_ratio": 1.665137614678899, "no_speech_prob": 2.0283280263710957e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 35344, "start": 353.44, "end": 364.66, "text": " Because if you forget that you are looking at reality through a highly specific optimized interface, you might mistake a glitch in the interface for a real physical feature of the universe.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 498, 291, 2870, 300, 291, 366, 1237, 412, 4103, 807, 257, 5405, 2685, 26941, 9226, 11, 291, 1062, 6146, 257, 23552, 294, 264, 9226, 337, 257, 957, 4001, 4111, 295, 264, 6445, 13, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1420487288002656, "compression_ratio": 1.6523297491039426, "no_speech_prob": 1.996896571709872e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 35344, "start": 365.06, "end": 365.32, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50946, 1079, 13, 50959], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1420487288002656, "compression_ratio": 1.6523297491039426, "no_speech_prob": 1.996896571709872e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 35344, "start": 365.7, "end": 368.28, "text": " Fliction has this great phrase for it, coordinate artifacts.", "tokens": [50978, 3235, 4105, 575, 341, 869, 9535, 337, 309, 11, 15670, 24617, 13, 51107], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1420487288002656, "compression_ratio": 1.6523297491039426, "no_speech_prob": 1.996896571709872e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 35344, "start": 368.6, "end": 370.52, "text": " The cost of forgetting the interface.", "tokens": [51123, 440, 2063, 295, 25428, 264, 9226, 13, 51219], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1420487288002656, "compression_ratio": 1.6523297491039426, "no_speech_prob": 1.996896571709872e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 35344, "start": 370.86, "end": 375.02, "text": " And they use the Earth as an example here, which perfectly illustrates the danger.", "tokens": [51236, 400, 436, 764, 264, 4755, 382, 364, 1365, 510, 11, 597, 6239, 41718, 264, 4330, 13, 51444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1420487288002656, "compression_ratio": 1.6523297491039426, "no_speech_prob": 1.996896571709872e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 35344, "start": 375.36, "end": 377.65999999999997, "text": " Think about 3D spherical coordinates.", "tokens": [51461, 6557, 466, 805, 35, 37300, 21056, 13, 51576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1420487288002656, "compression_ratio": 1.6523297491039426, "no_speech_prob": 1.996896571709872e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 35344, "start": 378.32, "end": 379.28, "text": " Longitude and latitude.", "tokens": [51609, 8282, 4377, 293, 45436, 13, 51657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1420487288002656, "compression_ratio": 1.6523297491039426, "no_speech_prob": 1.996896571709872e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 35344, "start": 379.42, "end": 380.22, "text": " We use them every day.", "tokens": [51664, 492, 764, 552, 633, 786, 13, 51704], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1420487288002656, "compression_ratio": 1.6523297491039426, "no_speech_prob": 1.996896571709872e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 38022, "start": 380.22, "end": 384.32000000000005, "text": " Now imagine you are standing exactly on the geographic North Pole.", "tokens": [50365, 823, 3811, 291, 366, 4877, 2293, 322, 264, 32318, 4067, 34212, 13, 50570], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11153818086813425, "compression_ratio": 1.7473684210526317, "no_speech_prob": 1.8533898374362145e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 38022, "start": 385.16, "end": 386.18, "text": " What is your longitude?", "tokens": [50612, 708, 307, 428, 938, 4377, 30, 50663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11153818086813425, "compression_ratio": 1.7473684210526317, "no_speech_prob": 1.8533898374362145e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 38022, "start": 386.74, "end": 389.28000000000003, "text": " Well, longitude lines run from pole to pole.", "tokens": [50691, 1042, 11, 938, 4377, 3876, 1190, 490, 13208, 281, 13208, 13, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11153818086813425, "compression_ratio": 1.7473684210526317, "no_speech_prob": 1.8533898374362145e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 38022, "start": 389.40000000000003, "end": 392.84000000000003, "text": " So if I'm standing exactly on the North Pole, it doesn't exist.", "tokens": [50824, 407, 498, 286, 478, 4877, 2293, 322, 264, 4067, 34212, 11, 309, 1177, 380, 2514, 13, 50996], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11153818086813425, "compression_ratio": 1.7473684210526317, "no_speech_prob": 1.8533898374362145e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 38022, "start": 393.0, "end": 393.1, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51004, 1779, 13, 51009], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11153818086813425, "compression_ratio": 1.7473684210526317, "no_speech_prob": 1.8533898374362145e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 38022, "start": 393.24, "end": 396.22, "text": " I mean, I'm at the point where all the longitude lines crash into each other.", "tokens": [51016, 286, 914, 11, 286, 478, 412, 264, 935, 689, 439, 264, 938, 4377, 3876, 8252, 666, 1184, 661, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11153818086813425, "compression_ratio": 1.7473684210526317, "no_speech_prob": 1.8533898374362145e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 38022, "start": 396.66, "end": 402.70000000000005, "text": " I could spin in a circle on my heel and theoretically pass through every single longitude on Earth in one second.", "tokens": [51187, 286, 727, 6060, 294, 257, 6329, 322, 452, 9430, 293, 29400, 1320, 807, 633, 2167, 938, 4377, 322, 4755, 294, 472, 1150, 13, 51489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11153818086813425, "compression_ratio": 1.7473684210526317, "no_speech_prob": 1.8533898374362145e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 38022, "start": 402.96000000000004, "end": 403.44000000000005, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51502, 7587, 13, 51526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11153818086813425, "compression_ratio": 1.7473684210526317, "no_speech_prob": 1.8533898374362145e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 38022, "start": 404.24, "end": 409.52000000000004, "text": " Mathematically, in that specific coordinate chart, the longitude at the pole is undefined.", "tokens": [51566, 15776, 40197, 11, 294, 300, 2685, 15670, 6927, 11, 264, 938, 4377, 412, 264, 13208, 307, 674, 5666, 2001, 13, 51830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11153818086813425, "compression_ratio": 1.7473684210526317, "no_speech_prob": 1.8533898374362145e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 40952, "start": 409.52, "end": 411.28, "text": " It looks like a singularity.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1542, 411, 257, 20010, 507, 13, 50453], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1659550909268654, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.5009373952046268e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 40952, "start": 411.64, "end": 414.5, "text": " Because multiple values exist at the same point simultaneously.", "tokens": [50471, 1436, 3866, 4190, 2514, 412, 264, 912, 935, 16561, 13, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1659550909268654, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.5009373952046268e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 40952, "start": 414.84, "end": 415.03999999999996, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50631, 1779, 13, 50641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1659550909268654, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.5009373952046268e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 40952, "start": 415.2, "end": 421.68, "text": " Now, if you are a physicist or a meteorologist running a careless weather simulation and your math hits the North Pole,", "tokens": [50649, 823, 11, 498, 291, 366, 257, 42466, 420, 257, 25313, 9201, 2614, 257, 46187, 5503, 16575, 293, 428, 5221, 8664, 264, 4067, 34212, 11, 50973], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1659550909268654, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.5009373952046268e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 40952, "start": 422.02, "end": 427.14, "text": " your equations might literally blow up to infinity because they can't handle an undefined variable.", "tokens": [50990, 428, 11787, 1062, 3736, 6327, 493, 281, 13202, 570, 436, 393, 380, 4813, 364, 674, 5666, 2001, 7006, 13, 51246], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1659550909268654, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.5009373952046268e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 40952, "start": 427.29999999999995, "end": 429.03999999999996, "text": " But this raises a vital question, right?", "tokens": [51254, 583, 341, 19658, 257, 11707, 1168, 11, 558, 30, 51341], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1659550909268654, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.5009373952046268e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 40952, "start": 429.12, "end": 429.32, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51345, 865, 13, 51355], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1659550909268654, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.5009373952046268e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 40952, "start": 429.62, "end": 433.34, "text": " Is there a physical gaping hole in the Earth at the North Pole?", "tokens": [51370, 1119, 456, 257, 4001, 7417, 278, 5458, 294, 264, 4755, 412, 264, 4067, 34212, 30, 51556], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1659550909268654, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.5009373952046268e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 40952, "start": 433.56, "end": 435.18, "text": " Is gravity collapsing there?", "tokens": [51567, 1119, 12110, 45339, 456, 30, 51648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1659550909268654, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.5009373952046268e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 40952, "start": 435.76, "end": 436.46, "text": " Is it?", "tokens": [51677, 1119, 309, 30, 51712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1659550909268654, "compression_ratio": 1.6236933797909407, "no_speech_prob": 1.5009373952046268e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 43646, "start": 436.46, "end": 436.97999999999996, "text": " No.", "tokens": [50365, 883, 13, 50391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.150629392234228, "compression_ratio": 1.5401785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594504432417164e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 43646, "start": 437.5, "end": 438.47999999999996, "text": " I mean, it's just ice.", "tokens": [50417, 286, 914, 11, 309, 311, 445, 4435, 13, 50466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.150629392234228, "compression_ratio": 1.5401785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594504432417164e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 43646, "start": 438.58, "end": 440.97999999999996, "text": " The space is smooth and perfectly ordinary.", "tokens": [50471, 440, 1901, 307, 5508, 293, 6239, 10547, 13, 50591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.150629392234228, "compression_ratio": 1.5401785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594504432417164e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 43646, "start": 441.21999999999997, "end": 444.53999999999996, "text": " The singularity is entirely a failure of our labeling scheme.", "tokens": [50603, 440, 20010, 507, 307, 7696, 257, 7763, 295, 527, 40244, 12232, 13, 50769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.150629392234228, "compression_ratio": 1.5401785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594504432417164e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 43646, "start": 445.02, "end": 450.79999999999995, "text": " The latitude-longitude system we chose is simply incapable of assigning a single well-defined number", "tokens": [50793, 440, 45436, 12, 13025, 4377, 1185, 321, 5111, 307, 2935, 44174, 295, 49602, 257, 2167, 731, 12, 37716, 1230, 51082], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.150629392234228, "compression_ratio": 1.5401785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594504432417164e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 43646, "start": 450.79999999999995, "end": 454.06, "text": " to a point that sits exactly on the axis of its own rotation.", "tokens": [51082, 281, 257, 935, 300, 12696, 2293, 322, 264, 10298, 295, 1080, 1065, 12447, 13, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.150629392234228, "compression_ratio": 1.5401785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594504432417164e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 43646, "start": 454.5, "end": 456.38, "text": " So the map is broken, not the territory.", "tokens": [51267, 407, 264, 4471, 307, 5463, 11, 406, 264, 11360, 13, 51361], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.150629392234228, "compression_ratio": 1.5401785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594504432417164e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 43646, "start": 456.53999999999996, "end": 457.02, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51369, 7587, 13, 51393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.150629392234228, "compression_ratio": 1.5401785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.2594504432417164e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 45702, "start": 457.02, "end": 460.0, "text": " So Flixian gives us a diagnostic rule to handle this.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 3235, 970, 952, 2709, 505, 257, 27897, 4978, 281, 4813, 341, 13, 50514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1639632849857725, "compression_ratio": 1.5336322869955157, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281925673504062e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 45702, "start": 460.08, "end": 462.0, "text": " They say, change the chart and see what survives.", "tokens": [50518, 814, 584, 11, 1319, 264, 6927, 293, 536, 437, 46231, 13, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1639632849857725, "compression_ratio": 1.5336322869955157, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281925673504062e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 45702, "start": 462.4, "end": 463.44, "text": " A very elegant rule.", "tokens": [50634, 316, 588, 21117, 4978, 13, 50686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1639632849857725, "compression_ratio": 1.5336322869955157, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281925673504062e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 45702, "start": 463.68, "end": 468.59999999999997, "text": " Meaning if the singularity disappears when you just use a different set of coordinates,", "tokens": [50698, 19948, 498, 264, 20010, 507, 25527, 562, 291, 445, 764, 257, 819, 992, 295, 21056, 11, 50944], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1639632849857725, "compression_ratio": 1.5336322869955157, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281925673504062e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 45702, "start": 468.79999999999995, "end": 474.06, "text": " like, say, sending your maps equator through the poles instead, then the problem was never real.", "tokens": [50954, 411, 11, 584, 11, 7750, 428, 11317, 45544, 807, 264, 24760, 2602, 11, 550, 264, 1154, 390, 1128, 957, 13, 51217], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1639632849857725, "compression_ratio": 1.5336322869955157, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281925673504062e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 45702, "start": 474.4, "end": 476.0, "text": " It was an artifact of your math.", "tokens": [51234, 467, 390, 364, 34806, 295, 428, 5221, 13, 51314], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1639632849857725, "compression_ratio": 1.5336322869955157, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281925673504062e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 47600, "start": 476.0, "end": 481.38, "text": " And if we connect this to the bigger picture of scientific research, it is a vital discipline.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 498, 321, 1745, 341, 281, 264, 3801, 3036, 295, 8134, 2132, 11, 309, 307, 257, 11707, 13635, 13, 50634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14610924591889252, "compression_ratio": 1.597938144329897, "no_speech_prob": 1.472218722799179e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 47600, "start": 481.78, "end": 485.94, "text": " Whether you are modeling fluid dynamics or black holes or stock markets,", "tokens": [50654, 8503, 291, 366, 15983, 9113, 15679, 420, 2211, 8118, 420, 4127, 8383, 11, 50862], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14610924591889252, "compression_ratio": 1.597938144329897, "no_speech_prob": 1.472218722799179e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 47600, "start": 486.16, "end": 490.84, "text": " you have to constantly ensure that the striking anomalous results you are getting", "tokens": [50873, 291, 362, 281, 6460, 5586, 300, 264, 18559, 24769, 11553, 3542, 291, 366, 1242, 51107], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14610924591889252, "compression_ratio": 1.597938144329897, "no_speech_prob": 1.472218722799179e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 47600, "start": 490.84, "end": 494.42, "text": " aren't just accidents of how you chose to format the data.", "tokens": [51107, 3212, 380, 445, 23875, 295, 577, 291, 5111, 281, 7877, 264, 1412, 13, 51286], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14610924591889252, "compression_ratio": 1.597938144329897, "no_speech_prob": 1.472218722799179e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 47600, "start": 494.76, "end": 495.84, "text": " I love that rule.", "tokens": [51303, 286, 959, 300, 4978, 13, 51357], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14610924591889252, "compression_ratio": 1.597938144329897, "no_speech_prob": 1.472218722799179e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 47600, "start": 496.0, "end": 497.94, "text": " It's incredibly empowering for a learner.", "tokens": [51365, 467, 311, 6252, 28261, 337, 257, 33347, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14610924591889252, "compression_ratio": 1.597938144329897, "no_speech_prob": 1.472218722799179e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 47600, "start": 498.24, "end": 502.04, "text": " But I kind of want to push back a little here because this sounds almost too convenient.", "tokens": [51477, 583, 286, 733, 295, 528, 281, 2944, 646, 257, 707, 510, 570, 341, 3263, 1920, 886, 10851, 13, 51667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14610924591889252, "compression_ratio": 1.597938144329897, "no_speech_prob": 1.472218722799179e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 47600, "start": 502.5, "end": 502.96, "text": " How so?", "tokens": [51690, 1012, 370, 30, 51713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14610924591889252, "compression_ratio": 1.597938144329897, "no_speech_prob": 1.472218722799179e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 50296, "start": 502.96, "end": 507.79999999999995, "text": " Wait, so is every weird geometric glitch just a bad labeling scheme?", "tokens": [50365, 3802, 11, 370, 307, 633, 3657, 33246, 23552, 445, 257, 1578, 40244, 12232, 30, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11772616577148437, "compression_ratio": 1.6069182389937107, "no_speech_prob": 1.2794049673858776e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 50296, "start": 507.9, "end": 511.78, "text": " Like, if I'm an astronomer and I find something in space that was mathematically broken,", "tokens": [50612, 1743, 11, 498, 286, 478, 364, 11117, 14301, 293, 286, 915, 746, 294, 1901, 300, 390, 44003, 5463, 11, 50806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11772616577148437, "compression_ratio": 1.6069182389937107, "no_speech_prob": 1.2794049673858776e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 50296, "start": 512.18, "end": 516.14, "text": " can I always just assume I'm using the wrong coordinate interface, pat myself on the back", "tokens": [50826, 393, 286, 1009, 445, 6552, 286, 478, 1228, 264, 2085, 15670, 9226, 11, 1947, 2059, 322, 264, 646, 51024], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11772616577148437, "compression_ratio": 1.6069182389937107, "no_speech_prob": 1.2794049673858776e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 50296, "start": 516.14, "end": 516.6999999999999, "text": " and wave it away?", "tokens": [51024, 293, 5772, 309, 1314, 30, 51052], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11772616577148437, "compression_ratio": 1.6069182389937107, "no_speech_prob": 1.2794049673858776e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 50296, "start": 516.86, "end": 521.78, "text": " It is a very tempting thought to believe that the universe is perfectly smooth and only our", "tokens": [51060, 467, 307, 257, 588, 37900, 1194, 281, 1697, 300, 264, 6445, 307, 6239, 5508, 293, 787, 527, 51306], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11772616577148437, "compression_ratio": 1.6069182389937107, "no_speech_prob": 1.2794049673858776e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 50296, "start": 521.78, "end": 522.6, "text": " maps are flawed.", "tokens": [51306, 11317, 366, 38823, 13, 51347], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11772616577148437, "compression_ratio": 1.6069182389937107, "no_speech_prob": 1.2794049673858776e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 50296, "start": 522.88, "end": 523.3199999999999, "text": " But no.", "tokens": [51361, 583, 572, 13, 51383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11772616577148437, "compression_ratio": 1.6069182389937107, "no_speech_prob": 1.2794049673858776e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 50296, "start": 523.66, "end": 527.46, "text": " And Flixian is extremely careful to address this exact point.", "tokens": [51400, 400, 3235, 970, 952, 307, 4664, 5026, 281, 2985, 341, 1900, 935, 13, 51590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11772616577148437, "compression_ratio": 1.6069182389937107, "no_speech_prob": 1.2794049673858776e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 50296, "start": 527.46, "end": 531.48, "text": " They draw a hard mathematical line between artifacts of the chart,", "tokens": [51590, 814, 2642, 257, 1152, 18894, 1622, 1296, 24617, 295, 264, 6927, 11, 51791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11772616577148437, "compression_ratio": 1.6069182389937107, "no_speech_prob": 1.2794049673858776e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 53148, "start": 531.48, "end": 536.02, "text": " like our North Pole example, and what topology calls invariance of the embedding.", "tokens": [50365, 411, 527, 4067, 34212, 1365, 11, 293, 437, 1192, 1793, 5498, 33270, 719, 295, 264, 12240, 3584, 13, 50592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20214505629106003, "compression_ratio": 1.472636815920398, "no_speech_prob": 1.4430380718480351e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 53148, "start": 536.28, "end": 537.82, "text": " Because sometimes the problem is real.", "tokens": [50605, 1436, 2171, 264, 1154, 307, 957, 13, 50682], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20214505629106003, "compression_ratio": 1.472636815920398, "no_speech_prob": 1.4430380718480351e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 53148, "start": 538.04, "end": 541.32, "text": " And they bring up this thing called the Alexander Horn Sphere to prove it.", "tokens": [50693, 400, 436, 1565, 493, 341, 551, 1219, 264, 14845, 31792, 318, 6605, 281, 7081, 309, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20214505629106003, "compression_ratio": 1.472636815920398, "no_speech_prob": 1.4430380718480351e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 53148, "start": 542.64, "end": 546.4200000000001, "text": " Which, just the name alone, sounds like an esoteric heavy metal band.", "tokens": [50923, 3013, 11, 445, 264, 1315, 3312, 11, 3263, 411, 364, 785, 21585, 299, 4676, 5760, 4116, 13, 51112], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20214505629106003, "compression_ratio": 1.472636815920398, "no_speech_prob": 1.4430380718480351e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 53148, "start": 546.84, "end": 548.82, "text": " What exactly is a horn sphere?", "tokens": [51133, 708, 2293, 307, 257, 13482, 16687, 30, 51232], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20214505629106003, "compression_ratio": 1.472636815920398, "no_speech_prob": 1.4430380718480351e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 54882, "start": 548.82, "end": 553.0400000000001, "text": " It is one of the most famous and unnerving mathematical constructs in topology.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 472, 295, 264, 881, 4618, 293, 517, 1193, 798, 18894, 7690, 82, 294, 1192, 1793, 13, 50576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1376477313298051, "compression_ratio": 1.559670781893004, "no_speech_prob": 1.6295931618004467e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 54882, "start": 553.6600000000001, "end": 558.6800000000001, "text": " It beautifully or perhaps terrifyingly illustrates the difference between a flat embedding where", "tokens": [50607, 467, 16525, 420, 4317, 18106, 356, 41718, 264, 2649, 1296, 257, 4962, 12240, 3584, 689, 50858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1376477313298051, "compression_ratio": 1.559670781893004, "no_speech_prob": 1.6295931618004467e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 54882, "start": 558.6800000000001, "end": 562.9000000000001, "text": " things behave normally and a wild embedding where the universe itself is tangled.", "tokens": [50858, 721, 15158, 5646, 293, 257, 4868, 12240, 3584, 689, 264, 6445, 2564, 307, 47192, 13, 51069], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1376477313298051, "compression_ratio": 1.559670781893004, "no_speech_prob": 1.6295931618004467e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 54882, "start": 562.98, "end": 564.0600000000001, "text": " Okay, I'm braced for this.", "tokens": [51073, 1033, 11, 286, 478, 738, 3839, 337, 341, 13, 51127], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1376477313298051, "compression_ratio": 1.559670781893004, "no_speech_prob": 1.6295931618004467e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 54882, "start": 564.2800000000001, "end": 569.4000000000001, "text": " I want you to imagine a standard, perfectly round sphere in your mind, a rubber ball.", "tokens": [51138, 286, 528, 291, 281, 3811, 257, 3832, 11, 6239, 3098, 16687, 294, 428, 1575, 11, 257, 11593, 2594, 13, 51394], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1376477313298051, "compression_ratio": 1.559670781893004, "no_speech_prob": 1.6295931618004467e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 54882, "start": 569.6400000000001, "end": 570.1, "text": " Got it.", "tokens": [51406, 5803, 309, 13, 51429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1376477313298051, "compression_ratio": 1.559670781893004, "no_speech_prob": 1.6295931618004467e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 57010, "start": 570.1, "end": 575.72, "text": " We know it has a distinct inside and a distinct outside separated by the rubber skin.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 458, 309, 575, 257, 10644, 1854, 293, 257, 10644, 2380, 12005, 538, 264, 11593, 3178, 13, 50646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16579360016121353, "compression_ratio": 1.6788321167883211, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667086989383904e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 57010, "start": 576.58, "end": 580.58, "text": " Now imagine taking two spots on the outside of that rubber ball, pinching them, pulling", "tokens": [50689, 823, 3811, 1940, 732, 10681, 322, 264, 2380, 295, 300, 11593, 2594, 11, 14614, 278, 552, 11, 8407, 50889], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16579360016121353, "compression_ratio": 1.6788321167883211, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667086989383904e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 57010, "start": 580.58, "end": 583.9, "text": " them out like two long horns and bringing them close together so they almost interlock.", "tokens": [50889, 552, 484, 411, 732, 938, 28818, 293, 5062, 552, 1998, 1214, 370, 436, 1920, 728, 4102, 13, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16579360016121353, "compression_ratio": 1.6788321167883211, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667086989383904e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 57010, "start": 584.14, "end": 586.22, "text": " Like two fingers just about to pinch each other.", "tokens": [51067, 1743, 732, 7350, 445, 466, 281, 14614, 1184, 661, 13, 51171], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16579360016121353, "compression_ratio": 1.6788321167883211, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667086989383904e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 57010, "start": 586.5600000000001, "end": 586.82, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51188, 1033, 13, 51201], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16579360016121353, "compression_ratio": 1.6788321167883211, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667086989383904e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 57010, "start": 587.1, "end": 591.26, "text": " I am picturing a sphere with two intertwined horns.", "tokens": [51215, 286, 669, 2317, 1345, 257, 16687, 365, 732, 44400, 2001, 28818, 13, 51423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16579360016121353, "compression_ratio": 1.6788321167883211, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667086989383904e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 57010, "start": 591.9, "end": 592.0, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51455, 1079, 13, 51460], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16579360016121353, "compression_ratio": 1.6788321167883211, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667086989383904e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 57010, "start": 592.0, "end": 593.4, "text": " A little weird, but still manageable.", "tokens": [51460, 316, 707, 3657, 11, 457, 920, 38798, 13, 51530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16579360016121353, "compression_ratio": 1.6788321167883211, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667086989383904e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 57010, "start": 593.64, "end": 595.0, "text": " It hasn't broken my brain yet.", "tokens": [51542, 467, 6132, 380, 5463, 452, 3567, 1939, 13, 51610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16579360016121353, "compression_ratio": 1.6788321167883211, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667086989383904e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 57010, "start": 595.0600000000001, "end": 595.48, "text": " Give it a moment.", "tokens": [51613, 5303, 309, 257, 1623, 13, 51634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16579360016121353, "compression_ratio": 1.6788321167883211, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667086989383904e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 59548, "start": 595.48, "end": 601.84, "text": " Now on each of the tips of those two horns, grow two more smaller horns and have those", "tokens": [50365, 823, 322, 1184, 295, 264, 6082, 295, 729, 732, 28818, 11, 1852, 732, 544, 4356, 28818, 293, 362, 729, 50683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15449171799879807, "compression_ratio": 1.7906976744186047, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182020559281975e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 59548, "start": 601.84, "end": 606.9200000000001, "text": " new pairs reach out and almost interlock and then do it again on the tips of those horns", "tokens": [50683, 777, 15494, 2524, 484, 293, 1920, 728, 4102, 293, 550, 360, 309, 797, 322, 264, 6082, 295, 729, 28818, 50937], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15449171799879807, "compression_ratio": 1.7906976744186047, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182020559281975e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 59548, "start": 606.9200000000001, "end": 609.3000000000001, "text": " and again, infinitely.", "tokens": [50937, 293, 797, 11, 36227, 13, 51056], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15449171799879807, "compression_ratio": 1.7906976744186047, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182020559281975e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 59548, "start": 609.52, "end": 610.1, "text": " Wait, infinitely.", "tokens": [51067, 3802, 11, 36227, 13, 51096], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15449171799879807, "compression_ratio": 1.7906976744186047, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182020559281975e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 59548, "start": 610.26, "end": 610.7, "text": " Infinitely.", "tokens": [51104, 682, 10925, 13, 51126], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15449171799879807, "compression_ratio": 1.7906976744186047, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182020559281975e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 59548, "start": 610.96, "end": 617.5600000000001, "text": " You create this fractal, infinitely branching, relentlessly interlocking structure that gets", "tokens": [51139, 509, 1884, 341, 17948, 304, 11, 36227, 9819, 278, 11, 34045, 12048, 728, 4102, 278, 3877, 300, 2170, 51469], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15449171799879807, "compression_ratio": 1.7906976744186047, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182020559281975e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 59548, "start": 617.5600000000001, "end": 619.94, "text": " smaller and smaller but never actually touches itself.", "tokens": [51469, 4356, 293, 4356, 457, 1128, 767, 17431, 2564, 13, 51588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15449171799879807, "compression_ratio": 1.7906976744186047, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182020559281975e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 59548, "start": 620.24, "end": 622.02, "text": " This is the Alexander horn sphere.", "tokens": [51603, 639, 307, 264, 14845, 13482, 16687, 13, 51692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15449171799879807, "compression_ratio": 1.7906976744186047, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182020559281975e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 59548, "start": 622.08, "end": 622.52, "text": " Okay, yes.", "tokens": [51695, 1033, 11, 2086, 13, 51717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15449171799879807, "compression_ratio": 1.7906976744186047, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182020559281975e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 59548, "start": 622.54, "end": 623.98, "text": " That sounds like an absolute nightmare.", "tokens": [51718, 663, 3263, 411, 364, 8236, 18724, 13, 51790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15449171799879807, "compression_ratio": 1.7906976744186047, "no_speech_prob": 1.8182020559281975e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 62398, "start": 623.98, "end": 626.3000000000001, "text": " Here is the truly fascinating part.", "tokens": [50365, 1692, 307, 264, 4908, 10343, 644, 13, 50481], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12520451653272585, "compression_ratio": 1.6816720257234727, "no_speech_prob": 2.0680256552357834e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 62398, "start": 626.44, "end": 630.22, "text": " From the perspective of an ant walking on the surface of that sphere, everything seems", "tokens": [50488, 3358, 264, 4585, 295, 364, 2511, 4494, 322, 264, 3753, 295, 300, 16687, 11, 1203, 2544, 50677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12520451653272585, "compression_ratio": 1.6816720257234727, "no_speech_prob": 2.0680256552357834e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 62398, "start": 630.22, "end": 631.0, "text": " perfectly normal.", "tokens": [50677, 6239, 2710, 13, 50716], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12520451653272585, "compression_ratio": 1.6816720257234727, "no_speech_prob": 2.0680256552357834e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 62398, "start": 631.22, "end": 631.5, "text": " Really?", "tokens": [50727, 4083, 30, 50741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12520451653272585, "compression_ratio": 1.6816720257234727, "no_speech_prob": 2.0680256552357834e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 62398, "start": 631.74, "end": 632.0600000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50753, 1079, 13, 50769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12520451653272585, "compression_ratio": 1.6816720257234727, "no_speech_prob": 2.0680256552357834e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 62398, "start": 632.4200000000001, "end": 636.36, "text": " The local coordinate charts on the surface of the sphere itself can be made to look completely", "tokens": [50787, 440, 2654, 15670, 17767, 322, 264, 3753, 295, 264, 16687, 2564, 393, 312, 1027, 281, 574, 2584, 50984], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12520451653272585, "compression_ratio": 1.6816720257234727, "no_speech_prob": 2.0680256552357834e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 62398, "start": 636.36, "end": 636.98, "text": " ordinary.", "tokens": [50984, 10547, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12520451653272585, "compression_ratio": 1.6816720257234727, "no_speech_prob": 2.0680256552357834e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 62398, "start": 637.58, "end": 638.76, "text": " The ant can walk everywhere.", "tokens": [51045, 440, 2511, 393, 1792, 5315, 13, 51104], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12520451653272585, "compression_ratio": 1.6816720257234727, "no_speech_prob": 2.0680256552357834e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 62398, "start": 639.5, "end": 644.66, "text": " The surface is technically still a continuous, intact, unbroken 2D skin.", "tokens": [51141, 440, 3753, 307, 12120, 920, 257, 10957, 11, 23493, 11, 517, 37947, 568, 35, 3178, 13, 51399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12520451653272585, "compression_ratio": 1.6816720257234727, "no_speech_prob": 2.0680256552357834e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 62398, "start": 644.8000000000001, "end": 646.28, "text": " But it's infinitely wrinkled.", "tokens": [51406, 583, 309, 311, 36227, 928, 475, 1493, 13, 51480], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12520451653272585, "compression_ratio": 1.6816720257234727, "no_speech_prob": 2.0680256552357834e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 62398, "start": 646.38, "end": 651.5, "text": " But the space around it, the 3D room you place this object into, has been permanently deformed", "tokens": [51485, 583, 264, 1901, 926, 309, 11, 264, 805, 35, 1808, 291, 1081, 341, 2657, 666, 11, 575, 668, 24042, 368, 22892, 51741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12520451653272585, "compression_ratio": 1.6816720257234727, "no_speech_prob": 2.0680256552357834e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 62398, "start": 651.5, "end": 653.7, "text": " by this infinitely intertwined shape.", "tokens": [51741, 538, 341, 36227, 44400, 2001, 3909, 13, 51851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12520451653272585, "compression_ratio": 1.6816720257234727, "no_speech_prob": 2.0680256552357834e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 65370, "start": 653.7, "end": 656.9000000000001, "text": " Wait, how does an object deform the empty room it's sitting in?", "tokens": [50365, 3802, 11, 577, 775, 364, 2657, 36094, 264, 6707, 1808, 309, 311, 3798, 294, 30, 50525], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12131508006605991, "compression_ratio": 1.5980861244019138, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832754366399085e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 65370, "start": 657.3000000000001, "end": 660.76, "text": " Think about empty space as having its own topology.", "tokens": [50545, 6557, 466, 6707, 1901, 382, 1419, 1080, 1065, 1192, 1793, 13, 50718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12131508006605991, "compression_ratio": 1.5980861244019138, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832754366399085e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 65370, "start": 661.72, "end": 667.5600000000001, "text": " Normally, if you tie a loop of string in the empty space outside a normal sphere, you can", "tokens": [50766, 17424, 11, 498, 291, 7582, 257, 6367, 295, 6798, 294, 264, 6707, 1901, 2380, 257, 2710, 16687, 11, 291, 393, 51058], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12131508006605991, "compression_ratio": 1.5980861244019138, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832754366399085e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 65370, "start": 667.5600000000001, "end": 671.9000000000001, "text": " always pull that string away and shrink it down to nothing without getting caught on the", "tokens": [51058, 1009, 2235, 300, 6798, 1314, 293, 23060, 309, 760, 281, 1825, 1553, 1242, 5415, 322, 264, 51275], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12131508006605991, "compression_ratio": 1.5980861244019138, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832754366399085e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 65370, "start": 671.9000000000001, "end": 672.1800000000001, "text": " sphere.", "tokens": [51275, 16687, 13, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12131508006605991, "compression_ratio": 1.5980861244019138, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832754366399085e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 65370, "start": 672.32, "end": 673.48, "text": " Right, it just slips right off.", "tokens": [51296, 1779, 11, 309, 445, 44690, 558, 766, 13, 51354], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12131508006605991, "compression_ratio": 1.5980861244019138, "no_speech_prob": 1.8832754366399085e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 67348, "start": 673.48, "end": 679.62, "text": " But with the Alexander horn sphere, the exterior space is so deeply, fractally invaded by the", "tokens": [50365, 583, 365, 264, 14845, 13482, 16687, 11, 264, 20677, 1901, 307, 370, 8760, 11, 17948, 379, 35882, 538, 264, 50672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11905344857109917, "compression_ratio": 1.5814977973568283, "no_speech_prob": 1.531105754334905e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 67348, "start": 679.62, "end": 684.04, "text": " horns that you can tie a loop of string in the empty space around the horns and it gets", "tokens": [50672, 28818, 300, 291, 393, 7582, 257, 6367, 295, 6798, 294, 264, 6707, 1901, 926, 264, 28818, 293, 309, 2170, 50893], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11905344857109917, "compression_ratio": 1.5814977973568283, "no_speech_prob": 1.531105754334905e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 67348, "start": 684.04, "end": 684.44, "text": " trapped.", "tokens": [50893, 14994, 13, 50913], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11905344857109917, "compression_ratio": 1.5814977973568283, "no_speech_prob": 1.531105754334905e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 67348, "start": 684.6800000000001, "end": 687.94, "text": " Because it's caught in the infinitely branching labyrinth.", "tokens": [50925, 1436, 309, 311, 5415, 294, 264, 36227, 9819, 278, 287, 46800, 392, 13, 51088], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11905344857109917, "compression_ratio": 1.5814977973568283, "no_speech_prob": 1.531105754334905e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 67348, "start": 688.04, "end": 688.48, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51093, 7587, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11905344857109917, "compression_ratio": 1.5814977973568283, "no_speech_prob": 1.531105754334905e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 67348, "start": 689.0600000000001, "end": 691.72, "text": " The outside space is no longer simply connected.", "tokens": [51144, 440, 2380, 1901, 307, 572, 2854, 2935, 4582, 13, 51277], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11905344857109917, "compression_ratio": 1.5814977973568283, "no_speech_prob": 1.531105754334905e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 67348, "start": 692.08, "end": 694.84, "text": " The shape has literally tangled the void around it.", "tokens": [51295, 440, 3909, 575, 3736, 47192, 264, 22009, 926, 309, 13, 51433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11905344857109917, "compression_ratio": 1.5814977973568283, "no_speech_prob": 1.531105754334905e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 69484, "start": 694.84, "end": 698.82, "text": " So unlike the North Pole, where you just change your map and the problem vanishes with the", "tokens": [50365, 407, 8343, 264, 4067, 34212, 11, 689, 291, 445, 1319, 428, 4471, 293, 264, 1154, 3161, 16423, 365, 264, 50564], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09886319820697491, "compression_ratio": 1.4727272727272727, "no_speech_prob": 1.7343174422632113e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 69484, "start": 698.82, "end": 702.2800000000001, "text": " horn sphere, the 3D space itself is genuinely compromised.", "tokens": [50564, 13482, 16687, 11, 264, 805, 35, 1901, 2564, 307, 17839, 32463, 13, 50737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09886319820697491, "compression_ratio": 1.4727272727272727, "no_speech_prob": 1.7343174422632113e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 69484, "start": 702.6, "end": 702.98, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50753, 7587, 13, 50772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09886319820697491, "compression_ratio": 1.4727272727272727, "no_speech_prob": 1.7343174422632113e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 69484, "start": 703.22, "end": 709.52, "text": " You cannot just adopt a clever new 3D Cartesian or polar coordinate system to make the Alexander", "tokens": [50784, 509, 2644, 445, 6878, 257, 13494, 777, 805, 35, 22478, 42434, 420, 12367, 15670, 1185, 281, 652, 264, 14845, 51099], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09886319820697491, "compression_ratio": 1.4727272727272727, "no_speech_prob": 1.7343174422632113e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 69484, "start": 709.52, "end": 713.02, "text": " horn sphere look like a normal smooth ball sitting in an empty room.", "tokens": [51099, 13482, 16687, 574, 411, 257, 2710, 5508, 2594, 3798, 294, 364, 6707, 1808, 13, 51274], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09886319820697491, "compression_ratio": 1.4727272727272727, "no_speech_prob": 1.7343174422632113e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 71302, "start": 713.02, "end": 714.24, "text": " The pathology is real.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3100, 1793, 307, 957, 13, 50426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15859347979227703, "compression_ratio": 1.6185185185185185, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656414083218943e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 71302, "start": 714.24, "end": 718.64, "text": " It is a real invariant feature of how that object is embedded in space.", "tokens": [50426, 467, 307, 257, 957, 33270, 394, 4111, 295, 577, 300, 2657, 307, 16741, 294, 1901, 13, 50646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15859347979227703, "compression_ratio": 1.6185185185185185, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656414083218943e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 71302, "start": 719.06, "end": 720.5, "text": " It is a wild embedding.", "tokens": [50667, 467, 307, 257, 4868, 12240, 3584, 13, 50739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15859347979227703, "compression_ratio": 1.6185185185185185, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656414083218943e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 71302, "start": 720.9, "end": 722.46, "text": " No ambient change of coordinates.", "tokens": [50759, 883, 22997, 1319, 295, 21056, 13, 50837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15859347979227703, "compression_ratio": 1.6185185185185185, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656414083218943e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 71302, "start": 723.22, "end": 726.4, "text": " No clever dashboard UI can rescue it.", "tokens": [50875, 883, 13494, 18342, 15682, 393, 13283, 309, 13, 51034], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15859347979227703, "compression_ratio": 1.6185185185185185, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656414083218943e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 71302, "start": 726.72, "end": 728.22, "text": " The map isn't broken here.", "tokens": [51050, 440, 4471, 1943, 380, 5463, 510, 13, 51125], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15859347979227703, "compression_ratio": 1.6185185185185185, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656414083218943e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 71302, "start": 728.56, "end": 729.46, "text": " Reality is.", "tokens": [51142, 33822, 307, 13, 51187], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15859347979227703, "compression_ratio": 1.6185185185185185, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656414083218943e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 71302, "start": 729.66, "end": 731.1999999999999, "text": " That distinction is so clarifying.", "tokens": [51197, 663, 16844, 307, 370, 6093, 5489, 13, 51274], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15859347979227703, "compression_ratio": 1.6185185185185185, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656414083218943e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 71302, "start": 731.52, "end": 735.22, "text": " Changing the chart doesn't fix it if the universe is actually weird in that spot.", "tokens": [51290, 45773, 264, 6927, 1177, 380, 3191, 309, 498, 264, 6445, 307, 767, 3657, 294, 300, 4008, 13, 51475], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15859347979227703, "compression_ratio": 1.6185185185185185, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656414083218943e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 71302, "start": 735.78, "end": 741.0799999999999, "text": " So if we know that some spaces are wildly tangled, but most of the things we study aren't,", "tokens": [51503, 407, 498, 321, 458, 300, 512, 7673, 366, 34731, 47192, 11, 457, 881, 295, 264, 721, 321, 2979, 3212, 380, 11, 51768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15859347979227703, "compression_ratio": 1.6185185185185185, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656414083218943e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 74108, "start": 741.08, "end": 744.48, "text": " how do we choose the right map for the normal stuff?", "tokens": [50365, 577, 360, 321, 2826, 264, 558, 4471, 337, 264, 2710, 1507, 30, 50535], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14314047992229462, "compression_ratio": 1.5931034482758621, "no_speech_prob": 2.03644956800475e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 74108, "start": 744.6800000000001, "end": 745.9200000000001, "text": " Yeah, that is the big question.", "tokens": [50545, 865, 11, 300, 307, 264, 955, 1168, 13, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14314047992229462, "compression_ratio": 1.5931034482758621, "no_speech_prob": 2.03644956800475e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 74108, "start": 746.2, "end": 746.36, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50621, 1779, 13, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14314047992229462, "compression_ratio": 1.5931034482758621, "no_speech_prob": 2.03644956800475e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 74108, "start": 746.4200000000001, "end": 750.96, "text": " Because if coordinates are just tools we choose to optimize our work and we want to analyze", "tokens": [50632, 1436, 498, 21056, 366, 445, 3873, 321, 2826, 281, 19719, 527, 589, 293, 321, 528, 281, 12477, 50859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14314047992229462, "compression_ratio": 1.5931034482758621, "no_speech_prob": 2.03644956800475e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 74108, "start": 750.96, "end": 755.9200000000001, "text": " the most common forces in nature, how do we know which tool is the absolute best?", "tokens": [50859, 264, 881, 2689, 5874, 294, 3687, 11, 577, 360, 321, 458, 597, 2290, 307, 264, 8236, 1151, 30, 51107], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14314047992229462, "compression_ratio": 1.5931034482758621, "no_speech_prob": 2.03644956800475e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 74108, "start": 756.48, "end": 761.58, "text": " We saw Cartesian is great for sliding, polar is great for 2D spinning, but we live in the", "tokens": [51135, 492, 1866, 22478, 42434, 307, 869, 337, 21169, 11, 12367, 307, 869, 337, 568, 35, 15640, 11, 457, 321, 1621, 294, 264, 51390], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14314047992229462, "compression_ratio": 1.5931034482758621, "no_speech_prob": 2.03644956800475e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 74108, "start": 761.58, "end": 762.2, "text": " 3D world.", "tokens": [51390, 805, 35, 1002, 13, 51421], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14314047992229462, "compression_ratio": 1.5931034482758621, "no_speech_prob": 2.03644956800475e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 74108, "start": 762.5400000000001, "end": 764.24, "text": " What happens when we level up to 3D?", "tokens": [51438, 708, 2314, 562, 321, 1496, 493, 281, 805, 35, 30, 51523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14314047992229462, "compression_ratio": 1.5931034482758621, "no_speech_prob": 2.03644956800475e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 74108, "start": 764.5, "end": 767.2800000000001, "text": " This brings us to the core thesis of Flickshman's geometry.", "tokens": [51536, 639, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 4965, 22288, 295, 3235, 618, 2716, 1601, 311, 18426, 13, 51675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14314047992229462, "compression_ratio": 1.5931034482758621, "no_speech_prob": 2.03644956800475e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 76728, "start": 767.28, "end": 772.28, "text": " They treat the selection of a coordinate system as a genuine, rigorous optimization problem.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 2387, 264, 9450, 295, 257, 15670, 1185, 382, 257, 16699, 11, 29882, 19618, 1154, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1448532451282848, "compression_ratio": 1.755485893416928, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232297624096947e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 76728, "start": 772.74, "end": 776.0799999999999, "text": " You don't just pick a coordinate system because it is traditional or because your teacher handed", "tokens": [50638, 509, 500, 380, 445, 1888, 257, 15670, 1185, 570, 309, 307, 5164, 420, 570, 428, 5027, 16013, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1448532451282848, "compression_ratio": 1.755485893416928, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232297624096947e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 76728, "start": 776.0799999999999, "end": 776.8199999999999, "text": " you graph paper.", "tokens": [50805, 291, 4295, 3035, 13, 50842], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1448532451282848, "compression_ratio": 1.755485893416928, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232297624096947e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 76728, "start": 777.0799999999999, "end": 781.38, "text": " You pick it because it mathematically minimizes the computational work required to express", "tokens": [50855, 509, 1888, 309, 570, 309, 44003, 4464, 5660, 264, 28270, 589, 4739, 281, 5109, 51070], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1448532451282848, "compression_ratio": 1.755485893416928, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232297624096947e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 76728, "start": 781.38, "end": 783.22, "text": " a specific class of transformations.", "tokens": [51070, 257, 2685, 1508, 295, 34852, 13, 51162], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1448532451282848, "compression_ratio": 1.755485893416928, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232297624096947e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 76728, "start": 783.68, "end": 785.4599999999999, "text": " What mathematicians call group actions.", "tokens": [51185, 708, 32811, 2567, 818, 1594, 5909, 13, 51274], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1448532451282848, "compression_ratio": 1.755485893416928, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232297624096947e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 76728, "start": 785.8, "end": 786.16, "text": " Correct.", "tokens": [51291, 12753, 13, 51309], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1448532451282848, "compression_ratio": 1.755485893416928, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232297624096947e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 76728, "start": 786.6, "end": 791.5, "text": " Group actions are just formal ways of describing how things change or move symmetrically.", "tokens": [51331, 10500, 5909, 366, 445, 9860, 2098, 295, 16141, 577, 721, 1319, 420, 1286, 14232, 27965, 984, 13, 51576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1448532451282848, "compression_ratio": 1.755485893416928, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232297624096947e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 76728, "start": 791.78, "end": 795.64, "text": " We already covered translation sliding left, right, up, down, where the Cartesian grid", "tokens": [51590, 492, 1217, 5343, 12853, 21169, 1411, 11, 558, 11, 493, 11, 760, 11, 689, 264, 22478, 42434, 10748, 51783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1448532451282848, "compression_ratio": 1.755485893416928, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232297624096947e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 79564, "start": 795.64, "end": 800.02, "text": " is king, then there is axial symmetry like the shape of a pipe or a cylinder.", "tokens": [50365, 307, 4867, 11, 550, 456, 307, 46851, 25440, 411, 264, 3909, 295, 257, 11240, 420, 257, 17884, 13, 50584], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14879866207347198, "compression_ratio": 1.6325757575757576, "no_speech_prob": 1.610850667264907e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 79564, "start": 800.68, "end": 805.5, "text": " If your physical system involves fluid spinning around inside a pipe or sliding down its length,", "tokens": [50617, 759, 428, 4001, 1185, 11626, 9113, 15640, 926, 1854, 257, 11240, 420, 21169, 760, 1080, 4641, 11, 50858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14879866207347198, "compression_ratio": 1.6325757575757576, "no_speech_prob": 1.610850667264907e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 79564, "start": 806.0, "end": 809.22, "text": " Flickshman points out that cylindrical coordinates are maximally adapted.", "tokens": [50883, 3235, 618, 2716, 1601, 2793, 484, 300, 28044, 15888, 21056, 366, 5138, 379, 20871, 13, 51044], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14879866207347198, "compression_ratio": 1.6325757575757576, "no_speech_prob": 1.610850667264907e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 79564, "start": 809.6999999999999, "end": 811.46, "text": " The math becomes almost effortless.", "tokens": [51068, 440, 5221, 3643, 1920, 4630, 1832, 13, 51156], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14879866207347198, "compression_ratio": 1.6325757575757576, "no_speech_prob": 1.610850667264907e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 79564, "start": 811.56, "end": 816.72, "text": " But the big one, the symmetry that this entire deep diet hinges on, is rotational symmetry around", "tokens": [51161, 583, 264, 955, 472, 11, 264, 25440, 300, 341, 2302, 2452, 6339, 46686, 322, 11, 307, 45420, 25440, 926, 51419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14879866207347198, "compression_ratio": 1.6325757575757576, "no_speech_prob": 1.610850667264907e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 79564, "start": 816.72, "end": 819.24, "text": " a single central point in three dimensions.", "tokens": [51419, 257, 2167, 5777, 935, 294, 1045, 12819, 13, 51545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14879866207347198, "compression_ratio": 1.6325757575757576, "no_speech_prob": 1.610850667264907e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 79564, "start": 819.4399999999999, "end": 819.78, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51555, 1079, 13, 51572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14879866207347198, "compression_ratio": 1.6325757575757576, "no_speech_prob": 1.610850667264907e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 81978, "start": 819.78, "end": 824.0799999999999, "text": " Things like gravity pulling toward a planet's core or an atom's nucleus or even a localized", "tokens": [50365, 9514, 411, 12110, 8407, 7361, 257, 5054, 311, 4965, 420, 364, 12018, 311, 28055, 420, 754, 257, 44574, 50580], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11740005114846978, "compression_ratio": 1.6037151702786379, "no_speech_prob": 2.0766376899322703e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 81978, "start": 824.0799999999999, "end": 825.6999999999999, "text": " explosion radiating outward.", "tokens": [50580, 15673, 16335, 990, 26914, 13, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11740005114846978, "compression_ratio": 1.6037151702786379, "no_speech_prob": 2.0766376899322703e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 81978, "start": 826.4, "end": 829.62, "text": " The math term for this group of rotations is SO3, right?", "tokens": [50696, 440, 5221, 1433, 337, 341, 1594, 295, 44796, 307, 10621, 18, 11, 558, 30, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11740005114846978, "compression_ratio": 1.6037151702786379, "no_speech_prob": 2.0766376899322703e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 81978, "start": 829.78, "end": 830.0799999999999, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50865, 1079, 13, 50880], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11740005114846978, "compression_ratio": 1.6037151702786379, "no_speech_prob": 2.0766376899322703e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 81978, "start": 830.1999999999999, "end": 833.3199999999999, "text": " The special orthogonal group in three dimensions or SO3.", "tokens": [50886, 440, 2121, 41488, 1594, 294, 1045, 12819, 420, 10621, 18, 13, 51042], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11740005114846978, "compression_ratio": 1.6037151702786379, "no_speech_prob": 2.0766376899322703e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 81978, "start": 833.66, "end": 839.24, "text": " When a physical or abstract system possesses that SO3 symmetry, when its dynamics are fundamentally", "tokens": [51059, 1133, 257, 4001, 420, 12649, 1185, 17490, 279, 300, 10621, 18, 25440, 11, 562, 1080, 15679, 366, 17879, 51338], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11740005114846978, "compression_ratio": 1.6037151702786379, "no_speech_prob": 2.0766376899322703e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 81978, "start": 839.24, "end": 844.4399999999999, "text": " organized around a single central point, Flickshman proves that the spherical coordinate", "tokens": [51338, 9983, 926, 257, 2167, 5777, 935, 11, 3235, 618, 2716, 1601, 25019, 300, 264, 37300, 15670, 51598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11740005114846978, "compression_ratio": 1.6037151702786379, "no_speech_prob": 2.0766376899322703e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 81978, "start": 844.4399999999999, "end": 847.22, "text": " system is the unique maximal adaptation.", "tokens": [51598, 1185, 307, 264, 3845, 49336, 21549, 13, 51737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11740005114846978, "compression_ratio": 1.6037151702786379, "no_speech_prob": 2.0766376899322703e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 81978, "start": 847.56, "end": 849.4599999999999, "text": " There is literally no better way to describe it.", "tokens": [51754, 821, 307, 3736, 572, 1101, 636, 281, 6786, 309, 13, 51849], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11740005114846978, "compression_ratio": 1.6037151702786379, "no_speech_prob": 2.0766376899322703e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 84946, "start": 849.46, "end": 850.82, "text": " There is no better way.", "tokens": [50365, 821, 307, 572, 1101, 636, 13, 50433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15407401375148608, "compression_ratio": 1.8284671532846715, "no_speech_prob": 2.298058228086819e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 84946, "start": 851.02, "end": 853.38, "text": " In spherical coordinates, you have exactly three numbers.", "tokens": [50443, 682, 37300, 21056, 11, 291, 362, 2293, 1045, 3547, 13, 50561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15407401375148608, "compression_ratio": 1.8284671532846715, "no_speech_prob": 2.298058228086819e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 84946, "start": 854.1600000000001, "end": 858.94, "text": " One radial coordinate, your distance from the center, and two angular coordinates, essentially", "tokens": [50600, 1485, 38783, 15670, 11, 428, 4560, 490, 264, 3056, 11, 293, 732, 24413, 21056, 11, 4476, 50839], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15407401375148608, "compression_ratio": 1.8284671532846715, "no_speech_prob": 2.298058228086819e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 84946, "start": 858.94, "end": 860.6600000000001, "text": " your longitude and latitude.", "tokens": [50839, 428, 938, 4377, 293, 45436, 13, 50925], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15407401375148608, "compression_ratio": 1.8284671532846715, "no_speech_prob": 2.298058228086819e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 84946, "start": 861.08, "end": 861.36, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50946, 1033, 13, 50960], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15407401375148608, "compression_ratio": 1.8284671532846715, "no_speech_prob": 2.298058228086819e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 84946, "start": 861.7800000000001, "end": 866.38, "text": " Under any 3D rotation, no matter how complex the spin, the radial coordinate stays exactly", "tokens": [50981, 6974, 604, 805, 35, 12447, 11, 572, 1871, 577, 3997, 264, 6060, 11, 264, 38783, 15670, 10834, 2293, 51211], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15407401375148608, "compression_ratio": 1.8284671532846715, "no_speech_prob": 2.298058228086819e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 84946, "start": 866.38, "end": 866.88, "text": " the same.", "tokens": [51211, 264, 912, 13, 51236], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15407401375148608, "compression_ratio": 1.8284671532846715, "no_speech_prob": 2.298058228086819e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 84946, "start": 867.2, "end": 872.58, "text": " The entire mathematical complexity of the rotation is absorbed purely by those two angular coordinates.", "tokens": [51252, 440, 2302, 18894, 14024, 295, 264, 12447, 307, 20799, 17491, 538, 729, 732, 24413, 21056, 13, 51521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15407401375148608, "compression_ratio": 1.8284671532846715, "no_speech_prob": 2.298058228086819e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 84946, "start": 872.7, "end": 876.84, "text": " It concentrates the math exactly where it needs to be, leaving the radius untouched.", "tokens": [51527, 467, 5512, 12507, 264, 5221, 2293, 689, 309, 2203, 281, 312, 11, 5012, 264, 15845, 1701, 36740, 13, 51734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15407401375148608, "compression_ratio": 1.8284671532846715, "no_speech_prob": 2.298058228086819e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 87684, "start": 876.84, "end": 881.98, "text": " But Flickshman takes this way further than just the neat geometry trick for physics homework.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 3235, 618, 2716, 1601, 2516, 341, 636, 3052, 813, 445, 264, 10654, 18426, 4282, 337, 10649, 14578, 13, 50622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17042352259159088, "compression_ratio": 1.4484536082474226, "no_speech_prob": 1.8217747189269717e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 87684, "start": 882.5, "end": 887.32, "text": " They argue that whenever we use the spherical chart, we should read it through two completely", "tokens": [50648, 814, 9695, 300, 5699, 321, 764, 264, 37300, 6927, 11, 321, 820, 1401, 309, 807, 732, 2584, 50889], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17042352259159088, "compression_ratio": 1.4484536082474226, "no_speech_prob": 1.8217747189269717e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 87684, "start": 887.32, "end": 888.58, "text": " different conceptual lenses.", "tokens": [50889, 819, 24106, 18059, 13, 50952], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17042352259159088, "compression_ratio": 1.4484536082474226, "no_speech_prob": 1.8217747189269717e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 87684, "start": 889.32, "end": 891.9200000000001, "text": " And missing them up is one of the biggest mistakes you can make.", "tokens": [50989, 400, 5361, 552, 493, 307, 472, 295, 264, 3880, 8038, 291, 393, 652, 13, 51119], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17042352259159088, "compression_ratio": 1.4484536082474226, "no_speech_prob": 1.8217747189269717e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 89192, "start": 891.92, "end": 895.5, "text": " This is perhaps one of the most vital conceptual leaps in the entire text.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 4317, 472, 295, 264, 881, 11707, 24106, 476, 2382, 294, 264, 2302, 2487, 13, 50544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19319609022632087, "compression_ratio": 1.5465116279069768, "no_speech_prob": 1.9806498021551766e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 89192, "start": 895.64, "end": 897.3, "text": " It requires a total shift in perspective.", "tokens": [50551, 467, 7029, 257, 3217, 5513, 294, 4585, 13, 50634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19319609022632087, "compression_ratio": 1.5465116279069768, "no_speech_prob": 1.9806498021551766e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 89192, "start": 898.14, "end": 903.36, "text": " Usually we think of coordinates as just a list of numbers XYZ or radius angle 1, angle 2.", "tokens": [50676, 11419, 321, 519, 295, 21056, 382, 445, 257, 1329, 295, 3547, 48826, 57, 420, 15845, 5802, 502, 11, 5802, 568, 13, 50937], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19319609022632087, "compression_ratio": 1.5465116279069768, "no_speech_prob": 1.9806498021551766e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 89192, "start": 903.52, "end": 904.3, "text": " Just data points.", "tokens": [50945, 1449, 1412, 2793, 13, 50984], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19319609022632087, "compression_ratio": 1.5465116279069768, "no_speech_prob": 1.9806498021551766e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 89192, "start": 904.66, "end": 904.9799999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51002, 1779, 13, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19319609022632087, "compression_ratio": 1.5465116279069768, "no_speech_prob": 1.9806498021551766e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 89192, "start": 905.42, "end": 910.8399999999999, "text": " But Flickshman insists that the radial coordinate and the angular coordinates represent qualitatively,", "tokens": [51040, 583, 3235, 618, 2716, 1601, 50137, 300, 264, 38783, 15670, 293, 264, 24413, 21056, 2906, 31312, 356, 11, 51311], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19319609022632087, "compression_ratio": 1.5465116279069768, "no_speech_prob": 1.9806498021551766e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 89192, "start": 910.9799999999999, "end": 912.4, "text": " fundamentally different phenomena.", "tokens": [51318, 17879, 819, 22004, 13, 51389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19319609022632087, "compression_ratio": 1.5465116279069768, "no_speech_prob": 1.9806498021551766e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 89192, "start": 912.86, "end": 914.18, "text": " They are not interchangeable.", "tokens": [51412, 814, 366, 406, 30358, 712, 13, 51478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19319609022632087, "compression_ratio": 1.5465116279069768, "no_speech_prob": 1.9806498021551766e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 91418, "start": 914.18, "end": 919.8599999999999, "text": " Flickshman defines the radial coordinate, the distance from the center, as progression across", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 618, 2716, 1601, 23122, 264, 38783, 15670, 11, 264, 4560, 490, 264, 3056, 11, 382, 18733, 2108, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15185757072604433, "compression_ratio": 1.7457627118644068, "no_speech_prob": 2.1253649881702863e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 91418, "start": 919.8599999999999, "end": 920.7399999999999, "text": " levels.", "tokens": [50649, 4358, 13, 50693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15185757072604433, "compression_ratio": 1.7457627118644068, "no_speech_prob": 2.1253649881702863e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 91418, "start": 920.88, "end": 922.0999999999999, "text": " Progression across levels.", "tokens": [50700, 1705, 13338, 2108, 4358, 13, 50761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15185757072604433, "compression_ratio": 1.7457627118644068, "no_speech_prob": 2.1253649881702863e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 91418, "start": 922.2399999999999, "end": 926.8, "text": " Depending on what you are studying, this could mean physical depth, scalar magnitude", "tokens": [50768, 22539, 322, 437, 291, 366, 7601, 11, 341, 727, 914, 4001, 7161, 11, 39684, 15668, 50996], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15185757072604433, "compression_ratio": 1.7457627118644068, "no_speech_prob": 2.1253649881702863e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 91418, "start": 926.8, "end": 931.5, "text": " concentration, or even the level of irreversible commitment a system has made.", "tokens": [50996, 9856, 11, 420, 754, 264, 1496, 295, 16014, 840, 964, 8371, 257, 1185, 575, 1027, 13, 51231], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15185757072604433, "compression_ratio": 1.7457627118644068, "no_speech_prob": 2.1253649881702863e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 91418, "start": 931.8599999999999, "end": 932.0799999999999, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51249, 1033, 13, 51260], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15185757072604433, "compression_ratio": 1.7457627118644068, "no_speech_prob": 2.1253649881702863e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 91418, "start": 932.1999999999999, "end": 933.3599999999999, "text": " Progression across levels.", "tokens": [51266, 1705, 13338, 2108, 4358, 13, 51324], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15185757072604433, "compression_ratio": 1.7457627118644068, "no_speech_prob": 2.1253649881702863e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 91418, "start": 933.5799999999999, "end": 934.3, "text": " And the two angles.", "tokens": [51335, 400, 264, 732, 14708, 13, 51371], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15185757072604433, "compression_ratio": 1.7457627118644068, "no_speech_prob": 2.1253649881702863e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 91418, "start": 934.56, "end": 938.2199999999999, "text": " The two angular coordinates represent organization within a level.", "tokens": [51384, 440, 732, 24413, 21056, 2906, 4475, 1951, 257, 1496, 13, 51567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15185757072604433, "compression_ratio": 1.7457627118644068, "no_speech_prob": 2.1253649881702863e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 93822, "start": 938.22, "end": 943.98, "text": " This encompasses circulation, patterning, or reorganization that happens without changing", "tokens": [50365, 639, 49866, 23168, 11, 3829, 773, 11, 420, 41203, 2144, 300, 2314, 1553, 4473, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15605303066879955, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.769177903135355e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 93822, "start": 943.98, "end": 946.32, "text": " which fundamental level the system occupies.", "tokens": [50653, 597, 8088, 1496, 264, 1185, 8073, 530, 13, 50770], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15605303066879955, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.769177903135355e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 93822, "start": 946.4, "end": 946.58, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50774, 1779, 13, 50783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15605303066879955, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.769177903135355e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 93822, "start": 946.84, "end": 947.02, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50796, 1033, 13, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15605303066879955, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.769177903135355e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 93822, "start": 947.1, "end": 950.64, "text": " So to make sure I'm really picturing this correctly, I was reading this chapter and thinking about", "tokens": [50809, 407, 281, 652, 988, 286, 478, 534, 2317, 1345, 341, 8944, 11, 286, 390, 3760, 341, 7187, 293, 1953, 466, 50986], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15605303066879955, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.769177903135355e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 93822, "start": 950.64, "end": 953.82, "text": " it like being at a massive multi-tiered music festival.", "tokens": [50986, 309, 411, 885, 412, 257, 5994, 4825, 12, 25402, 292, 1318, 12091, 13, 51145], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15605303066879955, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.769177903135355e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 93822, "start": 953.94, "end": 954.62, "text": " I am intrigued.", "tokens": [51151, 286, 669, 35140, 13, 51185], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15605303066879955, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.769177903135355e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 93822, "start": 954.78, "end": 955.08, "text": " Go on.", "tokens": [51193, 1037, 322, 13, 51208], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15605303066879955, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.769177903135355e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 93822, "start": 955.08, "end": 960.72, "text": " So imagine you're at this gigantic outdoor festival and there are concentric rings of access", "tokens": [51208, 407, 3811, 291, 434, 412, 341, 26800, 15942, 12091, 293, 456, 366, 5512, 1341, 11136, 295, 2105, 51490], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15605303066879955, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.769177903135355e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 93822, "start": 960.72, "end": 961.94, "text": " around the main stage.", "tokens": [51490, 926, 264, 2135, 3233, 13, 51551], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15605303066879955, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.769177903135355e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 93822, "start": 962.24, "end": 967.4, "text": " You have general admission in the outer ring VIP, in the middle ring, and the all-access backstage", "tokens": [51566, 509, 362, 2674, 24668, 294, 264, 10847, 4875, 29732, 11, 294, 264, 2808, 4875, 11, 293, 264, 439, 12, 326, 780, 31764, 51824], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15605303066879955, "compression_ratio": 1.6265060240963856, "no_speech_prob": 1.769177903135355e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 96740, "start": 967.4, "end": 968.68, "text": " pass right at the center.", "tokens": [50365, 1320, 558, 412, 264, 3056, 13, 50429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1470811667562533, "compression_ratio": 1.7043795620437956, "no_speech_prob": 1.882572873632138e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 96740, "start": 968.68, "end": 975.38, "text": " If I am moving, radially changing my distance to the stage, that means I am changing my fundamental", "tokens": [50429, 759, 286, 669, 2684, 11, 2843, 2270, 4473, 452, 4560, 281, 264, 3233, 11, 300, 1355, 286, 669, 4473, 452, 8088, 50764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1470811667562533, "compression_ratio": 1.7043795620437956, "no_speech_prob": 1.882572873632138e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 96740, "start": 975.38, "end": 976.28, "text": " level of access.", "tokens": [50764, 1496, 295, 2105, 13, 50809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1470811667562533, "compression_ratio": 1.7043795620437956, "no_speech_prob": 1.882572873632138e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 96740, "start": 977.1, "end": 981.38, "text": " I am crossing security barriers, leveling up from general admission to VIP.", "tokens": [50850, 286, 669, 14712, 3825, 13565, 11, 40617, 493, 490, 2674, 24668, 281, 29732, 13, 51064], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1470811667562533, "compression_ratio": 1.7043795620437956, "no_speech_prob": 1.882572873632138e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 96740, "start": 982.02, "end": 983.48, "text": " That is progression across levels.", "tokens": [51096, 663, 307, 18733, 2108, 4358, 13, 51169], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1470811667562533, "compression_ratio": 1.7043795620437956, "no_speech_prob": 1.882572873632138e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 96740, "start": 983.6, "end": 984.3199999999999, "text": " That's the radius.", "tokens": [51175, 663, 311, 264, 15845, 13, 51211], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1470811667562533, "compression_ratio": 1.7043795620437956, "no_speech_prob": 1.882572873632138e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 96740, "start": 984.4399999999999, "end": 984.8199999999999, "text": " I follow.", "tokens": [51217, 286, 1524, 13, 51236], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1470811667562533, "compression_ratio": 1.7043795620437956, "no_speech_prob": 1.882572873632138e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 96740, "start": 984.92, "end": 988.4, "text": " But the angular coordinates, that's just me walking around the perimeter checking out the", "tokens": [51241, 583, 264, 24413, 21056, 11, 300, 311, 445, 385, 4494, 926, 264, 32404, 8568, 484, 264, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1470811667562533, "compression_ratio": 1.7043795620437956, "no_speech_prob": 1.882572873632138e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 96740, "start": 988.4, "end": 992.06, "text": " food trucks or the merch tents within my current VIP zone.", "tokens": [51415, 1755, 16156, 420, 264, 12618, 39283, 1951, 452, 2190, 29732, 6668, 13, 51598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1470811667562533, "compression_ratio": 1.7043795620437956, "no_speech_prob": 1.882572873632138e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 96740, "start": 992.72, "end": 994.46, "text": " Radially, I am leveling up or down.", "tokens": [51631, 9654, 2270, 11, 286, 669, 40617, 493, 420, 760, 13, 51718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1470811667562533, "compression_ratio": 1.7043795620437956, "no_speech_prob": 1.882572873632138e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 99446, "start": 994.46, "end": 1000.14, "text": " I'm angularly, I am just reorganizing my physical position on the exact same level of access.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 478, 24413, 356, 11, 286, 669, 445, 41203, 3319, 452, 4001, 2535, 322, 264, 1900, 912, 1496, 295, 2105, 13, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17324772527662374, "compression_ratio": 1.7231833910034602, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043334195858794e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 99446, "start": 1000.4000000000001, "end": 1004.94, "text": " That is a brilliant analogy and it captures exactly what Fliction is warning against.", "tokens": [50662, 663, 307, 257, 10248, 21663, 293, 309, 27986, 2293, 437, 3235, 4105, 307, 9164, 1970, 13, 50889], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17324772527662374, "compression_ratio": 1.7231833910034602, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043334195858794e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 99446, "start": 1005.34, "end": 1009.5600000000001, "text": " Your movement toward the stage changes your fundamental relationship to the event.", "tokens": [50909, 2260, 3963, 7361, 264, 3233, 2962, 428, 8088, 2480, 281, 264, 2280, 13, 51120], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17324772527662374, "compression_ratio": 1.7231833910034602, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043334195858794e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 99446, "start": 1009.94, "end": 1012.02, "text": " Your privileges, your proximity, your access.", "tokens": [51139, 2260, 32588, 11, 428, 27632, 11, 428, 2105, 13, 51243], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17324772527662374, "compression_ratio": 1.7231833910034602, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043334195858794e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 99446, "start": 1012.1800000000001, "end": 1013.34, "text": " It is a phase change.", "tokens": [51251, 467, 307, 257, 5574, 1319, 13, 51309], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17324772527662374, "compression_ratio": 1.7231833910034602, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043334195858794e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 99446, "start": 1013.5600000000001, "end": 1013.6600000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51320, 1779, 13, 51325], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17324772527662374, "compression_ratio": 1.7231833910034602, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043334195858794e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 99446, "start": 1013.74, "end": 1017.5, "text": " Your movement around the food trucks just changes your local context, whether you are near", "tokens": [51329, 2260, 3963, 926, 264, 1755, 16156, 445, 2962, 428, 2654, 4319, 11, 1968, 291, 366, 2651, 51517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17324772527662374, "compression_ratio": 1.7231833910034602, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043334195858794e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 99446, "start": 1017.5, "end": 1021.0, "text": " the tacos or the t-shirts, without altering your access level at all.", "tokens": [51517, 264, 34776, 420, 264, 256, 12, 25892, 11, 1553, 11337, 278, 428, 2105, 1496, 412, 439, 13, 51692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17324772527662374, "compression_ratio": 1.7231833910034602, "no_speech_prob": 1.6043334195858794e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 102100, "start": 1021.0, "end": 1026.08, "text": " Fliction argues that in scientific modeling, conflating the two, treating a fundamental change", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 4105, 38218, 300, 294, 8134, 15983, 11, 1497, 75, 990, 264, 732, 11, 15083, 257, 8088, 1319, 50619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1487628425039896, "compression_ratio": 1.4355555555555555, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232318223938225e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 102100, "start": 1026.08, "end": 1031.16, "text": " in level as if it were just a lateral reorganization, is a devastating category error.", "tokens": [50619, 294, 1496, 382, 498, 309, 645, 445, 257, 25128, 41203, 2144, 11, 307, 257, 21280, 7719, 6713, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1487628425039896, "compression_ratio": 1.4355555555555555, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232318223938225e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 102100, "start": 1031.48, "end": 1036.64, "text": " Because if I try to use a standard Cartesian XYZ grid at the music festival, I'm mixing up", "tokens": [50889, 1436, 498, 286, 853, 281, 764, 257, 3832, 22478, 42434, 48826, 57, 10748, 412, 264, 1318, 12091, 11, 286, 478, 11983, 493, 51147], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1487628425039896, "compression_ratio": 1.4355555555555555, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232318223938225e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 102100, "start": 1036.64, "end": 1039.16, "text": " my VIP upgrades with my food truck rents.", "tokens": [51147, 452, 29732, 24868, 365, 452, 1755, 5898, 6214, 82, 13, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1487628425039896, "compression_ratio": 1.4355555555555555, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232318223938225e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 102100, "start": 1039.36, "end": 1039.84, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51283, 7587, 13, 51307], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1487628425039896, "compression_ratio": 1.4355555555555555, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232318223938225e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 103984, "start": 1039.84, "end": 1045.4599999999998, "text": " Moving 10 feet forward, a radial VIP upgrade, and moving 10 feet left, an angular walk to", "tokens": [50365, 14242, 1266, 3521, 2128, 11, 257, 38783, 29732, 11484, 11, 293, 2684, 1266, 3521, 1411, 11, 364, 24413, 1792, 281, 50646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1520689634176401, "compression_ratio": 1.6284584980237153, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214442761884219e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 103984, "start": 1045.4599999999998, "end": 1049.4399999999998, "text": " a food truck, both just look like adding a plus 10 to an X or Y axis.", "tokens": [50646, 257, 1755, 5898, 11, 1293, 445, 574, 411, 5127, 257, 1804, 1266, 281, 364, 1783, 420, 398, 10298, 13, 50845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1520689634176401, "compression_ratio": 1.6284584980237153, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214442761884219e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 103984, "start": 1050.24, "end": 1055.84, "text": " The Cartesian map treats them as geometrically identical, but the spherical map separates them", "tokens": [50885, 440, 22478, 42434, 4471, 19566, 552, 382, 12956, 81, 984, 14800, 11, 457, 264, 37300, 4471, 34149, 552, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1520689634176401, "compression_ratio": 1.6284584980237153, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214442761884219e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 103984, "start": 1055.84, "end": 1056.28, "text": " perfectly.", "tokens": [51165, 6239, 13, 51187], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1520689634176401, "compression_ratio": 1.6284584980237153, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214442761884219e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 103984, "start": 1056.5, "end": 1057.02, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51198, 7587, 13, 51224], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1520689634176401, "compression_ratio": 1.6284584980237153, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214442761884219e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 103984, "start": 1057.4599999999998, "end": 1060.32, "text": " The Cartesian grid is blind to the hierarchy of the system.", "tokens": [51246, 440, 22478, 42434, 10748, 307, 6865, 281, 264, 22333, 295, 264, 1185, 13, 51389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1520689634176401, "compression_ratio": 1.6284584980237153, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214442761884219e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 103984, "start": 1060.8, "end": 1064.76, "text": " The spherical chart perfectly isolates the leveling up from the reorganizing.", "tokens": [51413, 440, 37300, 6927, 6239, 7381, 1024, 264, 40617, 493, 490, 264, 41203, 3319, 13, 51611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1520689634176401, "compression_ratio": 1.6284584980237153, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214442761884219e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 106476, "start": 1064.76, "end": 1069.34, "text": " And once you adopt this lens, you start to see why the sphere is so dominant in nature.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 1564, 291, 6878, 341, 6765, 11, 291, 722, 281, 536, 983, 264, 16687, 307, 370, 15657, 294, 3687, 13, 50594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12331619836333998, "compression_ratio": 1.6614420062695925, "no_speech_prob": 1.5312412796064656e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 106476, "start": 1070.04, "end": 1071.4, "text": " Which sets us up for something fascinating.", "tokens": [50629, 3013, 6352, 505, 493, 337, 746, 10343, 13, 50697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12331619836333998, "compression_ratio": 1.6614420062695925, "no_speech_prob": 1.5312412796064656e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 106476, "start": 1072.06, "end": 1076.16, "text": " Because if you stop moving radially, if you stay at exactly one VIP level, say 100 feet", "tokens": [50730, 1436, 498, 291, 1590, 2684, 2843, 2270, 11, 498, 291, 1754, 412, 2293, 472, 29732, 1496, 11, 584, 2319, 3521, 50935], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12331619836333998, "compression_ratio": 1.6614420062695925, "no_speech_prob": 1.5312412796064656e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 106476, "start": 1076.16, "end": 1081.62, "text": " from the stage, and just walk the perimeter infinitely, you trace out a shell, a 2D sphere", "tokens": [50935, 490, 264, 3233, 11, 293, 445, 1792, 264, 32404, 36227, 11, 291, 13508, 484, 257, 8720, 11, 257, 568, 35, 16687, 51208], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12331619836333998, "compression_ratio": 1.6614420062695925, "no_speech_prob": 1.5312412796064656e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 106476, "start": 1081.62, "end": 1082.44, "text": " of fixed radius.", "tokens": [51208, 295, 6806, 15845, 13, 51249], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12331619836333998, "compression_ratio": 1.6614420062695925, "no_speech_prob": 1.5312412796064656e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 106476, "start": 1082.62, "end": 1082.96, "text": " Correct.", "tokens": [51258, 12753, 13, 51275], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12331619836333998, "compression_ratio": 1.6614420062695925, "no_speech_prob": 1.5312412796064656e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 106476, "start": 1083.16, "end": 1084.74, "text": " And a shell naturally treats a boundary.", "tokens": [51285, 400, 257, 8720, 8195, 19566, 257, 12866, 13, 51364], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12331619836333998, "compression_ratio": 1.6614420062695925, "no_speech_prob": 1.5312412796064656e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 106476, "start": 1085.16, "end": 1088.26, "text": " It separates the VIPs on the inside from the general admission on the outside.", "tokens": [51385, 467, 34149, 264, 29732, 82, 322, 264, 1854, 490, 264, 2674, 24668, 322, 264, 2380, 13, 51540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12331619836333998, "compression_ratio": 1.6614420062695925, "no_speech_prob": 1.5312412796064656e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 106476, "start": 1088.84, "end": 1092.04, "text": " But Fliction claims that boundaries in nature aren't just physical walls.", "tokens": [51569, 583, 3235, 4105, 9441, 300, 13180, 294, 3687, 3212, 380, 445, 4001, 7920, 13, 51729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12331619836333998, "compression_ratio": 1.6614420062695925, "no_speech_prob": 1.5312412796064656e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 109204, "start": 1092.04, "end": 1094.6399999999999, "text": " They actually perform computational work.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 767, 2042, 28270, 589, 13, 50495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1402643338768883, "compression_ratio": 1.6067796610169491, "no_speech_prob": 1.8613257636579394e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 109204, "start": 1095.1, "end": 1095.3, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50518, 1079, 13, 50528], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1402643338768883, "compression_ratio": 1.6067796610169491, "no_speech_prob": 1.8613257636579394e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 109204, "start": 1095.74, "end": 1099.1, "text": " We are shifting now into how these geometries dictate behavior.", "tokens": [50550, 492, 366, 17573, 586, 666, 577, 613, 12956, 2244, 36071, 5223, 13, 50718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1402643338768883, "compression_ratio": 1.6067796610169491, "no_speech_prob": 1.8613257636579394e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 109204, "start": 1099.72, "end": 1100.6399999999999, "text": " You are absolutely right.", "tokens": [50749, 509, 366, 3122, 558, 13, 50795], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1402643338768883, "compression_ratio": 1.6067796610169491, "no_speech_prob": 1.8613257636579394e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 109204, "start": 1100.72, "end": 1104.6, "text": " A fixed radius shell inherently separates an interior from an exterior.", "tokens": [50799, 316, 6806, 15845, 8720, 27993, 34149, 364, 10636, 490, 364, 20677, 13, 50993], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1402643338768883, "compression_ratio": 1.6067796610169491, "no_speech_prob": 1.8613257636579394e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 109204, "start": 1105.28, "end": 1111.1399999999999, "text": " But Fliction draws on literature from way outside pure geometry, biology, statistics, computer", "tokens": [51027, 583, 3235, 4105, 20045, 322, 10394, 490, 636, 2380, 6075, 18426, 11, 14956, 11, 12523, 11, 3820, 51320], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1402643338768883, "compression_ratio": 1.6067796610169491, "no_speech_prob": 1.8613257636579394e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 109204, "start": 1111.1399999999999, "end": 1116.74, "text": " science, to show that a boundary can mediate that separation in three structurally incompatible", "tokens": [51320, 3497, 11, 281, 855, 300, 257, 12866, 393, 1205, 13024, 300, 14634, 294, 1045, 6594, 6512, 40393, 267, 964, 51600], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1402643338768883, "compression_ratio": 1.6067796610169491, "no_speech_prob": 1.8613257636579394e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 109204, "start": 1116.74, "end": 1117.1599999999999, "text": " ways.", "tokens": [51600, 2098, 13, 51621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1402643338768883, "compression_ratio": 1.6067796610169491, "no_speech_prob": 1.8613257636579394e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 109204, "start": 1117.3999999999999, "end": 1118.54, "text": " Not all walls are the same.", "tokens": [51633, 1726, 439, 7920, 366, 264, 912, 13, 51690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1402643338768883, "compression_ratio": 1.6067796610169491, "no_speech_prob": 1.8613257636579394e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 109204, "start": 1119.0, "end": 1120.5, "text": " Let's break down these three typologies.", "tokens": [51713, 961, 311, 1821, 760, 613, 1045, 2125, 6204, 13, 51788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1402643338768883, "compression_ratio": 1.6067796610169491, "no_speech_prob": 1.8613257636579394e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 112050, "start": 1120.5, "end": 1123.54, "text": " The first one, Fliction calls the synchronic screen.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 700, 472, 11, 3235, 4105, 5498, 264, 5451, 339, 10011, 2568, 13, 50517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17351015346256768, "compression_ratio": 1.7481481481481482, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236441444800187e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 112050, "start": 1124.08, "end": 1126.86, "text": " And they specifically mention it's a Fristen-style boundary.", "tokens": [50544, 400, 436, 4682, 2152, 309, 311, 257, 1526, 4821, 12, 15014, 12866, 13, 50683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17351015346256768, "compression_ratio": 1.7481481481481482, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236441444800187e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 112050, "start": 1127.34, "end": 1127.92, "text": " What does that mean?", "tokens": [50707, 708, 775, 300, 914, 30, 50736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17351015346256768, "compression_ratio": 1.7481481481481482, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236441444800187e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 112050, "start": 1128.18, "end": 1133.08, "text": " This is a direct reference to the theoretical neuroscientist Karl Frister and his concept", "tokens": [50749, 639, 307, 257, 2047, 6408, 281, 264, 20864, 28813, 5412, 468, 20405, 1526, 1964, 293, 702, 3410, 50994], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17351015346256768, "compression_ratio": 1.7481481481481482, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236441444800187e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 112050, "start": 1133.08, "end": 1134.14, "text": " of a Markov blanket.", "tokens": [50994, 295, 257, 3934, 5179, 17907, 13, 51047], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17351015346256768, "compression_ratio": 1.7481481481481482, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236441444800187e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 112050, "start": 1134.32, "end": 1134.48, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51056, 1033, 13, 51064], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17351015346256768, "compression_ratio": 1.7481481481481482, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236441444800187e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 112050, "start": 1134.96, "end": 1137.6, "text": " Now, a Markov blanket is a statistical boundary.", "tokens": [51088, 823, 11, 257, 3934, 5179, 17907, 307, 257, 22820, 12866, 13, 51220], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17351015346256768, "compression_ratio": 1.7481481481481482, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236441444800187e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 112050, "start": 1138.26, "end": 1142.68, "text": " A synchronic screen is a boundary defined entirely in the present tense synchronic meaning", "tokens": [51253, 316, 5451, 339, 10011, 2568, 307, 257, 12866, 7642, 7696, 294, 264, 1974, 18760, 5451, 339, 10011, 3620, 51474], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17351015346256768, "compression_ratio": 1.7481481481481482, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236441444800187e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 112050, "start": 1142.68, "end": 1143.92, "text": " occurring at the same time.", "tokens": [51474, 18386, 412, 264, 912, 565, 13, 51536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17351015346256768, "compression_ratio": 1.7481481481481482, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236441444800187e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 112050, "start": 1144.18, "end": 1146.0, "text": " It acts as a statistical shield.", "tokens": [51549, 467, 10672, 382, 257, 22820, 10257, 13, 51640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17351015346256768, "compression_ratio": 1.7481481481481482, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236441444800187e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 112050, "start": 1146.24, "end": 1146.98, "text": " How does it shield?", "tokens": [51652, 1012, 775, 309, 10257, 30, 51689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17351015346256768, "compression_ratio": 1.7481481481481482, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236441444800187e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 114698, "start": 1146.98, "end": 1151.72, "text": " Imagine a complex system like a cell or even a brain where the internal states, the parts", "tokens": [50365, 11739, 257, 3997, 1185, 411, 257, 2815, 420, 754, 257, 3567, 689, 264, 6920, 4368, 11, 264, 3166, 50602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13959131033524222, "compression_ratio": 1.683982683982684, "no_speech_prob": 1.9047619384537917e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 114698, "start": 1151.72, "end": 1154.92, "text": " on the inside, cannot physically see the external states on the outside directly.", "tokens": [50602, 322, 264, 1854, 11, 2644, 9762, 536, 264, 8320, 4368, 322, 264, 2380, 3838, 13, 50762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13959131033524222, "compression_ratio": 1.683982683982684, "no_speech_prob": 1.9047619384537917e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 114698, "start": 1155.24, "end": 1157.3, "text": " They can only perceive the blanket itself.", "tokens": [50778, 814, 393, 787, 20281, 264, 17907, 2564, 13, 50881], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13959131033524222, "compression_ratio": 1.683982683982684, "no_speech_prob": 1.9047619384537917e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 114698, "start": 1157.84, "end": 1161.72, "text": " The boundary mediate perception and action based only on the current immediate moment.", "tokens": [50908, 440, 12866, 1205, 13024, 12860, 293, 3069, 2361, 787, 322, 264, 2190, 11629, 1623, 13, 51102], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13959131033524222, "compression_ratio": 1.683982683982684, "no_speech_prob": 1.9047619384537917e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 114698, "start": 1161.98, "end": 1166.6, "text": " So to build on the sensory deprivation idea, it's like a submarine's sonar screen.", "tokens": [51115, 407, 281, 1322, 322, 264, 27233, 27095, 11116, 1558, 11, 309, 311, 411, 257, 33995, 311, 1872, 289, 2568, 13, 51346], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13959131033524222, "compression_ratio": 1.683982683982684, "no_speech_prob": 1.9047619384537917e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 114698, "start": 1166.76, "end": 1167.1200000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51354, 1079, 13, 51372], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13959131033524222, "compression_ratio": 1.683982683982684, "no_speech_prob": 1.9047619384537917e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 116712, "start": 1167.12, "end": 1171.9399999999998, "text": " The crew inside the sump, the internal states, cannot look out a window and physically see", "tokens": [50365, 440, 7260, 1854, 264, 262, 1420, 11, 264, 6920, 4368, 11, 2644, 574, 484, 257, 4910, 293, 9762, 536, 50606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19640676659273815, "compression_ratio": 1.608695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.7315707244794365e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 116712, "start": 1171.9399999999998, "end": 1173.34, "text": " the ocean or the enemy ships.", "tokens": [50606, 264, 7810, 420, 264, 5945, 11434, 13, 50676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19640676659273815, "compression_ratio": 1.608695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.7315707244794365e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 116712, "start": 1173.5, "end": 1173.7199999999998, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50684, 865, 13, 50695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19640676659273815, "compression_ratio": 1.608695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.7315707244794365e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 116712, "start": 1174.0, "end": 1178.52, "text": " They can only look at the glowing sonar screen, the boundary in the present moment.", "tokens": [50709, 814, 393, 787, 574, 412, 264, 27064, 1872, 289, 2568, 11, 264, 12866, 294, 264, 1974, 1623, 13, 50935], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19640676659273815, "compression_ratio": 1.608695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.7315707244794365e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 116712, "start": 1179.06, "end": 1182.9199999999998, "text": " They make life or death decisions based on what that screen is showing them right now.", "tokens": [50962, 814, 652, 993, 420, 2966, 5327, 2361, 322, 437, 300, 2568, 307, 4099, 552, 558, 586, 13, 51155], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19640676659273815, "compression_ratio": 1.608695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.7315707244794365e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 116712, "start": 1183.28, "end": 1185.06, "text": " That is an excellent visualization.", "tokens": [51173, 663, 307, 364, 7103, 25801, 13, 51262], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19640676659273815, "compression_ratio": 1.608695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.7315707244794365e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 118506, "start": 1185.06, "end": 1191.24, "text": " The synchronic screen evaluates the present joint state of the system, the pressure outside,", "tokens": [50365, 440, 5451, 339, 10011, 2568, 6133, 1024, 264, 1974, 7225, 1785, 295, 264, 1185, 11, 264, 3321, 2380, 11, 50674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1212513274040775, "compression_ratio": 1.7081967213114755, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370915261089801e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 118506, "start": 1191.46, "end": 1196.02, "text": " the pings on the sonar, and mediates the flow of information inward and outward.", "tokens": [50685, 264, 280, 1109, 322, 264, 1872, 289, 11, 293, 17269, 1024, 264, 3095, 295, 1589, 29876, 293, 26914, 13, 50913], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1212513274040775, "compression_ratio": 1.7081967213114755, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370915261089801e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 118506, "start": 1196.46, "end": 1199.4199999999998, "text": " But crucially, the screen itself does not remember the past.", "tokens": [50935, 583, 5140, 1909, 11, 264, 2568, 2564, 775, 406, 1604, 264, 1791, 13, 51083], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1212513274040775, "compression_ratio": 1.7081967213114755, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370915261089801e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 118506, "start": 1199.74, "end": 1201.3799999999999, "text": " Doesn't know where the sub was yesterday.", "tokens": [51099, 12955, 380, 458, 689, 264, 1422, 390, 5186, 13, 51181], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1212513274040775, "compression_ratio": 1.7081967213114755, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370915261089801e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 118506, "start": 1201.6399999999999, "end": 1201.9199999999998, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51194, 1779, 13, 51208], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1212513274040775, "compression_ratio": 1.7081967213114755, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370915261089801e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 118506, "start": 1202.02, "end": 1204.84, "text": " And it does not have a predetermined rigid goal for the future.", "tokens": [51213, 400, 309, 775, 406, 362, 257, 3852, 35344, 2001, 22195, 3387, 337, 264, 2027, 13, 51354], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1212513274040775, "compression_ratio": 1.7081967213114755, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370915261089801e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 118506, "start": 1205.12, "end": 1206.8999999999999, "text": " It is a purely reactive surface.", "tokens": [51368, 467, 307, 257, 17491, 28897, 3753, 13, 51457], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1212513274040775, "compression_ratio": 1.7081967213114755, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370915261089801e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 118506, "start": 1207.32, "end": 1210.36, "text": " It just manages the now to keep the internal state stable.", "tokens": [51478, 467, 445, 22489, 264, 586, 281, 1066, 264, 6920, 1785, 8351, 13, 51630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1212513274040775, "compression_ratio": 1.7081967213114755, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370915261089801e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 118506, "start": 1210.5, "end": 1210.6399999999999, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51637, 1033, 13, 51644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1212513274040775, "compression_ratio": 1.7081967213114755, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370915261089801e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 118506, "start": 1210.6599999999999, "end": 1211.06, "text": " That makes sense.", "tokens": [51645, 663, 1669, 2020, 13, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1212513274040775, "compression_ratio": 1.7081967213114755, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370915261089801e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 118506, "start": 1211.12, "end": 1213.7, "text": " That's boundary number one, present tense, pure reaction.", "tokens": [51668, 663, 311, 12866, 1230, 472, 11, 1974, 18760, 11, 6075, 5480, 13, 51797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1212513274040775, "compression_ratio": 1.7081967213114755, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370915261089801e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 121370, "start": 1213.7, "end": 1218.0800000000002, "text": " But then fliction introduces the second type, the stored target boundary.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 550, 932, 4105, 31472, 264, 1150, 2010, 11, 264, 12187, 3779, 12866, 13, 50584], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14454381282512957, "compression_ratio": 1.6828358208955223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362199138988953e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 121370, "start": 1218.8, "end": 1224.04, "text": " And this is where they bring in Michael Levin's flatworm experiments, which honestly blew my", "tokens": [50620, 400, 341, 307, 689, 436, 1565, 294, 5116, 1456, 4796, 311, 4962, 30917, 12050, 11, 597, 6095, 19075, 452, 50882], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14454381282512957, "compression_ratio": 1.6828358208955223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362199138988953e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 121370, "start": 1224.04, "end": 1225.48, "text": " mind when I was reading the source material.", "tokens": [50882, 1575, 562, 286, 390, 3760, 264, 4009, 2527, 13, 50954], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14454381282512957, "compression_ratio": 1.6828358208955223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362199138988953e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 121370, "start": 1225.82, "end": 1227.5800000000002, "text": " Levin's work is paradigm shifting.", "tokens": [50971, 1456, 4796, 311, 589, 307, 24709, 17573, 13, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14454381282512957, "compression_ratio": 1.6828358208955223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362199138988953e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 121370, "start": 1228.3400000000001, "end": 1234.2, "text": " If the Friston screen is the present tense, this boundary operates entirely in the future tense.", "tokens": [51097, 759, 264, 1526, 47345, 2568, 307, 264, 1974, 18760, 11, 341, 12866, 22577, 7696, 294, 264, 2027, 18760, 13, 51390], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14454381282512957, "compression_ratio": 1.6828358208955223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362199138988953e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 121370, "start": 1234.32, "end": 1235.02, "text": " The future tense.", "tokens": [51396, 440, 2027, 18760, 13, 51431], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14454381282512957, "compression_ratio": 1.6828358208955223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362199138988953e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 121370, "start": 1235.16, "end": 1239.8400000000001, "text": " Michael Levin's research on developmental bioelectricity proves that boundaries in living", "tokens": [51438, 5116, 1456, 4796, 311, 2132, 322, 30160, 12198, 33243, 507, 25019, 300, 13180, 294, 2647, 51672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14454381282512957, "compression_ratio": 1.6828358208955223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362199138988953e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 123984, "start": 1239.84, "end": 1243.76, "text": " tissues aren't just passive walls where cellular growth happened to stop.", "tokens": [50365, 27353, 3212, 380, 445, 14975, 7920, 689, 29267, 4599, 2011, 281, 1590, 13, 50561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2229829482090326, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.68132044744973e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 123984, "start": 1244.1999999999998, "end": 1246.4199999999998, "text": " They are active computational layers.", "tokens": [50583, 814, 366, 4967, 28270, 7914, 13, 50694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2229829482090326, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.68132044744973e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 123984, "start": 1247.22, "end": 1251.36, "text": " They are the visible trace of a shape being actively pursued by the system.", "tokens": [50734, 814, 366, 264, 8974, 13508, 295, 257, 3909, 885, 13022, 34893, 538, 264, 1185, 13, 50941], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2229829482090326, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.68132044744973e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 123984, "start": 1251.9399999999998, "end": 1256.8799999999999, "text": " The bioelectric gradient across the cells acts as a stored target morphology.", "tokens": [50970, 440, 12198, 33243, 16235, 2108, 264, 5438, 10672, 382, 257, 12187, 3779, 25778, 1793, 13, 51217], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2229829482090326, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.68132044744973e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 123984, "start": 1257.1, "end": 1258.86, "text": " Well, you've got to unpack that term for me.", "tokens": [51228, 1042, 11, 291, 600, 658, 281, 26699, 300, 1433, 337, 385, 13, 51316], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2229829482090326, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.68132044744973e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 123984, "start": 1259.1599999999999, "end": 1260.6399999999999, "text": " Stored target morphology.", "tokens": [51331, 745, 2769, 3779, 25778, 1793, 13, 51405], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2229829482090326, "compression_ratio": 1.6153846153846154, "no_speech_prob": 1.68132044744973e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 126064, "start": 1260.64, "end": 1262.7, "text": " It sounds like something a terminator would say.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 3263, 411, 746, 257, 10761, 1639, 576, 584, 13, 50468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1405082897548258, "compression_ratio": 1.697452229299363, "no_speech_prob": 1.3196981485039116e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 126064, "start": 1263.18, "end": 1265.0200000000002, "text": " Morphology just means shape or structure.", "tokens": [50492, 5146, 950, 1793, 445, 1355, 3909, 420, 3877, 13, 50584], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1405082897548258, "compression_ratio": 1.697452229299363, "no_speech_prob": 1.3196981485039116e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 126064, "start": 1265.4, "end": 1269.5800000000002, "text": " So a stored target morphology means that the electrical boundary conditions of the tissue", "tokens": [50603, 407, 257, 12187, 3779, 25778, 1793, 1355, 300, 264, 12147, 12866, 4487, 295, 264, 12404, 50812], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1405082897548258, "compression_ratio": 1.697452229299363, "no_speech_prob": 1.3196981485039116e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 126064, "start": 1269.5800000000002, "end": 1273.8000000000002, "text": " literally contain the blueprint, the target for what the tissue is trying to become in", "tokens": [50812, 3736, 5304, 264, 35868, 11, 264, 3779, 337, 437, 264, 12404, 307, 1382, 281, 1813, 294, 51023], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1405082897548258, "compression_ratio": 1.697452229299363, "no_speech_prob": 1.3196981485039116e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 126064, "start": 1273.8000000000002, "end": 1274.18, "text": " the future.", "tokens": [51023, 264, 2027, 13, 51042], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1405082897548258, "compression_ratio": 1.697452229299363, "no_speech_prob": 1.3196981485039116e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 126064, "start": 1274.42, "end": 1277.76, "text": " And the experiment they cite in the text to prove this, it's wild.", "tokens": [51054, 400, 264, 5120, 436, 37771, 294, 264, 2487, 281, 7081, 341, 11, 309, 311, 4868, 13, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1405082897548258, "compression_ratio": 1.697452229299363, "no_speech_prob": 1.3196981485039116e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 126064, "start": 1278.1200000000001, "end": 1280.48, "text": " So Levin's team takes a planarian flatworm.", "tokens": [51239, 407, 1456, 4796, 311, 1469, 2516, 257, 1393, 10652, 4962, 30917, 13, 51357], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1405082897548258, "compression_ratio": 1.697452229299363, "no_speech_prob": 1.3196981485039116e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 126064, "start": 1280.88, "end": 1285.66, "text": " These worms are famous because if you cut them in half, the head grows a new tail and the", "tokens": [51377, 1981, 28271, 366, 4618, 570, 498, 291, 1723, 552, 294, 1922, 11, 264, 1378, 13156, 257, 777, 6838, 293, 264, 51616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1405082897548258, "compression_ratio": 1.697452229299363, "no_speech_prob": 1.3196981485039116e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 126064, "start": 1285.66, "end": 1286.5, "text": " tail grows a new head.", "tokens": [51616, 6838, 13156, 257, 777, 1378, 13, 51658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1405082897548258, "compression_ratio": 1.697452229299363, "no_speech_prob": 1.3196981485039116e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 126064, "start": 1286.5400000000002, "end": 1286.8000000000002, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51660, 1079, 13, 51673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1405082897548258, "compression_ratio": 1.697452229299363, "no_speech_prob": 1.3196981485039116e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 126064, "start": 1286.92, "end": 1287.64, "text": " Incredible regenerators.", "tokens": [51679, 35261, 26358, 3391, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1405082897548258, "compression_ratio": 1.697452229299363, "no_speech_prob": 1.3196981485039116e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 128764, "start": 1287.64, "end": 1293.74, "text": " But in this experiment, before the worm heals, they alter the voltage, just the electrical", "tokens": [50365, 583, 294, 341, 5120, 11, 949, 264, 23835, 45653, 11, 436, 11337, 264, 8352, 11, 445, 264, 12147, 50670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14733358015093886, "compression_ratio": 1.7207547169811321, "no_speech_prob": 2.245149378909961e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 128764, "start": 1293.74, "end": 1295.14, "text": " gradient at the wound site.", "tokens": [50670, 16235, 412, 264, 10999, 3621, 13, 50740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14733358015093886, "compression_ratio": 1.7207547169811321, "no_speech_prob": 2.245149378909961e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 128764, "start": 1295.46, "end": 1297.26, "text": " They don't touch the flatworm's DNA.", "tokens": [50756, 814, 500, 380, 2557, 264, 4962, 30917, 311, 8272, 13, 50846], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14733358015093886, "compression_ratio": 1.7207547169811321, "no_speech_prob": 2.245149378909961e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 128764, "start": 1297.6000000000001, "end": 1299.94, "text": " They don't add new stem cells or chemicals.", "tokens": [50863, 814, 500, 380, 909, 777, 12312, 5438, 420, 16152, 13, 50980], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14733358015093886, "compression_ratio": 1.7207547169811321, "no_speech_prob": 2.245149378909961e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 128764, "start": 1300.16, "end": 1303.0600000000002, "text": " They just manipulate the electrical boundary condition.", "tokens": [50991, 814, 445, 20459, 264, 12147, 12866, 4188, 13, 51136], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14733358015093886, "compression_ratio": 1.7207547169811321, "no_speech_prob": 2.245149378909961e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 128764, "start": 1303.6000000000001, "end": 1308.88, "text": " And the cells at the wound, using completely normal unaltered DNA, grow a second head instead", "tokens": [51163, 400, 264, 5438, 412, 264, 10999, 11, 1228, 2584, 2710, 517, 304, 40665, 8272, 11, 1852, 257, 1150, 1378, 2602, 51427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14733358015093886, "compression_ratio": 1.7207547169811321, "no_speech_prob": 2.245149378909961e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 128764, "start": 1308.88, "end": 1309.4, "text": " of a tail.", "tokens": [51427, 295, 257, 6838, 13, 51453], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14733358015093886, "compression_ratio": 1.7207547169811321, "no_speech_prob": 2.245149378909961e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 128764, "start": 1309.72, "end": 1313.0600000000002, "text": " It is a profound demonstration of how boundaries compute.", "tokens": [51469, 467, 307, 257, 14382, 16520, 295, 577, 13180, 14722, 13, 51636], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14733358015093886, "compression_ratio": 1.7207547169811321, "no_speech_prob": 2.245149378909961e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 128764, "start": 1313.7, "end": 1315.3400000000001, "text": " Think of it like a construction site.", "tokens": [51668, 6557, 295, 309, 411, 257, 6435, 3621, 13, 51750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14733358015093886, "compression_ratio": 1.7207547169811321, "no_speech_prob": 2.245149378909961e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 131534, "start": 1315.34, "end": 1320.12, "text": " The genome supplies the hardware, the bricks, the physical cells available to the tissue,", "tokens": [50365, 440, 21953, 11768, 264, 8837, 11, 264, 25497, 11, 264, 4001, 5438, 2435, 281, 264, 12404, 11, 50604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12674294395008306, "compression_ratio": 1.617117117117117, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213682314467846e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 131534, "start": 1320.26, "end": 1321.5, "text": " the basic local rules.", "tokens": [50611, 264, 3875, 2654, 4474, 13, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12674294395008306, "compression_ratio": 1.617117117117117, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213682314467846e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 131534, "start": 1322.1599999999999, "end": 1327.86, "text": " But the bioelectric boundary supplies the software target, the architect's blueprint that those", "tokens": [50706, 583, 264, 12198, 33243, 12866, 11768, 264, 4722, 3779, 11, 264, 6331, 311, 35868, 300, 729, 50991], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12674294395008306, "compression_ratio": 1.617117117117117, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213682314467846e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 131534, "start": 1327.86, "end": 1329.0, "text": " cells are assembling toward.", "tokens": [50991, 5438, 366, 43867, 7361, 13, 51048], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12674294395008306, "compression_ratio": 1.617117117117117, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213682314467846e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 131534, "start": 1329.34, "end": 1334.04, "text": " The boundary in Levin's flatworms is not just evaluating the present moment like our submarine", "tokens": [51065, 440, 12866, 294, 1456, 4796, 311, 4962, 30917, 82, 307, 406, 445, 27479, 264, 1974, 1623, 411, 527, 33995, 51300], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12674294395008306, "compression_ratio": 1.617117117117117, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213682314467846e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 131534, "start": 1334.04, "end": 1334.5, "text": " sonar.", "tokens": [51300, 1872, 289, 13, 51323], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12674294395008306, "compression_ratio": 1.617117117117117, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213682314467846e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 131534, "start": 1334.62, "end": 1335.56, "text": " It is an attractor.", "tokens": [51329, 467, 307, 364, 5049, 284, 13, 51376], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12674294395008306, "compression_ratio": 1.617117117117117, "no_speech_prob": 1.4213682314467846e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 133556, "start": 1335.56, "end": 1340.08, "text": " It is actively pulling the biological system toward a specific future state.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 13022, 8407, 264, 13910, 1185, 7361, 257, 2685, 2027, 1785, 13, 50591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874945357039168, "compression_ratio": 1.6653696498054475, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396532127512577e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 133556, "start": 1340.48, "end": 1342.32, "text": " So the boundary dictates the future.", "tokens": [50611, 407, 264, 12866, 12569, 1024, 264, 2027, 13, 50703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874945357039168, "compression_ratio": 1.6653696498054475, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396532127512577e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 133556, "start": 1342.4199999999998, "end": 1343.56, "text": " That's our future tense boundary.", "tokens": [50708, 663, 311, 527, 2027, 18760, 12866, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874945357039168, "compression_ratio": 1.6653696498054475, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396532127512577e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 133556, "start": 1343.6599999999999, "end": 1344.36, "text": " What about the third one?", "tokens": [50770, 708, 466, 264, 2636, 472, 30, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874945357039168, "compression_ratio": 1.6653696498054475, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396532127512577e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 133556, "start": 1344.72, "end": 1349.1599999999999, "text": " Flickhumman calls it the diachronic exclusion, diachronic meaning across time.", "tokens": [50823, 3235, 618, 71, 449, 1601, 5498, 309, 264, 1026, 608, 10011, 33049, 11, 1026, 608, 10011, 3620, 2108, 565, 13, 51045], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874945357039168, "compression_ratio": 1.6653696498054475, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396532127512577e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 133556, "start": 1349.56, "end": 1352.46, "text": " And they reference something called an RSVP style boundary.", "tokens": [51065, 400, 436, 6408, 746, 1219, 364, 25855, 53, 47, 3758, 12866, 13, 51210], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874945357039168, "compression_ratio": 1.6653696498054475, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396532127512577e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 133556, "start": 1352.7, "end": 1352.98, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51222, 1079, 13, 51236], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874945357039168, "compression_ratio": 1.6653696498054475, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396532127512577e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 133556, "start": 1353.48, "end": 1358.48, "text": " If the first is the present and the second is the future, this third boundary is strictly", "tokens": [51261, 759, 264, 700, 307, 264, 1974, 293, 264, 1150, 307, 264, 2027, 11, 341, 2636, 12866, 307, 20792, 51511], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874945357039168, "compression_ratio": 1.6653696498054475, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396532127512577e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 133556, "start": 1358.48, "end": 1359.6799999999998, "text": " defined by the past.", "tokens": [51511, 7642, 538, 264, 1791, 13, 51571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1874945357039168, "compression_ratio": 1.6653696498054475, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396532127512577e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 135968, "start": 1359.68, "end": 1366.1200000000001, "text": " A diachronic exclusion is an accumulated historical record of what has been permanently, irreversibly", "tokens": [50365, 316, 1026, 608, 10011, 33049, 307, 364, 31346, 8584, 2136, 295, 437, 575, 668, 24042, 11, 16014, 840, 3545, 50687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15438960847400485, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.636375930591516e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 135968, "start": 1366.1200000000001, "end": 1366.68, "text": " ruled out.", "tokens": [50687, 20077, 484, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15438960847400485, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.636375930591516e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 135968, "start": 1367.16, "end": 1370.68, "text": " It is a boundary constructed entirely out of rejected options.", "tokens": [50739, 467, 307, 257, 12866, 17083, 7696, 484, 295, 15749, 3956, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15438960847400485, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.636375930591516e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 135968, "start": 1370.8600000000001, "end": 1373.3600000000001, "text": " So it's not just a physical wall that says you can't go here.", "tokens": [50924, 407, 309, 311, 406, 445, 257, 4001, 2929, 300, 1619, 291, 393, 380, 352, 510, 13, 51049], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15438960847400485, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.636375930591516e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 135968, "start": 1373.54, "end": 1377.88, "text": " It's a conceptual wall built out of the fact that you already chose not to go there, and", "tokens": [51058, 467, 311, 257, 24106, 2929, 3094, 484, 295, 264, 1186, 300, 291, 1217, 5111, 406, 281, 352, 456, 11, 293, 51275], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15438960847400485, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.636375930591516e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 135968, "start": 1377.88, "end": 1380.02, "text": " now that door is locked and bricked over forever.", "tokens": [51275, 586, 300, 2853, 307, 9376, 293, 738, 12598, 670, 5680, 13, 51382], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15438960847400485, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.636375930591516e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 135968, "start": 1380.3400000000001, "end": 1380.8, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51398, 48746, 736, 13, 51421], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15438960847400485, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.636375930591516e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 135968, "start": 1381.26, "end": 1387.0, "text": " Now regarding RSVP, the text uses RSVP as a framework for modeling these irreversible", "tokens": [51444, 823, 8595, 25855, 53, 47, 11, 264, 2487, 4960, 25855, 53, 47, 382, 257, 8388, 337, 15983, 613, 16014, 840, 964, 51731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15438960847400485, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.636375930591516e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 135968, "start": 1387.0, "end": 1387.42, "text": " commitments.", "tokens": [51731, 26230, 13, 51752], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15438960847400485, "compression_ratio": 1.62, "no_speech_prob": 1.636375930591516e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 138742, "start": 1387.42, "end": 1392.16, "text": " Flickshen defines RSVP as regulated state veto protocols.", "tokens": [50365, 3235, 618, 2716, 268, 23122, 25855, 53, 47, 382, 26243, 1785, 42910, 20618, 13, 50602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18018633718708998, "compression_ratio": 1.5689655172413792, "no_speech_prob": 1.3619189326644077e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 138742, "start": 1392.42, "end": 1392.9, "text": " Wait, really?", "tokens": [50615, 3802, 11, 534, 30, 50639], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18018633718708998, "compression_ratio": 1.5689655172413792, "no_speech_prob": 1.3619189326644077e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 138742, "start": 1393.16, "end": 1397.02, "text": " Because later in the text when they're talking about the fields, they list scalar-Lanfron", "tokens": [50652, 1436, 1780, 294, 264, 2487, 562, 436, 434, 1417, 466, 264, 7909, 11, 436, 1329, 39684, 12, 43, 282, 69, 2044, 50845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18018633718708998, "compression_ratio": 1.5689655172413792, "no_speech_prob": 1.3619189326644077e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 138742, "start": 1397.02, "end": 1399.1000000000001, "text": " entropy and vector S-L-E-V.", "tokens": [50845, 30867, 293, 8062, 318, 12, 43, 12, 36, 12, 53, 13, 50949], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18018633718708998, "compression_ratio": 1.5689655172413792, "no_speech_prob": 1.3619189326644077e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 138742, "start": 1399.3200000000002, "end": 1402.6200000000001, "text": " I was staring at the book thinking, Flickshen, buddy, that doesn't spell RSVP.", "tokens": [50960, 286, 390, 18043, 412, 264, 1446, 1953, 11, 3235, 618, 2716, 268, 11, 10340, 11, 300, 1177, 380, 9827, 25855, 53, 47, 13, 51125], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18018633718708998, "compression_ratio": 1.5689655172413792, "no_speech_prob": 1.3619189326644077e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 138742, "start": 1402.76, "end": 1403.98, "text": " A very sharp observation.", "tokens": [51132, 316, 588, 8199, 14816, 13, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18018633718708998, "compression_ratio": 1.5689655172413792, "no_speech_prob": 1.3619189326644077e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 138742, "start": 1404.16, "end": 1405.88, "text": " The nomenclature is a bit tangled.", "tokens": [51202, 440, 297, 4726, 3474, 1503, 307, 257, 857, 47192, 13, 51288], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18018633718708998, "compression_ratio": 1.5689655172413792, "no_speech_prob": 1.3619189326644077e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 138742, "start": 1406.44, "end": 1411.1000000000001, "text": " RSVP, the regulated state veto protocol, is the overarching theoretical framework for how", "tokens": [51316, 25855, 53, 47, 11, 264, 26243, 1785, 42910, 10336, 11, 307, 264, 45501, 20864, 8388, 337, 577, 51549], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18018633718708998, "compression_ratio": 1.5689655172413792, "no_speech_prob": 1.3619189326644077e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 138742, "start": 1411.1000000000001, "end": 1412.74, "text": " a system handles permanent refusal.", "tokens": [51549, 257, 1185, 18722, 10996, 48948, 13, 51631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18018633718708998, "compression_ratio": 1.5689655172413792, "no_speech_prob": 1.3619189326644077e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 141274, "start": 1412.74, "end": 1418.6200000000001, "text": " The four fields, scalar-Lanfron entropy vector, are the internal mathematical components of", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1451, 7909, 11, 39684, 12, 43, 282, 69, 2044, 30867, 8062, 11, 366, 264, 6920, 18894, 6677, 295, 50659], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1448515745309683, "compression_ratio": 1.4307692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496209137584981e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 141274, "start": 1418.6200000000001, "end": 1419.1200000000001, "text": " that protocol.", "tokens": [50659, 300, 10336, 13, 50684], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1448515745309683, "compression_ratio": 1.4307692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496209137584981e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 141274, "start": 1419.52, "end": 1421.48, "text": " They are the mechanisms that enforce the veto.", "tokens": [50704, 814, 366, 264, 15902, 300, 24825, 264, 42910, 13, 50802], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1448515745309683, "compression_ratio": 1.4307692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496209137584981e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 141274, "start": 1421.82, "end": 1422.5, "text": " Ah, okay.", "tokens": [50819, 2438, 11, 1392, 13, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1448515745309683, "compression_ratio": 1.4307692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496209137584981e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 141274, "start": 1422.84, "end": 1423.88, "text": " That makes so much more sense.", "tokens": [50870, 663, 1669, 370, 709, 544, 2020, 13, 50922], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1448515745309683, "compression_ratio": 1.4307692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496209137584981e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 141274, "start": 1423.96, "end": 1424.94, "text": " Thank you for clarifying that.", "tokens": [50926, 1044, 291, 337, 6093, 5489, 300, 13, 50975], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1448515745309683, "compression_ratio": 1.4307692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496209137584981e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 141274, "start": 1425.34, "end": 1428.82, "text": " So how does this RSVP veto actually build a boundary?", "tokens": [50995, 407, 577, 775, 341, 25855, 53, 47, 42910, 767, 1322, 257, 12866, 30, 51169], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1448515745309683, "compression_ratio": 1.4307692307692308, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496209137584981e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 142882, "start": 1428.82, "end": 1434.98, "text": " In this view, when a system refuses an option, it doesn't just make that option less likely.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 341, 1910, 11, 562, 257, 1185, 33222, 364, 3614, 11, 309, 1177, 380, 445, 652, 300, 3614, 1570, 3700, 13, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.165890328678084, "compression_ratio": 1.5119617224880382, "no_speech_prob": 1.495405470459954e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 142882, "start": 1435.9199999999998, "end": 1440.06, "text": " A Fristin screen could handle less likely by just assigning a low probability to that", "tokens": [50720, 316, 1526, 468, 259, 2568, 727, 4813, 1570, 3700, 538, 445, 49602, 257, 2295, 8482, 281, 300, 50927], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.165890328678084, "compression_ratio": 1.5119617224880382, "no_speech_prob": 1.495405470459954e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 142882, "start": 1440.06, "end": 1441.26, "text": " path in the present moment.", "tokens": [50927, 3100, 294, 264, 1974, 1623, 13, 50987], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.165890328678084, "compression_ratio": 1.5119617224880382, "no_speech_prob": 1.495405470459954e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 142882, "start": 1441.98, "end": 1447.28, "text": " But a diachronic exclusion permanently deletes that trajectory from the universe of options.", "tokens": [51023, 583, 257, 1026, 608, 10011, 33049, 24042, 1103, 37996, 300, 21512, 490, 264, 6445, 295, 3956, 13, 51288], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.165890328678084, "compression_ratio": 1.5119617224880382, "no_speech_prob": 1.495405470459954e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 142882, "start": 1447.48, "end": 1448.04, "text": " It's gone.", "tokens": [51298, 467, 311, 2780, 13, 51326], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.165890328678084, "compression_ratio": 1.5119617224880382, "no_speech_prob": 1.495405470459954e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 142882, "start": 1448.3, "end": 1448.58, "text": " Gone.", "tokens": [51339, 39068, 13, 51353], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.165890328678084, "compression_ratio": 1.5119617224880382, "no_speech_prob": 1.495405470459954e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 144858, "start": 1448.58, "end": 1453.76, "text": " The boundary of the system is literally constituted by the history of barriers it has erected", "tokens": [50365, 440, 12866, 295, 264, 1185, 307, 3736, 23079, 4866, 538, 264, 2503, 295, 13565, 309, 575, 34201, 292, 50624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14500475263262128, "compression_ratio": 1.7115384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.71473805207073e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 144858, "start": 1453.76, "end": 1455.26, "text": " against its own past choices.", "tokens": [50624, 1970, 1080, 1065, 1791, 7994, 13, 50699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14500475263262128, "compression_ratio": 1.7115384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.71473805207073e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 144858, "start": 1455.58, "end": 1456.72, "text": " It is a boundary of history.", "tokens": [50715, 467, 307, 257, 12866, 295, 2503, 13, 50772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14500475263262128, "compression_ratio": 1.7115384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.71473805207073e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 144858, "start": 1457.26, "end": 1460.62, "text": " So to recap, we have boundaries that mediate the present, like the sonar screen.", "tokens": [50799, 407, 281, 20928, 11, 321, 362, 13180, 300, 1205, 13024, 264, 1974, 11, 411, 264, 1872, 289, 2568, 13, 50967], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14500475263262128, "compression_ratio": 1.7115384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.71473805207073e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 144858, "start": 1461.22, "end": 1464.1999999999998, "text": " Boundaries that pull toward a future target, like the flatworm blueprint.", "tokens": [50997, 363, 554, 4889, 300, 2235, 7361, 257, 2027, 3779, 11, 411, 264, 4962, 30917, 35868, 13, 51146], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14500475263262128, "compression_ratio": 1.7115384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.71473805207073e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 144858, "start": 1464.72, "end": 1469.08, "text": " And boundaries built from past irreversible exclusions, like the RSVP history wall.", "tokens": [51172, 400, 13180, 3094, 490, 1791, 16014, 840, 964, 15085, 626, 11, 411, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 2503, 2929, 13, 51390], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14500475263262128, "compression_ratio": 1.7115384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.71473805207073e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 144858, "start": 1469.1799999999998, "end": 1469.36, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51395, 7587, 13, 51404], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14500475263262128, "compression_ratio": 1.7115384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.71473805207073e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 144858, "start": 1469.56, "end": 1472.48, "text": " Now here is where I really want to push back on Flickshen.", "tokens": [51414, 823, 510, 307, 689, 286, 534, 528, 281, 2944, 646, 322, 3235, 618, 2716, 268, 13, 51560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14500475263262128, "compression_ratio": 1.7115384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.71473805207073e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 144858, "start": 1473.1599999999999, "end": 1475.48, "text": " Can't a boundary be all three at once?", "tokens": [51594, 1664, 380, 257, 12866, 312, 439, 1045, 412, 1564, 30, 51710], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14500475263262128, "compression_ratio": 1.7115384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.71473805207073e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 144858, "start": 1475.6, "end": 1477.0, "text": " I mean, look at biological reality.", "tokens": [51716, 286, 914, 11, 574, 412, 13910, 4103, 13, 51786], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14500475263262128, "compression_ratio": 1.7115384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.71473805207073e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 147700, "start": 1477.0, "end": 1478.56, "text": " My cells have a cell wall.", "tokens": [50365, 1222, 5438, 362, 257, 2815, 2929, 13, 50443], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16917379628057067, "compression_ratio": 1.6644295302013423, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108496914829518e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 147700, "start": 1479.2, "end": 1483.12, "text": " That wall has a history of evolution and past cellular divisions.", "tokens": [50475, 663, 2929, 575, 257, 2503, 295, 9303, 293, 1791, 29267, 24328, 13, 50671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16917379628057067, "compression_ratio": 1.6644295302013423, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108496914829518e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 147700, "start": 1483.46, "end": 1484.0, "text": " That's past.", "tokens": [50688, 663, 311, 1791, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16917379628057067, "compression_ratio": 1.6644295302013423, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108496914829518e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 147700, "start": 1484.4, "end": 1487.44, "text": " It is currently managing the temperature and chemical flow right now present.", "tokens": [50735, 467, 307, 4362, 11642, 264, 4292, 293, 7313, 3095, 558, 586, 1974, 13, 50887], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16917379628057067, "compression_ratio": 1.6644295302013423, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108496914829518e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 147700, "start": 1487.86, "end": 1492.36, "text": " And it contains genetic and electrical targets for dividing into a new cell tomorrow future.", "tokens": [50908, 400, 309, 8306, 12462, 293, 12147, 12911, 337, 26764, 666, 257, 777, 2815, 4153, 2027, 13, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16917379628057067, "compression_ratio": 1.6644295302013423, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108496914829518e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 147700, "start": 1493.08, "end": 1497.46, "text": " How can Flickshen say that's mathematically impossible when it literally happens in my own", "tokens": [51169, 1012, 393, 3235, 618, 2716, 268, 584, 300, 311, 44003, 6243, 562, 309, 3736, 2314, 294, 452, 1065, 51388], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16917379628057067, "compression_ratio": 1.6644295302013423, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108496914829518e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 147700, "start": 1497.46, "end": 1497.8, "text": " body?", "tokens": [51388, 1772, 30, 51405], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16917379628057067, "compression_ratio": 1.6644295302013423, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108496914829518e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 147700, "start": 1498.04, "end": 1499.8, "text": " It is a phenomenal challenge.", "tokens": [51417, 467, 307, 257, 17778, 3430, 13, 51505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16917379628057067, "compression_ratio": 1.6644295302013423, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108496914829518e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 147700, "start": 1500.12, "end": 1504.22, "text": " And it goes right to the heart of the difference between biology and mathematical formalism.", "tokens": [51521, 400, 309, 1709, 558, 281, 264, 1917, 295, 264, 2649, 1296, 14956, 293, 18894, 9860, 1434, 13, 51726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16917379628057067, "compression_ratio": 1.6644295302013423, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108496914829518e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 150422, "start": 1504.22, "end": 1510.78, "text": " You are entirely correct that a biological cell is a messy, pragmatic kludge of overlapping", "tokens": [50365, 509, 366, 7696, 3006, 300, 257, 13910, 2815, 307, 257, 16191, 11, 46904, 350, 1471, 432, 295, 33535, 50693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17063248023558197, "compression_ratio": 1.6059322033898304, "no_speech_prob": 1.4747895829905766e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 150422, "start": 1510.78, "end": 1511.38, "text": " systems.", "tokens": [50693, 3652, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17063248023558197, "compression_ratio": 1.6059322033898304, "no_speech_prob": 1.4747895829905766e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 150422, "start": 1511.94, "end": 1515.3600000000001, "text": " Biology will stack a million different mechanisms on top of each other to survive.", "tokens": [50751, 48132, 486, 8630, 257, 2459, 819, 15902, 322, 1192, 295, 1184, 661, 281, 7867, 13, 50922], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17063248023558197, "compression_ratio": 1.6059322033898304, "no_speech_prob": 1.4747895829905766e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 150422, "start": 1515.44, "end": 1515.58, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50926, 1779, 13, 50933], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17063248023558197, "compression_ratio": 1.6059322033898304, "no_speech_prob": 1.4747895829905766e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 150422, "start": 1515.66, "end": 1516.18, "text": " Whatever works.", "tokens": [50937, 8541, 1985, 13, 50963], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17063248023558197, "compression_ratio": 1.6059322033898304, "no_speech_prob": 1.4747895829905766e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 150422, "start": 1516.24, "end": 1516.8600000000001, "text": " Whatever works.", "tokens": [50966, 8541, 1985, 13, 50997], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17063248023558197, "compression_ratio": 1.6059322033898304, "no_speech_prob": 1.4747895829905766e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 150422, "start": 1517.18, "end": 1520.08, "text": " But Flickshen is not describing a biological cell wall.", "tokens": [51013, 583, 3235, 618, 2716, 268, 307, 406, 16141, 257, 13910, 2815, 2929, 13, 51158], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17063248023558197, "compression_ratio": 1.6059322033898304, "no_speech_prob": 1.4747895829905766e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 150422, "start": 1520.26, "end": 1525.16, "text": " They are describing a singular, unbroken mathematical boundary operating under a single optimization", "tokens": [51167, 814, 366, 16141, 257, 20010, 11, 517, 37947, 18894, 12866, 7447, 833, 257, 2167, 19618, 51412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17063248023558197, "compression_ratio": 1.6059322033898304, "no_speech_prob": 1.4747895829905766e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 152516, "start": 1525.16, "end": 1525.66, "text": " rule.", "tokens": [50365, 4978, 13, 50390], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19316414919766514, "compression_ratio": 1.546468401486989, "no_speech_prob": 1.6744081164990487e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 152516, "start": 1525.66, "end": 1531.48, "text": " And they point to theorem 3.6 in the text to prove that these three pure types are formally", "tokens": [50390, 400, 436, 935, 281, 20904, 805, 13, 21, 294, 264, 2487, 281, 7081, 300, 613, 1045, 6075, 3467, 366, 25983, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19316414919766514, "compression_ratio": 1.546468401486989, "no_speech_prob": 1.6744081164990487e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 152516, "start": 1531.48, "end": 1535.8400000000001, "text": " mathematically incompatible if you try to combine them into one seamless equation.", "tokens": [50681, 44003, 40393, 267, 964, 498, 291, 853, 281, 10432, 552, 666, 472, 28677, 5367, 13, 50899], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19316414919766514, "compression_ratio": 1.546468401486989, "no_speech_prob": 1.6744081164990487e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 152516, "start": 1536.3000000000002, "end": 1537.5, "text": " Okay, walk me through the crash.", "tokens": [50922, 1033, 11, 1792, 385, 807, 264, 8252, 13, 50982], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19316414919766514, "compression_ratio": 1.546468401486989, "no_speech_prob": 1.6744081164990487e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 152516, "start": 1537.6000000000001, "end": 1538.68, "text": " Why does the math break?", "tokens": [50987, 1545, 775, 264, 5221, 1821, 30, 51041], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19316414919766514, "compression_ratio": 1.546468401486989, "no_speech_prob": 1.6744081164990487e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 152516, "start": 1539.0400000000002, "end": 1541.5, "text": " Let's test your hypothesis by combining them.", "tokens": [51059, 961, 311, 1500, 428, 17291, 538, 21928, 552, 13, 51182], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19316414919766514, "compression_ratio": 1.546468401486989, "no_speech_prob": 1.6744081164990487e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 152516, "start": 1542.38, "end": 1545.22, "text": " Consider the synchronic screen or submarine sonar.", "tokens": [51226, 17416, 264, 5451, 339, 10011, 2568, 420, 33995, 1872, 289, 13, 51368], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19316414919766514, "compression_ratio": 1.546468401486989, "no_speech_prob": 1.6744081164990487e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 152516, "start": 1545.76, "end": 1549.02, "text": " Remember, it minimizes discrepancy based strictly on the present moment.", "tokens": [51395, 5459, 11, 309, 4464, 5660, 2983, 265, 6040, 1344, 2361, 20792, 322, 264, 1974, 1623, 13, 51558], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19316414919766514, "compression_ratio": 1.546468401486989, "no_speech_prob": 1.6744081164990487e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 152516, "start": 1549.14, "end": 1549.3400000000001, "text": " Got it.", "tokens": [51564, 5803, 309, 13, 51574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19316414919766514, "compression_ratio": 1.546468401486989, "no_speech_prob": 1.6744081164990487e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 154934, "start": 1549.34, "end": 1554.6599999999999, "text": " Suppose the sonar is guiding the suba toward what its algorithms calculate is the absolute", "tokens": [50365, 21360, 264, 1872, 289, 307, 25061, 264, 1422, 64, 7361, 437, 1080, 14642, 8873, 307, 264, 8236, 50631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1318106921213978, "compression_ratio": 1.6289752650176679, "no_speech_prob": 1.661987171150403e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 154934, "start": 1554.6599999999999, "end": 1556.6599999999999, "text": " optimal path forward right now.", "tokens": [50631, 16252, 3100, 2128, 558, 586, 13, 50731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1318106921213978, "compression_ratio": 1.6289752650176679, "no_speech_prob": 1.661987171150403e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 154934, "start": 1557.26, "end": 1563.86, "text": " Now suddenly impose a diachronic exclusion and RSVP veto onto that exact same system, meaning", "tokens": [50761, 823, 5800, 26952, 257, 1026, 608, 10011, 33049, 293, 25855, 53, 47, 42910, 3911, 300, 1900, 912, 1185, 11, 3620, 51091], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1318106921213978, "compression_ratio": 1.6289752650176679, "no_speech_prob": 1.661987171150403e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 154934, "start": 1563.86, "end": 1568.86, "text": " you permanently delete that optimal path from the universe of options because of some historical", "tokens": [51091, 291, 24042, 12097, 300, 16252, 3100, 490, 264, 6445, 295, 3956, 570, 295, 512, 8584, 51341], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1318106921213978, "compression_ratio": 1.6289752650176679, "no_speech_prob": 1.661987171150403e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 154934, "start": 1568.86, "end": 1570.1, "text": " rule a system just triggered.", "tokens": [51341, 4978, 257, 1185, 445, 21710, 13, 51403], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1318106921213978, "compression_ratio": 1.6289752650176679, "no_speech_prob": 1.661987171150403e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 154934, "start": 1570.36, "end": 1572.22, "text": " What happens to the synchronic screen?", "tokens": [51416, 708, 2314, 281, 264, 5451, 339, 10011, 2568, 30, 51509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1318106921213978, "compression_ratio": 1.6289752650176679, "no_speech_prob": 1.661987171150403e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 154934, "start": 1572.98, "end": 1577.4199999999998, "text": " Well, it's trying to optimize for a paint that suddenly doesn't exist anymore.", "tokens": [51547, 1042, 11, 309, 311, 1382, 281, 19719, 337, 257, 4225, 300, 5800, 1177, 380, 2514, 3602, 13, 51769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1318106921213978, "compression_ratio": 1.6289752650176679, "no_speech_prob": 1.661987171150403e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 157742, "start": 1577.42, "end": 1582.5600000000002, "text": " And because it's a synchronic screen, it has no memory to understand why the path disappeared.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 570, 309, 311, 257, 5451, 339, 10011, 2568, 11, 309, 575, 572, 4675, 281, 1223, 983, 264, 3100, 13954, 13, 50622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13902223110198975, "compression_ratio": 1.697749196141479, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250509610517884e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 157742, "start": 1582.74, "end": 1583.02, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50631, 7587, 13, 50645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13902223110198975, "compression_ratio": 1.697749196141479, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250509610517884e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 157742, "start": 1583.3400000000001, "end": 1587.88, "text": " The mathematical formalism of a synchronic screen has no architecture to process a historical", "tokens": [50661, 440, 18894, 9860, 1434, 295, 257, 5451, 339, 10011, 2568, 575, 572, 9482, 281, 1399, 257, 8584, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13902223110198975, "compression_ratio": 1.697749196141479, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250509610517884e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 157742, "start": 1587.88, "end": 1588.4, "text": " deletion.", "tokens": [50888, 1103, 302, 313, 13, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13902223110198975, "compression_ratio": 1.697749196141479, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250509610517884e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 157742, "start": 1589.04, "end": 1593.46, "text": " To the present tense optimizer, its absolute best choice just vanished into thin air without", "tokens": [50946, 1407, 264, 1974, 18760, 5028, 6545, 11, 1080, 8236, 1151, 3922, 445, 37518, 666, 5862, 1988, 1553, 51167], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13902223110198975, "compression_ratio": 1.697749196141479, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250509610517884e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 157742, "start": 1593.46, "end": 1594.42, "text": " physical explanation.", "tokens": [51167, 4001, 10835, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13902223110198975, "compression_ratio": 1.697749196141479, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250509610517884e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 157742, "start": 1594.94, "end": 1597.7, "text": " The optimization algorithm will literally fail to converge.", "tokens": [51241, 440, 19618, 9284, 486, 3736, 3061, 281, 41881, 13, 51379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13902223110198975, "compression_ratio": 1.697749196141479, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250509610517884e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 157742, "start": 1597.94, "end": 1598.3600000000001, "text": " It crashes.", "tokens": [51391, 467, 28642, 13, 51412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13902223110198975, "compression_ratio": 1.697749196141479, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250509610517884e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 157742, "start": 1598.5600000000002, "end": 1599.78, "text": " Because it just doesn't compute.", "tokens": [51422, 1436, 309, 445, 1177, 380, 14722, 13, 51483], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13902223110198975, "compression_ratio": 1.697749196141479, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250509610517884e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 157742, "start": 1600.1000000000001, "end": 1600.3200000000002, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51499, 1779, 13, 51510], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13902223110198975, "compression_ratio": 1.697749196141479, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250509610517884e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 157742, "start": 1600.44, "end": 1605.96, "text": " To fix the math, you would have to force the present tense screen to suddenly carry a massive", "tokens": [51516, 1407, 3191, 264, 5221, 11, 291, 576, 362, 281, 3464, 264, 1974, 18760, 2568, 281, 5800, 3985, 257, 5994, 51792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13902223110198975, "compression_ratio": 1.697749196141479, "no_speech_prob": 1.8250509610517884e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 160596, "start": 1605.96, "end": 1611.18, "text": " database of historical memory which fundamentally changes its architecture into something else.", "tokens": [50365, 8149, 295, 8584, 4675, 597, 17879, 2962, 1080, 9482, 666, 746, 1646, 13, 50626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16100440154204498, "compression_ratio": 1.5701754385964912, "no_speech_prob": 1.8389695148612883e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 160596, "start": 1611.92, "end": 1614.04, "text": " They are structurally different mechanisms.", "tokens": [50663, 814, 366, 6594, 6512, 819, 15902, 13, 50769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16100440154204498, "compression_ratio": 1.5701754385964912, "no_speech_prob": 1.8389695148612883e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 160596, "start": 1614.78, "end": 1620.3400000000001, "text": " A single mathematical boundary cannot seamlessly be a purely memoryless present tense optimizer", "tokens": [50806, 316, 2167, 18894, 12866, 2644, 38083, 312, 257, 17491, 4675, 1832, 1974, 18760, 5028, 6545, 51084], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16100440154204498, "compression_ratio": 1.5701754385964912, "no_speech_prob": 1.8389695148612883e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 160596, "start": 1620.3400000000001, "end": 1625.66, "text": " and a permanent historical lock at the exact same time without the equations contradicting", "tokens": [51084, 293, 257, 10996, 8584, 4017, 412, 264, 1900, 912, 565, 1553, 264, 11787, 15858, 21490, 51350], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16100440154204498, "compression_ratio": 1.5701754385964912, "no_speech_prob": 1.8389695148612883e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 160596, "start": 1625.66, "end": 1626.1200000000001, "text": " each other.", "tokens": [51350, 1184, 661, 13, 51373], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16100440154204498, "compression_ratio": 1.5701754385964912, "no_speech_prob": 1.8389695148612883e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 160596, "start": 1626.16, "end": 1626.96, "text": " Okay, I can see it.", "tokens": [51375, 1033, 11, 286, 393, 536, 309, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16100440154204498, "compression_ratio": 1.5701754385964912, "no_speech_prob": 1.8389695148612883e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 162696, "start": 1626.96, "end": 1628.58, "text": " The math literally crashes.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 5221, 3736, 28642, 13, 50446], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14840885601212492, "compression_ratio": 1.6575342465753424, "no_speech_prob": 1.761997015306549e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 162696, "start": 1629.42, "end": 1633.26, "text": " The biology only works because it's cheating and using multiple different physical layers", "tokens": [50488, 440, 14956, 787, 1985, 570, 309, 311, 18309, 293, 1228, 3866, 819, 4001, 7914, 50680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14840885601212492, "compression_ratio": 1.6575342465753424, "no_speech_prob": 1.761997015306549e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 162696, "start": 1633.26, "end": 1634.22, "text": " to do different jobs.", "tokens": [50680, 281, 360, 819, 4782, 13, 50728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14840885601212492, "compression_ratio": 1.6575342465753424, "no_speech_prob": 1.761997015306549e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 162696, "start": 1634.32, "end": 1634.76, "text": " Precise.", "tokens": [50733, 6001, 66, 908, 13, 50755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14840885601212492, "compression_ratio": 1.6575342465753424, "no_speech_prob": 1.761997015306549e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 162696, "start": 1635.1000000000001, "end": 1637.08, "text": " So boundaries dictate the rules of the shell.", "tokens": [50772, 407, 13180, 36071, 264, 4474, 295, 264, 8720, 13, 50871], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14840885601212492, "compression_ratio": 1.6575342465753424, "no_speech_prob": 1.761997015306549e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 162696, "start": 1637.44, "end": 1639.42, "text": " But what happens when a rule gets broken?", "tokens": [50889, 583, 437, 2314, 562, 257, 4978, 2170, 5463, 30, 50988], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14840885601212492, "compression_ratio": 1.6575342465753424, "no_speech_prob": 1.761997015306549e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 162696, "start": 1640.0, "end": 1644.56, "text": " What happens when a physical field inside that boundary suddenly disagrees with its neighbors?", "tokens": [51017, 708, 2314, 562, 257, 4001, 2519, 1854, 300, 12866, 5800, 10414, 4856, 365, 1080, 12512, 30, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14840885601212492, "compression_ratio": 1.6575342465753424, "no_speech_prob": 1.761997015306549e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 162696, "start": 1645.1000000000001, "end": 1648.6200000000001, "text": " Like if the temperature in one tiny spot is vastly different from the temperature an inch", "tokens": [51272, 1743, 498, 264, 4292, 294, 472, 5870, 4008, 307, 41426, 819, 490, 264, 4292, 364, 7227, 51448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14840885601212492, "compression_ratio": 1.6575342465753424, "no_speech_prob": 1.761997015306549e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 162696, "start": 1648.6200000000001, "end": 1652.46, "text": " away, how does the universe even know that discrepancy exists?", "tokens": [51448, 1314, 11, 577, 775, 264, 6445, 754, 458, 300, 2983, 265, 6040, 1344, 8198, 30, 51640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14840885601212492, "compression_ratio": 1.6575342465753424, "no_speech_prob": 1.761997015306549e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 165246, "start": 1652.46, "end": 1657.6200000000001, "text": " That brings us to Fliction's concept of the ultimate mathematical referee, the incompatibility", "tokens": [50365, 663, 5607, 505, 281, 3235, 4105, 311, 3410, 295, 264, 9705, 18894, 43096, 11, 264, 40393, 267, 2841, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1083853575434998, "compression_ratio": 1.65527950310559, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906347841463056e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 165246, "start": 1657.6200000000001, "end": 1658.1000000000001, "text": " detector.", "tokens": [50623, 25712, 13, 50647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1083853575434998, "compression_ratio": 1.65527950310559, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906347841463056e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 165246, "start": 1658.76, "end": 1663.8400000000001, "text": " This is where they reintroduce a very old mathematical tool in a completely new light, the Laplacian", "tokens": [50680, 639, 307, 689, 436, 319, 38132, 384, 257, 588, 1331, 18894, 2290, 294, 257, 2584, 777, 1442, 11, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1083853575434998, "compression_ratio": 1.65527950310559, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906347841463056e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 165246, "start": 1663.8400000000001, "end": 1664.3600000000001, "text": " operator.", "tokens": [50934, 12973, 13, 50960], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1083853575434998, "compression_ratio": 1.65527950310559, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906347841463056e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 165246, "start": 1664.64, "end": 1666.8400000000001, "text": " Now I remember the Laplacian from physics classes.", "tokens": [50974, 823, 286, 1604, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 490, 10649, 5359, 13, 51084], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1083853575434998, "compression_ratio": 1.65527950310559, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906347841463056e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 165246, "start": 1667.3, "end": 1671.5, "text": " Usually you see an upside down triangle symbol and it's dealing with heat equations or maybe", "tokens": [51107, 11419, 291, 536, 364, 14119, 760, 13369, 5986, 293, 309, 311, 6260, 365, 3738, 11787, 420, 1310, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1083853575434998, "compression_ratio": 1.65527950310559, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906347841463056e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 165246, "start": 1671.5, "end": 1673.32, "text": " how sound waves propagate through a room.", "tokens": [51317, 577, 1626, 9417, 48256, 807, 257, 1808, 13, 51408], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1083853575434998, "compression_ratio": 1.65527950310559, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906347841463056e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 165246, "start": 1673.82, "end": 1675.74, "text": " But Fliction totally rebrands it here.", "tokens": [51433, 583, 3235, 4105, 3879, 12970, 3699, 82, 309, 510, 13, 51529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1083853575434998, "compression_ratio": 1.65527950310559, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906347841463056e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 165246, "start": 1675.8400000000001, "end": 1676.06, "text": " They do.", "tokens": [51534, 814, 360, 13, 51545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1083853575434998, "compression_ratio": 1.65527950310559, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906347841463056e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 165246, "start": 1676.16, "end": 1680.24, "text": " They argue that the Laplacian isn't just a clever trick for solving how heat flows.", "tokens": [51550, 814, 9695, 300, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 13494, 4282, 337, 12606, 577, 3738, 12867, 13, 51754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1083853575434998, "compression_ratio": 1.65527950310559, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906347841463056e-12}, {"id": 545, "seek": 168024, "start": 1680.24, "end": 1684.34, "text": " It is a universal geometric incompatibility detector.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 257, 11455, 33246, 40393, 267, 2841, 25712, 13, 50570], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09524003053322816, "compression_ratio": 1.586092715231788, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552405062916775e-12}, {"id": 546, "seek": 168024, "start": 1684.96, "end": 1689.86, "text": " If you look at equation 4.1 in the text, it strips away all the complex physics and shows", "tokens": [50601, 759, 291, 574, 412, 5367, 1017, 13, 16, 294, 264, 2487, 11, 309, 19842, 1314, 439, 264, 3997, 10649, 293, 3110, 50846], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09524003053322816, "compression_ratio": 1.586092715231788, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552405062916775e-12}, {"id": 547, "seek": 168024, "start": 1689.86, "end": 1692.64, "text": " exactly what this operator does purely geographically.", "tokens": [50846, 2293, 437, 341, 12973, 775, 17491, 25435, 984, 13, 50985], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09524003053322816, "compression_ratio": 1.586092715231788, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552405062916775e-12}, {"id": 548, "seek": 168024, "start": 1693.18, "end": 1698.3, "text": " At any given microscopic point in a space, the Laplacian measures exactly one thing.", "tokens": [51012, 1711, 604, 2212, 47897, 935, 294, 257, 1901, 11, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 8000, 2293, 472, 551, 13, 51268], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09524003053322816, "compression_ratio": 1.586092715231788, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552405062916775e-12}, {"id": 549, "seek": 168024, "start": 1698.7, "end": 1703.26, "text": " How much the value of a field at that point disagrees with the average value of its immediate", "tokens": [51288, 1012, 709, 264, 2158, 295, 257, 2519, 412, 300, 935, 10414, 4856, 365, 264, 4274, 2158, 295, 1080, 11629, 51516], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09524003053322816, "compression_ratio": 1.586092715231788, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552405062916775e-12}, {"id": 550, "seek": 168024, "start": 1703.26, "end": 1703.76, "text": " surroundings.", "tokens": [51516, 25314, 13, 51541], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09524003053322816, "compression_ratio": 1.586092715231788, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552405062916775e-12}, {"id": 551, "seek": 168024, "start": 1704.18, "end": 1708.78, "text": " So to use a visual analogy, if I'm a single pixel on a computer screen and I am glowing", "tokens": [51562, 407, 281, 764, 257, 5056, 21663, 11, 498, 286, 478, 257, 2167, 19261, 322, 257, 3820, 2568, 293, 286, 669, 27064, 51792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09524003053322816, "compression_ratio": 1.586092715231788, "no_speech_prob": 1.6552405062916775e-12}, {"id": 552, "seek": 170878, "start": 1708.78, "end": 1714.32, "text": " bright, blinding white, but every single pixel touching me on all sides is pitch black, the", "tokens": [50365, 4730, 11, 6865, 278, 2418, 11, 457, 633, 2167, 19261, 11175, 385, 322, 439, 4881, 307, 7293, 2211, 11, 264, 50642], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14981797097743244, "compression_ratio": 1.518348623853211, "no_speech_prob": 1.5073614014968206e-12}, {"id": 553, "seek": 170878, "start": 1714.32, "end": 1718.62, "text": " Laplacian is essentially an alarm bell screaming massive disagreement here.", "tokens": [50642, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 307, 4476, 364, 14183, 4549, 12636, 5994, 38947, 510, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14981797097743244, "compression_ratio": 1.518348623853211, "no_speech_prob": 1.5073614014968206e-12}, {"id": 554, "seek": 170878, "start": 1719.02, "end": 1721.06, "text": " This pixel is incompatible with its neighbors.", "tokens": [50877, 639, 19261, 307, 40393, 267, 964, 365, 1080, 12512, 13, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14981797097743244, "compression_ratio": 1.518348623853211, "no_speech_prob": 1.5073614014968206e-12}, {"id": 555, "seek": 170878, "start": 1721.54, "end": 1722.02, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51003, 7587, 13, 51027], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14981797097743244, "compression_ratio": 1.518348623853211, "no_speech_prob": 1.5073614014968206e-12}, {"id": 556, "seek": 170878, "start": 1722.26, "end": 1723.62, "text": " It spots the local mismatch.", "tokens": [51039, 467, 10681, 264, 2654, 23220, 852, 13, 51107], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14981797097743244, "compression_ratio": 1.518348623853211, "no_speech_prob": 1.5073614014968206e-12}, {"id": 557, "seek": 170878, "start": 1723.7, "end": 1724.68, "text": " It calculates the tension.", "tokens": [51111, 467, 4322, 1024, 264, 8980, 13, 51160], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14981797097743244, "compression_ratio": 1.518348623853211, "no_speech_prob": 1.5073614014968206e-12}, {"id": 558, "seek": 170878, "start": 1725.06, "end": 1727.92, "text": " But here is where Fliction's earlier work pays off.", "tokens": [51179, 583, 510, 307, 689, 3235, 4105, 311, 3071, 589, 10604, 766, 13, 51322], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14981797097743244, "compression_ratio": 1.518348623853211, "no_speech_prob": 1.5073614014968206e-12}, {"id": 559, "seek": 172792, "start": 1727.92, "end": 1732.96, "text": " Because Fliction has already established the supreme mathematical dominance of the spherical", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 3235, 4105, 575, 1217, 7545, 264, 27756, 18894, 34987, 295, 264, 37300, 50617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09991469951944613, "compression_ratio": 1.6750902527075813, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169089721643215e-12}, {"id": 560, "seek": 172792, "start": 1732.96, "end": 1738.48, "text": " coordinate system for these kinds of spaces, they apply that radial and angular split to", "tokens": [50617, 15670, 1185, 337, 613, 3685, 295, 7673, 11, 436, 3079, 300, 38783, 293, 24413, 7472, 281, 50893], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09991469951944613, "compression_ratio": 1.6750902527075813, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169089721643215e-12}, {"id": 561, "seek": 172792, "start": 1738.48, "end": 1739.78, "text": " the Laplacian itself.", "tokens": [50893, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 2564, 13, 50958], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09991469951944613, "compression_ratio": 1.6750902527075813, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169089721643215e-12}, {"id": 562, "seek": 172792, "start": 1739.88, "end": 1742.18, "text": " Wait, so the Laplacian doesn't just sound a general alarm.", "tokens": [50963, 3802, 11, 370, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 1177, 380, 445, 1626, 257, 2674, 14183, 13, 51078], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09991469951944613, "compression_ratio": 1.6750902527075813, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169089721643215e-12}, {"id": 563, "seek": 172792, "start": 1742.4, "end": 1745.78, "text": " It actually has two different sirens depending on what kind of mismatch it is.", "tokens": [51089, 467, 767, 575, 732, 819, 262, 44511, 5413, 322, 437, 733, 295, 23220, 852, 309, 307, 13, 51258], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09991469951944613, "compression_ratio": 1.6750902527075813, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169089721643215e-12}, {"id": 564, "seek": 172792, "start": 1745.88, "end": 1746.3400000000001, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51263, 48746, 736, 13, 51286], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09991469951944613, "compression_ratio": 1.6750902527075813, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169089721643215e-12}, {"id": 565, "seek": 172792, "start": 1746.8400000000001, "end": 1750.44, "text": " The disagreement splits perfectly mathematically into two distinct parts.", "tokens": [51311, 440, 38947, 37741, 6239, 44003, 666, 732, 10644, 3166, 13, 51491], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09991469951944613, "compression_ratio": 1.6750902527075813, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169089721643215e-12}, {"id": 566, "seek": 172792, "start": 1750.98, "end": 1754.0800000000002, "text": " Radial mismatch and angular mismatch.", "tokens": [51518, 9654, 831, 23220, 852, 293, 24413, 23220, 852, 13, 51673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09991469951944613, "compression_ratio": 1.6750902527075813, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169089721643215e-12}, {"id": 567, "seek": 175408, "start": 1754.08, "end": 1756.6999999999998, "text": " Okay, ground this in our music festival analogy from earlier.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 2727, 341, 294, 527, 1318, 12091, 21663, 490, 3071, 13, 50496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12449109915531043, "compression_ratio": 1.768976897689769, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102581507776437e-12}, {"id": 568, "seek": 175408, "start": 1757.08, "end": 1758.6799999999998, "text": " What does a radial mismatch mean?", "tokens": [50515, 708, 775, 257, 38783, 23220, 852, 914, 30, 50595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12449109915531043, "compression_ratio": 1.768976897689769, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102581507776437e-12}, {"id": 569, "seek": 175408, "start": 1759.08, "end": 1763.48, "text": " Radial mismatch measures how much you disagree with the shells immediately above you and", "tokens": [50615, 9654, 831, 23220, 852, 8000, 577, 709, 291, 14091, 365, 264, 22523, 4258, 3673, 291, 293, 50835], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12449109915531043, "compression_ratio": 1.768976897689769, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102581507776437e-12}, {"id": 570, "seek": 175408, "start": 1763.48, "end": 1766.12, "text": " below you, your progression across levels.", "tokens": [50835, 2507, 291, 11, 428, 18733, 2108, 4358, 13, 50967], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12449109915531043, "compression_ratio": 1.768976897689769, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102581507776437e-12}, {"id": 571, "seek": 175408, "start": 1766.54, "end": 1770.1, "text": " In the festival, it's like a guy standing in the general admission section demanding free", "tokens": [50988, 682, 264, 12091, 11, 309, 311, 411, 257, 2146, 4877, 294, 264, 2674, 24668, 3541, 19960, 1737, 51166], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12449109915531043, "compression_ratio": 1.768976897689769, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102581507776437e-12}, {"id": 572, "seek": 175408, "start": 1770.1, "end": 1771.02, "text": " drinks like a VIP.", "tokens": [51166, 12142, 411, 257, 29732, 13, 51212], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12449109915531043, "compression_ratio": 1.768976897689769, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102581507776437e-12}, {"id": 573, "seek": 175408, "start": 1771.56, "end": 1774.12, "text": " He is radially mismatched with his environment.", "tokens": [51239, 634, 307, 2843, 2270, 23220, 24102, 365, 702, 2823, 13, 51367], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12449109915531043, "compression_ratio": 1.768976897689769, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102581507776437e-12}, {"id": 574, "seek": 175408, "start": 1774.32, "end": 1776.0, "text": " Right, he's on the wrong level for what he's doing.", "tokens": [51377, 1779, 11, 415, 311, 322, 264, 2085, 1496, 337, 437, 415, 311, 884, 13, 51461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12449109915531043, "compression_ratio": 1.768976897689769, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102581507776437e-12}, {"id": 575, "seek": 175408, "start": 1776.48, "end": 1777.0, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51485, 7587, 13, 51511], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12449109915531043, "compression_ratio": 1.768976897689769, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102581507776437e-12}, {"id": 576, "seek": 175408, "start": 1777.58, "end": 1781.96, "text": " Angular mismatch, on the other hand, measures how much you disagree with your neighbors on", "tokens": [51540, 34107, 23220, 852, 11, 322, 264, 661, 1011, 11, 8000, 577, 709, 291, 14091, 365, 428, 12512, 322, 51759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12449109915531043, "compression_ratio": 1.768976897689769, "no_speech_prob": 1.6102581507776437e-12}, {"id": 577, "seek": 178196, "start": 1781.96, "end": 1785.46, "text": " the exact same shell, your organization within a level.", "tokens": [50365, 264, 1900, 912, 8720, 11, 428, 4475, 1951, 257, 1496, 13, 50540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12890109237359496, "compression_ratio": 1.6016597510373445, "no_speech_prob": 2.1842818352657556e-12}, {"id": 578, "seek": 178196, "start": 1785.96, "end": 1791.08, "text": " It's like being in the VIP section where everyone is quietly sipping cocktails and you", "tokens": [50565, 467, 311, 411, 885, 294, 264, 29732, 3541, 689, 1518, 307, 19141, 1511, 3759, 49006, 293, 291, 50821], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12890109237359496, "compression_ratio": 1.6016597510373445, "no_speech_prob": 2.1842818352657556e-12}, {"id": 579, "seek": 178196, "start": 1791.08, "end": 1792.08, "text": " are starting a mosh pit.", "tokens": [50821, 366, 2891, 257, 275, 3019, 10147, 13, 50871], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12890109237359496, "compression_ratio": 1.6016597510373445, "no_speech_prob": 2.1842818352657556e-12}, {"id": 580, "seek": 178196, "start": 1792.6200000000001, "end": 1796.42, "text": " You are on the right level, but you are angularly incompatible with your immediate peers.", "tokens": [50898, 509, 366, 322, 264, 558, 1496, 11, 457, 291, 366, 24413, 356, 40393, 267, 964, 365, 428, 11629, 16739, 13, 51088], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12890109237359496, "compression_ratio": 1.6016597510373445, "no_speech_prob": 2.1842818352657556e-12}, {"id": 581, "seek": 178196, "start": 1797.44, "end": 1800.26, "text": " The Laplacian doesn't just say there is a mismatch.", "tokens": [51139, 440, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 1177, 380, 445, 584, 456, 307, 257, 23220, 852, 13, 51280], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12890109237359496, "compression_ratio": 1.6016597510373445, "no_speech_prob": 2.1842818352657556e-12}, {"id": 582, "seek": 178196, "start": 1800.42, "end": 1804.44, "text": " It tells you exactly which geometric direction the mismatch is occurring in.", "tokens": [51288, 467, 5112, 291, 2293, 597, 33246, 3513, 264, 23220, 852, 307, 18386, 294, 13, 51489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12890109237359496, "compression_ratio": 1.6016597510373445, "no_speech_prob": 2.1842818352657556e-12}, {"id": 583, "seek": 180444, "start": 1804.44, "end": 1810.28, "text": " Here's where it gets really interesting because the text dives incredibly deep into how the", "tokens": [50365, 1692, 311, 689, 309, 2170, 534, 1880, 570, 264, 2487, 274, 1539, 6252, 2452, 666, 577, 264, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10293165842692058, "compression_ratio": 1.6262626262626263, "no_speech_prob": 1.846162979435295e-12}, {"id": 584, "seek": 180444, "start": 1810.28, "end": 1815.72, "text": " Laplacian handles that angular mismatch on a single shell, the mosh pit in the VIP section.", "tokens": [50657, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 18722, 300, 24413, 23220, 852, 322, 257, 2167, 8720, 11, 264, 275, 3019, 10147, 294, 264, 29732, 3541, 13, 50929], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10293165842692058, "compression_ratio": 1.6262626262626263, "no_speech_prob": 1.846162979435295e-12}, {"id": 585, "seek": 180444, "start": 1816.04, "end": 1818.66, "text": " It introduces something called spherical harmonics.", "tokens": [50945, 467, 31472, 746, 1219, 37300, 14750, 1167, 13, 51076], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10293165842692058, "compression_ratio": 1.6262626262626263, "no_speech_prob": 1.846162979435295e-12}, {"id": 586, "seek": 180444, "start": 1819.26, "end": 1820.6000000000001, "text": " Now, I've seen images of these online.", "tokens": [51106, 823, 11, 286, 600, 1612, 5267, 295, 613, 2950, 13, 51173], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10293165842692058, "compression_ratio": 1.6262626262626263, "no_speech_prob": 1.846162979435295e-12}, {"id": 587, "seek": 180444, "start": 1820.68, "end": 1822.3400000000001, "text": " They look like weird, colorful, bumpy balloons.", "tokens": [51177, 814, 574, 411, 3657, 11, 18506, 11, 49400, 26193, 13, 51260], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10293165842692058, "compression_ratio": 1.6262626262626263, "no_speech_prob": 1.846162979435295e-12}, {"id": 588, "seek": 180444, "start": 1822.6200000000001, "end": 1823.74, "text": " What are they actually doing?", "tokens": [51274, 708, 366, 436, 767, 884, 30, 51330], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10293165842692058, "compression_ratio": 1.6262626262626263, "no_speech_prob": 1.846162979435295e-12}, {"id": 589, "seek": 180444, "start": 1823.98, "end": 1827.94, "text": " Think of spherical harmonics as the natural vibrational modes of a sphere.", "tokens": [51342, 6557, 295, 37300, 14750, 1167, 382, 264, 3303, 11599, 1478, 14068, 295, 257, 16687, 13, 51540], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10293165842692058, "compression_ratio": 1.6262626262626263, "no_speech_prob": 1.846162979435295e-12}, {"id": 590, "seek": 180444, "start": 1828.0800000000002, "end": 1830.3400000000001, "text": " They are the mathematical equivalent of ringing a bell.", "tokens": [51547, 814, 366, 264, 18894, 10344, 295, 18423, 257, 4549, 13, 51660], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10293165842692058, "compression_ratio": 1.6262626262626263, "no_speech_prob": 1.846162979435295e-12}, {"id": 591, "seek": 183034, "start": 1830.34, "end": 1834.1599999999999, "text": " When you strike a bell, the metal doesn't just vibrate randomly.", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 291, 9302, 257, 4549, 11, 264, 5760, 1177, 380, 445, 11666, 4404, 16979, 13, 50556], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11136213938395183, "compression_ratio": 1.7304964539007093, "no_speech_prob": 2.108805968389915e-12}, {"id": 592, "seek": 183034, "start": 1834.5, "end": 1837.4599999999998, "text": " It vibrates in specific, recognizable, stable patterns.", "tokens": [50573, 467, 11599, 1024, 294, 2685, 11, 40757, 11, 8351, 8294, 13, 50721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11136213938395183, "compression_ratio": 1.7304964539007093, "no_speech_prob": 2.108805968389915e-12}, {"id": 593, "seek": 183034, "start": 1837.9399999999998, "end": 1840.1799999999998, "text": " Some parts of the metal move out while others move in.", "tokens": [50745, 2188, 3166, 295, 264, 5760, 1286, 484, 1339, 2357, 1286, 294, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11136213938395183, "compression_ratio": 1.7304964539007093, "no_speech_prob": 2.108805968389915e-12}, {"id": 594, "seek": 183034, "start": 1840.6799999999998, "end": 1845.82, "text": " The sphere does the exact same thing mathematically when energy or information moves across its surface.", "tokens": [50882, 440, 16687, 775, 264, 1900, 912, 551, 44003, 562, 2281, 420, 1589, 6067, 2108, 1080, 3753, 13, 51139], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11136213938395183, "compression_ratio": 1.7304964539007093, "no_speech_prob": 2.108805968389915e-12}, {"id": 595, "seek": 183034, "start": 1846.1799999999998, "end": 1851.02, "text": " Infliction assigns a specific index to these patterns, the letter L index.", "tokens": [51157, 682, 3423, 4105, 6269, 82, 257, 2685, 8186, 281, 613, 8294, 11, 264, 5063, 441, 8186, 13, 51399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11136213938395183, "compression_ratio": 1.7304964539007093, "no_speech_prob": 2.108805968389915e-12}, {"id": 596, "seek": 183034, "start": 1851.3799999999999, "end": 1852.52, "text": " How does that index work?", "tokens": [51417, 1012, 775, 300, 8186, 589, 30, 51474], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11136213938395183, "compression_ratio": 1.7304964539007093, "no_speech_prob": 2.108805968389915e-12}, {"id": 597, "seek": 183034, "start": 1852.72, "end": 1855.1599999999999, "text": " The L index measures the complexity of the vibration.", "tokens": [51484, 440, 441, 8186, 8000, 264, 14024, 295, 264, 20006, 13, 51606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11136213938395183, "compression_ratio": 1.7304964539007093, "no_speech_prob": 2.108805968389915e-12}, {"id": 598, "seek": 183034, "start": 1855.58, "end": 1858.22, "text": " An L of zero means the sphere is completely uniform.", "tokens": [51627, 1107, 441, 295, 4018, 1355, 264, 16687, 307, 2584, 9452, 13, 51759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11136213938395183, "compression_ratio": 1.7304964539007093, "no_speech_prob": 2.108805968389915e-12}, {"id": 599, "seek": 185822, "start": 1858.22, "end": 1861.98, "text": " It is expanding and contracting perfectly smoothly all at once.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 14702, 293, 36095, 6239, 19565, 439, 412, 1564, 13, 50553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13753030901757357, "compression_ratio": 1.570921985815603, "no_speech_prob": 2.068343976993625e-12}, {"id": 600, "seek": 185822, "start": 1862.14, "end": 1863.76, "text": " No angular variation at all.", "tokens": [50561, 883, 24413, 12990, 412, 439, 13, 50642], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13753030901757357, "compression_ratio": 1.570921985815603, "no_speech_prob": 2.068343976993625e-12}, {"id": 601, "seek": 185822, "start": 1864.4, "end": 1872.64, "text": " As the L index increases, 1, 2, 10, 50, you get progressively finer, more complex, patchier structures on the surface of the sphere.", "tokens": [50674, 1018, 264, 441, 8186, 8637, 11, 502, 11, 568, 11, 1266, 11, 2625, 11, 291, 483, 46667, 39130, 11, 544, 3997, 11, 9972, 811, 9227, 322, 264, 3753, 295, 264, 16687, 13, 51086], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13753030901757357, "compression_ratio": 1.570921985815603, "no_speech_prob": 2.068343976993625e-12}, {"id": 602, "seek": 185822, "start": 1872.74, "end": 1873.6200000000001, "text": " The bumps get smaller.", "tokens": [51091, 440, 27719, 483, 4356, 13, 51135], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13753030901757357, "compression_ratio": 1.570921985815603, "no_speech_prob": 2.068343976993625e-12}, {"id": 603, "seek": 185822, "start": 1873.84, "end": 1877.48, "text": " Yes, the bumps on those colorful balloons get smaller and more numerous.", "tokens": [51146, 1079, 11, 264, 27719, 322, 729, 18506, 26193, 483, 4356, 293, 544, 12546, 13, 51328], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13753030901757357, "compression_ratio": 1.570921985815603, "no_speech_prob": 2.068343976993625e-12}, {"id": 604, "seek": 185822, "start": 1877.96, "end": 1883.92, "text": " It's the difference between a gentle rolling wave across an ocean and a million tiny choppy chaotic ripples in a bathtub.", "tokens": [51352, 467, 311, 264, 2649, 1296, 257, 6424, 9439, 5772, 2108, 364, 7810, 293, 257, 2459, 5870, 7931, 8200, 27013, 367, 37674, 294, 257, 42901, 13, 51650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13753030901757357, "compression_ratio": 1.570921985815603, "no_speech_prob": 2.068343976993625e-12}, {"id": 605, "seek": 188392, "start": 1883.92, "end": 1889.3000000000002, "text": " And the text points out that the Laplacian operator absolutely hates high index structures.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 2487, 2793, 484, 300, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 12973, 3122, 23000, 1090, 8186, 9227, 13, 50634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09883434708054001, "compression_ratio": 1.5263157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 2.084562123610967e-12}, {"id": 606, "seek": 188392, "start": 1889.76, "end": 1891.92, "text": " It penalizes them severely in the equations.", "tokens": [50657, 467, 13661, 5660, 552, 26271, 294, 264, 11787, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09883434708054001, "compression_ratio": 1.5263157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 2.084562123610967e-12}, {"id": 607, "seek": 188392, "start": 1892.3600000000001, "end": 1900.5600000000002, "text": " It is mathematically designed to crack down on fine, complex, patchy disagreements much, much harder than it cracks down on broad, smooth disagreements.", "tokens": [50787, 467, 307, 44003, 4761, 281, 6226, 760, 322, 2489, 11, 3997, 11, 9972, 88, 23926, 6400, 709, 11, 709, 6081, 813, 309, 21770, 760, 322, 4152, 11, 5508, 23926, 6400, 13, 51197], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09883434708054001, "compression_ratio": 1.5263157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 2.084562123610967e-12}, {"id": 608, "seek": 188392, "start": 1900.8400000000001, "end": 1902.0, "text": " That is the crucial takeaway.", "tokens": [51211, 663, 307, 264, 11462, 30681, 13, 51269], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09883434708054001, "compression_ratio": 1.5263157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 2.084562123610967e-12}, {"id": 609, "seek": 190200, "start": 1902.0, "end": 1909.38, "text": " The Laplacian's math intrinsically treats fine angular structure choppiness as highly costly in terms of energy.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 311, 5221, 28621, 984, 19566, 2489, 24413, 3877, 7931, 79, 1324, 382, 5405, 28328, 294, 2115, 295, 2281, 13, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11223531538440336, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 2.158366801258138e-12}, {"id": 610, "seek": 190200, "start": 1910.16, "end": 1914.02, "text": " Infliction shows how this applies to those RSVP fields we clarified earlier.", "tokens": [50773, 682, 3423, 4105, 3110, 577, 341, 13165, 281, 729, 25855, 53, 47, 7909, 321, 47605, 3071, 13, 50966], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11223531538440336, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 2.158366801258138e-12}, {"id": 611, "seek": 190200, "start": 1914.44, "end": 1920.06, "text": " Let's look at the vector field, which generally represents transport or physical flow like wind or water currents.", "tokens": [50987, 961, 311, 574, 412, 264, 8062, 2519, 11, 597, 5101, 8855, 5495, 420, 4001, 3095, 411, 2468, 420, 1281, 30110, 13, 51268], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11223531538440336, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 2.158366801258138e-12}, {"id": 612, "seek": 190200, "start": 1920.2, "end": 1924.24, "text": " Okay, so how does the Laplacian's hatred of patchiness affect a flowing vector field?", "tokens": [51275, 1033, 11, 370, 577, 775, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 311, 21890, 295, 9972, 1324, 3345, 257, 13974, 8062, 2519, 30, 51477], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11223531538440336, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 2.158366801258138e-12}, {"id": 613, "seek": 192424, "start": 1924.24, "end": 1928.92, "text": " In physics, there is a measurement called the curl or vorticity of a vector field.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 10649, 11, 456, 307, 257, 13160, 1219, 264, 22591, 420, 371, 477, 44198, 295, 257, 8062, 2519, 13, 50599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11774154076209435, "compression_ratio": 1.6935483870967742, "no_speech_prob": 2.100924469117249e-12}, {"id": 614, "seek": 192424, "start": 1929.38, "end": 1934.18, "text": " It measures how much the flow rotates or squirrels locally like tiny whirlpools in a river.", "tokens": [50622, 467, 8000, 577, 709, 264, 3095, 42133, 420, 28565, 82, 16143, 411, 5870, 35706, 17374, 82, 294, 257, 6810, 13, 50862], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11774154076209435, "compression_ratio": 1.6935483870967742, "no_speech_prob": 2.100924469117249e-12}, {"id": 615, "seek": 192424, "start": 1934.8, "end": 1938.2, "text": " Fliction points out that vorticity is an intrinsically angular penalty.", "tokens": [50893, 3235, 4105, 2793, 484, 300, 371, 477, 44198, 307, 364, 28621, 984, 24413, 16263, 13, 51063], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11774154076209435, "compression_ratio": 1.6935483870967742, "no_speech_prob": 2.100924469117249e-12}, {"id": 616, "seek": 192424, "start": 1938.8, "end": 1941.32, "text": " It is a measurement of circulation strictly within a shell.", "tokens": [51093, 467, 307, 257, 13160, 295, 23168, 20792, 1951, 257, 8720, 13, 51219], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11774154076209435, "compression_ratio": 1.6935483870967742, "no_speech_prob": 2.100924469117249e-12}, {"id": 617, "seek": 192424, "start": 1941.98, "end": 1949.5, "text": " Because whirlpools are essentially highly localized, patchy, high-l index phenomena, the Laplacian penalizes this heavy swirling.", "tokens": [51252, 1436, 35706, 17374, 82, 366, 4476, 5405, 44574, 11, 9972, 88, 11, 1090, 12, 75, 8186, 22004, 11, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 13661, 5660, 341, 4676, 30310, 278, 13, 51628], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11774154076209435, "compression_ratio": 1.6935483870967742, "no_speech_prob": 2.100924469117249e-12}, {"id": 618, "seek": 192424, "start": 1949.86, "end": 1952.7, "text": " The math demands that the field try to unswirl itself.", "tokens": [51646, 440, 5221, 15107, 300, 264, 2519, 853, 281, 2693, 86, 1648, 2564, 13, 51788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11774154076209435, "compression_ratio": 1.6935483870967742, "no_speech_prob": 2.100924469117249e-12}, {"id": 619, "seek": 192424, "start": 1952.7, "end": 1954.16, "text": " And what about the entropy field?", "tokens": [51788, 400, 437, 466, 264, 30867, 2519, 30, 51861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11774154076209435, "compression_ratio": 1.6935483870967742, "no_speech_prob": 2.100924469117249e-12}, {"id": 620, "seek": 195424, "start": 1954.58, "end": 1957.34, "text": " Entropy is the universe's tendency toward chaos and disorder.", "tokens": [50382, 3951, 27514, 307, 264, 6445, 311, 18187, 7361, 14158, 293, 13399, 13, 50520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18770114898681642, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 2.0201271211384153e-12}, {"id": 621, "seek": 195424, "start": 1957.8, "end": 1960.32, "text": " Flick, she notes something deeply counterintuitive here.", "tokens": [50543, 3235, 618, 11, 750, 5570, 746, 8760, 5682, 686, 48314, 510, 13, 50669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18770114898681642, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 2.0201271211384153e-12}, {"id": 622, "seek": 195424, "start": 1961.06, "end": 1968.32, "text": " Local entropy can decrease, meaning order can increase in one specific spot, in two distinct genometric ways.", "tokens": [50706, 22755, 30867, 393, 11514, 11, 3620, 1668, 393, 3488, 294, 472, 2685, 4008, 11, 294, 732, 10644, 1049, 29470, 2098, 13, 51069], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18770114898681642, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 2.0201271211384153e-12}, {"id": 623, "seek": 195424, "start": 1968.74, "end": 1971.56, "text": " It can move across levels, which is a radial change.", "tokens": [51090, 467, 393, 1286, 2108, 4358, 11, 597, 307, 257, 38783, 1319, 13, 51231], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18770114898681642, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 2.0201271211384153e-12}, {"id": 624, "seek": 195424, "start": 1971.94, "end": 1977.7, "text": " Think of a mixture of oil and water spontaneously separating into two flat layers based on density.", "tokens": [51250, 6557, 295, 257, 9925, 295, 3184, 293, 1281, 47632, 29279, 666, 732, 4962, 7914, 2361, 322, 10305, 13, 51538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18770114898681642, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 2.0201271211384153e-12}, {"id": 625, "seek": 195424, "start": 1977.92, "end": 1979.44, "text": " That is a radial organization.", "tokens": [51549, 663, 307, 257, 38783, 4475, 13, 51625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18770114898681642, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 2.0201271211384153e-12}, {"id": 626, "seek": 195424, "start": 1979.44, "end": 1980.02, "text": " Got it.", "tokens": [51625, 5803, 309, 13, 51654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18770114898681642, "compression_ratio": 1.5909090909090908, "no_speech_prob": 2.0201271211384153e-12}, {"id": 627, "seek": 198002, "start": 1980.02, "end": 1985.48, "text": " Or it can form patchy, ordered patterns on a single level, like ice crystals forming on a windowpane.", "tokens": [50365, 1610, 309, 393, 1254, 9972, 88, 11, 8866, 8294, 322, 257, 2167, 1496, 11, 411, 4435, 23772, 15745, 322, 257, 4910, 79, 1929, 13, 50638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15326247007950491, "compression_ratio": 1.489010989010989, "no_speech_prob": 2.266865731584411e-12}, {"id": 628, "seek": 198002, "start": 1985.94, "end": 1987.68, "text": " That is an angular change.", "tokens": [50661, 663, 307, 364, 24413, 1319, 13, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15326247007950491, "compression_ratio": 1.489010989010989, "no_speech_prob": 2.266865731584411e-12}, {"id": 629, "seek": 198002, "start": 1988.1399999999999, "end": 1995.22, "text": " The Laplacian can detect exactly which of those two mechanisms is trying to reduce entropy, and it penalizes the patchy, angular one severely.", "tokens": [50771, 440, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 393, 5531, 2293, 597, 295, 729, 732, 15902, 307, 1382, 281, 5407, 30867, 11, 293, 309, 13661, 5660, 264, 9972, 88, 11, 24413, 472, 26271, 13, 51125], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15326247007950491, "compression_ratio": 1.489010989010989, "no_speech_prob": 2.266865731584411e-12}, {"id": 630, "seek": 199522, "start": 1995.22, "end": 2000.58, "text": " It forces the system to prefer radial layering over angular patchiness whenever possible.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 5874, 264, 1185, 281, 4382, 38783, 40754, 670, 24413, 9972, 1324, 5699, 1944, 13, 50633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10930183198716906, "compression_ratio": 1.4891304347826086, "no_speech_prob": 1.9966023192402593e-12}, {"id": 631, "seek": 199522, "start": 2001.0, "end": 2010.54, "text": " So if the Laplacian is this hypervigilant detector spotting this local mismatch, detecting the choppiness and penalizing it, what happens when nature tries to actually fix the problem?", "tokens": [50654, 407, 498, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 307, 341, 9848, 85, 328, 25824, 25712, 4008, 783, 341, 2654, 23220, 852, 11, 40237, 264, 7931, 79, 1324, 293, 13661, 3319, 309, 11, 437, 2314, 562, 3687, 9898, 281, 767, 3191, 264, 1154, 30, 51131], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10930183198716906, "compression_ratio": 1.4891304347826086, "no_speech_prob": 1.9966023192402593e-12}, {"id": 632, "seek": 201054, "start": 2010.54, "end": 2017.54, "text": " That brings us to Flick's concept of the geometry of repair, because repair in this framework isn't some magical healing force.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 5607, 505, 281, 3235, 618, 311, 3410, 295, 264, 18426, 295, 10535, 11, 570, 10535, 294, 341, 8388, 1943, 380, 512, 12066, 9745, 3464, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15009676615397136, "compression_ratio": 1.6701030927835052, "no_speech_prob": 1.74855128206447e-12}, {"id": 633, "seek": 201054, "start": 2017.6599999999999, "end": 2020.8799999999999, "text": " It is simply geometric gradient descent on local mismatch.", "tokens": [50721, 467, 307, 2935, 33246, 16235, 23475, 322, 2654, 23220, 852, 13, 50882], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15009676615397136, "compression_ratio": 1.6701030927835052, "no_speech_prob": 1.74855128206447e-12}, {"id": 634, "seek": 201054, "start": 2021.18, "end": 2021.92, "text": " Gradient descent.", "tokens": [50897, 16710, 1196, 23475, 13, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15009676615397136, "compression_ratio": 1.6701030927835052, "no_speech_prob": 1.74855128206447e-12}, {"id": 635, "seek": 201054, "start": 2022.42, "end": 2025.12, "text": " That's a term I hear all the time in machine learning and AI.", "tokens": [50959, 663, 311, 257, 1433, 286, 1568, 439, 264, 565, 294, 3479, 2539, 293, 7318, 13, 51094], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15009676615397136, "compression_ratio": 1.6701030927835052, "no_speech_prob": 1.74855128206447e-12}, {"id": 636, "seek": 201054, "start": 2025.84, "end": 2030.04, "text": " But what does it mean physically, like a ball rolling down a hill to find the lowest point of energy?", "tokens": [51130, 583, 437, 775, 309, 914, 9762, 11, 411, 257, 2594, 9439, 760, 257, 10997, 281, 915, 264, 12437, 935, 295, 2281, 30, 51340], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15009676615397136, "compression_ratio": 1.6701030927835052, "no_speech_prob": 1.74855128206447e-12}, {"id": 637, "seek": 201054, "start": 2030.2, "end": 2031.0, "text": " Exactly that.", "tokens": [51348, 7587, 300, 13, 51388], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15009676615397136, "compression_ratio": 1.6701030927835052, "no_speech_prob": 1.74855128206447e-12}, {"id": 638, "seek": 201054, "start": 2031.18, "end": 2033.24, "text": " Imagine a landscape of hills and valleys.", "tokens": [51397, 11739, 257, 9661, 295, 21379, 293, 45614, 13, 51500], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15009676615397136, "compression_ratio": 1.6701030927835052, "no_speech_prob": 1.74855128206447e-12}, {"id": 639, "seek": 201054, "start": 2033.6399999999999, "end": 2037.46, "text": " The hills represent high mismatch, high tension, high energy.", "tokens": [51520, 440, 21379, 2906, 1090, 23220, 852, 11, 1090, 8980, 11, 1090, 2281, 13, 51711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15009676615397136, "compression_ratio": 1.6701030927835052, "no_speech_prob": 1.74855128206447e-12}, {"id": 640, "seek": 203746, "start": 2037.46, "end": 2040.64, "text": " The valleys represent smoothness and agreement.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 45614, 2906, 5508, 1287, 293, 8106, 13, 50524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13845381976889193, "compression_ratio": 1.5975609756097562, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884339641542787e-12}, {"id": 641, "seek": 203746, "start": 2041.38, "end": 2051.26, "text": " When the Laplacian detects a high amount of mismatch, a peak on that landscape, the natural physical dynamics of the system will try to reduce it by rolling down the steepest slope.", "tokens": [50561, 1133, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 5531, 82, 257, 1090, 2372, 295, 23220, 852, 11, 257, 10651, 322, 300, 9661, 11, 264, 3303, 4001, 15679, 295, 264, 1185, 486, 853, 281, 5407, 309, 538, 9439, 760, 264, 16841, 377, 13525, 13, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13845381976889193, "compression_ratio": 1.5975609756097562, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884339641542787e-12}, {"id": 642, "seek": 203746, "start": 2051.7, "end": 2054.64, "text": " It wants to reach a smoother, lower energy state.", "tokens": [51077, 467, 2738, 281, 2524, 257, 28640, 11, 3126, 2281, 1785, 13, 51224], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13845381976889193, "compression_ratio": 1.5975609756097562, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884339641542787e-12}, {"id": 643, "seek": 203746, "start": 2055.26, "end": 2060.34, "text": " And to do this, Flick's introduces a specific mechanism from the RSVP theory called the lamphrodine.", "tokens": [51255, 400, 281, 360, 341, 11, 3235, 618, 311, 31472, 257, 2685, 7513, 490, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 5261, 1219, 264, 24688, 950, 11452, 533, 13, 51509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13845381976889193, "compression_ratio": 1.5975609756097562, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884339641542787e-12}, {"id": 644, "seek": 203746, "start": 2060.7400000000002, "end": 2061.26, "text": " Lamphrodine.", "tokens": [51529, 18825, 950, 11452, 533, 13, 51555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13845381976889193, "compression_ratio": 1.5975609756097562, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884339641542787e-12}, {"id": 645, "seek": 203746, "start": 2061.46, "end": 2064.2200000000003, "text": " I have to admit, it sounds like an over-the-counter allergy medication.", "tokens": [51565, 286, 362, 281, 9796, 11, 309, 3263, 411, 364, 670, 12, 3322, 12, 66, 47489, 41505, 13851, 13, 51703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13845381976889193, "compression_ratio": 1.5975609756097562, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884339641542787e-12}, {"id": 646, "seek": 203746, "start": 2064.2200000000003, "end": 2067.2400000000002, "text": " Take two lamphrodine and your sinuses will clear right up.", "tokens": [51703, 3664, 732, 24688, 950, 11452, 533, 293, 428, 3343, 8355, 486, 1850, 558, 493, 13, 51854], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13845381976889193, "compression_ratio": 1.5975609756097562, "no_speech_prob": 1.3884339641542787e-12}, {"id": 647, "seek": 206724, "start": 2067.24, "end": 2069.08, "text": " It does have a pharmaceutical ring to it.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 775, 362, 257, 27130, 4875, 281, 309, 13, 50457], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12634233258805186, "compression_ratio": 1.6352941176470588, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839965194191063e-12}, {"id": 648, "seek": 206724, "start": 2069.2, "end": 2075.8599999999997, "text": " But in Flick's text, the lamphrodine is the exact physical manifestation of the Laplacian operator acting as a repair pressure.", "tokens": [50463, 583, 294, 3235, 618, 311, 2487, 11, 264, 24688, 950, 11452, 533, 307, 264, 1900, 4001, 29550, 295, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 12973, 6577, 382, 257, 10535, 3321, 13, 50796], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12634233258805186, "compression_ratio": 1.6352941176470588, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839965194191063e-12}, {"id": 649, "seek": 206724, "start": 2076.56, "end": 2079.9199999999996, "text": " The lamphrodine is the active force that smooths out the entropy fields.", "tokens": [50831, 440, 24688, 950, 11452, 533, 307, 264, 4967, 3464, 300, 5508, 82, 484, 264, 30867, 7909, 13, 50999], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12634233258805186, "compression_ratio": 1.6352941176470588, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839965194191063e-12}, {"id": 650, "seek": 206724, "start": 2079.9199999999996, "end": 2090.04, "text": " It looks at the patchy-heil index disagreements, the chaotic mosh pits, and actively pushes the system to relax, diffuse, and smooth them out into a gentle, uniform baseline.", "tokens": [50999, 467, 1542, 412, 264, 9972, 88, 12, 675, 388, 8186, 23926, 6400, 11, 264, 27013, 275, 3019, 40312, 11, 293, 13022, 21020, 264, 1185, 281, 5789, 11, 42165, 11, 293, 5508, 552, 484, 666, 257, 6424, 11, 9452, 20518, 13, 51505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12634233258805186, "compression_ratio": 1.6352941176470588, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839965194191063e-12}, {"id": 651, "seek": 209004, "start": 2090.04, "end": 2092.72, "text": " But wait, this is where the text gets really philosophical.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 1699, 11, 341, 307, 689, 264, 2487, 2170, 534, 25066, 13, 50499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14036481857299804, "compression_ratio": 1.5949367088607596, "no_speech_prob": 1.681575560220916e-12}, {"id": 652, "seek": 209004, "start": 2093.82, "end": 2096.44, "text": " Repair isn't an unqualified good in this book.", "tokens": [50554, 3696, 1246, 1943, 380, 364, 517, 46094, 665, 294, 341, 1446, 13, 50685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14036481857299804, "compression_ratio": 1.5949367088607596, "no_speech_prob": 1.681575560220916e-12}, {"id": 653, "seek": 209004, "start": 2096.98, "end": 2101.04, "text": " The text sets up this really elegant, almost tragic duality.", "tokens": [50712, 440, 2487, 6352, 493, 341, 534, 21117, 11, 1920, 20385, 11848, 507, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14036481857299804, "compression_ratio": 1.5949367088607596, "no_speech_prob": 1.681575560220916e-12}, {"id": 654, "seek": 209004, "start": 2101.3, "end": 2104.96, "text": " You have the lamphrodine, which relaxes structure and smooths things out.", "tokens": [50928, 509, 362, 264, 24688, 950, 11452, 533, 11, 597, 5789, 279, 3877, 293, 5508, 82, 721, 484, 13, 51111], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14036481857299804, "compression_ratio": 1.5949367088607596, "no_speech_prob": 1.681575560220916e-12}, {"id": 655, "seek": 209004, "start": 2105.12, "end": 2109.64, "text": " But you also have its counterpart, the lamphron, which stabilizes structure.", "tokens": [51119, 583, 291, 611, 362, 1080, 22335, 11, 264, 24688, 950, 2044, 11, 597, 11652, 5660, 3877, 13, 51345], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14036481857299804, "compression_ratio": 1.5949367088607596, "no_speech_prob": 1.681575560220916e-12}, {"id": 656, "seek": 209004, "start": 2109.7799999999997, "end": 2112.2599999999998, "text": " This tension is vital for existence itself.", "tokens": [51352, 639, 8980, 307, 11707, 337, 9123, 2564, 13, 51476], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14036481857299804, "compression_ratio": 1.5949367088607596, "no_speech_prob": 1.681575560220916e-12}, {"id": 657, "seek": 209004, "start": 2112.48, "end": 2113.04, "text": " Think about it.", "tokens": [51487, 6557, 466, 309, 13, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14036481857299804, "compression_ratio": 1.5949367088607596, "no_speech_prob": 1.681575560220916e-12}, {"id": 658, "seek": 211304, "start": 2113.04, "end": 2117.6, "text": " If the lamphrodine, the repair pressure, went completely unchecked, what would happen?", "tokens": [50365, 759, 264, 24688, 950, 11452, 533, 11, 264, 10535, 3321, 11, 1437, 2584, 46672, 292, 11, 437, 576, 1051, 30, 50593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12974001467227936, "compression_ratio": 1.1919191919191918, "no_speech_prob": 2.08425898068354e-12}, {"id": 659, "seek": 211304, "start": 2117.62, "end": 2118.66, "text": " It would just erase everything.", "tokens": [50594, 467, 576, 445, 23525, 1203, 13, 50646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12974001467227936, "compression_ratio": 1.1919191919191918, "no_speech_prob": 2.08425898068354e-12}, {"id": 660, "seek": 211866, "start": 2118.66, "end": 2123.72, "text": " It would smooth out every single gradient, every single difference in temperature, every boundary, everywhere.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 576, 5508, 484, 633, 2167, 16235, 11, 633, 2167, 2649, 294, 4292, 11, 633, 12866, 11, 5315, 13, 50618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14568758010864258, "compression_ratio": 1.6055045871559632, "no_speech_prob": 2.07643949777514e-12}, {"id": 661, "seek": 211866, "start": 2124.2999999999997, "end": 2126.3199999999997, "text": " The system would become a featureless void.", "tokens": [50647, 440, 1185, 576, 1813, 257, 4111, 1832, 22009, 13, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14568758010864258, "compression_ratio": 1.6055045871559632, "no_speech_prob": 2.07643949777514e-12}, {"id": 662, "seek": 211866, "start": 2126.8199999999997, "end": 2127.7799999999997, "text": " Total uniformity.", "tokens": [50773, 23170, 9452, 507, 13, 50821], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14568758010864258, "compression_ratio": 1.6055045871559632, "no_speech_prob": 2.07643949777514e-12}, {"id": 663, "seek": 211866, "start": 2128.2, "end": 2128.8799999999997, "text": " Heat death.", "tokens": [50842, 27359, 2966, 13, 50876], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14568758010864258, "compression_ratio": 1.6055045871559632, "no_speech_prob": 2.07643949777514e-12}, {"id": 664, "seek": 211866, "start": 2129.2799999999997, "end": 2137.22, "text": " You need the lamphron to artificially stabilize some of that structure to lock some of the mismatch into place so that the system doesn't just melt into nothingness.", "tokens": [50896, 509, 643, 264, 24688, 950, 2044, 281, 39905, 2270, 31870, 512, 295, 300, 3877, 281, 4017, 512, 295, 264, 23220, 852, 666, 1081, 370, 300, 264, 1185, 1177, 380, 445, 10083, 666, 1825, 1287, 13, 51293], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14568758010864258, "compression_ratio": 1.6055045871559632, "no_speech_prob": 2.07643949777514e-12}, {"id": 665, "seek": 213722, "start": 2137.22, "end": 2150.2, "text": " The constant agonizing tension between the lamphron holding things together and the lamphrodine trying to melt them down is what allows complex, coherent configurations like stars, planets, and living cells to exist at all.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 5754, 623, 266, 3319, 8980, 1296, 264, 24688, 950, 2044, 5061, 721, 1214, 293, 264, 24688, 950, 11452, 533, 1382, 281, 10083, 552, 760, 307, 437, 4045, 3997, 11, 36239, 31493, 411, 6105, 11, 15126, 11, 293, 2647, 5438, 281, 2514, 412, 439, 13, 51014], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08929092795760543, "compression_ratio": 1.6573426573426573, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815713318324432e-12}, {"id": 666, "seek": 213722, "start": 2150.3199999999997, "end": 2152.72, "text": " So repair is a delicate balancing act.", "tokens": [51020, 407, 10535, 307, 257, 21417, 22495, 605, 13, 51140], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08929092795760543, "compression_ratio": 1.6573426573426573, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815713318324432e-12}, {"id": 667, "seek": 213722, "start": 2152.8599999999997, "end": 2154.54, "text": " You need some tension to exist.", "tokens": [51147, 509, 643, 512, 8980, 281, 2514, 13, 51231], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08929092795760543, "compression_ratio": 1.6573426573426573, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815713318324432e-12}, {"id": 668, "seek": 213722, "start": 2155.04, "end": 2159.3599999999997, "text": " But here is the part of the repair chapter that really stuck with me, and it feels so profound.", "tokens": [51256, 583, 510, 307, 264, 644, 295, 264, 10535, 7187, 300, 534, 5541, 365, 385, 11, 293, 309, 3417, 370, 14382, 13, 51472], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08929092795760543, "compression_ratio": 1.6573426573426573, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815713318324432e-12}, {"id": 669, "seek": 213722, "start": 2160.3199999999997, "end": 2164.7599999999998, "text": " Fliction gives a massive mathematical warning about the geometry of a closed shell.", "tokens": [51520, 3235, 4105, 2709, 257, 5994, 18894, 9164, 466, 264, 18426, 295, 257, 5395, 8720, 13, 51742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08929092795760543, "compression_ratio": 1.6573426573426573, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815713318324432e-12}, {"id": 670, "seek": 216476, "start": 2164.76, "end": 2171.5400000000004, "text": " They say that repair processes can redistribute mismatch, but they cannot always eliminate it.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 584, 300, 10535, 7555, 393, 36198, 2024, 1169, 23220, 852, 11, 457, 436, 2644, 1009, 13819, 309, 13, 50704], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11690966564676036, "compression_ratio": 1.6631578947368422, "no_speech_prob": 1.701393908572213e-12}, {"id": 671, "seek": 216476, "start": 2172.2000000000003, "end": 2178.0400000000004, "text": " Because the shell is a closed loop, there is a global constraint on how much smoothing can actually happen.", "tokens": [50737, 1436, 264, 8720, 307, 257, 5395, 6367, 11, 456, 307, 257, 4338, 25534, 322, 577, 709, 899, 6259, 571, 393, 767, 1051, 13, 51029], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11690966564676036, "compression_ratio": 1.6631578947368422, "no_speech_prob": 1.701393908572213e-12}, {"id": 672, "seek": 216476, "start": 2178.1400000000003, "end": 2178.46, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51034, 1079, 13, 51050], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11690966564676036, "compression_ratio": 1.6631578947368422, "no_speech_prob": 1.701393908572213e-12}, {"id": 673, "seek": 216476, "start": 2178.9, "end": 2180.94, "text": " The topology of a sphere guarantees this.", "tokens": [51072, 440, 1192, 1793, 295, 257, 16687, 32567, 341, 13, 51174], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11690966564676036, "compression_ratio": 1.6631578947368422, "no_speech_prob": 1.701393908572213e-12}, {"id": 674, "seek": 216476, "start": 2181.28, "end": 2187.5400000000004, "text": " The math explicitly proves that you cannot always drive the mismatch to zero everywhere at once on a continuous spherical shell.", "tokens": [51191, 440, 5221, 20803, 25019, 300, 291, 2644, 1009, 3332, 264, 23220, 852, 281, 4018, 5315, 412, 1564, 322, 257, 10957, 37300, 8720, 13, 51504], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11690966564676036, "compression_ratio": 1.6631578947368422, "no_speech_prob": 1.701393908572213e-12}, {"id": 675, "seek": 216476, "start": 2187.88, "end": 2189.5400000000004, "text": " The shape itself won't allow it.", "tokens": [51521, 440, 3909, 2564, 1582, 380, 2089, 309, 13, 51604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11690966564676036, "compression_ratio": 1.6631578947368422, "no_speech_prob": 1.701393908572213e-12}, {"id": 676, "seek": 216476, "start": 2189.76, "end": 2192.0400000000004, "text": " I was trying to visualize this, and I came up with an analogy.", "tokens": [51615, 286, 390, 1382, 281, 23273, 341, 11, 293, 286, 1361, 493, 365, 364, 21663, 13, 51729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11690966564676036, "compression_ratio": 1.6631578947368422, "no_speech_prob": 1.701393908572213e-12}, {"id": 677, "seek": 219204, "start": 2192.04, "end": 2196.7799999999997, "text": " It's like trying to perfectly flatten a piece of crumpled spherical aluminum foil.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 411, 1382, 281, 6239, 24183, 257, 2522, 295, 941, 449, 15551, 37300, 15656, 22444, 13, 50602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14094782951182888, "compression_ratio": 1.7467532467532467, "no_speech_prob": 1.410517644524767e-12}, {"id": 678, "seek": 219204, "start": 2196.88, "end": 2200.9, "text": " Like you take a foil ball, and you put it on a table, and you try to smooth it out flat with your hands.", "tokens": [50607, 1743, 291, 747, 257, 22444, 2594, 11, 293, 291, 829, 309, 322, 257, 3199, 11, 293, 291, 853, 281, 5508, 309, 484, 4962, 365, 428, 2377, 13, 50808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14094782951182888, "compression_ratio": 1.7467532467532467, "no_speech_prob": 1.410517644524767e-12}, {"id": 679, "seek": 219204, "start": 2201.1, "end": 2203.38, "text": " You can rub one side perfectly brilliantly smooth.", "tokens": [50818, 509, 393, 5915, 472, 1252, 6239, 8695, 42580, 5508, 13, 50932], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14094782951182888, "compression_ratio": 1.7467532467532467, "no_speech_prob": 1.410517644524767e-12}, {"id": 680, "seek": 219204, "start": 2203.66, "end": 2205.04, "text": " The repair works perfectly locally.", "tokens": [50946, 440, 10535, 1985, 6239, 16143, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14094782951182888, "compression_ratio": 1.7467532467532467, "no_speech_prob": 1.410517644524767e-12}, {"id": 681, "seek": 219204, "start": 2205.38, "end": 2205.6, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51032, 1079, 13, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14094782951182888, "compression_ratio": 1.7467532467532467, "no_speech_prob": 1.410517644524767e-12}, {"id": 682, "seek": 219204, "start": 2205.7599999999998, "end": 2206.56, "text": " Locally, you succeed.", "tokens": [51051, 12859, 379, 11, 291, 7754, 13, 51091], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14094782951182888, "compression_ratio": 1.7467532467532467, "no_speech_prob": 1.410517644524767e-12}, {"id": 683, "seek": 219204, "start": 2206.82, "end": 2209.8, "text": " But because it's a closed sphere, you just push the wrinkles somewhere else.", "tokens": [51104, 583, 570, 309, 311, 257, 5395, 16687, 11, 291, 445, 2944, 264, 34822, 4079, 1646, 13, 51253], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14094782951182888, "compression_ratio": 1.7467532467532467, "no_speech_prob": 1.410517644524767e-12}, {"id": 684, "seek": 219204, "start": 2210.2, "end": 2211.42, "text": " They bunch up on the other side.", "tokens": [51273, 814, 3840, 493, 322, 264, 661, 1252, 13, 51334], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14094782951182888, "compression_ratio": 1.7467532467532467, "no_speech_prob": 1.410517644524767e-12}, {"id": 685, "seek": 219204, "start": 2211.7599999999998, "end": 2218.14, "text": " You can never get the entire sphere completely smooth without physically ripping the foil, which breaks the boundary entirely.", "tokens": [51351, 509, 393, 1128, 483, 264, 2302, 16687, 2584, 5508, 1553, 9762, 38776, 264, 22444, 11, 597, 9857, 264, 12866, 7696, 13, 51670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14094782951182888, "compression_ratio": 1.7467532467532467, "no_speech_prob": 1.410517644524767e-12}, {"id": 686, "seek": 221814, "start": 2218.14, "end": 2224.8199999999997, "text": " The wrinkles, the mismatch to the tension, are globally conserved by the shape of the sphere itself.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 34822, 11, 264, 23220, 852, 281, 264, 8980, 11, 366, 18958, 1014, 6913, 538, 264, 3909, 295, 264, 16687, 2564, 13, 50699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15953951615553635, "compression_ratio": 1.1764705882352942, "no_speech_prob": 1.351193137412443e-12}, {"id": 687, "seek": 222482, "start": 2224.82, "end": 2227.4, "text": " A very apt, highly physical analogy.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 588, 29427, 11, 5405, 4001, 21663, 13, 50494], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12951666461534736, "compression_ratio": 1.720257234726688, "no_speech_prob": 1.3833626084924777e-12}, {"id": 688, "seek": 222482, "start": 2227.92, "end": 2232.96, "text": " The local repair dynamics, your hands smoothing the foil, the lamphrodine, are working perfectly.", "tokens": [50520, 440, 2654, 10535, 15679, 11, 428, 2377, 899, 6259, 571, 264, 22444, 11, 264, 24688, 950, 11452, 533, 11, 366, 1364, 6239, 13, 50772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12951666461534736, "compression_ratio": 1.720257234726688, "no_speech_prob": 1.3833626084924777e-12}, {"id": 689, "seek": 222482, "start": 2233.1000000000004, "end": 2234.0800000000004, "text": " They are following the rules.", "tokens": [50779, 814, 366, 3480, 264, 4474, 13, 50828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12951666461534736, "compression_ratio": 1.720257234726688, "no_speech_prob": 1.3833626084924777e-12}, {"id": 690, "seek": 222482, "start": 2234.48, "end": 2239.0, "text": " But they are operating on a global geometry that inherently prevents total success.", "tokens": [50848, 583, 436, 366, 7447, 322, 257, 4338, 18426, 300, 27993, 22367, 3217, 2245, 13, 51074], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12951666461534736, "compression_ratio": 1.720257234726688, "no_speech_prob": 1.3833626084924777e-12}, {"id": 691, "seek": 222482, "start": 2239.5, "end": 2246.34, "text": " The apparent failure to fully smooth the field across the entire object isn't because the repair process is broken or because the universe made a mistake.", "tokens": [51099, 440, 18335, 7763, 281, 4498, 5508, 264, 2519, 2108, 264, 2302, 2657, 1943, 380, 570, 264, 10535, 1399, 307, 5463, 420, 570, 264, 6445, 1027, 257, 6146, 13, 51441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12951666461534736, "compression_ratio": 1.720257234726688, "no_speech_prob": 1.3833626084924777e-12}, {"id": 692, "seek": 222482, "start": 2246.82, "end": 2251.56, "text": " It's because the field lives on a topological shell where no process could possibly do better.", "tokens": [51465, 467, 311, 570, 264, 2519, 2909, 322, 257, 1192, 4383, 8720, 689, 572, 1399, 727, 6264, 360, 1101, 13, 51702], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12951666461534736, "compression_ratio": 1.720257234726688, "no_speech_prob": 1.3833626084924777e-12}, {"id": 693, "seek": 222482, "start": 2252.04, "end": 2253.7400000000002, "text": " Tension is geographically mandatory.", "tokens": [51726, 314, 3378, 307, 25435, 984, 22173, 13, 51811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12951666461534736, "compression_ratio": 1.720257234726688, "no_speech_prob": 1.3833626084924777e-12}, {"id": 694, "seek": 225374, "start": 2253.74, "end": 2257.2599999999998, "text": " Okay, let's take a breath because this next pivot is wild.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 747, 257, 6045, 570, 341, 958, 14538, 307, 4868, 13, 50541], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12787953444889613, "compression_ratio": 1.6464285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736799884036312e-12}, {"id": 695, "seek": 225374, "start": 2257.62, "end": 2264.52, "text": " We've been talking a lot about physical fields, geometry spheres, flatworms, crumpled foil, physical topology.", "tokens": [50559, 492, 600, 668, 1417, 257, 688, 466, 4001, 7909, 11, 18426, 41225, 11, 4962, 30917, 82, 11, 941, 449, 15551, 22444, 11, 4001, 1192, 1793, 13, 50904], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12787953444889613, "compression_ratio": 1.6464285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736799884036312e-12}, {"id": 696, "seek": 225374, "start": 2264.8799999999997, "end": 2268.74, "text": " But then fliction takes this massive audacious leap.", "tokens": [50922, 583, 550, 932, 4105, 2516, 341, 5994, 2379, 22641, 19438, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12787953444889613, "compression_ratio": 1.6464285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736799884036312e-12}, {"id": 697, "seek": 225374, "start": 2268.9199999999996, "end": 2280.2599999999998, "text": " They take this exact same spherical geometry, the radial levels, the angular patchiness, the laplacian repair, and they apply it to something with absolutely no physical shape at all, computer code.", "tokens": [51124, 814, 747, 341, 1900, 912, 37300, 18426, 11, 264, 38783, 4358, 11, 264, 24413, 9972, 1324, 11, 264, 635, 564, 326, 952, 10535, 11, 293, 436, 3079, 309, 281, 746, 365, 3122, 572, 4001, 3909, 412, 439, 11, 3820, 3089, 13, 51691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12787953444889613, "compression_ratio": 1.6464285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736799884036312e-12}, {"id": 698, "seek": 225374, "start": 2280.4599999999996, "end": 2282.18, "text": " This is the introduction of sphere pop.", "tokens": [51701, 639, 307, 264, 9339, 295, 16687, 1665, 13, 51787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12787953444889613, "compression_ratio": 1.6464285714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.5736799884036312e-12}, {"id": 699, "seek": 228218, "start": 2282.18, "end": 2285.2799999999997, "text": " It is, without a doubt, the most demanding part of the text.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 11, 1553, 257, 6385, 11, 264, 881, 19960, 644, 295, 264, 2487, 13, 50520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12625581567937677, "compression_ratio": 1.6909722222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6490525308124337e-12}, {"id": 700, "seek": 228218, "start": 2285.7599999999998, "end": 2290.7599999999998, "text": " Sphere pop is a formal computational calculus dealing with irreversible commitments in programming.", "tokens": [50544, 318, 6605, 1665, 307, 257, 9860, 28270, 33400, 6260, 365, 16014, 840, 964, 26230, 294, 9410, 13, 50794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12625581567937677, "compression_ratio": 1.6909722222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6490525308124337e-12}, {"id": 701, "seek": 228218, "start": 2290.9199999999996, "end": 2291.8399999999997, "text": " It's totally abstract.", "tokens": [50802, 467, 311, 3879, 12649, 13, 50848], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12625581567937677, "compression_ratio": 1.6909722222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6490525308124337e-12}, {"id": 702, "seek": 228218, "start": 2292.14, "end": 2293.8199999999997, "text": " It exists entirely in the abstract.", "tokens": [50863, 467, 8198, 7696, 294, 264, 12649, 13, 50947], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12625581567937677, "compression_ratio": 1.6909722222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6490525308124337e-12}, {"id": 703, "seek": 228218, "start": 2294.2, "end": 2298.04, "text": " There are no physical planets, no spatial metrics, no 3D distances in a server rack.", "tokens": [50966, 821, 366, 572, 4001, 15126, 11, 572, 23598, 16367, 11, 572, 805, 35, 22182, 294, 257, 7154, 14788, 13, 51158], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12625581567937677, "compression_ratio": 1.6909722222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6490525308124337e-12}, {"id": 704, "seek": 228218, "start": 2298.3999999999996, "end": 2306.2999999999997, "text": " And yet, fliction mathematically demonstrates that the structure of irreversible computation perfectly flawlessly matches the sphere's mathematical shape.", "tokens": [51176, 400, 1939, 11, 932, 4105, 44003, 31034, 300, 264, 3877, 295, 16014, 840, 964, 24903, 6239, 13717, 12048, 10676, 264, 16687, 311, 18894, 3909, 13, 51571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12625581567937677, "compression_ratio": 1.6909722222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6490525308124337e-12}, {"id": 705, "seek": 228218, "start": 2306.64, "end": 2307.74, "text": " Computing without a planet.", "tokens": [51588, 37804, 278, 1553, 257, 5054, 13, 51643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12625581567937677, "compression_ratio": 1.6909722222222223, "no_speech_prob": 1.6490525308124337e-12}, {"id": 706, "seek": 230774, "start": 2307.74, "end": 2308.66, "text": " Yeah, I love that concept.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 11, 286, 959, 300, 3410, 13, 50411], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.27389678439578496, "compression_ratio": 1.1559633027522935, "no_speech_prob": 2.067035778652304e-12}, {"id": 707, "seek": 230774, "start": 2308.7799999999997, "end": 2311.18, "text": " So how does abstract code form a sphere?", "tokens": [50417, 407, 577, 775, 12649, 3089, 1254, 257, 16687, 30, 50537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.27389678439578496, "compression_ratio": 1.1559633027522935, "no_speech_prob": 2.067035778652304e-12}, {"id": 708, "seek": 230774, "start": 2311.3199999999997, "end": 2313.8199999999997, "text": " Let's map the vocabulary we've learned in this new domain.", "tokens": [50544, 961, 311, 4471, 264, 19864, 321, 600, 3264, 294, 341, 777, 9274, 13, 50669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.27389678439578496, "compression_ratio": 1.1559633027522935, "no_speech_prob": 2.067035778652304e-12}, {"id": 709, "seek": 231382, "start": 2313.82, "end": 2317.36, "text": " Let's recall the Friston-style synchronic screen from earlier.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 9901, 264, 1526, 47345, 12, 15014, 5451, 339, 10011, 2568, 490, 3071, 13, 50542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599697168322577, "compression_ratio": 1.566137566137566, "no_speech_prob": 2.2448193477686562e-12}, {"id": 710, "seek": 231382, "start": 2318.1800000000003, "end": 2322.2000000000003, "text": " The present tense boundary that isolates the inside from the outside, like the submarine.", "tokens": [50583, 440, 1974, 18760, 12866, 300, 7381, 1024, 264, 1854, 490, 264, 2380, 11, 411, 264, 33995, 13, 50784], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599697168322577, "compression_ratio": 1.566137566137566, "no_speech_prob": 2.2448193477686562e-12}, {"id": 711, "seek": 231382, "start": 2322.88, "end": 2327.6200000000003, "text": " In sphere pop, a block of computation operates inside what friction calls a bubble.", "tokens": [50818, 682, 16687, 1665, 11, 257, 3461, 295, 24903, 22577, 1854, 437, 17710, 5498, 257, 12212, 13, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599697168322577, "compression_ratio": 1.566137566137566, "no_speech_prob": 2.2448193477686562e-12}, {"id": 712, "seek": 231382, "start": 2328.28, "end": 2331.48, "text": " This computational bubble acts exactly as a Friston screen.", "tokens": [51088, 639, 28270, 12212, 10672, 2293, 382, 257, 1526, 47345, 2568, 13, 51248], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1599697168322577, "compression_ratio": 1.566137566137566, "no_speech_prob": 2.2448193477686562e-12}, {"id": 713, "seek": 233148, "start": 2331.48, "end": 2339.3, "text": " The outside program cannot see the variables changing inside the bubble until the bubble fully evaluates its math and pops out a final result.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2380, 1461, 2644, 536, 264, 9102, 4473, 1854, 264, 12212, 1826, 264, 12212, 4498, 6133, 1024, 1080, 5221, 293, 16795, 484, 257, 2572, 1874, 13, 50756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16881537437438965, "compression_ratio": 1.654867256637168, "no_speech_prob": 1.9659432502067142e-12}, {"id": 714, "seek": 233148, "start": 2339.6, "end": 2345.04, "text": " The boundary perfectly isolates the internal evaluation from the present tense state of the rest of the program.", "tokens": [50771, 440, 12866, 6239, 7381, 1024, 264, 6920, 13344, 490, 264, 1974, 18760, 1785, 295, 264, 1472, 295, 264, 1461, 13, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16881537437438965, "compression_ratio": 1.654867256637168, "no_speech_prob": 1.9659432502067142e-12}, {"id": 715, "seek": 233148, "start": 2345.5, "end": 2348.06, "text": " Okay, so the computational bubble is our boundary shell.", "tokens": [51066, 1033, 11, 370, 264, 28270, 12212, 307, 527, 12866, 8720, 13, 51194], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16881537437438965, "compression_ratio": 1.654867256637168, "no_speech_prob": 1.9659432502067142e-12}, {"id": 716, "seek": 233148, "start": 2348.86, "end": 2349.92, "text": " What about our coordinates?", "tokens": [51234, 708, 466, 527, 21056, 30, 51287], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16881537437438965, "compression_ratio": 1.654867256637168, "no_speech_prob": 1.9659432502067142e-12}, {"id": 717, "seek": 233148, "start": 2350.62, "end": 2352.36, "text": " Our radial and angular movements?", "tokens": [51322, 2621, 38783, 293, 24413, 9981, 30, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16881537437438965, "compression_ratio": 1.654867256637168, "no_speech_prob": 1.9659432502067142e-12}, {"id": 718, "seek": 235236, "start": 2352.36, "end": 2355.1400000000003, "text": " This is where the mapping becomes incredibly elegant.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 689, 264, 18350, 3643, 6252, 21117, 13, 50504], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11852154731750489, "compression_ratio": 1.6837606837606838, "no_speech_prob": 2.0439208051753477e-12}, {"id": 719, "seek": 235236, "start": 2356.04, "end": 2365.54, "text": " In sphere pop, making an irreversible computational commitment making, a choice that fundamentally consumes a portion of your available option space, is executed by the pop operator.", "tokens": [50549, 682, 16687, 1665, 11, 1455, 364, 16014, 840, 964, 28270, 8371, 1455, 11, 257, 3922, 300, 17879, 48823, 257, 8044, 295, 428, 2435, 3614, 1901, 11, 307, 17577, 538, 264, 1665, 12973, 13, 51024], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11852154731750489, "compression_ratio": 1.6837606837606838, "no_speech_prob": 2.0439208051753477e-12}, {"id": 720, "seek": 235236, "start": 2365.96, "end": 2371.88, "text": " And because making a permanent choice consumes your potential options, it pushes the state of the computation radially outward.", "tokens": [51045, 400, 570, 1455, 257, 10996, 3922, 48823, 428, 3995, 3956, 11, 309, 21020, 264, 1785, 295, 264, 24903, 2843, 2270, 26914, 13, 51341], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11852154731750489, "compression_ratio": 1.6837606837606838, "no_speech_prob": 2.0439208051753477e-12}, {"id": 721, "seek": 235236, "start": 2372.34, "end": 2373.7400000000002, "text": " Pop is the radial coordinate.", "tokens": [51364, 10215, 307, 264, 38783, 15670, 13, 51434], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11852154731750489, "compression_ratio": 1.6837606837606838, "no_speech_prob": 2.0439208051753477e-12}, {"id": 722, "seek": 237374, "start": 2373.74, "end": 2376.7799999999997, "text": " Because radial means progression across levels.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 38783, 1355, 18733, 2108, 4358, 13, 50517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1739626331489627, "compression_ratio": 1.6631205673758864, "no_speech_prob": 1.649197054962026e-12}, {"id": 723, "seek": 237374, "start": 2377.4399999999996, "end": 2378.62, "text": " You are committing to a choice.", "tokens": [50550, 509, 366, 26659, 281, 257, 3922, 13, 50609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1739626331489627, "compression_ratio": 1.6631205673758864, "no_speech_prob": 1.649197054962026e-12}, {"id": 724, "seek": 237374, "start": 2379.16, "end": 2380.12, "text": " You are leveling up.", "tokens": [50636, 509, 366, 40617, 493, 13, 50684], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1739626331489627, "compression_ratio": 1.6631205673758864, "no_speech_prob": 1.649197054962026e-12}, {"id": 725, "seek": 237374, "start": 2380.5, "end": 2382.3799999999997, "text": " You are moving deeper into the computation.", "tokens": [50703, 509, 366, 2684, 7731, 666, 264, 24903, 13, 50797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1739626331489627, "compression_ratio": 1.6631205673758864, "no_speech_prob": 1.649197054962026e-12}, {"id": 726, "seek": 237374, "start": 2382.7, "end": 2383.9599999999996, "text": " And you cannot go back.", "tokens": [50813, 400, 291, 2644, 352, 646, 13, 50876], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1739626331489627, "compression_ratio": 1.6631205673758864, "no_speech_prob": 1.649197054962026e-12}, {"id": 727, "seek": 237374, "start": 2384.4599999999996, "end": 2385.8799999999997, "text": " You've crossed the VIP rope.", "tokens": [50901, 509, 600, 14622, 264, 29732, 13540, 13, 50972], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1739626331489627, "compression_ratio": 1.6631205673758864, "no_speech_prob": 1.649197054962026e-12}, {"id": 728, "seek": 237374, "start": 2386.16, "end": 2386.72, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50986, 48746, 736, 13, 51014], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1739626331489627, "compression_ratio": 1.6631205673758864, "no_speech_prob": 1.649197054962026e-12}, {"id": 729, "seek": 237374, "start": 2387.22, "end": 2392.66, "text": " It is a monotone, irreversible measure of how much of the initial option space has been permanently consumed.", "tokens": [51039, 467, 307, 257, 1108, 310, 546, 11, 16014, 840, 964, 3481, 295, 577, 709, 295, 264, 5883, 3614, 1901, 575, 668, 24042, 21226, 13, 51311], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1739626331489627, "compression_ratio": 1.6631205673758864, "no_speech_prob": 1.649197054962026e-12}, {"id": 730, "seek": 237374, "start": 2393.2999999999997, "end": 2397.1, "text": " You are moving radially away from the origin of infinite potential.", "tokens": [51343, 509, 366, 2684, 2843, 2270, 1314, 490, 264, 4957, 295, 13785, 3995, 13, 51533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1739626331489627, "compression_ratio": 1.6631205673758864, "no_speech_prob": 1.649197054962026e-12}, {"id": 731, "seek": 237374, "start": 2397.7, "end": 2402.18, "text": " So if pop is our radial movement, what are the angular movements in computer code?", "tokens": [51563, 407, 498, 1665, 307, 527, 38783, 3963, 11, 437, 366, 264, 24413, 9981, 294, 3820, 3089, 30, 51787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1739626331489627, "compression_ratio": 1.6631205673758864, "no_speech_prob": 1.649197054962026e-12}, {"id": 732, "seek": 240218, "start": 2402.18, "end": 2410.0, "text": " The angular coordinates are the programming operators that reorganize the computation without advancing to a new level of irreversible commitment.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 24413, 21056, 366, 264, 9410, 19077, 300, 41203, 1125, 264, 24903, 1553, 27267, 281, 257, 777, 1496, 295, 16014, 840, 964, 8371, 13, 50756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11154856924283302, "compression_ratio": 1.6482084690553747, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881495116735645e-12}, {"id": 733, "seek": 240218, "start": 2410.54, "end": 2413.7799999999997, "text": " In sphere pop, these are defined as refuse bind and merge.", "tokens": [50783, 682, 16687, 1665, 11, 613, 366, 7642, 382, 16791, 14786, 293, 22183, 13, 50945], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11154856924283302, "compression_ratio": 1.6482084690553747, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881495116735645e-12}, {"id": 734, "seek": 240218, "start": 2414.12, "end": 2417.72, "text": " Let's tie these back to our boundary typologies to see if the theory holds up.", "tokens": [50962, 961, 311, 7582, 613, 646, 281, 527, 12866, 2125, 6204, 281, 536, 498, 264, 5261, 9190, 493, 13, 51142], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11154856924283302, "compression_ratio": 1.6482084690553747, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881495116735645e-12}, {"id": 735, "seek": 240218, "start": 2418.06, "end": 2419.06, "text": " Indeed, let's test it.", "tokens": [51159, 15061, 11, 718, 311, 1500, 309, 13, 51209], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11154856924283302, "compression_ratio": 1.6482084690553747, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881495116735645e-12}, {"id": 736, "seek": 240218, "start": 2419.48, "end": 2424.2599999999998, "text": " The bind operator introduces a constraint or a variable assignment for the future of the computation.", "tokens": [51230, 440, 14786, 12973, 31472, 257, 25534, 420, 257, 7006, 15187, 337, 264, 2027, 295, 264, 24903, 13, 51469], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11154856924283302, "compression_ratio": 1.6482084690553747, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881495116735645e-12}, {"id": 737, "seek": 240218, "start": 2424.7799999999997, "end": 2429.1, "text": " It acts exactly as a Levin style stored target, a blueprint for the code to follow.", "tokens": [51495, 467, 10672, 2293, 382, 257, 1456, 4796, 3758, 12187, 3779, 11, 257, 35868, 337, 264, 3089, 281, 1524, 13, 51711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11154856924283302, "compression_ratio": 1.6482084690553747, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881495116735645e-12}, {"id": 738, "seek": 240218, "start": 2429.2799999999997, "end": 2429.7799999999997, "text": " Okay, check.", "tokens": [51720, 1033, 11, 1520, 13, 51745], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11154856924283302, "compression_ratio": 1.6482084690553747, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881495116735645e-12}, {"id": 739, "seek": 242978, "start": 2429.78, "end": 2435.0600000000004, "text": " The refuse operator records that a specific computational path was considered and permanently rejected.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 16791, 12973, 7724, 300, 257, 2685, 28270, 3100, 390, 4888, 293, 24042, 15749, 13, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15453213314677394, "compression_ratio": 1.550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897990610260314e-12}, {"id": 740, "seek": 242978, "start": 2436.0, "end": 2441.3, "text": " It acts exactly as our RSVP style diachronic exclusion, a wall made of history.", "tokens": [50676, 467, 10672, 2293, 382, 527, 25855, 53, 47, 3758, 1026, 608, 10011, 33049, 11, 257, 2929, 1027, 295, 2503, 13, 50941], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15453213314677394, "compression_ratio": 1.550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897990610260314e-12}, {"id": 741, "seek": 242978, "start": 2441.82, "end": 2444.2400000000002, "text": " And merge combines parallel regions.", "tokens": [50967, 400, 22183, 29520, 8952, 10682, 13, 51088], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15453213314677394, "compression_ratio": 1.550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897990610260314e-12}, {"id": 742, "seek": 242978, "start": 2444.82, "end": 2448.78, "text": " Crucially, none of these operators consume fundamental option space.", "tokens": [51117, 13586, 1909, 11, 6022, 295, 613, 19077, 14732, 8088, 3614, 1901, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15453213314677394, "compression_ratio": 1.550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897990610260314e-12}, {"id": 743, "seek": 242978, "start": 2449.1000000000004, "end": 2452.6200000000003, "text": " They just reorganize the structure within the current level of commitment.", "tokens": [51331, 814, 445, 41203, 1125, 264, 3877, 1951, 264, 2190, 1496, 295, 8371, 13, 51507], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15453213314677394, "compression_ratio": 1.550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897990610260314e-12}, {"id": 744, "seek": 242978, "start": 2452.86, "end": 2454.6400000000003, "text": " They are purely angular operations.", "tokens": [51519, 814, 366, 17491, 24413, 7705, 13, 51608], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15453213314677394, "compression_ratio": 1.550387596899225, "no_speech_prob": 1.4897990610260314e-12}, {"id": 745, "seek": 245464, "start": 2454.64, "end": 2458.5, "text": " It is genuinely uncanny how perfectly the math lines up.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 17839, 6219, 11612, 577, 6239, 264, 5221, 3876, 493, 13, 50558], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.143421779979359, "compression_ratio": 1.4898989898989898, "no_speech_prob": 1.965654852428833e-12}, {"id": 746, "seek": 245464, "start": 2458.56, "end": 2459.74, "text": " It's the exact same geometry.", "tokens": [50561, 467, 311, 264, 1900, 912, 18426, 13, 50620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.143421779979359, "compression_ratio": 1.4898989898989898, "no_speech_prob": 1.965654852428833e-12}, {"id": 747, "seek": 245464, "start": 2460.06, "end": 2463.04, "text": " But the text goes even deeper with the angular stuff.", "tokens": [50636, 583, 264, 2487, 1709, 754, 7731, 365, 264, 24413, 1507, 13, 50785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.143421779979359, "compression_ratio": 1.4898989898989898, "no_speech_prob": 1.965654852428833e-12}, {"id": 748, "seek": 245464, "start": 2463.3399999999997, "end": 2471.22, "text": " They introduced these things called collapse operators in sphere pop, and they explicitly compare them to the spherical harmonics we talked about earlier.", "tokens": [50800, 814, 7268, 613, 721, 1219, 15584, 19077, 294, 16687, 1665, 11, 293, 436, 20803, 6794, 552, 281, 264, 37300, 14750, 1167, 321, 2825, 466, 3071, 13, 51194], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.143421779979359, "compression_ratio": 1.4898989898989898, "no_speech_prob": 1.965654852428833e-12}, {"id": 749, "seek": 247122, "start": 2471.22, "end": 2484.04, "text": " Yes. Remember that spherical harmonics dictate the granularity of the angular structure on our shell from broad, smooth waves with a low L index to find complex, choppy patches with a high L index.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 5459, 300, 37300, 14750, 1167, 36071, 264, 39962, 507, 295, 264, 24413, 3877, 322, 527, 8720, 490, 4152, 11, 5508, 9417, 365, 257, 2295, 441, 8186, 281, 915, 3997, 11, 7931, 8200, 26531, 365, 257, 1090, 441, 8186, 13, 51006], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08052621389690198, "compression_ratio": 1.5644444444444445, "no_speech_prob": 2.5042576519418436e-12}, {"id": 750, "seek": 247122, "start": 2484.6, "end": 2492.3799999999997, "text": " In sphere pop, a collapse operator is a function that determines how much of a computation's granular history you choose to remember when you evaluate it.", "tokens": [51034, 682, 16687, 1665, 11, 257, 15584, 12973, 307, 257, 2445, 300, 24799, 577, 709, 295, 257, 24903, 311, 39962, 2503, 291, 2826, 281, 1604, 562, 291, 13059, 309, 13, 51423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08052621389690198, "compression_ratio": 1.5644444444444445, "no_speech_prob": 2.5042576519418436e-12}, {"id": 751, "seek": 249238, "start": 2492.38, "end": 2501.52, "text": " So if I run a terminal value collapse only cares about the final output of the code, if I ask a calculator for 2 plus 2, it just says 4, it doesn't care how the microchip got there.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 498, 286, 1190, 257, 14709, 2158, 15584, 787, 12310, 466, 264, 2572, 5598, 295, 264, 3089, 11, 498, 286, 1029, 257, 24993, 337, 568, 1804, 568, 11, 309, 445, 1619, 1017, 11, 309, 1177, 380, 1127, 577, 264, 4532, 339, 647, 658, 456, 13, 50822], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10042131142538102, "compression_ratio": 1.637630662020906, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977471503978105e-12}, {"id": 752, "seek": 249238, "start": 2501.82, "end": 2504.0, "text": " That's a coarse, low-level harmonic.", "tokens": [50837, 663, 311, 257, 39312, 11, 2295, 12, 12418, 32270, 13, 50946], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10042131142538102, "compression_ratio": 1.637630662020906, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977471503978105e-12}, {"id": 753, "seek": 249238, "start": 2504.1600000000003, "end": 2505.04, "text": " It's smooth and broad.", "tokens": [50954, 467, 311, 5508, 293, 4152, 13, 50998], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10042131142538102, "compression_ratio": 1.637630662020906, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977471503978105e-12}, {"id": 754, "seek": 249238, "start": 2505.3, "end": 2512.6600000000003, "text": " But a full provenance collapse tracks the entire history of every single microevaluation step the computer took to get to 4.", "tokens": [51011, 583, 257, 1577, 12785, 719, 15584, 10218, 264, 2302, 2503, 295, 633, 2167, 4532, 68, 46504, 1823, 264, 3820, 1890, 281, 483, 281, 1017, 13, 51379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10042131142538102, "compression_ratio": 1.637630662020906, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977471503978105e-12}, {"id": 755, "seek": 249238, "start": 2513.6600000000003, "end": 2519.32, "text": " That is a fine, high-level harmonic because it preserves all the complex, choppy detail of the journey.", "tokens": [51429, 663, 307, 257, 2489, 11, 1090, 12, 12418, 32270, 570, 309, 1183, 9054, 439, 264, 3997, 11, 7931, 8200, 2607, 295, 264, 4671, 13, 51712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10042131142538102, "compression_ratio": 1.637630662020906, "no_speech_prob": 1.8977471503978105e-12}, {"id": 756, "seek": 251932, "start": 2519.32, "end": 2525.0800000000004, "text": " Exactly. The collapse operator fixes the indistinguishability relation over the space of computational histories.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 440, 15584, 12973, 32539, 264, 1016, 468, 7050, 742, 2310, 9721, 670, 264, 1901, 295, 28270, 30631, 13, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10769873683892407, "compression_ratio": 1.69, "no_speech_prob": 2.1847942292124722e-12}, {"id": 757, "seek": 251932, "start": 2525.6800000000003, "end": 2531.52, "text": " It is a mathematical dial that decides which details are erased as irrelevant and which are preserved as essential.", "tokens": [50683, 467, 307, 257, 18894, 5502, 300, 14898, 597, 4365, 366, 38359, 382, 28682, 293, 597, 366, 22242, 382, 7115, 13, 50975], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10769873683892407, "compression_ratio": 1.69, "no_speech_prob": 2.1847942292124722e-12}, {"id": 758, "seek": 251932, "start": 2531.9, "end": 2538.0, "text": " Which leads fliction to a genuinely radical, almost aggressive claim about computer science itself.", "tokens": [50994, 3013, 6689, 932, 4105, 281, 257, 17839, 12001, 11, 1920, 10762, 3932, 466, 3820, 3497, 2564, 13, 51299], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10769873683892407, "compression_ratio": 1.69, "no_speech_prob": 2.1847942292124722e-12}, {"id": 759, "seek": 251932, "start": 2538.34, "end": 2542.6600000000003, "text": " They state there is no such thing as two computations being really the same context independently.", "tokens": [51316, 814, 1785, 456, 307, 572, 1270, 551, 382, 732, 2807, 763, 885, 534, 264, 912, 4319, 21761, 13, 51532], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10769873683892407, "compression_ratio": 1.69, "no_speech_prob": 2.1847942292124722e-12}, {"id": 760, "seek": 251932, "start": 2542.84, "end": 2546.78, "text": " It is a profound axiom that challenges a lot of basic programming assumptions.", "tokens": [51541, 467, 307, 257, 14382, 6360, 72, 298, 300, 4759, 257, 688, 295, 3875, 9410, 17695, 13, 51738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10769873683892407, "compression_ratio": 1.69, "no_speech_prob": 2.1847942292124722e-12}, {"id": 761, "seek": 254678, "start": 2546.78, "end": 2553.42, "text": " You fundamentally cannot ask if two algorithms are the same without explicitly specifying your collapse operator.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 17879, 2644, 1029, 498, 732, 14642, 366, 264, 912, 1553, 20803, 1608, 5489, 428, 15584, 12973, 13, 50697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09839983990317897, "compression_ratio": 1.8131487889273357, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906412893593405e-12}, {"id": 762, "seek": 254678, "start": 2553.7200000000003, "end": 2554.76, "text": " That makes total sense now.", "tokens": [50712, 663, 1669, 3217, 2020, 586, 13, 50764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09839983990317897, "compression_ratio": 1.8131487889273357, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906412893593405e-12}, {"id": 763, "seek": 254678, "start": 2555.0, "end": 2563.92, "text": " If you use a terminal value collapse, the low-resolution smooth wave, the algorithm 2 plus 2, and the algorithm 3 plus 1 are exactly the same computation they both output 4.", "tokens": [50776, 759, 291, 764, 257, 14709, 2158, 15584, 11, 264, 2295, 12, 495, 3386, 5508, 5772, 11, 264, 9284, 568, 1804, 568, 11, 293, 264, 9284, 805, 1804, 502, 366, 2293, 264, 912, 24903, 436, 1293, 5598, 1017, 13, 51222], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09839983990317897, "compression_ratio": 1.8131487889273357, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906412893593405e-12}, {"id": 764, "seek": 254678, "start": 2564.42, "end": 2575.84, "text": " But if you use a full provenance collapse, the high-resolution patchy wave, they are entirely geometrically different computations because the historical path they took to arrive at 4 is completely different.", "tokens": [51247, 583, 498, 291, 764, 257, 1577, 12785, 719, 15584, 11, 264, 1090, 12, 495, 3386, 9972, 88, 5772, 11, 436, 366, 7696, 12956, 81, 984, 819, 2807, 763, 570, 264, 8584, 3100, 436, 1890, 281, 8881, 412, 1017, 307, 2584, 819, 13, 51818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09839983990317897, "compression_ratio": 1.8131487889273357, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906412893593405e-12}, {"id": 765, "seek": 257584, "start": 2575.84, "end": 2581.04, "text": " The equivalence of two ideas is entirely dependent on your chosen coordinate ontology.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 9052, 655, 295, 732, 3487, 307, 7696, 12334, 322, 428, 8614, 15670, 6592, 1793, 13, 50625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18440038401906084, "compression_ratio": 1.5575221238938053, "no_speech_prob": 1.912924029248697e-12}, {"id": 766, "seek": 257584, "start": 2581.28, "end": 2583.7200000000003, "text": " So abstract computer science forms a sphere.", "tokens": [50637, 407, 12649, 3820, 3497, 6422, 257, 16687, 13, 50759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18440038401906084, "compression_ratio": 1.5575221238938053, "no_speech_prob": 1.912924029248697e-12}, {"id": 767, "seek": 257584, "start": 2584.1000000000004, "end": 2586.28, "text": " Physical fields and flatworms form a sphere.", "tokens": [50778, 31918, 7909, 293, 4962, 30917, 82, 1254, 257, 16687, 13, 50887], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18440038401906084, "compression_ratio": 1.5575221238938053, "no_speech_prob": 1.912924029248697e-12}, {"id": 768, "seek": 257584, "start": 2586.9, "end": 2590.58, "text": " But fliction saves the ultimate plot twist for the very end of the book.", "tokens": [50918, 583, 932, 4105, 19155, 264, 9705, 7542, 8203, 337, 264, 588, 917, 295, 264, 1446, 13, 51102], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18440038401906084, "compression_ratio": 1.5575221238938053, "no_speech_prob": 1.912924029248697e-12}, {"id": 769, "seek": 257584, "start": 2591.44, "end": 2592.46, "text": " What about human thought?", "tokens": [51145, 708, 466, 1952, 1194, 30, 51196], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18440038401906084, "compression_ratio": 1.5575221238938053, "no_speech_prob": 1.912924029248697e-12}, {"id": 770, "seek": 257584, "start": 2592.7000000000003, "end": 2596.28, "text": " What about observation statistics and the way our brains categorize reality?", "tokens": [51208, 708, 466, 14816, 12523, 293, 264, 636, 527, 15442, 19250, 1125, 4103, 30, 51387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18440038401906084, "compression_ratio": 1.5575221238938053, "no_speech_prob": 1.912924029248697e-12}, {"id": 771, "seek": 259628, "start": 2596.28, "end": 2599.1600000000003, "text": " We enter Chapter 8, Distinguishability Geometry.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 3242, 18874, 1649, 11, 9840, 7050, 742, 2310, 2876, 34730, 13, 50509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1292301907258875, "compression_ratio": 1.5827586206896551, "no_speech_prob": 2.3251335752594304e-12}, {"id": 772, "seek": 259628, "start": 2599.6000000000004, "end": 2609.1000000000004, "text": " And this is where fliction pulls all the disparate threads together to show that for a specific class of observable spaces, the sphere isn't just a clever metaphor or useful UI.", "tokens": [50531, 400, 341, 307, 689, 932, 4105, 16982, 439, 264, 14548, 473, 19314, 1214, 281, 855, 300, 337, 257, 2685, 1508, 295, 9951, 712, 7673, 11, 264, 16687, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 13494, 19157, 420, 4420, 15682, 13, 51006], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1292301907258875, "compression_ratio": 1.5827586206896551, "no_speech_prob": 2.3251335752594304e-12}, {"id": 773, "seek": 259628, "start": 2609.42, "end": 2614.44, "text": " It is the literal mathematical geometric object that distinguishability itself produces.", "tokens": [51022, 467, 307, 264, 20411, 18894, 33246, 2657, 300, 20206, 2310, 2564, 14725, 13, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1292301907258875, "compression_ratio": 1.5827586206896551, "no_speech_prob": 2.3251335752594304e-12}, {"id": 774, "seek": 259628, "start": 2614.84, "end": 2617.1800000000003, "text": " Okay, you're going to have to deeply unpack that for me.", "tokens": [51293, 1033, 11, 291, 434, 516, 281, 362, 281, 8760, 26699, 300, 337, 385, 13, 51410], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1292301907258875, "compression_ratio": 1.5827586206896551, "no_speech_prob": 2.3251335752594304e-12}, {"id": 775, "seek": 259628, "start": 2617.42, "end": 2622.6800000000003, "text": " How does statistics, just numbers representing probability, literally become a sphere?", "tokens": [51422, 1012, 775, 12523, 11, 445, 3547, 13460, 8482, 11, 3736, 1813, 257, 16687, 30, 51685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1292301907258875, "compression_ratio": 1.5827586206896551, "no_speech_prob": 2.3251335752594304e-12}, {"id": 776, "seek": 262268, "start": 2622.68, "end": 2626.72, "text": " It relies on the underlying geometry of categorical distributions.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 30910, 322, 264, 14217, 18426, 295, 19250, 804, 37870, 13, 50567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820047378540039, "compression_ratio": 1.5776699029126213, "no_speech_prob": 1.8533894037553456e-12}, {"id": 777, "seek": 262268, "start": 2627.72, "end": 2630.7799999999997, "text": " Imagine you have a set of probabilities for different outcomes.", "tokens": [50617, 11739, 291, 362, 257, 992, 295, 33783, 337, 819, 10070, 13, 50770], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820047378540039, "compression_ratio": 1.5776699029126213, "no_speech_prob": 1.8533894037553456e-12}, {"id": 778, "seek": 262268, "start": 2631.4199999999996, "end": 2633.2999999999997, "text": " Let's say you are predicting the weather.", "tokens": [50802, 961, 311, 584, 291, 366, 32884, 264, 5503, 13, 50896], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820047378540039, "compression_ratio": 1.5776699029126213, "no_speech_prob": 1.8533894037553456e-12}, {"id": 779, "seek": 262268, "start": 2634.12, "end": 2635.3399999999997, "text": " Rain, sun, or snow.", "tokens": [50937, 14487, 11, 3295, 11, 420, 5756, 13, 50998], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820047378540039, "compression_ratio": 1.5776699029126213, "no_speech_prob": 1.8533894037553456e-12}, {"id": 780, "seek": 262268, "start": 2635.8199999999997, "end": 2640.08, "text": " The probabilities must add up to 100%, or in math terms, exactly 1.", "tokens": [51022, 440, 33783, 1633, 909, 493, 281, 2319, 8923, 420, 294, 5221, 2115, 11, 2293, 502, 13, 51235], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820047378540039, "compression_ratio": 1.5776699029126213, "no_speech_prob": 1.8533894037553456e-12}, {"id": 781, "seek": 262268, "start": 2640.2999999999997, "end": 2644.3399999999997, "text": " So probability 1 plus probability 2 plus probability 3 equals 1.", "tokens": [51246, 407, 8482, 502, 1804, 8482, 568, 1804, 8482, 805, 6915, 502, 13, 51448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820047378540039, "compression_ratio": 1.5776699029126213, "no_speech_prob": 1.8533894037553456e-12}, {"id": 782, "seek": 264434, "start": 2644.34, "end": 2644.6200000000003, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11275846382667279, "compression_ratio": 1.75, "no_speech_prob": 2.262426357368952e-12}, {"id": 783, "seek": 264434, "start": 2644.82, "end": 2654.92, "text": " Flixian shows that if you map these probabilities using what's called a square root embedding, meaning you simply take the square root of each probability, you map them into a new mathematical space.", "tokens": [50389, 3235, 970, 952, 3110, 300, 498, 291, 4471, 613, 33783, 1228, 437, 311, 1219, 257, 3732, 5593, 12240, 3584, 11, 3620, 291, 2935, 747, 264, 3732, 5593, 295, 1184, 8482, 11, 291, 4471, 552, 666, 257, 777, 18894, 1901, 13, 50894], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11275846382667279, "compression_ratio": 1.75, "no_speech_prob": 2.262426357368952e-12}, {"id": 784, "seek": 264434, "start": 2655.32, "end": 2657.82, "text": " Wait, I think I see where this is going based on high school algebra.", "tokens": [50914, 3802, 11, 286, 519, 286, 536, 689, 341, 307, 516, 2361, 322, 1090, 1395, 21989, 13, 51039], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11275846382667279, "compression_ratio": 1.75, "no_speech_prob": 2.262426357368952e-12}, {"id": 785, "seek": 264434, "start": 2658.3, "end": 2668.6800000000003, "text": " If p1 plus p2 plus p3 equals 1, and I make a new variable that is the square root of p, let's call it q, then q1 squared plus q2 squared plus 2, 3 squared equals 1.", "tokens": [51063, 759, 280, 16, 1804, 280, 17, 1804, 280, 18, 6915, 502, 11, 293, 286, 652, 257, 777, 7006, 300, 307, 264, 3732, 5593, 295, 280, 11, 718, 311, 818, 309, 9505, 11, 550, 9505, 16, 8889, 1804, 9505, 17, 8889, 1804, 568, 11, 805, 8889, 6915, 502, 13, 51582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11275846382667279, "compression_ratio": 1.75, "no_speech_prob": 2.262426357368952e-12}, {"id": 786, "seek": 266868, "start": 2668.68, "end": 2674.24, "text": " You've got it. And what is the geometric equation for x squared plus y squared plus z squared equals 1?", "tokens": [50365, 509, 600, 658, 309, 13, 400, 437, 307, 264, 33246, 5367, 337, 2031, 8889, 1804, 288, 8889, 1804, 710, 8889, 6915, 502, 30, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07545260588328044, "compression_ratio": 1.6628787878787878, "no_speech_prob": 1.573302577627389e-12}, {"id": 787, "seek": 266868, "start": 2674.3399999999997, "end": 2678.5, "text": " That is the literal Pythagorean equation for a 3D sphere with a radius of 1.", "tokens": [50648, 663, 307, 264, 20411, 9953, 392, 559, 25885, 5367, 337, 257, 805, 35, 16687, 365, 257, 15845, 295, 502, 13, 50856], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07545260588328044, "compression_ratio": 1.6628787878787878, "no_speech_prob": 1.573302577627389e-12}, {"id": 788, "seek": 266868, "start": 2678.58, "end": 2690.02, "text": " Exactly. And when statisticians calculate the metric for this space, specifically the Fisher information metric, which measures how mathematically easy it is to distinguish between two different probability distributions.", "tokens": [50860, 7587, 13, 400, 562, 29588, 2567, 8873, 264, 20678, 337, 341, 1901, 11, 4682, 264, 26676, 1589, 20678, 11, 597, 8000, 577, 44003, 1858, 309, 307, 281, 20206, 1296, 732, 819, 8482, 37870, 13, 51432], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07545260588328044, "compression_ratio": 1.6628787878787878, "no_speech_prob": 1.573302577627389e-12}, {"id": 789, "seek": 266868, "start": 2690.14, "end": 2691.6, "text": " The map of how we tell things apart.", "tokens": [51438, 440, 4471, 295, 577, 321, 980, 721, 4936, 13, 51511], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07545260588328044, "compression_ratio": 1.6628787878787878, "no_speech_prob": 1.573302577627389e-12}, {"id": 790, "seek": 269160, "start": 2691.6, "end": 2698.36, "text": " The math rigorously proves that this statistical space is exactly isometric to the round metric on a sphere.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 5221, 42191, 5098, 25019, 300, 341, 22820, 1901, 307, 2293, 307, 29470, 281, 264, 3098, 20678, 322, 257, 16687, 13, 50703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1338416508265904, "compression_ratio": 1.654708520179372, "no_speech_prob": 2.466044512691723e-12}, {"id": 791, "seek": 269160, "start": 2698.92, "end": 2700.66, "text": " It is not an analogy. It is not poetry.", "tokens": [50731, 467, 307, 406, 364, 21663, 13, 467, 307, 406, 15155, 13, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1338416508265904, "compression_ratio": 1.654708520179372, "no_speech_prob": 2.466044512691723e-12}, {"id": 792, "seek": 269160, "start": 2701.14, "end": 2708.86, "text": " Up to a constant factor, the statistical manifold of a finite outcome space, literally geometrically, is a positive orthent of a sphere.", "tokens": [50842, 5858, 281, 257, 5754, 5952, 11, 264, 22820, 47138, 295, 257, 19362, 9700, 1901, 11, 3736, 12956, 81, 984, 11, 307, 257, 3353, 19052, 317, 295, 257, 16687, 13, 51228], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1338416508265904, "compression_ratio": 1.654708520179372, "no_speech_prob": 2.466044512691723e-12}, {"id": 793, "seek": 269160, "start": 2709.0, "end": 2709.88, "text": " So what does this all mean?", "tokens": [51235, 407, 437, 775, 341, 439, 914, 30, 51279], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1338416508265904, "compression_ratio": 1.654708520179372, "no_speech_prob": 2.466044512691723e-12}, {"id": 794, "seek": 269160, "start": 2710.52, "end": 2712.92, "text": " It means everything we just learned over the last hour.", "tokens": [51311, 467, 1355, 1203, 321, 445, 3264, 670, 264, 1036, 1773, 13, 51431], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1338416508265904, "compression_ratio": 1.654708520179372, "no_speech_prob": 2.466044512691723e-12}, {"id": 795, "seek": 271292, "start": 2712.92, "end": 2731.98, "text": " The Laplacian incompatibility detector, the radial progression versus angular reorganization, the tension between the stabilizing Lamphron and the smoothing Lamphrodine, the absolute inability to perfectly repair wrinkles on a closed shell, all of it literally mathematically applies to how we distinguish information and ideas.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 40393, 267, 2841, 25712, 11, 264, 38783, 18733, 5717, 24413, 41203, 2144, 11, 264, 8980, 1296, 264, 11652, 3319, 18825, 950, 2044, 293, 264, 899, 6259, 571, 18825, 950, 11452, 533, 11, 264, 8236, 33162, 281, 6239, 10535, 34822, 322, 257, 5395, 8720, 11, 439, 295, 309, 3736, 44003, 13165, 281, 577, 321, 20206, 1589, 293, 3487, 13, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10970675073018889, "compression_ratio": 1.5857740585774058, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813231579551613e-12}, {"id": 796, "seek": 271292, "start": 2732.16, "end": 2732.84, "text": " Oh my God.", "tokens": [51327, 876, 452, 1265, 13, 51361], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10970675073018889, "compression_ratio": 1.5857740585774058, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813231579551613e-12}, {"id": 797, "seek": 271292, "start": 2733.2000000000003, "end": 2734.92, "text": " The text mentions the curvature defect.", "tokens": [51379, 440, 2487, 23844, 264, 37638, 16445, 13, 51465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10970675073018889, "compression_ratio": 1.5857740585774058, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813231579551613e-12}, {"id": 798, "seek": 273492, "start": 2734.92, "end": 2742.38, "text": " We talked about this with the crumpled foil, how you can't smooth out all the wrinkles on a sphere because the spherical shape mathematically forbids it.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 2825, 466, 341, 365, 264, 941, 449, 15551, 22444, 11, 577, 291, 393, 380, 5508, 484, 439, 264, 34822, 322, 257, 16687, 570, 264, 37300, 3909, 44003, 16603, 3742, 309, 13, 50738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11219022332168208, "compression_ratio": 1.5843621399176955, "no_speech_prob": 1.59831707331054e-12}, {"id": 799, "seek": 273492, "start": 2742.76, "end": 2744.12, "text": " The topology demands tension.", "tokens": [50757, 440, 1192, 1793, 15107, 8980, 13, 50825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11219022332168208, "compression_ratio": 1.5843621399176955, "no_speech_prob": 1.59831707331054e-12}, {"id": 800, "seek": 273492, "start": 2744.52, "end": 2746.92, "text": " How does that translate to ideas and statistics?", "tokens": [50845, 1012, 775, 300, 13799, 281, 3487, 293, 12523, 30, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11219022332168208, "compression_ratio": 1.5843621399176955, "no_speech_prob": 1.59831707331054e-12}, {"id": 801, "seek": 273492, "start": 2747.44, "end": 2755.56, "text": " In information geometry, positive curvature on this statistical sphere corresponds to a phenomenon called overfitting or the collapsing of distinctions.", "tokens": [50991, 682, 1589, 18426, 11, 3353, 37638, 322, 341, 22820, 16687, 23249, 281, 257, 14029, 1219, 670, 69, 2414, 420, 264, 45339, 295, 1483, 49798, 13, 51397], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11219022332168208, "compression_ratio": 1.5843621399176955, "no_speech_prob": 1.59831707331054e-12}, {"id": 802, "seek": 275556, "start": 2755.56, "end": 2765.5, "text": " Because a sphere is a closed, positively curved surface, it mathematically forces lines that start out parallel to eventually converge and cross.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 257, 16687, 307, 257, 5395, 11, 25795, 24991, 3753, 11, 309, 44003, 5874, 3876, 300, 722, 484, 8952, 281, 4728, 41881, 293, 3278, 13, 50862], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12798133649324117, "compression_ratio": 1.7406015037593985, "no_speech_prob": 1.74855128206447e-12}, {"id": 803, "seek": 275556, "start": 2765.7599999999998, "end": 2768.2999999999997, "text": " It forces nearby points to crowd together.", "tokens": [50875, 467, 5874, 11184, 2793, 281, 6919, 1214, 13, 51002], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12798133649324117, "compression_ratio": 1.7406015037593985, "no_speech_prob": 1.74855128206447e-12}, {"id": 804, "seek": 275556, "start": 2768.58, "end": 2776.64, "text": " Meaning nearby theories or highly nuanced ideas are geometrically forced to blur together and become indistinguishable from each other.", "tokens": [51016, 19948, 11184, 13667, 420, 5405, 45115, 3487, 366, 12956, 81, 984, 7579, 281, 14257, 1214, 293, 1813, 1016, 468, 7050, 742, 712, 490, 1184, 661, 13, 51419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12798133649324117, "compression_ratio": 1.7406015037593985, "no_speech_prob": 1.74855128206447e-12}, {"id": 805, "seek": 275556, "start": 2776.7999999999997, "end": 2777.36, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51427, 48746, 736, 13, 51455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12798133649324117, "compression_ratio": 1.7406015037593985, "no_speech_prob": 1.74855128206447e-12}, {"id": 806, "seek": 275556, "start": 2777.5, "end": 2784.2599999999998, "text": " Because a statistical sphere must have positive curvature, a closed system of observations must lose some distinguishing power.", "tokens": [51462, 1436, 257, 22820, 16687, 1633, 362, 3353, 37638, 11, 257, 5395, 1185, 295, 18163, 1633, 3624, 512, 11365, 3807, 1347, 13, 51800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12798133649324117, "compression_ratio": 1.7406015037593985, "no_speech_prob": 1.74855128206447e-12}, {"id": 807, "seek": 278426, "start": 2784.26, "end": 2786.76, "text": " However, the topology demands a defect.", "tokens": [50365, 2908, 11, 264, 1192, 1793, 15107, 257, 16445, 13, 50490], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1615163077295354, "compression_ratio": 1.638036809815951, "no_speech_prob": 1.586080008650348e-12}, {"id": 808, "seek": 278426, "start": 2787.26, "end": 2790.6200000000003, "text": " You cannot perfectly separate every idea on a curved surface.", "tokens": [50515, 509, 2644, 6239, 4994, 633, 1558, 322, 257, 24991, 3753, 13, 50683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1615163077295354, "compression_ratio": 1.638036809815951, "no_speech_prob": 1.586080008650348e-12}, {"id": 809, "seek": 278426, "start": 2791.1800000000003, "end": 2795.44, "text": " So you're telling me that when I struggle to tell two incredibly complex political theories apart,", "tokens": [50711, 407, 291, 434, 3585, 385, 300, 562, 286, 7799, 281, 980, 732, 6252, 3997, 3905, 13667, 4936, 11, 50924], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1615163077295354, "compression_ratio": 1.638036809815951, "no_speech_prob": 1.586080008650348e-12}, {"id": 810, "seek": 278426, "start": 2795.6400000000003, "end": 2799.82, "text": " or when I can't distinguish between the outputs of two massively dense AI models,", "tokens": [50934, 420, 562, 286, 393, 380, 20206, 1296, 264, 23930, 295, 732, 29379, 18011, 7318, 5245, 11, 51143], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1615163077295354, "compression_ratio": 1.638036809815951, "no_speech_prob": 1.586080008650348e-12}, {"id": 811, "seek": 278426, "start": 2800.3, "end": 2802.8, "text": " it's not necessarily because I'm unintelligent or not paying attention,", "tokens": [51167, 309, 311, 406, 4725, 570, 286, 478, 517, 20761, 25002, 420, 406, 6229, 3202, 11, 51292], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1615163077295354, "compression_ratio": 1.638036809815951, "no_speech_prob": 1.586080008650348e-12}, {"id": 812, "seek": 278426, "start": 2803.34, "end": 2808.46, "text": " but because the mathematical shape of probability itself geometrically forces those ideas to blur together.", "tokens": [51319, 457, 570, 264, 18894, 3909, 295, 8482, 2564, 12956, 81, 984, 5874, 729, 3487, 281, 14257, 1214, 13, 51575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1615163077295354, "compression_ratio": 1.638036809815951, "no_speech_prob": 1.586080008650348e-12}, {"id": 813, "seek": 278426, "start": 2808.78, "end": 2812.6800000000003, "text": " The curvature defect of information geometry practically guarantees it.", "tokens": [51591, 440, 37638, 16445, 295, 1589, 18426, 15667, 32567, 309, 13, 51786], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1615163077295354, "compression_ratio": 1.638036809815951, "no_speech_prob": 1.586080008650348e-12}, {"id": 814, "seek": 281268, "start": 2812.68, "end": 2815.68, "text": " If your observational space is closed and finite,", "tokens": [50365, 759, 428, 9951, 1478, 1901, 307, 5395, 293, 19362, 11, 50515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17815098904147006, "compression_ratio": 1.5935251798561152, "no_speech_prob": 2.3074025329306025e-12}, {"id": 815, "seek": 281268, "start": 2815.68, "end": 2822.18, "text": " you will mathematically lose the ability to perfectly distinguish between highly complex proximate theories.", "tokens": [50515, 291, 486, 44003, 3624, 264, 3485, 281, 6239, 20206, 1296, 5405, 3997, 447, 87, 2905, 13667, 13, 50840], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17815098904147006, "compression_ratio": 1.5935251798561152, "no_speech_prob": 2.3074025329306025e-12}, {"id": 816, "seek": 281268, "start": 2822.8599999999997, "end": 2825.04, "text": " They will inevitably collapse into each other.", "tokens": [50874, 814, 486, 28171, 15584, 666, 1184, 661, 13, 50983], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17815098904147006, "compression_ratio": 1.5935251798561152, "no_speech_prob": 2.3074025329306025e-12}, {"id": 817, "seek": 281268, "start": 2825.52, "end": 2829.68, "text": " It is an irreducible geometric obstruction to uniform distinguishability.", "tokens": [51007, 467, 307, 364, 16014, 769, 32128, 33246, 49711, 281, 9452, 20206, 2310, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17815098904147006, "compression_ratio": 1.5935251798561152, "no_speech_prob": 2.3074025329306025e-12}, {"id": 818, "seek": 281268, "start": 2830.2799999999997, "end": 2834.3199999999997, "text": " The wrinkles on the foil of human knowledge can never be perfectly flattened.", "tokens": [51245, 440, 34822, 322, 264, 22444, 295, 1952, 3601, 393, 1128, 312, 6239, 24183, 292, 13, 51447], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17815098904147006, "compression_ratio": 1.5935251798561152, "no_speech_prob": 2.3074025329306025e-12}, {"id": 819, "seek": 281268, "start": 2834.3599999999997, "end": 2835.54, "text": " That is just wow.", "tokens": [51449, 663, 307, 445, 6076, 13, 51508], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17815098904147006, "compression_ratio": 1.5935251798561152, "no_speech_prob": 2.3074025329306025e-12}, {"id": 820, "seek": 281268, "start": 2836.08, "end": 2838.7799999999997, "text": " Okay, we need to take a breath and recap this mind-bending journey.", "tokens": [51535, 1033, 11, 321, 643, 281, 747, 257, 6045, 293, 20928, 341, 1575, 12, 65, 2029, 4671, 13, 51670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17815098904147006, "compression_ratio": 1.5935251798561152, "no_speech_prob": 2.3074025329306025e-12}, {"id": 821, "seek": 283878, "start": 2838.78, "end": 2844.82, "text": " We started by realizing that the coordinate grids we use to map reality are just interfaces,", "tokens": [50365, 492, 1409, 538, 16734, 300, 264, 15670, 677, 3742, 321, 764, 281, 4471, 4103, 366, 445, 28416, 11, 50667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12067114434591154, "compression_ratio": 1.6224899598393574, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756296429195407e-12}, {"id": 822, "seek": 283878, "start": 2845.26, "end": 2848.84, "text": " computational dashboards that prioritize some math over others.", "tokens": [50689, 28270, 8240, 17228, 300, 25164, 512, 5221, 670, 2357, 13, 50868], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12067114434591154, "compression_ratio": 1.6224899598393574, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756296429195407e-12}, {"id": 823, "seek": 283878, "start": 2848.96, "end": 2852.38, "text": " We then discovered that for any system organized around a central point,", "tokens": [50874, 492, 550, 6941, 300, 337, 604, 1185, 9983, 926, 257, 5777, 935, 11, 51045], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12067114434591154, "compression_ratio": 1.6224899598393574, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756296429195407e-12}, {"id": 824, "seek": 283878, "start": 2852.92, "end": 2855.5600000000004, "text": " the sphere is the uniquely optimal interface,", "tokens": [51072, 264, 16687, 307, 264, 31474, 16252, 9226, 11, 51204], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12067114434591154, "compression_ratio": 1.6224899598393574, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756296429195407e-12}, {"id": 825, "seek": 283878, "start": 2855.7000000000003, "end": 2858.96, "text": " dividing the world perfectly into radial progression across levels of commitment", "tokens": [51211, 26764, 264, 1002, 6239, 666, 38783, 18733, 2108, 4358, 295, 8371, 51374], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12067114434591154, "compression_ratio": 1.6224899598393574, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756296429195407e-12}, {"id": 826, "seek": 283878, "start": 2858.96, "end": 2861.5800000000004, "text": " and angular reorganization within those levels.", "tokens": [51374, 293, 24413, 41203, 2144, 1951, 729, 4358, 13, 51505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12067114434591154, "compression_ratio": 1.6224899598393574, "no_speech_prob": 1.8756296429195407e-12}, {"id": 827, "seek": 286158, "start": 2861.58, "end": 2864.86, "text": " We found that the boundaries separating those levels aren't just dead walls.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 1352, 300, 264, 13180, 29279, 729, 4358, 3212, 380, 445, 3116, 7920, 13, 50529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17389272760461877, "compression_ratio": 1.5936395759717314, "no_speech_prob": 2.3617416616134035e-12}, {"id": 828, "seek": 286158, "start": 2865.2799999999997, "end": 2865.7599999999998, "text": " They compute.", "tokens": [50550, 814, 14722, 13, 50574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17389272760461877, "compression_ratio": 1.5936395759717314, "no_speech_prob": 2.3617416616134035e-12}, {"id": 829, "seek": 286158, "start": 2866.38, "end": 2869.22, "text": " They can mediate the present like Friston's submarine sonar.", "tokens": [50605, 814, 393, 1205, 13024, 264, 1974, 411, 1526, 47345, 311, 33995, 1872, 289, 13, 50747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17389272760461877, "compression_ratio": 1.5936395759717314, "no_speech_prob": 2.3617416616134035e-12}, {"id": 830, "seek": 286158, "start": 2869.68, "end": 2873.72, "text": " They can actively pull us toward a stored future like Levin's flatworm blueprints.", "tokens": [50770, 814, 393, 13022, 2235, 505, 7361, 257, 12187, 2027, 411, 1456, 4796, 311, 4962, 30917, 888, 23547, 47523, 13, 50972], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17389272760461877, "compression_ratio": 1.5936395759717314, "no_speech_prob": 2.3617416616134035e-12}, {"id": 831, "seek": 286158, "start": 2874.1, "end": 2878.46, "text": " Or they can permanently lock out the past like the RSVP historical veto.", "tokens": [50991, 1610, 436, 393, 24042, 4017, 484, 264, 1791, 411, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 8584, 42910, 13, 51209], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17389272760461877, "compression_ratio": 1.5936395759717314, "no_speech_prob": 2.3617416616134035e-12}, {"id": 832, "seek": 286158, "start": 2878.88, "end": 2882.72, "text": " We explored how the Laplacian operator acts as a universal referee,", "tokens": [51230, 492, 24016, 577, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 12973, 10672, 382, 257, 11455, 43096, 11, 51422], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17389272760461877, "compression_ratio": 1.5936395759717314, "no_speech_prob": 2.3617416616134035e-12}, {"id": 833, "seek": 286158, "start": 2882.94, "end": 2886.5, "text": " mathematically detecting the wrinkles and angular disagreements in reality.", "tokens": [51433, 44003, 40237, 264, 34822, 293, 24413, 23926, 6400, 294, 4103, 13, 51611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17389272760461877, "compression_ratio": 1.5936395759717314, "no_speech_prob": 2.3617416616134035e-12}, {"id": 834, "seek": 288650, "start": 2886.5, "end": 2891.46, "text": " And we watched as the Lamprodine repair pressure desperately tried to smooth them out", "tokens": [50365, 400, 321, 6337, 382, 264, 441, 1215, 11452, 533, 10535, 3321, 23726, 3031, 281, 5508, 552, 484, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14299150910040345, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.875639834419962e-12}, {"id": 835, "seek": 288650, "start": 2891.46, "end": 2896.26, "text": " while locked in an eternal tug-of-war with the stabilizing force of the Lampron.", "tokens": [50613, 1339, 9376, 294, 364, 14503, 33543, 12, 2670, 12, 6925, 365, 264, 11652, 3319, 3464, 295, 264, 441, 1215, 2044, 13, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14299150910040345, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.875639834419962e-12}, {"id": 836, "seek": 288650, "start": 2896.6, "end": 2901.7, "text": " We saw the entire beautiful framework map flawlessly onto abstract computer science", "tokens": [50870, 492, 1866, 264, 2302, 2238, 8388, 4471, 13717, 12048, 3911, 12649, 3820, 3497, 51125], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14299150910040345, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.875639834419962e-12}, {"id": 837, "seek": 288650, "start": 2901.7, "end": 2906.9, "text": " through sphere pop, where popping a bubble is a radial level up and collapsing a history", "tokens": [51125, 807, 16687, 1665, 11, 689, 18374, 257, 12212, 307, 257, 38783, 1496, 493, 293, 45339, 257, 2503, 51385], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14299150910040345, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.875639834419962e-12}, {"id": 838, "seek": 288650, "start": 2906.9, "end": 2909.2, "text": " is just changing your angular resolution.", "tokens": [51385, 307, 445, 4473, 428, 24413, 8669, 13, 51500], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14299150910040345, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.875639834419962e-12}, {"id": 839, "seek": 288650, "start": 2909.52, "end": 2912.24, "text": " And finally, we arrived at the ultimate realization.", "tokens": [51516, 400, 2721, 11, 321, 6678, 412, 264, 9705, 25138, 13, 51652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14299150910040345, "compression_ratio": 1.5781818181818181, "no_speech_prob": 1.875639834419962e-12}, {"id": 840, "seek": 291224, "start": 2912.24, "end": 2919.24, "text": " The realm of possibilities, statistics, and probability itself is mathematically a literal geometric sphere.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 15355, 295, 12178, 11, 12523, 11, 293, 8482, 2564, 307, 44003, 257, 20411, 33246, 16687, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12196461538250526, "compression_ratio": 1.6833976833976834, "no_speech_prob": 1.958287698666794e-12}, {"id": 841, "seek": 291224, "start": 2919.4199999999996, "end": 2923.56, "text": " A sphere that because of its inherent positive curvature forces a statistical defect,", "tokens": [50724, 316, 16687, 300, 570, 295, 1080, 26387, 3353, 37638, 5874, 257, 22820, 16445, 11, 50931], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12196461538250526, "compression_ratio": 1.6833976833976834, "no_speech_prob": 1.958287698666794e-12}, {"id": 842, "seek": 291224, "start": 2924.04, "end": 2928.24, "text": " a blurring of distinctions that no amount of intellectual repair can perfectly resolve.", "tokens": [50955, 257, 14257, 2937, 295, 1483, 49798, 300, 572, 2372, 295, 12576, 10535, 393, 6239, 14151, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12196461538250526, "compression_ratio": 1.6833976833976834, "no_speech_prob": 1.958287698666794e-12}, {"id": 843, "seek": 291224, "start": 2928.4199999999996, "end": 2930.7, "text": " Which leaves me with a final thought for you to mull over.", "tokens": [51174, 3013, 5510, 385, 365, 257, 2572, 1194, 337, 291, 281, 275, 858, 670, 13, 51288], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12196461538250526, "compression_ratio": 1.6833976833976834, "no_speech_prob": 1.958287698666794e-12}, {"id": 844, "seek": 291224, "start": 2931.8399999999997, "end": 2936.68, "text": " If the mathematical space of all our choices, our categories, and our statistical observations", "tokens": [51345, 759, 264, 18894, 1901, 295, 439, 527, 7994, 11, 527, 10479, 11, 293, 527, 22820, 18163, 51587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12196461538250526, "compression_ratio": 1.6833976833976834, "no_speech_prob": 1.958287698666794e-12}, {"id": 845, "seek": 293668, "start": 2936.68, "end": 2941.94, "text": " is literally a sphere, and a sphere mathematically cannot be perfectly smoothed out", "tokens": [50365, 307, 3736, 257, 16687, 11, 293, 257, 16687, 44003, 2644, 312, 6239, 5508, 292, 484, 50628], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12210852524329877, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760990161236334e-12}, {"id": 846, "seek": 293668, "start": 2941.94, "end": 2945.8599999999997, "text": " without leaving a curvature defect, does that mean human misunderstandings?", "tokens": [50628, 1553, 5012, 257, 37638, 16445, 11, 775, 300, 914, 1952, 35736, 1109, 30, 50824], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12210852524329877, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760990161236334e-12}, {"id": 847, "seek": 293668, "start": 2946.3799999999997, "end": 2951.46, "text": " The blurring of nuanced ideas and the inability to ever perfectly communicate our thoughts", "tokens": [50850, 440, 14257, 2937, 295, 45115, 3487, 293, 264, 33162, 281, 1562, 6239, 7890, 527, 4598, 51104], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12210852524329877, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760990161236334e-12}, {"id": 848, "seek": 293668, "start": 2951.46, "end": 2955.9199999999996, "text": " are not flaws in our psychology, but hard-coded geometric features of the universe.", "tokens": [51104, 366, 406, 27108, 294, 527, 15105, 11, 457, 1152, 12, 66, 12340, 33246, 4122, 295, 264, 6445, 13, 51327], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12210852524329877, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.7760990161236334e-12}, {"id": 849, "seek": 293668, "start": 2955.9199999999996, "end": 2959.9