compression_ratio": 1.6609589041095891, "no_speech_prob": 1.543107655543885e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 5696, "start": 79.52, "end": 84.96000000000001, "text": " you start mistaking the quirks of your map for the literal laws of physics.", "tokens": [51493, 291, 722, 3544, 2456, 264, 35645, 1694, 295, 428, 4471, 337, 264, 20411, 6064, 295, 10649, 13, 51765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11754409665983867, "compression_ratio": 1.6609589041095891, "no_speech_prob": 1.543107655543885e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 8496, "start": 84.96, "end": 87.64, "text": " And that is exactly what we are getting into today.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 300, 307, 2293, 437, 321, 366, 1242, 666, 965, 13, 50499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12952443092100083, "compression_ratio": 1.6187290969899666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4725783526597924e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 8496, "start": 87.75999999999999, "end": 90.89999999999999, "text": " We are taking a deep dive into a stack of source material", "tokens": [50505, 492, 366, 1940, 257, 2452, 9192, 666, 257, 8630, 295, 4009, 2527, 50662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12952443092100083, "compression_ratio": 1.6187290969899666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4725783526597924e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 8496, "start": 90.89999999999999, "end": 93.25999999999999, "text": " that completely exposes this illusion.", "tokens": [50662, 300, 2584, 1278, 4201, 341, 18854, 13, 50780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12952443092100083, "compression_ratio": 1.6187290969899666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4725783526597924e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 8496, "start": 93.63999999999999, "end": 98.82, "text": " It's a really mind-bending mathematical and philosophical monograph.", "tokens": [50799, 467, 311, 257, 534, 1575, 12, 65, 2029, 18894, 293, 25066, 1108, 3108, 13, 51058], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12952443092100083, "compression_ratio": 1.6187290969899666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4725783526597924e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 8496, "start": 99.19999999999999, "end": 103.32, "text": " It's called Geometry as Computational Infrastructure by a Flixson independent researcher.", "tokens": [51077, 467, 311, 1219, 2876, 34730, 382, 37804, 1478, 38425, 2885, 538, 257, 3235, 970, 3015, 6695, 21751, 13, 51283], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12952443092100083, "compression_ratio": 1.6187290969899666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4725783526597924e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 8496, "start": 103.46, "end": 103.67999999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51290, 1779, 13, 51301], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12952443092100083, "compression_ratio": 1.6187290969899666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4725783526597924e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 8496, "start": 103.83999999999999, "end": 106.13999999999999, "text": " And our mission for this deep dive is ambitious.", "tokens": [51309, 400, 527, 4447, 337, 341, 2452, 9192, 307, 20239, 13, 51424], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12952443092100083, "compression_ratio": 1.6187290969899666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4725783526597924e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 8496, "start": 106.33999999999999, "end": 111.41999999999999, "text": " We want to fundamentally rewire how you think about space, about data, and structure.", "tokens": [51434, 492, 528, 281, 17879, 319, 42689, 577, 291, 519, 466, 1901, 11, 466, 1412, 11, 293, 3877, 13, 51688], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12952443092100083, "compression_ratio": 1.6187290969899666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4725783526597924e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 8496, "start": 111.53999999999999, "end": 112.28, "text": " It's going to get deep.", "tokens": [51694, 467, 311, 516, 281, 483, 2452, 13, 51731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12952443092100083, "compression_ratio": 1.6187290969899666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4725783526597924e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 8496, "start": 112.86, "end": 113.47999999999999, "text": " Very deep.", "tokens": [51760, 4372, 2452, 13, 51791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12952443092100083, "compression_ratio": 1.6187290969899666, "no_speech_prob": 1.4725783526597924e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 11348, "start": 113.48, "end": 117.38000000000001, "text": " We're going to explore how choosing a coordinate system", "tokens": [50365, 492, 434, 516, 281, 6839, 577, 10875, 257, 15670, 1185, 50560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14539787832614595, "compression_ratio": 1.5723905723905724, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612936291042878e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 11348, "start": 117.38000000000001, "end": 120.0, "text": " is actually this intricate optimization game.", "tokens": [50560, 307, 767, 341, 38015, 19618, 1216, 13, 50691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14539787832614595, "compression_ratio": 1.5723905723905724, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612936291042878e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 11348, "start": 120.42, "end": 123.12, "text": " We'll look at why the specific shape of a sphere", "tokens": [50712, 492, 603, 574, 412, 983, 264, 2685, 3909, 295, 257, 16687, 50847], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14539787832614595, "compression_ratio": 1.5723905723905724, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612936291042878e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 11348, "start": 123.12, "end": 126.94, "text": " keeps secretly dictating the math of, well,", "tokens": [50847, 5965, 22611, 12569, 990, 264, 5221, 295, 11, 731, 11, 51038], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14539787832614595, "compression_ratio": 1.5723905723905724, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612936291042878e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 11348, "start": 127.14, "end": 131.04, "text": " everything from physical fields to abstract human decision-making.", "tokens": [51048, 1203, 490, 4001, 7909, 281, 12649, 1952, 3537, 12, 12402, 13, 51243], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14539787832614595, "compression_ratio": 1.5723905723905724, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612936291042878e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 11348, "start": 131.34, "end": 131.52, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51258, 865, 13, 51267], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14539787832614595, "compression_ratio": 1.5723905723905724, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612936291042878e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 11348, "start": 131.64000000000001, "end": 132.72, "text": " And maybe most importantly,", "tokens": [51273, 400, 1310, 881, 8906, 11, 51327], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14539787832614595, "compression_ratio": 1.5723905723905724, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612936291042878e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 11348, "start": 132.82, "end": 135.34, "text": " we'll discover how boundaries aren't just inert walls.", "tokens": [51332, 321, 603, 4411, 577, 13180, 3212, 380, 445, 25832, 7920, 13, 51458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14539787832614595, "compression_ratio": 1.5723905723905724, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612936291042878e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 11348, "start": 135.5, "end": 138.92000000000002, "text": " They are active computers constantly calculating the universe.", "tokens": [51466, 814, 366, 4967, 10807, 6460, 28258, 264, 6445, 13, 51637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14539787832614595, "compression_ratio": 1.5723905723905724, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612936291042878e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 11348, "start": 139.24, "end": 141.22, "text": " The scope of this text is just massive.", "tokens": [51653, 440, 11923, 295, 341, 2487, 307, 445, 5994, 13, 51752], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14539787832614595, "compression_ratio": 1.5723905723905724, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612936291042878e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 11348, "start": 141.48000000000002, "end": 142.18, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [51765, 467, 534, 307, 13, 51800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14539787832614595, "compression_ratio": 1.5723905723905724, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612936291042878e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 14218, "start": 142.18, "end": 146.3, "text": " What the author does here is pull back the curtain to show these hidden structural connections", "tokens": [50365, 708, 264, 3793, 775, 510, 307, 2235, 646, 264, 26789, 281, 855, 613, 7633, 15067, 9271, 50571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12616322257302023, "compression_ratio": 1.5024630541871922, "no_speech_prob": 1.931406206842623e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 14218, "start": 146.3, "end": 149.4, "text": " between fields you would normally never put in the same room together.", "tokens": [50571, 1296, 7909, 291, 576, 5646, 1128, 829, 294, 264, 912, 1808, 1214, 13, 50726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12616322257302023, "compression_ratio": 1.5024630541871922, "no_speech_prob": 1.931406206842623e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 14218, "start": 149.52, "end": 150.44, "text": " Like what kind of fields?", "tokens": [50732, 1743, 437, 733, 295, 7909, 30, 50778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12616322257302023, "compression_ratio": 1.5024630541871922, "no_speech_prob": 1.931406206842623e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 14218, "start": 150.6, "end": 152.22, "text": " Well, over the course of this discussion,", "tokens": [50786, 1042, 11, 670, 264, 1164, 295, 341, 5017, 11, 50867], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12616322257302023, "compression_ratio": 1.5024630541871922, "no_speech_prob": 1.931406206842623e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 14218, "start": 152.38, "end": 155.58, "text": " we're going to connect planetary engineering to statistical probability", "tokens": [50875, 321, 434, 516, 281, 1745, 35788, 7043, 281, 22820, 8482, 51035], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12616322257302023, "compression_ratio": 1.5024630541871922, "no_speech_prob": 1.931406206842623e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 15558, "start": 155.58, "end": 161.54000000000002, "text": " and biological tissue regeneration to the pure mathematics of irreversible choices.", "tokens": [50365, 293, 13910, 12404, 43813, 281, 264, 6075, 18666, 295, 16014, 840, 964, 7994, 13, 50663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26815327731045807, "compression_ratio": 1.4893617021276595, "no_speech_prob": 1.7865441114331415e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 15558, "start": 161.54000000000002, "end": 163.64000000000001, "text": " Which sounds insane until you read the math.", "tokens": [50663, 3013, 3263, 10838, 1826, 291, 1401, 264, 5221, 13, 50768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26815327731045807, "compression_ratio": 1.4893617021276595, "no_speech_prob": 1.7865441114331415e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 15558, "start": 163.72000000000003, "end": 164.16000000000003, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50772, 7587, 13, 50794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26815327731045807, "compression_ratio": 1.4893617021276595, "no_speech_prob": 1.7865441114331415e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 15558, "start": 164.64000000000001, "end": 168.46, "text": " And the anchor for all of this, the hidden gear turning all this machinery,", "tokens": [50818, 400, 264, 18487, 337, 439, 295, 341, 11, 264, 7633, 7394, 6246, 439, 341, 27302, 11, 51009], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26815327731045807, "compression_ratio": 1.4893617021276595, "no_speech_prob": 1.7865441114331415e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 15558, "start": 168.72000000000003, "end": 172.44, "text": " is a very specific, rigorous way of looking at spherical geometry.", "tokens": [51022, 307, 257, 588, 2685, 11, 29882, 636, 295, 1237, 412, 37300, 18426, 13, 51208], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26815327731045807, "compression_ratio": 1.4893617021276595, "no_speech_prob": 1.7865441114331415e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 17244, "start": 172.44, "end": 177.06, "text": " I have to admit, reading through these sources, it was a true matrix moment for me.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 362, 281, 9796, 11, 3760, 807, 613, 7139, 11, 309, 390, 257, 2074, 8141, 1623, 337, 385, 13, 50596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17463225903718368, "compression_ratio": 1.5663716814159292, "no_speech_prob": 2.4803171669307567e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 17244, "start": 177.28, "end": 181.0, "text": " It really felt like taking the red pill and unmasking reality.", "tokens": [50607, 467, 534, 2762, 411, 1940, 264, 2182, 8100, 293, 517, 3799, 5092, 4103, 13, 50793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17463225903718368, "compression_ratio": 1.5663716814159292, "no_speech_prob": 2.4803171669307567e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 17244, "start": 181.12, "end": 183.2, "text": " It completely upends how we're taught math in school.", "tokens": [50799, 467, 2584, 493, 2581, 577, 321, 434, 5928, 5221, 294, 1395, 13, 50903], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17463225903718368, "compression_ratio": 1.5663716814159292, "no_speech_prob": 2.4803171669307567e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 17244, "start": 183.44, "end": 183.76, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50915, 1079, 13, 50931], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17463225903718368, "compression_ratio": 1.5663716814159292, "no_speech_prob": 2.4803171669307567e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 17244, "start": 184.02, "end": 188.35999999999999, "text": " We're taught math is this rigid, objective, ultimate truth.", "tokens": [50944, 492, 434, 5928, 5221, 307, 341, 22195, 11, 10024, 11, 9705, 3494, 13, 51161], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17463225903718368, "compression_ratio": 1.5663716814159292, "no_speech_prob": 2.4803171669307567e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 17244, "start": 189.0, "end": 189.26, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51193, 865, 13, 51206], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17463225903718368, "compression_ratio": 1.5663716814159292, "no_speech_prob": 2.4803171669307567e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 17244, "start": 189.48, "end": 194.34, "text": " But this text argues our foundational tools are far more like chosen perspectives.", "tokens": [51217, 583, 341, 2487, 38218, 527, 32195, 3873, 366, 1400, 544, 411, 8614, 16766, 13, 51460], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17463225903718368, "compression_ratio": 1.5663716814159292, "no_speech_prob": 2.4803171669307567e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 19434, "start": 194.34, "end": 196.20000000000002, "text": " So let's unpack this.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 718, 311, 26699, 341, 13, 50458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17217273142800402, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922409874954968e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 19434, "start": 196.44, "end": 201.4, "text": " Let's start with this core idea that coordinates are interfaces, not reality.", "tokens": [50470, 961, 311, 722, 365, 341, 4965, 1558, 300, 21056, 366, 28416, 11, 406, 4103, 13, 50718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17217273142800402, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922409874954968e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 19434, "start": 201.72, "end": 203.04, "text": " The author brings up a circle.", "tokens": [50734, 440, 3793, 5607, 493, 257, 6329, 13, 50800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17217273142800402, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922409874954968e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 19434, "start": 203.36, "end": 203.46, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50816, 865, 13, 50821], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17217273142800402, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922409874954968e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 19434, "start": 203.58, "end": 205.04, "text": " A simple geometric circle.", "tokens": [50827, 316, 2199, 33246, 6329, 13, 50900], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17217273142800402, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922409874954968e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 19434, "start": 205.3, "end": 205.48000000000002, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50913, 1779, 13, 50922], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17217273142800402, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922409874954968e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 19434, "start": 205.64000000000001, "end": 210.1, "text": " And they say a point on a circle has a location, but it does not inherently have coordinates.", "tokens": [50930, 400, 436, 584, 257, 935, 322, 257, 6329, 575, 257, 4914, 11, 457, 309, 775, 406, 27993, 362, 21056, 13, 51153], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17217273142800402, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922409874954968e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 19434, "start": 210.5, "end": 211.36, "text": " No, it doesn't.", "tokens": [51173, 883, 11, 309, 1177, 380, 13, 51216], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17217273142800402, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922409874954968e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 19434, "start": 211.58, "end": 218.12, "text": " Coordinates only exist once an observer, you, me, a computer, chooses an origin and a reference direction.", "tokens": [51227, 39620, 1024, 787, 2514, 1564, 364, 27878, 11, 291, 11, 385, 11, 257, 3820, 11, 25963, 364, 4957, 293, 257, 6408, 3513, 13, 51554], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17217273142800402, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922409874954968e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 19434, "start": 218.28, "end": 220.76, "text": " That is the essential starting point for all of this.", "tokens": [51562, 663, 307, 264, 7115, 2891, 935, 337, 439, 295, 341, 13, 51686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17217273142800402, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922409874954968e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 19434, "start": 220.88, "end": 223.6, "text": " Think about a physical circle drawn on a blank piece of paper.", "tokens": [51692, 6557, 466, 257, 4001, 6329, 10117, 322, 257, 8247, 2522, 295, 3035, 13, 51828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17217273142800402, "compression_ratio": 1.6578947368421053, "no_speech_prob": 1.5922409874954968e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 22360, "start": 223.6, "end": 227.07999999999998, "text": " Remember, the points on that circle exist in relation to one another.", "tokens": [50365, 5459, 11, 264, 2793, 322, 300, 6329, 2514, 294, 9721, 281, 472, 1071, 13, 50539], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21100256872958825, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.4273135624798261e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 22360, "start": 227.46, "end": 228.34, "text": " They have adjacency.", "tokens": [50558, 814, 362, 22940, 3020, 13, 50602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21100256872958825, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.4273135624798261e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 22360, "start": 228.48, "end": 229.18, "text": " They have continuity.", "tokens": [50609, 814, 362, 23807, 13, 50644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21100256872958825, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.4273135624798261e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 22360, "start": 229.66, "end": 231.28, "text": " The circle has a circumference.", "tokens": [50668, 440, 6329, 575, 257, 7125, 5158, 13, 50749], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21100256872958825, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.4273135624798261e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 22360, "start": 231.74, "end": 232.18, "text": " Just naturally.", "tokens": [50772, 1449, 8195, 13, 50794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21100256872958825, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.4273135624798261e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 22360, "start": 232.54, "end": 232.72, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50812, 1779, 13, 50821], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21100256872958825, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.4273135624798261e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 22360, "start": 232.92, "end": 238.45999999999998, "text": " All of those things are true properties of the shades, entirely independent of any numbers or grids.", "tokens": [50831, 1057, 295, 729, 721, 366, 2074, 7221, 295, 264, 20639, 11, 7696, 6695, 295, 604, 3547, 420, 677, 3742, 13, 51108], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21100256872958825, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.4273135624798261e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 22360, "start": 238.98, "end": 243.44, "text": " Now, if we want to do math with that circle, we introduce a coordinate chart.", "tokens": [51134, 823, 11, 498, 321, 528, 281, 360, 5221, 365, 300, 6329, 11, 321, 5366, 257, 15670, 6927, 13, 51357], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21100256872958825, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.4273135624798261e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 22360, "start": 244.22, "end": 246.88, "text": " Mathematically, the text calls this an injective map.", "tokens": [51396, 15776, 40197, 11, 264, 2487, 5498, 341, 364, 10711, 488, 4471, 13, 51529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21100256872958825, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.4273135624798261e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 22360, "start": 247.1, "end": 248.2, "text": " Okay, let's pause right there.", "tokens": [51540, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 10465, 558, 456, 13, 51595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21100256872958825, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.4273135624798261e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 22360, "start": 248.82, "end": 249.66, "text": " Injective map.", "tokens": [51626, 682, 1020, 488, 4471, 13, 51668], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21100256872958825, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.4273135624798261e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 24966, "start": 249.66, "end": 254.6, "text": " If I'm listening to this on my drive to work, that phrase is just going to bounce right off my brain.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 286, 478, 4764, 281, 341, 322, 452, 3332, 281, 589, 11, 300, 9535, 307, 445, 516, 281, 15894, 558, 766, 452, 3567, 13, 50612], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1715012040249137, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 1.1422796302590355e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 24966, "start": 254.82, "end": 255.64, "text": " Break that down for me.", "tokens": [50623, 16925, 300, 760, 337, 385, 13, 50664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1715012040249137, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 1.1422796302590355e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 24966, "start": 255.85999999999999, "end": 256.36, "text": " Fair enough.", "tokens": [50675, 12157, 1547, 13, 50700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1715012040249137, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 1.1422796302590355e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 24966, "start": 256.48, "end": 257.78, "text": " Let's strip away the jargon.", "tokens": [50706, 961, 311, 12828, 1314, 264, 15181, 10660, 13, 50771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1715012040249137, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 1.1422796302590355e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 24966, "start": 258.4, "end": 261.96, "text": " Think of an injective map simply as a very strict labeling device.", "tokens": [50802, 6557, 295, 364, 10711, 488, 4471, 2935, 382, 257, 588, 10910, 40244, 4302, 13, 50980], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1715012040249137, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 1.1422796302590355e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 24966, "start": 262.78, "end": 264.15999999999997, "text": " Imagine you have a sticker gun.", "tokens": [51021, 11739, 291, 362, 257, 20400, 3874, 13, 51090], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1715012040249137, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 1.1422796302590355e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 24966, "start": 264.48, "end": 264.74, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51106, 1033, 13, 51119], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1715012040249137, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 1.1422796302590355e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 24966, "start": 264.86, "end": 265.56, "text": " A sticker gun.", "tokens": [51125, 316, 20400, 3874, 13, 51160], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1715012040249137, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 1.1422796302590355e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 26556, "start": 265.56, "end": 269.3, "text": " And every sticker has a unique pair of numbers printed on it.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 633, 20400, 575, 257, 3845, 6119, 295, 3547, 13567, 322, 309, 13, 50552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15623319874639097, "compression_ratio": 1.6765799256505576, "no_speech_prob": 1.3198901607086588e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 26556, "start": 269.72, "end": 274.8, "text": " An injective map means you are walking around the circle and placing one unique sticker on every single point.", "tokens": [50573, 1107, 10711, 488, 4471, 1355, 291, 366, 4494, 926, 264, 6329, 293, 17221, 472, 3845, 20400, 322, 633, 2167, 935, 13, 50827], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15623319874639097, "compression_ratio": 1.6765799256505576, "no_speech_prob": 1.3198901607086588e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 26556, "start": 275.3, "end": 278.14, "text": " No two points get the same sticker and no point is left out.", "tokens": [50852, 883, 732, 2793, 483, 264, 912, 20400, 293, 572, 935, 307, 1411, 484, 13, 50994], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15623319874639097, "compression_ratio": 1.6765799256505576, "no_speech_prob": 1.3198901607086588e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 26556, "start": 278.26, "end": 278.58, "text": " Got it.", "tokens": [51000, 5803, 309, 13, 51016], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15623319874639097, "compression_ratio": 1.6765799256505576, "no_speech_prob": 1.3198901607086588e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 26556, "start": 278.66, "end": 280.02, "text": " So I'm just labeling locations.", "tokens": [51020, 407, 286, 478, 445, 40244, 9253, 13, 51088], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15623319874639097, "compression_ratio": 1.6765799256505576, "no_speech_prob": 1.3198901607086588e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 26556, "start": 280.26, "end": 280.68, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51100, 7587, 13, 51121], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15623319874639097, "compression_ratio": 1.6765799256505576, "no_speech_prob": 1.3198901607086588e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 26556, "start": 281.2, "end": 285.94, "text": " You are assigning a numerical identity to a location so you can run calculations on it.", "tokens": [51147, 509, 366, 49602, 257, 29054, 6575, 281, 257, 4914, 370, 291, 393, 1190, 20448, 322, 309, 13, 51384], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15623319874639097, "compression_ratio": 1.6765799256505576, "no_speech_prob": 1.3198901607086588e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 26556, "start": 286.4, "end": 290.42, "text": " But, and the author stresses this heavily, the sticker is not the circle.", "tokens": [51407, 583, 11, 293, 264, 3793, 27732, 341, 10950, 11, 264, 20400, 307, 406, 264, 6329, 13, 51608], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15623319874639097, "compression_ratio": 1.6765799256505576, "no_speech_prob": 1.3198901607086588e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 26556, "start": 290.62, "end": 290.86, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51618, 1779, 13, 51630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15623319874639097, "compression_ratio": 1.6765799256505576, "no_speech_prob": 1.3198901607086588e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 29086, "start": 290.86, "end": 294.64, "text": " The coordinate system is a computational interface between you and the space.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 15670, 1185, 307, 257, 28270, 9226, 1296, 291, 293, 264, 1901, 13, 50554], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11183804839196866, "compression_ratio": 1.7408536585365855, "no_speech_prob": 1.2891187683300442e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 29086, "start": 294.84000000000003, "end": 295.46000000000004, "text": " It's a tool.", "tokens": [50564, 467, 311, 257, 2290, 13, 50595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11183804839196866, "compression_ratio": 1.7408536585365855, "no_speech_prob": 1.2891187683300442e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 29086, "start": 295.72, "end": 298.6, "text": " It is not a physical property of the space itself.", "tokens": [50608, 467, 307, 406, 257, 4001, 4707, 295, 264, 1901, 2564, 13, 50752], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11183804839196866, "compression_ratio": 1.7408536585365855, "no_speech_prob": 1.2891187683300442e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 29086, "start": 299.02000000000004, "end": 305.36, "text": " I was trying to wrap my head around this and the best analogy I could come up with is your smartphone's operating system.", "tokens": [50773, 286, 390, 1382, 281, 7019, 452, 1378, 926, 341, 293, 264, 1151, 21663, 286, 727, 808, 493, 365, 307, 428, 13307, 311, 7447, 1185, 13, 51090], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11183804839196866, "compression_ratio": 1.7408536585365855, "no_speech_prob": 1.2891187683300442e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 29086, "start": 305.58000000000004, "end": 306.44, "text": " Oh, I like that.", "tokens": [51101, 876, 11, 286, 411, 300, 13, 51144], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11183804839196866, "compression_ratio": 1.7408536585365855, "no_speech_prob": 1.2891187683300442e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 29086, "start": 306.64, "end": 308.18, "text": " Like, let's say you take a picture of your dog.", "tokens": [51154, 1743, 11, 718, 311, 584, 291, 747, 257, 3036, 295, 428, 3000, 13, 51231], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11183804839196866, "compression_ratio": 1.7408536585365855, "no_speech_prob": 1.2891187683300442e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 29086, "start": 309.02000000000004, "end": 314.58000000000004, "text": " If you look at that photo on an iOS device versus an Android device, they display it totally differently, right?", "tokens": [51273, 759, 291, 574, 412, 300, 5052, 322, 364, 17430, 4302, 5717, 364, 8853, 4302, 11, 436, 4674, 309, 3879, 7614, 11, 558, 30, 51551], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11183804839196866, "compression_ratio": 1.7408536585365855, "no_speech_prob": 1.2891187683300442e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 29086, "start": 314.64, "end": 317.42, "text": " They have different menus, different file structures, different zoom gestures.", "tokens": [51554, 814, 362, 819, 30347, 11, 819, 3991, 9227, 11, 819, 8863, 28475, 13, 51693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11183804839196866, "compression_ratio": 1.7408536585365855, "no_speech_prob": 1.2891187683300442e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 29086, "start": 317.64, "end": 320.12, "text": " Yes, the interface behaves completely differently.", "tokens": [51704, 1079, 11, 264, 9226, 36896, 2584, 7614, 13, 51828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11183804839196866, "compression_ratio": 1.7408536585365855, "no_speech_prob": 1.2891187683300442e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 32012, "start": 320.12, "end": 324.94, "text": " But the photo itself, the raw pixel data, hasn't changed at all.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 5052, 2564, 11, 264, 8936, 19261, 1412, 11, 6132, 380, 3105, 412, 439, 13, 50606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08927299037124171, "compression_ratio": 1.781512605042017, "no_speech_prob": 1.681574692859178e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 32012, "start": 325.24, "end": 333.38, "text": " If we sit there arguing over whether a photo is inherently an iOS photo or an Android photo, we are totally missing the point.", "tokens": [50621, 759, 321, 1394, 456, 19697, 670, 1968, 257, 5052, 307, 27993, 364, 17430, 5052, 420, 364, 8853, 5052, 11, 321, 366, 3879, 5361, 264, 935, 13, 51028], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08927299037124171, "compression_ratio": 1.781512605042017, "no_speech_prob": 1.681574692859178e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 32012, "start": 333.58, "end": 335.84000000000003, "text": " We're mistaking the operating system for the hardware.", "tokens": [51038, 492, 434, 3544, 2456, 264, 7447, 1185, 337, 264, 8837, 13, 51151], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08927299037124171, "compression_ratio": 1.781512605042017, "no_speech_prob": 1.681574692859178e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 32012, "start": 336.18, "end": 338.1, "text": " That captures the mechanics of it perfectly.", "tokens": [51168, 663, 27986, 264, 12939, 295, 309, 6239, 13, 51264], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08927299037124171, "compression_ratio": 1.781512605042017, "no_speech_prob": 1.681574692859178e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 32012, "start": 338.36, "end": 344.46, "text": " And mistaking the OS for the hardware leads to what the author calls the coordinate artifact danger.", "tokens": [51277, 400, 3544, 2456, 264, 12731, 337, 264, 8837, 6689, 281, 437, 264, 3793, 5498, 264, 15670, 34806, 4330, 13, 51582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08927299037124171, "compression_ratio": 1.781512605042017, "no_speech_prob": 1.681574692859178e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 32012, "start": 344.62, "end": 346.14, "text": " The coordinate artifact danger.", "tokens": [51590, 440, 15670, 34806, 4330, 13, 51666], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08927299037124171, "compression_ratio": 1.781512605042017, "no_speech_prob": 1.681574692859178e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 34614, "start": 346.14, "end": 350.96, "text": " Yes, it's this recurring, deeply entrenched error in science and math.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 11, 309, 311, 341, 32279, 11, 8760, 948, 42388, 6713, 294, 3497, 293, 5221, 13, 50606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17767890691757202, "compression_ratio": 1.0, "no_speech_prob": 1.9279142084854817e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 35096, "start": 350.96, "end": 360.79999999999995, "text": " It happens when features discovered in a coordinate representation are blindly assumed to be physical realities, when in fact, they might just be glitches in the labeling scheme.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 2314, 562, 4122, 6941, 294, 257, 15670, 10290, 366, 47744, 15895, 281, 312, 4001, 27785, 11, 562, 294, 1186, 11, 436, 1062, 445, 312, 23552, 279, 294, 264, 40244, 12232, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10612876547707452, "compression_ratio": 1.4764150943396226, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013964022372097e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 35096, "start": 360.94, "end": 365.14, "text": " The text gives this amazing real-world example of this with the North and South Poles.", "tokens": [50864, 440, 2487, 2709, 341, 2243, 957, 12, 13217, 1365, 295, 341, 365, 264, 4067, 293, 4242, 3635, 279, 13, 51074], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10612876547707452, "compression_ratio": 1.4764150943396226, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013964022372097e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 35096, "start": 365.34, "end": 367.03999999999996, "text": " Oh, the map projection example.", "tokens": [51084, 876, 11, 264, 4471, 22743, 1365, 13, 51169], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10612876547707452, "compression_ratio": 1.4764150943396226, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013964022372097e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 35096, "start": 367.14, "end": 367.79999999999995, "text": " It's brilliant.", "tokens": [51174, 467, 311, 10248, 13, 51207], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10612876547707452, "compression_ratio": 1.4764150943396226, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013964022372097e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 36780, "start": 367.8, "end": 368.2, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50385], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16659026215041894, "compression_ratio": 1.4314720812182742, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656589723970885e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 36780, "start": 368.36, "end": 377.6, "text": " If you picture a standard flat map of the Earth, you know, the Mercator projection from middle school, the poles look completely distorted.", "tokens": [50393, 759, 291, 3036, 257, 3832, 4962, 4471, 295, 264, 4755, 11, 291, 458, 11, 264, 18897, 1639, 22743, 490, 2808, 1395, 11, 264, 24760, 574, 2584, 33431, 13, 50855], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16659026215041894, "compression_ratio": 1.4314720812182742, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656589723970885e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 36780, "start": 378.0, "end": 383.40000000000003, "text": " Antarctica is just smeared across the entire bottom edge, looking bigger than all the other continents combined.", "tokens": [50875, 39866, 307, 445, 41818, 1642, 2108, 264, 2302, 2767, 4691, 11, 1237, 3801, 813, 439, 264, 661, 38598, 9354, 13, 51145], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16659026215041894, "compression_ratio": 1.4314720812182742, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656589723970885e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 36780, "start": 383.54, "end": 384.18, "text": " Which it isn't.", "tokens": [51152, 3013, 309, 1943, 380, 13, 51184], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16659026215041894, "compression_ratio": 1.4314720812182742, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656589723970885e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 36780, "start": 384.44, "end": 384.66, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51197, 1779, 13, 51208], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16659026215041894, "compression_ratio": 1.4314720812182742, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656589723970885e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 38466, "start": 384.66, "end": 393.04, "text": " And mathematically, in a standard spherical coordinate system, using latitude and longitude, the math actually breaks down at the exact North Pole.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 44003, 11, 294, 257, 3832, 37300, 15670, 1185, 11, 1228, 45436, 293, 938, 4377, 11, 264, 5221, 767, 9857, 760, 412, 264, 1900, 4067, 34212, 13, 50784], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12471454719017291, "compression_ratio": 1.7050359712230216, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160390525083666e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 38466, "start": 393.36, "end": 393.8, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [50800, 467, 775, 13, 50822], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12471454719017291, "compression_ratio": 1.7050359712230216, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160390525083666e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 38466, "start": 393.90000000000003, "end": 394.90000000000003, "text": " It completely fails.", "tokens": [50827, 467, 2584, 18199, 13, 50877], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12471454719017291, "compression_ratio": 1.7050359712230216, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160390525083666e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 38466, "start": 395.3, "end": 399.38000000000005, "text": " Let's look at why that happens mathematically, but, you know, conversationally.", "tokens": [50897, 961, 311, 574, 412, 983, 300, 2314, 44003, 11, 457, 11, 291, 458, 11, 3761, 379, 13, 51101], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12471454719017291, "compression_ratio": 1.7050359712230216, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160390525083666e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 38466, "start": 399.72, "end": 400.06, "text": " Please.", "tokens": [51118, 2555, 13, 51135], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12471454719017291, "compression_ratio": 1.7050359712230216, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160390525083666e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 38466, "start": 400.24, "end": 404.84000000000003, "text": " So, longitude lines are the vertical lines running from the North Pole to the South Pole.", "tokens": [51144, 407, 11, 938, 4377, 3876, 366, 264, 9429, 3876, 2614, 490, 264, 4067, 34212, 281, 264, 4242, 34212, 13, 51374], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12471454719017291, "compression_ratio": 1.7050359712230216, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160390525083666e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 38466, "start": 405.44000000000005, "end": 410.3, "text": " To define your longitude, you need to be a certain angular distance away from the Prime Meridian.", "tokens": [51404, 1407, 6964, 428, 938, 4377, 11, 291, 643, 281, 312, 257, 1629, 24413, 4560, 1314, 490, 264, 9655, 6124, 34681, 13, 51647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12471454719017291, "compression_ratio": 1.7050359712230216, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160390525083666e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 38466, "start": 410.44000000000005, "end": 411.24, "text": " Okay, simple enough.", "tokens": [51654, 1033, 11, 2199, 1547, 13, 51694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12471454719017291, "compression_ratio": 1.7050359712230216, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160390525083666e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 41124, "start": 411.24, "end": 417.96000000000004, "text": " But if you are standing exactly on the North Pole, every single line of longitude converges underneath your boots.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 498, 291, 366, 4877, 2293, 322, 264, 4067, 34212, 11, 633, 2167, 1622, 295, 938, 4377, 9652, 2880, 7223, 428, 15194, 13, 50701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12156842648983002, "compression_ratio": 1.706896551724138, "no_speech_prob": 1.8321891313149985e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 41124, "start": 418.12, "end": 418.62, "text": " Oh, right.", "tokens": [50709, 876, 11, 558, 13, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12156842648983002, "compression_ratio": 1.706896551724138, "no_speech_prob": 1.8321891313149985e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 41124, "start": 418.8, "end": 419.98, "text": " Because they all meet at the top.", "tokens": [50743, 1436, 436, 439, 1677, 412, 264, 1192, 13, 50802], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12156842648983002, "compression_ratio": 1.706896551724138, "no_speech_prob": 1.8321891313149985e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 41124, "start": 420.1, "end": 420.56, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50808, 7587, 13, 50831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12156842648983002, "compression_ratio": 1.706896551724138, "no_speech_prob": 1.8321891313149985e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 41124, "start": 420.96000000000004, "end": 426.3, "text": " So, the metric coefficient that multiplies the longitude essentially vanishes to zero at that exact spot.", "tokens": [50851, 407, 11, 264, 20678, 17619, 300, 12788, 530, 264, 938, 4377, 4476, 3161, 16423, 281, 4018, 412, 300, 1900, 4008, 13, 51118], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12156842648983002, "compression_ratio": 1.706896551724138, "no_speech_prob": 1.8321891313149985e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 41124, "start": 426.40000000000003, "end": 430.28000000000003, "text": " So, you literally can't assign a single longitude to the North Pole.", "tokens": [51123, 407, 11, 291, 3736, 393, 380, 6269, 257, 2167, 938, 4377, 281, 264, 4067, 34212, 13, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12156842648983002, "compression_ratio": 1.706896551724138, "no_speech_prob": 1.8321891313149985e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 41124, "start": 430.46000000000004, "end": 431.18, "text": " It's undefined.", "tokens": [51326, 467, 311, 674, 5666, 2001, 13, 51362], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12156842648983002, "compression_ratio": 1.706896551724138, "no_speech_prob": 1.8321891313149985e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 41124, "start": 431.36, "end": 431.8, "text": " Correct.", "tokens": [51371, 12753, 13, 51393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12156842648983002, "compression_ratio": 1.706896551724138, "no_speech_prob": 1.8321891313149985e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 41124, "start": 431.8, "end": 439.26, "text": " If you do a careless calculation using that specific grid, you end up with infinite or undefined quantities right at the pole.", "tokens": [51393, 759, 291, 360, 257, 46187, 17108, 1228, 300, 2685, 10748, 11, 291, 917, 493, 365, 13785, 420, 674, 5666, 2001, 22927, 558, 412, 264, 13208, 13, 51766], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12156842648983002, "compression_ratio": 1.706896551724138, "no_speech_prob": 1.8321891313149985e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 43926, "start": 439.26, "end": 449.36, "text": " And the danger here is the temptation for a physicist or a mathematician to look at their chalkboard, see that undefined result, and just declare AHA.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 4330, 510, 307, 264, 30423, 337, 257, 42466, 420, 257, 48281, 281, 574, 412, 641, 28660, 3787, 11, 536, 300, 674, 5666, 2001, 1874, 11, 293, 445, 19710, 316, 4983, 13, 50870], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13350698012339918, "compression_ratio": 1.5336787564766838, "no_speech_prob": 1.7411067162673155e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 43926, "start": 449.8, "end": 452.21999999999997, "text": " There is a physical singularity here.", "tokens": [50892, 821, 307, 257, 4001, 20010, 507, 510, 13, 51013], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13350698012339918, "compression_ratio": 1.5336787564766838, "no_speech_prob": 1.7411067162673155e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 43926, "start": 452.48, "end": 455.0, "text": " The laws of space and time break down at the top of the planet.", "tokens": [51026, 440, 6064, 295, 1901, 293, 565, 1821, 760, 412, 264, 1192, 295, 264, 5054, 13, 51152], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13350698012339918, "compression_ratio": 1.5336787564766838, "no_speech_prob": 1.7411067162673155e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 43926, "start": 455.2, "end": 455.71999999999997, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51162, 7587, 13, 51188], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13350698012339918, "compression_ratio": 1.5336787564766838, "no_speech_prob": 1.7411067162673155e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 43926, "start": 455.96, "end": 457.44, "text": " But there is no hole in the Earth.", "tokens": [51200, 583, 456, 307, 572, 5458, 294, 264, 4755, 13, 51274], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13350698012339918, "compression_ratio": 1.5336787564766838, "no_speech_prob": 1.7411067162673155e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 45744, "start": 457.44, "end": 462.64, "text": " If you put on a parka and walk to the North Pole, it's just a flat expanse of ice.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 829, 322, 257, 3884, 64, 293, 1792, 281, 264, 4067, 34212, 11, 309, 311, 445, 257, 4962, 1278, 47661, 295, 4435, 13, 50625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14002220187566977, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.2443267987174988e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 45744, "start": 462.82, "end": 463.66, "text": " Just normal ice.", "tokens": [50634, 1449, 2710, 4435, 13, 50676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14002220187566977, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.2443267987174988e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 45744, "start": 463.9, "end": 464.98, "text": " Just normal ice.", "tokens": [50688, 1449, 2710, 4435, 13, 50742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14002220187566977, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.2443267987174988e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 45744, "start": 465.46, "end": 470.04, "text": " The physical geometry of the space is perfectly smooth, ordinary, unbroken.", "tokens": [50766, 440, 4001, 18426, 295, 264, 1901, 307, 6239, 5508, 11, 10547, 11, 517, 37947, 13, 50995], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14002220187566977, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.2443267987174988e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 45744, "start": 470.74, "end": 473.48, "text": " The failure belongs entirely to the labeling scheme.", "tokens": [51030, 440, 7763, 12953, 7696, 281, 264, 40244, 12232, 13, 51167], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14002220187566977, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.2443267987174988e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 45744, "start": 473.84, "end": 479.64, "text": " The interface just cannot handle a point sitting exactly on the axis it uses to define its own rotation.", "tokens": [51185, 440, 9226, 445, 2644, 4813, 257, 935, 3798, 2293, 322, 264, 10298, 309, 4960, 281, 6964, 1080, 1065, 12447, 13, 51475], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14002220187566977, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.2443267987174988e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 45744, "start": 479.94, "end": 481.82, "text": " It is literally a glitch in the matrix.", "tokens": [51490, 467, 307, 3736, 257, 23552, 294, 264, 8141, 13, 51584], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14002220187566977, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.2443267987174988e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 45744, "start": 482.12, "end": 484.7, "text": " The math crashes, but reality is totally fine.", "tokens": [51599, 440, 5221, 28642, 11, 457, 4103, 307, 3879, 2489, 13, 51728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14002220187566977, "compression_ratio": 1.6428571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.2443267987174988e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 48470, "start": 484.7, "end": 493.62, "text": " And the text points out that if you just change the chart, if you take that mathematical sticker gun and center your coordinates on the equator instead of the poles, the singularity completely vanishes.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 2487, 2793, 484, 300, 498, 291, 445, 1319, 264, 6927, 11, 498, 291, 747, 300, 18894, 20400, 3874, 293, 3056, 428, 21056, 322, 264, 45544, 2602, 295, 264, 24760, 11, 264, 20010, 507, 2584, 3161, 16423, 13, 50811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08968077008686369, "compression_ratio": 1.697452229299363, "no_speech_prob": 1.36158272157072e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 48470, "start": 493.82, "end": 495.12, "text": " Because it was never there to begin with.", "tokens": [50821, 1436, 309, 390, 1128, 456, 281, 1841, 365, 13, 50886], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08968077008686369, "compression_ratio": 1.697452229299363, "no_speech_prob": 1.36158272157072e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 48470, "start": 495.36, "end": 497.92, "text": " And there is a deeper layer to that realization.", "tokens": [50898, 400, 456, 307, 257, 7731, 4583, 281, 300, 25138, 13, 51026], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08968077008686369, "compression_ratio": 1.697452229299363, "no_speech_prob": 1.36158272157072e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 48470, "start": 498.52, "end": 500.78, "text": " It's a discipline the text demands of us.", "tokens": [51056, 467, 311, 257, 13635, 264, 2487, 15107, 295, 505, 13, 51169], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08968077008686369, "compression_ratio": 1.697452229299363, "no_speech_prob": 1.36158272157072e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 48470, "start": 501.56, "end": 505.7, "text": " To avoid this trap, the author states a rigid diagnostic principle.", "tokens": [51208, 1407, 5042, 341, 11487, 11, 264, 3793, 4368, 257, 22195, 27897, 8665, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08968077008686369, "compression_ratio": 1.697452229299363, "no_speech_prob": 1.36158272157072e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 48470, "start": 506.4, "end": 512.12, "text": " A feature is only a genuine feature of the underlying space if it persists under a change of chart.", "tokens": [51450, 316, 4111, 307, 787, 257, 16699, 4111, 295, 264, 14217, 1901, 498, 309, 868, 1751, 833, 257, 1319, 295, 6927, 13, 51736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08968077008686369, "compression_ratio": 1.697452229299363, "no_speech_prob": 1.36158272157072e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 48470, "start": 512.36, "end": 513.58, "text": " Oh, that makes so much sense.", "tokens": [51748, 876, 11, 300, 1669, 370, 709, 2020, 13, 51809], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08968077008686369, "compression_ratio": 1.697452229299363, "no_speech_prob": 1.36158272157072e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 51358, "start": 513.58, "end": 519.96, "text": " Right. If you find a surprising anomaly in your data and it disappears the second you change your coordinate system, it was just geometry.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 759, 291, 915, 257, 8830, 42737, 294, 428, 1412, 293, 309, 25527, 264, 1150, 291, 1319, 428, 15670, 1185, 11, 309, 390, 445, 18426, 13, 50684], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08598381897498822, "compression_ratio": 1.6188524590163935, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158157068608346e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 51358, "start": 520.2, "end": 522.5, "text": " It was an artifact of your labels. It wasn't physics.", "tokens": [50696, 467, 390, 364, 34806, 295, 428, 16949, 13, 467, 2067, 380, 10649, 13, 50811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08598381897498822, "compression_ratio": 1.6188524590163935, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158157068608346e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 51358, "start": 522.7, "end": 524.5, "text": " The underlying reality didn't budge.", "tokens": [50821, 440, 14217, 4103, 994, 380, 3265, 432, 13, 50911], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08598381897498822, "compression_ratio": 1.6188524590163935, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158157068608346e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 51358, "start": 524.7, "end": 535.22, "text": " Exactly. We have to maintain the mathematical discipline of actively changing the chart to test reality rather than blindly trusting the first grid we throw over it.", "tokens": [50921, 7587, 13, 492, 362, 281, 6909, 264, 18894, 13635, 295, 13022, 4473, 264, 6927, 281, 1500, 4103, 2831, 813, 47744, 28235, 264, 700, 10748, 321, 3507, 670, 309, 13, 51447], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08598381897498822, "compression_ratio": 1.6188524590163935, "no_speech_prob": 1.4158157068608346e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 53522, "start": 535.22, "end": 539.82, "text": " I have to pause here because this challenges how we approach so much problem solving.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 362, 281, 10465, 510, 570, 341, 4759, 577, 321, 3109, 370, 709, 1154, 12606, 13, 50595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2078855514526367, "compression_ratio": 1.118421052631579, "no_speech_prob": 1.8614972844416267e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 53982, "start": 539.82, "end": 549.5200000000001, "text": " Like, how often in science or economics or just reading the news do we mistake the measurement tool for the actual thing being measured?", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 11, 577, 2049, 294, 3497, 420, 14564, 420, 445, 3760, 264, 2583, 360, 321, 6146, 264, 13160, 2290, 337, 264, 3539, 551, 885, 12690, 30, 50850], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09211766560872396, "compression_ratio": 1.5772727272727274, "no_speech_prob": 1.6621941453451305e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 53982, "start": 549.74, "end": 550.32, "text": " All the time.", "tokens": [50861, 1057, 264, 565, 13, 50890], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09211766560872396, "compression_ratio": 1.5772727272727274, "no_speech_prob": 1.6621941453451305e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 53982, "start": 550.44, "end": 554.74, "text": " If an economic theory breaks down during a recession, maybe human behavior isn't breaking down.", "tokens": [50896, 759, 364, 4836, 5261, 9857, 760, 1830, 257, 24828, 11, 1310, 1952, 5223, 1943, 380, 7697, 760, 13, 51111], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09211766560872396, "compression_ratio": 1.5772727272727274, "no_speech_prob": 1.6621941453451305e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 53982, "start": 555.2, "end": 561.2800000000001, "text": " Maybe our interface, our chosen coordinate system for measuring value just reached its glitch point.", "tokens": [51134, 2704, 527, 9226, 11, 527, 8614, 15670, 1185, 337, 13389, 2158, 445, 6488, 1080, 23552, 935, 13, 51438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09211766560872396, "compression_ratio": 1.5772727272727274, "no_speech_prob": 1.6621941453451305e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 56128, "start": 561.28, "end": 563.0799999999999, "text": " The implications are vast.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 16602, 366, 8369, 13, 50455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1887281168074835, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.405024967898738e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 56128, "start": 563.8, "end": 574.12, "text": " And to truly understand how deeply our choice of interface dictates what we can and cannot see, the text asks us to contrast the two most common ways to describe that circle you mentioned earlier.", "tokens": [50491, 400, 281, 4908, 1223, 577, 8760, 527, 3922, 295, 9226, 12569, 1024, 437, 321, 393, 293, 2644, 536, 11, 264, 2487, 8962, 505, 281, 8712, 264, 732, 881, 2689, 2098, 281, 6786, 300, 6329, 291, 2835, 3071, 13, 51007], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1887281168074835, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.405024967898738e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 56128, "start": 574.6999999999999, "end": 576.76, "text": " Cartesian coordinates and polar coordinates.", "tokens": [51036, 22478, 42434, 21056, 293, 12367, 21056, 13, 51139], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1887281168074835, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.405024967898738e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 56128, "start": 576.9399999999999, "end": 577.4599999999999, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51148, 7587, 13, 51174], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1887281168074835, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.405024967898738e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 56128, "start": 577.9399999999999, "end": 583.16, "text": " Right. So going back to high school geometry, Cartesian is your standard X and Y grid.", "tokens": [51198, 1779, 13, 407, 516, 646, 281, 1090, 1395, 18426, 11, 22478, 42434, 307, 428, 3832, 1783, 293, 398, 10748, 13, 51459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1887281168074835, "compression_ratio": 1.5555555555555556, "no_speech_prob": 1.405024967898738e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 58316, "start": 583.16, "end": 589.4599999999999, "text": " You go left or right, a certain X amount, up or down, a certain Y amount, and boom, you plot your point.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 352, 1411, 420, 558, 11, 257, 1629, 1783, 2372, 11, 493, 420, 760, 11, 257, 1629, 398, 2372, 11, 293, 9351, 11, 291, 7542, 428, 935, 13, 50680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11552691628746953, "compression_ratio": 1.7181818181818183, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056904491943083e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 58316, "start": 589.9599999999999, "end": 594.54, "text": " And polar coordinates are different. They use a distance from the center, the radius, and an angle.", "tokens": [50705, 400, 12367, 21056, 366, 819, 13, 814, 764, 257, 4560, 490, 264, 3056, 11, 264, 15845, 11, 293, 364, 5802, 13, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11552691628746953, "compression_ratio": 1.7181818181818183, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056904491943083e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 58316, "start": 594.7199999999999, "end": 596.36, "text": " Okay, so how do they compare in practice?", "tokens": [50943, 1033, 11, 370, 577, 360, 436, 6794, 294, 3124, 30, 51025], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11552691628746953, "compression_ratio": 1.7181818181818183, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056904491943083e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 58316, "start": 596.9599999999999, "end": 600.68, "text": " Consider what happens mathematically when you want to compute a simple rotation.", "tokens": [51055, 17416, 437, 2314, 44003, 562, 291, 528, 281, 14722, 257, 2199, 12447, 13, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11552691628746953, "compression_ratio": 1.7181818181818183, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056904491943083e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 58316, "start": 601.1, "end": 603.26, "text": " Say you want to rotate your circle by 30 degrees.", "tokens": [51262, 6463, 291, 528, 281, 13121, 428, 6329, 538, 2217, 5310, 13, 51370], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11552691628746953, "compression_ratio": 1.7181818181818183, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056904491943083e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 58316, "start": 603.6999999999999, "end": 608.98, "text": " In polar coordinates, where a point is already defined by its angle, rotating is the easiest math in the world.", "tokens": [51392, 682, 12367, 21056, 11, 689, 257, 935, 307, 1217, 7642, 538, 1080, 5802, 11, 19627, 307, 264, 12889, 5221, 294, 264, 1002, 13, 51656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11552691628746953, "compression_ratio": 1.7181818181818183, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056904491943083e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 58316, "start": 609.28, "end": 611.56, "text": " You just take your existing angle and you add 30 to it.", "tokens": [51671, 509, 445, 747, 428, 6741, 5802, 293, 291, 909, 2217, 281, 309, 13, 51785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11552691628746953, "compression_ratio": 1.7181818181818183, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056904491943083e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 58316, "start": 611.66, "end": 612.76, "text": " Just simple addition.", "tokens": [51790, 1449, 2199, 4500, 13, 51845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11552691628746953, "compression_ratio": 1.7181818181818183, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056904491943083e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 61276, "start": 612.76, "end": 614.36, "text": " A simple linear addition.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 2199, 8213, 4500, 13, 50445], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1313881252122962, "compression_ratio": 1.5345454545454544, "no_speech_prob": 2.280140919824758e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 61276, "start": 614.76, "end": 622.42, "text": " But if you try to compute that exact same 30 degree rotation using Cartesian X and Y coordinates, it becomes an absolute nightmare.", "tokens": [50465, 583, 498, 291, 853, 281, 14722, 300, 1900, 912, 2217, 4314, 12447, 1228, 22478, 42434, 1783, 293, 398, 21056, 11, 309, 3643, 364, 8236, 18724, 13, 50848], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1313881252122962, "compression_ratio": 1.5345454545454544, "no_speech_prob": 2.280140919824758e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 61276, "start": 622.58, "end": 624.72, "text": " Why is it so much harder? It's just a grid.", "tokens": [50856, 1545, 307, 309, 370, 709, 6081, 30, 467, 311, 445, 257, 10748, 13, 50963], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1313881252122962, "compression_ratio": 1.5345454545454544, "no_speech_prob": 2.280140919824758e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 61276, "start": 625.0, "end": 627.76, "text": " Because X and Y don't understand angles natively.", "tokens": [50977, 1436, 1783, 293, 398, 500, 380, 1223, 14708, 8470, 356, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1313881252122962, "compression_ratio": 1.5345454545454544, "no_speech_prob": 2.280140919824758e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 61276, "start": 628.7, "end": 635.22, "text": " To rotate a point in Cartesian space, you have to run your X and Y values through a complex trigonometric matrix.", "tokens": [51162, 1407, 13121, 257, 935, 294, 22478, 42434, 1901, 11, 291, 362, 281, 1190, 428, 1783, 293, 398, 4190, 807, 257, 3997, 35386, 266, 29470, 8141, 13, 51488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1313881252122962, "compression_ratio": 1.5345454545454544, "no_speech_prob": 2.280140919824758e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 61276, "start": 635.62, "end": 637.36, "text": " You're dealing with sines and cosines.", "tokens": [51508, 509, 434, 6260, 365, 262, 1652, 293, 3792, 1652, 13, 51595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1313881252122962, "compression_ratio": 1.5345454545454544, "no_speech_prob": 2.280140919824758e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 61276, "start": 637.5, "end": 638.04, "text": " Oh, gross.", "tokens": [51602, 876, 11, 11367, 13, 51629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1313881252122962, "compression_ratio": 1.5345454545454544, "no_speech_prob": 2.280140919824758e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 61276, "start": 638.28, "end": 638.5, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51641, 1779, 13, 51652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1313881252122962, "compression_ratio": 1.5345454545454544, "no_speech_prob": 2.280140919824758e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 63850, "start": 638.5, "end": 644.22, "text": " You have to multiply the X by the cosine of the angle, subtract the Y multiplied by the sine, and so on.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 362, 281, 12972, 264, 1783, 538, 264, 23565, 295, 264, 5802, 11, 16390, 264, 398, 17207, 538, 264, 18609, 11, 293, 370, 322, 13, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1153603446099066, "compression_ratio": 1.503030303030303, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014845920410802e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 63850, "start": 644.64, "end": 649.64, "text": " It's messy, it introduces rounding errors in computers, and it's computationally expensive.", "tokens": [50672, 467, 311, 16191, 11, 309, 31472, 48237, 13603, 294, 10807, 11, 293, 309, 311, 24903, 379, 5124, 13, 50922], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1153603446099066, "compression_ratio": 1.503030303030303, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014845920410802e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 63850, "start": 650.1, "end": 652.48, "text": " Okay, so polar is obviously the better system then.", "tokens": [50945, 1033, 11, 370, 12367, 307, 2745, 264, 1101, 1185, 550, 13, 51064], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1153603446099066, "compression_ratio": 1.503030303030303, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014845920410802e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 65248, "start": 652.48, "end": 660.62, "text": " Well, not entirely. What if you don't want to rotate the circle? What if you want to translate it, meaning you just want to slide it two inches to the left across the page?", "tokens": [50365, 1042, 11, 406, 7696, 13, 708, 498, 291, 500, 380, 528, 281, 13121, 264, 6329, 30, 708, 498, 291, 528, 281, 13799, 309, 11, 3620, 291, 445, 528, 281, 4137, 309, 732, 8478, 281, 264, 1411, 2108, 264, 3028, 30, 50772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10854591900789284, "compression_ratio": 1.641711229946524, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406791952649821e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 65248, "start": 660.74, "end": 660.96, "text": " Oh.", "tokens": [50778, 876, 13, 50789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10854591900789284, "compression_ratio": 1.641711229946524, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406791952649821e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 65248, "start": 661.6, "end": 667.1800000000001, "text": " In Cartesian coordinates, translation is incredibly easy. You just add two inches to your X coordinate and you're done.", "tokens": [50821, 682, 22478, 42434, 21056, 11, 12853, 307, 6252, 1858, 13, 509, 445, 909, 732, 8478, 281, 428, 1783, 15670, 293, 291, 434, 1096, 13, 51100], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10854591900789284, "compression_ratio": 1.641711229946524, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406791952649821e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 65248, "start": 667.3000000000001, "end": 667.82, "text": " And polar.", "tokens": [51106, 400, 12367, 13, 51132], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10854591900789284, "compression_ratio": 1.641711229946524, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406791952649821e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 66782, "start": 667.82, "end": 678.96, "text": " In polar coordinates, sliding the circle ruins your entire frame of reference. Your distance from the original center is now constantly changing in weird, nonlinear ways for every single point on the circle.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 12367, 21056, 11, 21169, 264, 6329, 24747, 428, 2302, 3920, 295, 6408, 13, 2260, 4560, 490, 264, 3380, 3056, 307, 586, 6460, 4473, 294, 3657, 11, 2107, 28263, 2098, 337, 633, 2167, 935, 322, 264, 6329, 13, 50922], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07116430393163709, "compression_ratio": 1.6262626262626263, "no_speech_prob": 2.108322197380552e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 66782, "start": 679.08, "end": 686.22, "text": " Ah, I see. Cartesian makes sliding things easy but rotating them hard. Polar makes rotating easy but sliding hard.", "tokens": [50928, 2438, 11, 286, 536, 13, 22478, 42434, 1669, 21169, 721, 1858, 457, 19627, 552, 1152, 13, 3635, 289, 1669, 19627, 1858, 457, 21169, 1152, 13, 51285], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07116430393163709, "compression_ratio": 1.6262626262626263, "no_speech_prob": 2.108322197380552e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 68622, "start": 686.22, "end": 699.6, "text": " The takeaway here is that neither chart is wrong. Neither chart is the objective, true description of the circle. They are simply different computational interfaces that prioritize different actions. They optimize for different kinds of work.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 30681, 510, 307, 300, 9662, 6927, 307, 2085, 13, 23956, 6927, 307, 264, 10024, 11, 2074, 3855, 295, 264, 6329, 13, 814, 366, 2935, 819, 28270, 28416, 300, 25164, 819, 5909, 13, 814, 19719, 337, 819, 3685, 295, 589, 13, 51034], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0459894819079705, "compression_ratio": 1.6883116883116882, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938719969908142e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 68622, "start": 699.84, "end": 713.94, "text": " Which brings us to the first massive paradigm shift in this deep dive. If charts are just interfaces that make certain things easy and others hard, how do we know which one to pick? I mean, we shouldn't just default to the XY grid because we learned it in middle school, right?", "tokens": [51046, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 700, 5994, 24709, 5513, 294, 341, 2452, 9192, 13, 759, 17767, 366, 445, 28416, 300, 652, 1629, 721, 1858, 293, 2357, 1152, 11, 577, 360, 321, 458, 597, 472, 281, 1888, 30, 286, 914, 11, 321, 4659, 380, 445, 7576, 281, 264, 48826, 10748, 570, 321, 3264, 309, 294, 2808, 1395, 11, 558, 30, 51751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0459894819079705, "compression_ratio": 1.6883116883116882, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938719969908142e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 71394, "start": 713.94, "end": 723.5400000000001, "text": " Absolutely not. The author argues that selecting a coordinate system isn't a matter of tradition. It's not about aesthetics. It is a strict optimization problem.", "tokens": [50365, 7021, 406, 13, 440, 3793, 38218, 300, 18182, 257, 15670, 1185, 1943, 380, 257, 1871, 295, 6994, 13, 467, 311, 406, 466, 35517, 13, 467, 307, 257, 10910, 19618, 1154, 13, 50845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09601034684614702, "compression_ratio": 1.7157190635451505, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236335192987283e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 71394, "start": 724.2600000000001, "end": 725.46, "text": " Optimization based on what?", "tokens": [50881, 35013, 2144, 2361, 322, 437, 30, 50941], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09601034684614702, "compression_ratio": 1.7157190635451505, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236335192987283e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 71394, "start": 725.58, "end": 734.1400000000001, "text": " Based on group symmetry. When you face a problem, you want to select a chart that is maximally adapted to the specific transformation you're dealing with.", "tokens": [50947, 18785, 322, 1594, 25440, 13, 1133, 291, 1851, 257, 1154, 11, 291, 528, 281, 3048, 257, 6927, 300, 307, 5138, 379, 20871, 281, 264, 2685, 9887, 291, 434, 6260, 365, 13, 51375], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09601034684614702, "compression_ratio": 1.7157190635451505, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236335192987283e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 71394, "start": 734.36, "end": 736.7, "text": " Maximally adapted. Meaning what, practically?", "tokens": [51386, 29076, 379, 20871, 13, 19948, 437, 11, 15667, 30, 51503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09601034684614702, "compression_ratio": 1.7157190635451505, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236335192987283e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 71394, "start": 737.12, "end": 743.36, "text": " Meaning you want a chart that leaves the maximum possible number of coordinates fixed or unchanged when an action happens.", "tokens": [51524, 19948, 291, 528, 257, 6927, 300, 5510, 264, 6674, 1944, 1230, 295, 21056, 6806, 420, 44553, 562, 364, 3069, 2314, 13, 51836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09601034684614702, "compression_ratio": 1.7157190635451505, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236335192987283e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 74336, "start": 743.36, "end": 756.66, "text": " Okay. Let me make sure I'm following this. If my problem involves things sliding around in straight lines, like, I don't know, boxes on a conveyor belt, I use Cartesian because X and Y handle straight lines easily.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 13, 961, 385, 652, 988, 286, 478, 3480, 341, 13, 759, 452, 1154, 11626, 721, 21169, 926, 294, 2997, 3876, 11, 411, 11, 286, 500, 380, 458, 11, 9002, 322, 257, 18053, 2454, 10750, 11, 286, 764, 22478, 42434, 570, 1783, 293, 398, 4813, 2997, 3876, 3612, 13, 51030], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10730842967609783, "compression_ratio": 1.6176470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.573540343163815e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 74336, "start": 756.72, "end": 757.0600000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51033, 1079, 13, 51050], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10730842967609783, "compression_ratio": 1.6176470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.573540343163815e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 74336, "start": 757.26, "end": 766.44, "text": " And if my problem involves axial symmetry, like water flowing through a cylindrical pipe or a magnetic field wrapping around a wire, I'd use cylindrical coordinates.", "tokens": [51060, 400, 498, 452, 1154, 11626, 46851, 25440, 11, 411, 1281, 13974, 807, 257, 28044, 15888, 11240, 420, 257, 12688, 2519, 21993, 926, 257, 6234, 11, 286, 1116, 764, 28044, 15888, 21056, 13, 51519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10730842967609783, "compression_ratio": 1.6176470588235294, "no_speech_prob": 1.573540343163815e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 76644, "start": 766.44, "end": 774.0, "text": " Exactly. And if your problem involves rotation in three dimensions, what mathematicians formally call the SO3 group...", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 400, 498, 428, 1154, 11626, 12447, 294, 1045, 12819, 11, 437, 32811, 2567, 25983, 818, 264, 10621, 18, 1594, 485, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08648598194122314, "compression_ratio": 1.533112582781457, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496167937902427e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 76644, "start": 774.0, "end": 778.34, "text": " Whoa. Let me stop you right there. SO3 group. E-L-I-5. Explain like I'm five, please.", "tokens": [50743, 7521, 13, 961, 385, 1590, 291, 558, 456, 13, 10621, 18, 1594, 13, 462, 12, 43, 12, 40, 12, 20, 13, 39574, 411, 286, 478, 1732, 11, 1767, 13, 50960], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08648598194122314, "compression_ratio": 1.533112582781457, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496167937902427e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 76644, "start": 778.36, "end": 792.84, "text": " Sure. It stands for the Special Orthogonal Group in Three Dimensions. But for our purposes, just think of it as the complete mathematical catalog of every possible way you can rotate a 3D object around a fixed center point without changing its size or shape.", "tokens": [50961, 4894, 13, 467, 7382, 337, 264, 11863, 27554, 664, 21523, 10500, 294, 6244, 20975, 8302, 13, 583, 337, 527, 9932, 11, 445, 519, 295, 309, 382, 264, 3566, 18894, 19746, 295, 633, 1944, 636, 291, 393, 13121, 257, 805, 35, 2657, 926, 257, 6806, 3056, 935, 1553, 4473, 1080, 2744, 420, 3909, 13, 51685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08648598194122314, "compression_ratio": 1.533112582781457, "no_speech_prob": 1.4496167937902427e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 79284, "start": 792.84, "end": 794.3000000000001, "text": " Okay. Tumbling, spinning.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 13, 314, 14188, 11, 15640, 13, 50438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.130572285568505, "compression_ratio": 1.671641791044776, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271449690420046e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 79284, "start": 794.5600000000001, "end": 801.5400000000001, "text": " Right. If you're dealing with a system that can tumble, spin, or orbit in any direction, a planet, a gyroscope, an atom, you're dealing with SO3.", "tokens": [50451, 1779, 13, 759, 291, 434, 6260, 365, 257, 1185, 300, 393, 13102, 638, 11, 6060, 11, 420, 13991, 294, 604, 3513, 11, 257, 5054, 11, 257, 15823, 2635, 13960, 11, 364, 12018, 11, 291, 434, 6260, 365, 10621, 18, 13, 50800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.130572285568505, "compression_ratio": 1.671641791044776, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271449690420046e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 79284, "start": 801.94, "end": 808.02, "text": " And for that kind of symmetry, the text proves that the unique maximal adaptation is the spherical coordinate system.", "tokens": [50820, 400, 337, 300, 733, 295, 25440, 11, 264, 2487, 25019, 300, 264, 3845, 49336, 21549, 307, 264, 37300, 15670, 1185, 13, 51124], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.130572285568505, "compression_ratio": 1.671641791044776, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271449690420046e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 79284, "start": 808.36, "end": 810.96, "text": " Spherical coordinates, radius, and two angles.", "tokens": [51141, 1738, 34340, 21056, 11, 15845, 11, 293, 732, 14708, 13, 51271], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.130572285568505, "compression_ratio": 1.671641791044776, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271449690420046e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 79284, "start": 811.36, "end": 816.02, "text": " So in geographical terms, that's your distance from the center of the Earth, your latitude, and your longitude.", "tokens": [51291, 407, 294, 39872, 2115, 11, 300, 311, 428, 4560, 490, 264, 3056, 295, 264, 4755, 11, 428, 45436, 11, 293, 428, 938, 4377, 13, 51524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.130572285568505, "compression_ratio": 1.671641791044776, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271449690420046e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 81602, "start": 816.02, "end": 828.78, "text": " Think about the pure elegance of that adaptation. In a spherical chart, no matter how wildly you rotate a system around its origin, the radial coordinate, the distance from the center, never changes.", "tokens": [50365, 6557, 466, 264, 6075, 14459, 719, 295, 300, 21549, 13, 682, 257, 37300, 6927, 11, 572, 1871, 577, 34731, 291, 13121, 257, 1185, 926, 1080, 4957, 11, 264, 38783, 15670, 11, 264, 4560, 490, 264, 3056, 11, 1128, 2962, 13, 51003], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11091526164564976, "compression_ratio": 1.5387931034482758, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368534353119023e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 81602, "start": 828.92, "end": 829.84, "text": " It just stays fixed.", "tokens": [51010, 467, 445, 10834, 6806, 13, 51056], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11091526164564976, "compression_ratio": 1.5387931034482758, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368534353119023e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 81602, "start": 830.12, "end": 836.84, "text": " Mathematically fixed. You can spin a globe all day long, but Paris is always the exact same distance from the Earth's core.", "tokens": [51070, 15776, 40197, 6806, 13, 509, 393, 6060, 257, 15371, 439, 786, 938, 11, 457, 8380, 307, 1009, 264, 1900, 912, 4560, 490, 264, 4755, 311, 4965, 13, 51406], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11091526164564976, "compression_ratio": 1.5387931034482758, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368534353119023e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 81602, "start": 837.06, "end": 837.66, "text": " That's true.", "tokens": [51417, 663, 311, 2074, 13, 51447], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11091526164564976, "compression_ratio": 1.5387931034482758, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368534353119023e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 83766, "start": 837.66, "end": 844.12, "text": " The entire mathematical complexity of that 3D rotation is absorbed purely into the two angular coordinates.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2302, 18894, 14024, 295, 300, 805, 35, 12447, 307, 20799, 17491, 666, 264, 732, 24413, 21056, 13, 50688], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14192838668823243, "compression_ratio": 1.606694560669456, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667031695073107e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 83766, "start": 844.8399999999999, "end": 851.56, "text": " The text proves that literally no other chart can do this better for 3D rotation. It is the ultimate optimization.", "tokens": [50724, 440, 2487, 25019, 300, 3736, 572, 661, 6927, 393, 360, 341, 1101, 337, 805, 35, 12447, 13, 467, 307, 264, 9705, 19618, 13, 51060], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14192838668823243, "compression_ratio": 1.606694560669456, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667031695073107e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 83766, "start": 852.4, "end": 855.8399999999999, "text": " Okay, but here is where it gets really interesting and honestly a little philosophical.", "tokens": [51102, 1033, 11, 457, 510, 307, 689, 309, 2170, 534, 1880, 293, 6095, 257, 707, 25066, 13, 51274], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14192838668823243, "compression_ratio": 1.606694560669456, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667031695073107e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 83766, "start": 856.4599999999999, "end": 860.28, "text": " The text doesn't just stop at saying spherical coordinates are efficient.", "tokens": [51305, 440, 2487, 1177, 380, 445, 1590, 412, 1566, 37300, 21056, 366, 7148, 13, 51496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14192838668823243, "compression_ratio": 1.606694560669456, "no_speech_prob": 1.4667031695073107e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 86028, "start": 860.28, "end": 867.74, "text": " It introduces this profound shift in how we read them, which the author calls the radial angular decomposition.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 31472, 341, 14382, 5513, 294, 577, 321, 1401, 552, 11, 597, 264, 3793, 5498, 264, 38783, 24413, 48356, 13, 50738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09921976236196664, "compression_ratio": 1.7038461538461538, "no_speech_prob": 1.421711273014159e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 86028, "start": 868.18, "end": 872.4399999999999, "text": " Yes, this decomposition is the conceptual engine driving the entire monograph.", "tokens": [50760, 1079, 11, 341, 48356, 307, 264, 24106, 2848, 4840, 264, 2302, 1108, 3108, 13, 50973], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09921976236196664, "compression_ratio": 1.7038461538461538, "no_speech_prob": 1.421711273014159e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 86028, "start": 872.72, "end": 878.02, "text": " It assigns totally different conceptual meanings to moving radially versus moving angularly.", "tokens": [50987, 467, 6269, 82, 3879, 819, 24106, 28138, 281, 2684, 2843, 2270, 5717, 2684, 24413, 356, 13, 51252], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09921976236196664, "compression_ratio": 1.7038461538461538, "no_speech_prob": 1.421711273014159e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 86028, "start": 878.1999999999999, "end": 886.26, "text": " Right. In this framework, the radial coordinate moving toward or away from the center represents progression across levels.", "tokens": [51261, 1779, 13, 682, 341, 8388, 11, 264, 38783, 15670, 2684, 7361, 420, 1314, 490, 264, 3056, 8855, 18733, 2108, 4358, 13, 51664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09921976236196664, "compression_ratio": 1.7038461538461538, "no_speech_prob": 1.421711273014159e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 86028, "start": 886.3199999999999, "end": 887.78, "text": " So it's not just physical distance.", "tokens": [51667, 407, 309, 311, 406, 445, 4001, 4560, 13, 51740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09921976236196664, "compression_ratio": 1.7038461538461538, "no_speech_prob": 1.421711273014159e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 88778, "start": 887.78, "end": 894.12, "text": " Not at all. It can represent depth, scale, concentration, physical realization, hierarchy.", "tokens": [50365, 1726, 412, 439, 13, 467, 393, 2906, 7161, 11, 4373, 11, 9856, 11, 4001, 25138, 11, 22333, 13, 50682], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07915788378034319, "compression_ratio": 1.5986159169550174, "no_speech_prob": 1.3511907521676636e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 88778, "start": 894.38, "end": 901.24, "text": " And the angular coordinates moving along the surface of a sphere at a fixed radius represent organization within a level.", "tokens": [50695, 400, 264, 24413, 21056, 2684, 2051, 264, 3753, 295, 257, 16687, 412, 257, 6806, 15845, 2906, 4475, 1951, 257, 1496, 13, 51038], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07915788378034319, "compression_ratio": 1.5986159169550174, "no_speech_prob": 1.3511907521676636e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 88778, "start": 901.4, "end": 905.3199999999999, "text": " Yes. Lateral circulation, pattern formation, symmetry breaking.", "tokens": [51046, 1079, 13, 11965, 304, 23168, 11, 5102, 11723, 11, 25440, 7697, 13, 51242], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07915788378034319, "compression_ratio": 1.5986159169550174, "no_speech_prob": 1.3511907521676636e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 88778, "start": 905.98, "end": 909.68, "text": " But crucially, it happens without changing your depth.", "tokens": [51275, 583, 5140, 1909, 11, 309, 2314, 1553, 4473, 428, 7161, 13, 51460], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07915788378034319, "compression_ratio": 1.5986159169550174, "no_speech_prob": 1.3511907521676636e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 88778, "start": 909.92, "end": 914.0799999999999, "text": " To ground this in human terms, I was thinking about the structure of a massive corporation.", "tokens": [51472, 1407, 2727, 341, 294, 1952, 2115, 11, 286, 390, 1953, 466, 264, 3877, 295, 257, 5994, 22197, 13, 51680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07915788378034319, "compression_ratio": 1.5986159169550174, "no_speech_prob": 1.3511907521676636e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 88778, "start": 914.28, "end": 915.6999999999999, "text": " Oh, that's a good way to visualize it.", "tokens": [51690, 876, 11, 300, 311, 257, 665, 636, 281, 23273, 309, 13, 51761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07915788378034319, "compression_ratio": 1.5986159169550174, "no_speech_prob": 1.3511907521676636e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 91570, "start": 915.7, "end": 918.0600000000001, "text": " Right. So the radial axis is the chain of command.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 407, 264, 38783, 10298, 307, 264, 5021, 295, 5622, 13, 50483], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11915109422471788, "compression_ratio": 1.6342592592592593, "no_speech_prob": 1.623245158080544e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 91570, "start": 918.62, "end": 920.1400000000001, "text": " The CEO is at the center point.", "tokens": [50511, 440, 9282, 307, 412, 264, 3056, 935, 13, 50587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11915109422471788, "compression_ratio": 1.6342592592592593, "no_speech_prob": 1.623245158080544e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 91570, "start": 920.6400000000001, "end": 923.5200000000001, "text": " The executive VPs are a shell slightly further out.", "tokens": [50612, 440, 10140, 691, 23043, 366, 257, 8720, 4748, 3052, 484, 13, 50756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11915109422471788, "compression_ratio": 1.6342592592592593, "no_speech_prob": 1.623245158080544e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 91570, "start": 923.96, "end": 929.26, "text": " The middle managers are a shell further out from that, all the way down to the interns at the outermost radius.", "tokens": [50778, 440, 2808, 14084, 366, 257, 8720, 3052, 484, 490, 300, 11, 439, 264, 636, 760, 281, 264, 46145, 412, 264, 484, 966, 555, 15845, 13, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11915109422471788, "compression_ratio": 1.6342592592592593, "no_speech_prob": 1.623245158080544e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 91570, "start": 929.38, "end": 935.4200000000001, "text": " Yes. So moving radially means moving up or down the hierarchy, a fundamental change in scale or authority.", "tokens": [51049, 1079, 13, 407, 2684, 2843, 2270, 1355, 2684, 493, 420, 760, 264, 22333, 11, 257, 8088, 1319, 294, 4373, 420, 8281, 13, 51351], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11915109422471788, "compression_ratio": 1.6342592592592593, "no_speech_prob": 1.623245158080544e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 93542, "start": 935.42, "end": 939.4, "text": " Exactly. So then what is the angular axis in this corporate sphere?", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 407, 550, 437, 307, 264, 24413, 10298, 294, 341, 10896, 16687, 30, 50564], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11168158054351807, "compression_ratio": 0.9710144927536232, "no_speech_prob": 1.6488003453871136e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 93940, "start": 939.4, "end": 951.52, "text": " The angular axis is the lateral structure. It's human resources, marketing, and sales, all existing on the exact same hierarchical level, the same fixed radius shell.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 24413, 10298, 307, 264, 25128, 3877, 13, 467, 311, 1952, 3593, 11, 6370, 11, 293, 5763, 11, 439, 6741, 322, 264, 1900, 912, 35250, 804, 1496, 11, 264, 912, 6806, 15845, 8720, 13, 50971], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11324662082600144, "compression_ratio": 1.46875, "no_speech_prob": 1.548579081807333e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 93940, "start": 951.84, "end": 955.76, "text": " So moving angularly is like shifting budget from marketing to sales.", "tokens": [50987, 407, 2684, 24413, 356, 307, 411, 17573, 4706, 490, 6370, 281, 5763, 13, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11324662082600144, "compression_ratio": 1.46875, "no_speech_prob": 1.548579081807333e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 95576, "start": 955.76, "end": 963.18, "text": " Precisely. You are reorganizing the structure within a given level, but you aren't changing the hierarchical depth of those resources.", "tokens": [50365, 48746, 736, 13, 509, 366, 41203, 3319, 264, 3877, 1951, 257, 2212, 1496, 11, 457, 291, 3212, 380, 4473, 264, 35250, 804, 7161, 295, 729, 3593, 13, 50736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0829100523676191, "compression_ratio": 1.494047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014886035891184e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 95576, "start": 963.54, "end": 970.48, "text": " An intern moving from marketing to sales is an angular move. An intern getting promoted to manager is a radial move.", "tokens": [50754, 1107, 2154, 2684, 490, 6370, 281, 5763, 307, 364, 24413, 1286, 13, 1107, 2154, 1242, 21162, 281, 6598, 307, 257, 38783, 1286, 13, 51101], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0829100523676191, "compression_ratio": 1.494047619047619, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014886035891184e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 97048, "start": 970.48, "end": 975.16, "text": " Okay. I love that analogy, but I have to play devil's advocate here and push back on this a little bit.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 13, 286, 959, 300, 21663, 11, 457, 286, 362, 281, 862, 13297, 311, 14608, 510, 293, 2944, 646, 322, 341, 257, 707, 857, 13, 50599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1724852048433744, "compression_ratio": 1.5461254612546125, "no_speech_prob": 2.0680401835448947e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 97048, "start": 975.28, "end": 975.8000000000001, "text": " Go for it.", "tokens": [50605, 1037, 337, 309, 13, 50631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1724852048433744, "compression_ratio": 1.5461254612546125, "no_speech_prob": 2.0680401835448947e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 97048, "start": 976.14, "end": 980.94, "text": " Is this just a really elegant metaphor or is this a literal mathematical distinction?", "tokens": [50648, 1119, 341, 445, 257, 534, 21117, 19157, 420, 307, 341, 257, 20411, 18894, 16844, 30, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1724852048433744, "compression_ratio": 1.5461254612546125, "no_speech_prob": 2.0680401835448947e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 97048, "start": 981.14, "end": 981.4, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50898, 865, 13, 50911], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1724852048433744, "compression_ratio": 1.5461254612546125, "no_speech_prob": 2.0680401835448947e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 97048, "start": 981.4, "end": 983.34, "text": " Like are they really that completely disconnected?", "tokens": [50911, 1743, 366, 436, 534, 300, 2584, 29426, 30, 51008], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1724852048433744, "compression_ratio": 1.5461254612546125, "no_speech_prob": 2.0680401835448947e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 97048, "start": 983.66, "end": 991.16, "text": " Because, for example, if I'm holding a radio transmitter and the signal is fading as it travels outward from the antenna, that's radial movement, right?", "tokens": [51024, 1436, 11, 337, 1365, 11, 498, 286, 478, 5061, 257, 6477, 40121, 293, 264, 6358, 307, 38644, 382, 309, 19863, 26914, 490, 264, 24573, 11, 300, 311, 38783, 3963, 11, 558, 30, 51399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1724852048433744, "compression_ratio": 1.5461254612546125, "no_speech_prob": 2.0680401835448947e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 97048, "start": 991.24, "end": 991.48, "text": " Correct.", "tokens": [51403, 12753, 13, 51415], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1724852048433744, "compression_ratio": 1.5461254612546125, "no_speech_prob": 2.0680401835448947e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 99148, "start": 991.48, "end": 997.5, "text": " And if the signal happens to be stronger to the north than to the south at the exact same distance, that's angular variation.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 498, 264, 6358, 2314, 281, 312, 7249, 281, 264, 6830, 813, 281, 264, 7377, 412, 264, 1900, 912, 4560, 11, 300, 311, 24413, 12990, 13, 50666], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15136201453931403, "compression_ratio": 1.6581818181818182, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840944670425292e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 99148, "start": 997.6800000000001, "end": 997.8000000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50675, 1779, 13, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15136201453931403, "compression_ratio": 1.6581818181818182, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840944670425292e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 99148, "start": 998.2, "end": 1004.86, "text": " Are those two behaviors genuinely different categories of math or are we just playing word games with coordinates?", "tokens": [50701, 2014, 729, 732, 15501, 17839, 819, 10479, 295, 5221, 420, 366, 321, 445, 2433, 1349, 2813, 365, 21056, 30, 51034], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15136201453931403, "compression_ratio": 1.6581818181818182, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840944670425292e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 99148, "start": 1005.3000000000001, "end": 1009.12, "text": " The author's argument is that they absolutely are different categories of math.", "tokens": [51056, 440, 3793, 311, 6770, 307, 300, 436, 3122, 366, 819, 10479, 295, 5221, 13, 51247], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15136201453931403, "compression_ratio": 1.6581818181818182, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840944670425292e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 99148, "start": 1009.54, "end": 1016.48, "text": " And treating them as interchangeable is a massive category error that constantly plagues how we analyze complex systems.", "tokens": [51268, 400, 15083, 552, 382, 30358, 712, 307, 257, 5994, 7719, 6713, 300, 6460, 499, 7063, 577, 321, 12477, 3997, 3652, 13, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15136201453931403, "compression_ratio": 1.6581818181818182, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840944670425292e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 99148, "start": 1016.86, "end": 1017.34, "text": " How so?", "tokens": [51634, 1012, 370, 30, 51658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15136201453931403, "compression_ratio": 1.6581818181818182, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840944670425292e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 101734, "start": 1017.34, "end": 1023.84, "text": " When a signal fades radially, it is experiencing a change in realization or concentration across space.", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 257, 6358, 32679, 2843, 2270, 11, 309, 307, 11139, 257, 1319, 294, 25138, 420, 9856, 2108, 1901, 13, 50690], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12655349363360488, "compression_ratio": 1.6594427244582044, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552840269660416e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 101734, "start": 1024.3600000000001, "end": 1025.6200000000001, "text": " It is crossing levels.", "tokens": [50716, 467, 307, 14712, 4358, 13, 50779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12655349363360488, "compression_ratio": 1.6594427244582044, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552840269660416e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 101734, "start": 1026.14, "end": 1031.16, "text": " When it varies angularly, it's exhibiting a pattern within a perfectly equivalent domain.", "tokens": [50805, 1133, 309, 21716, 24413, 356, 11, 309, 311, 8144, 1748, 257, 5102, 1951, 257, 6239, 10344, 9274, 13, 51056], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12655349363360488, "compression_ratio": 1.6594427244582044, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552840269660416e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 101734, "start": 1031.7, "end": 1040.38, "text": " The fundamental math of the sphere inherently tracks these two behaviors separately because they represent entirely different physical and computational realities.", "tokens": [51083, 440, 8088, 5221, 295, 264, 16687, 27993, 10218, 613, 732, 15501, 14759, 570, 436, 2906, 7696, 819, 4001, 293, 28270, 27785, 13, 51517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12655349363360488, "compression_ratio": 1.6594427244582044, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552840269660416e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 101734, "start": 1040.58, "end": 1042.38, "text": " You can't just mix them together in an equation.", "tokens": [51527, 509, 393, 380, 445, 2890, 552, 1214, 294, 364, 5367, 13, 51617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12655349363360488, "compression_ratio": 1.6594427244582044, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552840269660416e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 101734, "start": 1042.38, "end": 1046.2, "text": " Mixing them up is like trying to measure the volume of a liquid using a thermometer.", "tokens": [51617, 12769, 278, 552, 493, 307, 411, 1382, 281, 3481, 264, 5523, 295, 257, 6553, 1228, 257, 42539, 13, 51808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12655349363360488, "compression_ratio": 1.6594427244582044, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552840269660416e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 101734, "start": 1046.42, "end": 1047.22, "text": " It just doesn't work.", "tokens": [51819, 467, 445, 1177, 380, 589, 13, 51859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12655349363360488, "compression_ratio": 1.6594427244582044, "no_speech_prob": 1.4552840269660416e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 104734, "start": 1047.34, "end": 1047.58, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50365, 3153, 13, 50377], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09727518899100167, "compression_ratio": 1.6317689530685922, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839958688978028e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 104734, "start": 1047.98, "end": 1051.6599999999999, "text": " So if we follow this logic, what does this mean for boundaries?", "tokens": [50397, 407, 498, 321, 1524, 341, 9952, 11, 437, 775, 341, 914, 337, 13180, 30, 50581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09727518899100167, "compression_ratio": 1.6317689530685922, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839958688978028e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 104734, "start": 1052.6, "end": 1059.82, "text": " Because we look at just the angular part, a fixed shell at a specific radius, that shell creates a boundary between the inside of the sphere and the outside.", "tokens": [50628, 1436, 321, 574, 412, 445, 264, 24413, 644, 11, 257, 6806, 8720, 412, 257, 2685, 15845, 11, 300, 8720, 7829, 257, 12866, 1296, 264, 1854, 295, 264, 16687, 293, 264, 2380, 13, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09727518899100167, "compression_ratio": 1.6317689530685922, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839958688978028e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 104734, "start": 1059.9199999999998, "end": 1061.6999999999998, "text": " Like the wall of a biological cell?", "tokens": [50994, 1743, 264, 2929, 295, 257, 13910, 2815, 30, 51083], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09727518899100167, "compression_ratio": 1.6317689530685922, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839958688978028e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 104734, "start": 1061.84, "end": 1063.02, "text": " Or the border of a country.", "tokens": [51090, 1610, 264, 7838, 295, 257, 1941, 13, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09727518899100167, "compression_ratio": 1.6317689530685922, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839958688978028e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 104734, "start": 1063.1599999999999, "end": 1063.4199999999998, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51156, 1779, 13, 51169], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09727518899100167, "compression_ratio": 1.6317689530685922, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839958688978028e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 104734, "start": 1063.6599999999999, "end": 1070.6399999999999, "text": " But as I was reading this section, the text argued that boundaries do far more than just sit there inertly keeping things apart like some dumb brick wall.", "tokens": [51181, 583, 382, 286, 390, 3760, 341, 3541, 11, 264, 2487, 20219, 300, 13180, 360, 1400, 544, 813, 445, 1394, 456, 25832, 356, 5145, 721, 4936, 411, 512, 10316, 16725, 2929, 13, 51530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09727518899100167, "compression_ratio": 1.6317689530685922, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839958688978028e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 107064, "start": 1070.64, "end": 1073.8400000000001, "text": " The text posits what it calls an architecture of limits.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2487, 1366, 1208, 437, 309, 5498, 364, 9482, 295, 10406, 13, 50525], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1786624558117925, "compression_ratio": 1.4, "no_speech_prob": 1.6751693348443508e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 107064, "start": 1074.4, "end": 1078.94, "text": " It argues that boundaries perform active, intense computational work for the universe.", "tokens": [50553, 467, 38218, 300, 13180, 2042, 4967, 11, 9447, 28270, 589, 337, 264, 6445, 13, 50780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1786624558117925, "compression_ratio": 1.4, "no_speech_prob": 1.6751693348443508e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 107064, "start": 1079.6200000000001, "end": 1083.2800000000002, "text": " And crucially, not all boundaries are doing the same kind of work.", "tokens": [50814, 400, 5140, 1909, 11, 406, 439, 13180, 366, 884, 264, 912, 733, 295, 589, 13, 50997], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1786624558117925, "compression_ratio": 1.4, "no_speech_prob": 1.6751693348443508e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 108328, "start": 1083.28, "end": 1087.04, "text": " This was easily one of the most fascinating parts of the source material for me.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 390, 3612, 472, 295, 264, 881, 10343, 3166, 295, 264, 4009, 2527, 337, 385, 13, 50553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13670685797026663, "compression_ratio": 1.4948453608247423, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396373833995394e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 108328, "start": 1087.04, "end": 1091.08, "text": " Let's really take our time and break these down because they build up to a pretty wild conclusion.", "tokens": [50553, 961, 311, 534, 747, 527, 565, 293, 1821, 613, 760, 570, 436, 1322, 493, 281, 257, 1238, 4868, 10063, 13, 50755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13670685797026663, "compression_ratio": 1.4948453608247423, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396373833995394e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 108328, "start": 1092.12, "end": 1098.8999999999999, "text": " The text identifies three structurally distinct types of boundaries that can occupy a fixed radius shell.", "tokens": [50807, 440, 2487, 34597, 1045, 6594, 6512, 10644, 3467, 295, 13180, 300, 393, 30645, 257, 6806, 15845, 8720, 13, 51146], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13670685797026663, "compression_ratio": 1.4948453608247423, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396373833995394e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 108328, "start": 1099.1, "end": 1099.3999999999999, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51156, 1079, 13, 51171], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13670685797026663, "compression_ratio": 1.4948453608247423, "no_speech_prob": 1.8396373833995394e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 109940, "start": 1099.4, "end": 1102.6200000000001, "text": " The first type of boundary is called the synchronic screen.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 700, 2010, 295, 12866, 307, 1219, 264, 5451, 339, 10011, 2568, 13, 50526], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17068752489591899, "compression_ratio": 1.74, "no_speech_prob": 1.9131571327157815e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 109940, "start": 1103.16, "end": 1107.68, "text": " The text refers to it as Fristen style, after the neuroscientist Carl Fristen.", "tokens": [50553, 440, 2487, 14942, 281, 309, 382, 1526, 4821, 3758, 11, 934, 264, 28813, 5412, 468, 14256, 1526, 4821, 13, 50779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17068752489591899, "compression_ratio": 1.74, "no_speech_prob": 1.9131571327157815e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 109940, "start": 1107.92, "end": 1108.16, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50791, 1779, 13, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17068752489591899, "compression_ratio": 1.74, "no_speech_prob": 1.9131571327157815e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 109940, "start": 1108.3600000000001, "end": 1111.3200000000002, "text": " This builds heavily on Fristen's concept of a Markov blanket.", "tokens": [50813, 639, 15182, 10950, 322, 1526, 4821, 311, 3410, 295, 257, 3934, 5179, 17907, 13, 50961], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17068752489591899, "compression_ratio": 1.74, "no_speech_prob": 1.9131571327157815e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 109940, "start": 1111.8200000000002, "end": 1115.5600000000002, "text": " A synchronic screen is evaluated entirely on the present state of affairs.", "tokens": [50986, 316, 5451, 339, 10011, 2568, 307, 25509, 7696, 322, 264, 1974, 1785, 295, 17478, 13, 51173], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17068752489591899, "compression_ratio": 1.74, "no_speech_prob": 1.9131571327157815e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 109940, "start": 1115.74, "end": 1116.3600000000001, "text": " The present tense?", "tokens": [51182, 440, 1974, 18760, 30, 51213], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17068752489591899, "compression_ratio": 1.74, "no_speech_prob": 1.9131571327157815e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 109940, "start": 1116.5400000000002, "end": 1116.8200000000002, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51222, 1079, 13, 51236], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17068752489591899, "compression_ratio": 1.74, "no_speech_prob": 1.9131571327157815e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 109940, "start": 1117.3000000000002, "end": 1122.6000000000001, "text": " It is a statistical boundary where the internal states of a system are hidden from the external states.", "tokens": [51260, 467, 307, 257, 22820, 12866, 689, 264, 6920, 4368, 295, 257, 1185, 366, 7633, 490, 264, 8320, 4368, 13, 51525], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17068752489591899, "compression_ratio": 1.74, "no_speech_prob": 1.9131571327157815e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 109940, "start": 1123.16, "end": 1127.8000000000002, "text": " If you are a process inside the system, you cannot observe the outside world directly.", "tokens": [51553, 759, 291, 366, 257, 1399, 1854, 264, 1185, 11, 291, 2644, 11441, 264, 2380, 1002, 3838, 13, 51785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17068752489591899, "compression_ratio": 1.74, "no_speech_prob": 1.9131571327157815e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 109940, "start": 1127.8000000000002, "end": 1128.92, "text": " So what can you observe?", "tokens": [51785, 407, 437, 393, 291, 11441, 30, 51841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17068752489591899, "compression_ratio": 1.74, "no_speech_prob": 1.9131571327157815e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 112892, "start": 1128.92, "end": 1138.5, "text": " You can only observe the blanket, the screen, and infer what is outside based on the present information hitting the screen right at this exact millisecond.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 393, 787, 11441, 264, 17907, 11, 264, 2568, 11, 293, 13596, 437, 307, 2380, 2361, 322, 264, 1974, 1589, 8850, 264, 2568, 558, 412, 341, 1900, 27940, 18882, 13, 50844], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14307223021529103, "compression_ratio": 1.7315436241610738, "no_speech_prob": 1.513396938150613e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 112892, "start": 1138.9, "end": 1142.52, "text": " It's entirely about perception and action right now in the current moment.", "tokens": [50864, 467, 311, 7696, 466, 12860, 293, 3069, 558, 586, 294, 264, 2190, 1623, 13, 51045], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14307223021529103, "compression_ratio": 1.7315436241610738, "no_speech_prob": 1.513396938150613e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 112892, "start": 1142.68, "end": 1144.7, "text": " Let's try to map this to something relatable.", "tokens": [51053, 961, 311, 853, 281, 4471, 341, 281, 746, 42355, 13, 51154], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14307223021529103, "compression_ratio": 1.7315436241610738, "no_speech_prob": 1.513396938150613e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 112892, "start": 1145.04, "end": 1149.16, "text": " I was thinking it's like a bouncer at a nightclub who only looks at your ID right this second.", "tokens": [51171, 286, 390, 1953, 309, 311, 411, 257, 272, 14296, 412, 257, 1818, 40607, 567, 787, 1542, 412, 428, 7348, 558, 341, 1150, 13, 51377], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14307223021529103, "compression_ratio": 1.7315436241610738, "no_speech_prob": 1.513396938150613e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 112892, "start": 1149.3200000000002, "end": 1149.8600000000001, "text": " That works.", "tokens": [51385, 663, 1985, 13, 51412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14307223021529103, "compression_ratio": 1.7315436241610738, "no_speech_prob": 1.513396938150613e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 112892, "start": 1150.02, "end": 1151.54, "text": " He doesn't care who you were yesterday.", "tokens": [51420, 634, 1177, 380, 1127, 567, 291, 645, 5186, 13, 51496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14307223021529103, "compression_ratio": 1.7315436241610738, "no_speech_prob": 1.513396938150613e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 112892, "start": 1151.8200000000002, "end": 1151.98, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51510, 865, 13, 51518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14307223021529103, "compression_ratio": 1.7315436241610738, "no_speech_prob": 1.513396938150613e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 112892, "start": 1152.04, "end": 1153.54, "text": " He doesn't care if you're going to be famous tomorrow.", "tokens": [51521, 634, 1177, 380, 1127, 498, 291, 434, 516, 281, 312, 4618, 4153, 13, 51596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14307223021529103, "compression_ratio": 1.7315436241610738, "no_speech_prob": 1.513396938150613e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 112892, "start": 1154.0, "end": 1155.22, "text": " He looks at the present facts.", "tokens": [51619, 634, 1542, 412, 264, 1974, 9130, 13, 51680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14307223021529103, "compression_ratio": 1.7315436241610738, "no_speech_prob": 1.513396938150613e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 115522, "start": 1155.22, "end": 1161.0, "text": " Does the name on this piece of plastic match the name on his clipboard right now?", "tokens": [50365, 4402, 264, 1315, 322, 341, 2522, 295, 5900, 2995, 264, 1315, 322, 702, 7353, 3787, 558, 586, 30, 50654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2229001045227051, "compression_ratio": 1.3305785123966942, "no_speech_prob": 1.299432458336247e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 115522, "start": 1161.26, "end": 1162.4, "text": " If yes, you go in.", "tokens": [50667, 759, 2086, 11, 291, 352, 294, 13, 50724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2229001045227051, "compression_ratio": 1.3305785123966942, "no_speech_prob": 1.299432458336247e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 115522, "start": 1162.6000000000001, "end": 1164.44, "text": " If no, you stay out.", "tokens": [50734, 759, 572, 11, 291, 1754, 484, 13, 50826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2229001045227051, "compression_ratio": 1.3305785123966942, "no_speech_prob": 1.299432458336247e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 115522, "start": 1164.8, "end": 1167.88, "text": " It's a purely present tense evaluation.", "tokens": [50844, 467, 311, 257, 17491, 1974, 18760, 13344, 13, 50998], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2229001045227051, "compression_ratio": 1.3305785123966942, "no_speech_prob": 1.299432458336247e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 116788, "start": 1167.88, "end": 1170.48, "text": " That's a highly accurate way to frame it.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 311, 257, 5405, 8559, 636, 281, 3920, 309, 13, 50495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16110904320426608, "compression_ratio": 1.5357142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.33544987134665e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 116788, "start": 1170.5800000000002, "end": 1173.5800000000002, "text": " The synchronic screen has no memory, and it has no foresight.", "tokens": [50500, 440, 5451, 339, 10011, 2568, 575, 572, 4675, 11, 293, 309, 575, 572, 2091, 28654, 13, 50650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16110904320426608, "compression_ratio": 1.5357142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.33544987134665e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 116788, "start": 1173.74, "end": 1174.64, "text": " It only knows now.", "tokens": [50658, 467, 787, 3255, 586, 13, 50703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16110904320426608, "compression_ratio": 1.5357142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.33544987134665e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 116788, "start": 1174.74, "end": 1176.0, "text": " Okay, so what's the second type?", "tokens": [50708, 1033, 11, 370, 437, 311, 264, 1150, 2010, 30, 50771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16110904320426608, "compression_ratio": 1.5357142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.33544987134665e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 116788, "start": 1176.16, "end": 1179.42, "text": " The second type operates on a completely different temporal axis.", "tokens": [50779, 440, 1150, 2010, 22577, 322, 257, 2584, 819, 30881, 10298, 13, 50942], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16110904320426608, "compression_ratio": 1.5357142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.33544987134665e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 116788, "start": 1179.68, "end": 1181.5200000000002, "text": " It is the stored target boundary.", "tokens": [50955, 467, 307, 264, 12187, 3779, 12866, 13, 51047], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16110904320426608, "compression_ratio": 1.5357142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.33544987134665e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 116788, "start": 1181.9, "end": 1186.44, "text": " The text calls this Levin style, referring to the developmental biologist Michael Levin.", "tokens": [51066, 440, 2487, 5498, 341, 1456, 4796, 3758, 11, 13761, 281, 264, 30160, 3228, 9201, 5116, 1456, 4796, 13, 51293], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16110904320426608, "compression_ratio": 1.5357142857142858, "no_speech_prob": 1.33544987134665e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 118644, "start": 1186.44, "end": 1190.48, "text": " A stored target boundary, and this one is evaluated against a future state.", "tokens": [50365, 316, 12187, 3779, 12866, 11, 293, 341, 472, 307, 25509, 1970, 257, 2027, 1785, 13, 50567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293701915417688, "compression_ratio": 1.6486486486486487, "no_speech_prob": 1.399533917575968e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 118644, "start": 1190.78, "end": 1195.5800000000002, "text": " This was the part that absolutely short-circuited my brain with the biology examples.", "tokens": [50582, 639, 390, 264, 644, 300, 3122, 2099, 12, 23568, 12032, 1226, 452, 3567, 365, 264, 14956, 5110, 13, 50822], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293701915417688, "compression_ratio": 1.6486486486486487, "no_speech_prob": 1.399533917575968e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 118644, "start": 1196.3600000000001, "end": 1199.2, "text": " We're talking about developmental bioelectricity here, right?", "tokens": [50861, 492, 434, 1417, 466, 30160, 12198, 33243, 507, 510, 11, 558, 30, 51003], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293701915417688, "compression_ratio": 1.6486486486486487, "no_speech_prob": 1.399533917575968e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 118644, "start": 1199.28, "end": 1199.78, "text": " We are.", "tokens": [51007, 492, 366, 13, 51032], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293701915417688, "compression_ratio": 1.6486486486486487, "no_speech_prob": 1.399533917575968e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 118644, "start": 1200.24, "end": 1201.5800000000002, "text": " Levin's research is revolutionary.", "tokens": [51055, 1456, 4796, 311, 2132, 307, 22687, 13, 51122], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293701915417688, "compression_ratio": 1.6486486486486487, "no_speech_prob": 1.399533917575968e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 118644, "start": 1202.28, "end": 1208.72, "text": " It shows that the slow voltage gradients across ordinary non-neural cells in a body form a pattern,", "tokens": [51157, 467, 3110, 300, 264, 2964, 8352, 2771, 2448, 2108, 10547, 2107, 12, 716, 1807, 5438, 294, 257, 1772, 1254, 257, 5102, 11, 51479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293701915417688, "compression_ratio": 1.6486486486486487, "no_speech_prob": 1.399533917575968e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 118644, "start": 1209.3400000000001, "end": 1212.44, "text": " and that pattern functions as a stored target morphology.", "tokens": [51510, 293, 300, 5102, 6828, 382, 257, 12187, 3779, 25778, 1793, 13, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293701915417688, "compression_ratio": 1.6486486486486487, "no_speech_prob": 1.399533917575968e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 118644, "start": 1212.6200000000001, "end": 1216.22, "text": " A stored target morphology, meaning like an architectural plan.", "tokens": [51674, 316, 12187, 3779, 25778, 1793, 11, 3620, 411, 364, 26621, 1393, 13, 51854], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293701915417688, "compression_ratio": 1.6486486486486487, "no_speech_prob": 1.399533917575968e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 121622, "start": 1216.22, "end": 1218.2, "text": " Essentially an anatomical dew print.", "tokens": [50365, 23596, 364, 21618, 298, 804, 48745, 4482, 13, 50464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13283255004882813, "compression_ratio": 1.68, "no_speech_prob": 1.443955848987044e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 121622, "start": 1218.6000000000001, "end": 1222.52, "text": " It's a blueprint that the collective behavior of the cells is organized to reach.", "tokens": [50484, 467, 311, 257, 35868, 300, 264, 12590, 5223, 295, 264, 5438, 307, 9983, 281, 2524, 13, 50680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13283255004882813, "compression_ratio": 1.68, "no_speech_prob": 1.443955848987044e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 121622, "start": 1222.84, "end": 1228.72, "text": " The boundary of a regenerating piece of tissue isn't just the physical place where growth happens to have stopped today.", "tokens": [50696, 440, 12866, 295, 257, 26358, 990, 2522, 295, 12404, 1943, 380, 445, 264, 4001, 1081, 689, 4599, 2314, 281, 362, 5936, 965, 13, 50990], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13283255004882813, "compression_ratio": 1.68, "no_speech_prob": 1.443955848987044e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 121622, "start": 1228.98, "end": 1233.8, "text": " It is the visible trace of a shape that is actively being pursued for tomorrow.", "tokens": [51003, 467, 307, 264, 8974, 13508, 295, 257, 3909, 300, 307, 13022, 885, 34893, 337, 4153, 13, 51244], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13283255004882813, "compression_ratio": 1.68, "no_speech_prob": 1.443955848987044e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 121622, "start": 1234.2, "end": 1239.16, "text": " The text mentions this flatworm experiment, and if you are listening to this, you really need to try and picture this.", "tokens": [51264, 440, 2487, 23844, 341, 4962, 30917, 5120, 11, 293, 498, 291, 366, 4764, 281, 341, 11, 291, 534, 643, 281, 853, 293, 3036, 341, 13, 51512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13283255004882813, "compression_ratio": 1.68, "no_speech_prob": 1.443955848987044e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 121622, "start": 1239.6200000000001, "end": 1241.88, "text": " Scientists can take a flatworm and they cut off its head.", "tokens": [51535, 32958, 393, 747, 257, 4962, 30917, 293, 436, 1723, 766, 1080, 1378, 13, 51648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13283255004882813, "compression_ratio": 1.68, "no_speech_prob": 1.443955848987044e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 121622, "start": 1242.04, "end": 1244.3600000000001, "text": " Which is pretty standard in regeneration studies.", "tokens": [51656, 3013, 307, 1238, 3832, 294, 43813, 5313, 13, 51772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13283255004882813, "compression_ratio": 1.68, "no_speech_prob": 1.443955848987044e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 124436, "start": 1244.36, "end": 1249.62, "text": " Right, but then they briefly alter the bioelectric gradient at the side of the wound.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 11, 457, 550, 436, 10515, 11337, 264, 12198, 33243, 16235, 412, 264, 1252, 295, 264, 10999, 13, 50628], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13136859562086023, "compression_ratio": 1.4666666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204100115688405e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 124436, "start": 1249.86, "end": 1251.56, "text": " They don't touch the DNA at all.", "tokens": [50640, 814, 500, 380, 2557, 264, 8272, 412, 439, 13, 50725], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13136859562086023, "compression_ratio": 1.4666666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204100115688405e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 124436, "start": 1251.6399999999999, "end": 1253.82, "text": " The genome is completely untouched, perfectly normal.", "tokens": [50729, 440, 21953, 307, 2584, 1701, 36740, 11, 6239, 2710, 13, 50838], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13136859562086023, "compression_ratio": 1.4666666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204100115688405e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 124436, "start": 1254.08, "end": 1260.32, "text": " But by changing the bioelectric boundary, the stored target, the worm grows two heads.", "tokens": [50851, 583, 538, 4473, 264, 12198, 33243, 12866, 11, 264, 12187, 3779, 11, 264, 23835, 13156, 732, 8050, 13, 51163], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13136859562086023, "compression_ratio": 1.4666666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204100115688405e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 124436, "start": 1260.4199999999998, "end": 1260.8799999999999, "text": " Yes!", "tokens": [51168, 1079, 0, 51191], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13136859562086023, "compression_ratio": 1.4666666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 1.9204100115688405e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 126088, "start": 1260.88, "end": 1262.4, "text": " And here's the craziest part.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 510, 311, 264, 46339, 644, 13, 50441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18045570038177156, "compression_ratio": 1.6088709677419355, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126263073321326e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 126088, "start": 1262.6000000000001, "end": 1269.88, "text": " If you cut off those two heads later on, the worm will naturally regrow two heads again, without any further interference.", "tokens": [50451, 759, 291, 1723, 766, 729, 732, 8050, 1780, 322, 11, 264, 23835, 486, 8195, 319, 26685, 732, 8050, 797, 11, 1553, 604, 3052, 24497, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18045570038177156, "compression_ratio": 1.6088709677419355, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126263073321326e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 126088, "start": 1270.2, "end": 1275.64, "text": " Because the bioelectric boundary is still instructing the tissue to pursue that future two-headed state.", "tokens": [50831, 1436, 264, 12198, 33243, 12866, 307, 920, 7232, 278, 264, 12404, 281, 12392, 300, 2027, 732, 12, 28409, 1785, 13, 51103], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18045570038177156, "compression_ratio": 1.6088709677419355, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126263073321326e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 126088, "start": 1276.22, "end": 1278.6200000000001, "text": " It fundamentally upends how we think about biology.", "tokens": [51132, 467, 17879, 493, 2581, 577, 321, 519, 466, 14956, 13, 51252], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18045570038177156, "compression_ratio": 1.6088709677419355, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126263073321326e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 126088, "start": 1279.16, "end": 1283.88, "text": " It proves that the genome is just the hardware, it provides the cellular building blocks,", "tokens": [51279, 467, 25019, 300, 264, 21953, 307, 445, 264, 8837, 11, 309, 6417, 264, 29267, 2390, 8474, 11, 51515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18045570038177156, "compression_ratio": 1.6088709677419355, "no_speech_prob": 1.9126263073321326e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 128388, "start": 1283.88, "end": 1289.0600000000002, "text": " but the boundary itself is the software, supplying the future target morphology.", "tokens": [50365, 457, 264, 12866, 2564, 307, 264, 4722, 11, 46815, 264, 2027, 3779, 25778, 1793, 13, 50624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12938086967158124, "compression_ratio": 1.69, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671240788742933e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 128388, "start": 1289.2, "end": 1290.0, "text": " That is wild.", "tokens": [50631, 663, 307, 4868, 13, 50671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12938086967158124, "compression_ratio": 1.69, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671240788742933e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 128388, "start": 1290.3000000000002, "end": 1295.7800000000002, "text": " The boundary evaluates the present state of the cells strictly against a future state that does not yet exist,", "tokens": [50686, 440, 12866, 6133, 1024, 264, 1974, 1785, 295, 264, 5438, 20792, 1970, 257, 2027, 1785, 300, 775, 406, 1939, 2514, 11, 50960], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12938086967158124, "compression_ratio": 1.69, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671240788742933e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 128388, "start": 1296.22, "end": 1300.0400000000002, "text": " and it applies pressure to force the cells to close the gap between the two.", "tokens": [50982, 293, 309, 13165, 3321, 281, 3464, 264, 5438, 281, 1998, 264, 7417, 1296, 264, 732, 13, 51173], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12938086967158124, "compression_ratio": 1.69, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671240788742933e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 128388, "start": 1300.3200000000002, "end": 1302.14, "text": " I was trying to come up with an analogy for this one,", "tokens": [51187, 286, 390, 1382, 281, 808, 493, 365, 364, 21663, 337, 341, 472, 11, 51278], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12938086967158124, "compression_ratio": 1.69, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671240788742933e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 128388, "start": 1302.3000000000002, "end": 1305.5400000000002, "text": " and originally I thought about another kind of club bouncer, but that doesn't really work.", "tokens": [51286, 293, 7993, 286, 1194, 466, 1071, 733, 295, 6482, 272, 14296, 11, 457, 300, 1177, 380, 534, 589, 13, 51448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12938086967158124, "compression_ratio": 1.69, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671240788742933e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 128388, "start": 1305.7600000000002, "end": 1309.0400000000002, "text": " A better analogy is that the GPS navigation system in your car.", "tokens": [51459, 316, 1101, 21663, 307, 300, 264, 19462, 17346, 1185, 294, 428, 1032, 13, 51623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12938086967158124, "compression_ratio": 1.69, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671240788742933e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 128388, "start": 1309.1200000000001, "end": 1309.66, "text": " Oh, absolutely.", "tokens": [51627, 876, 11, 3122, 13, 51654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12938086967158124, "compression_ratio": 1.69, "no_speech_prob": 1.3671240788742933e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 130966, "start": 1309.66, "end": 1313.94, "text": " Because a stored target boundary is like your GPS when you've typed in a destination.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 257, 12187, 3779, 12866, 307, 411, 428, 19462, 562, 291, 600, 33941, 294, 257, 12236, 13, 50579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14376241069729045, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796963346789705e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 130966, "start": 1314.96, "end": 1318.38, "text": " The GPS doesn't define itself by where your car is currently parked.", "tokens": [50630, 440, 19462, 1177, 380, 6964, 2564, 538, 689, 428, 1032, 307, 4362, 28491, 13, 50801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14376241069729045, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796963346789705e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 130966, "start": 1318.6000000000001, "end": 1323.0400000000002, "text": " It defines its entire operation by where you were supposed to be in an hour.", "tokens": [50812, 467, 23122, 1080, 2302, 6916, 538, 689, 291, 645, 3442, 281, 312, 294, 364, 1773, 13, 51034], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14376241069729045, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796963346789705e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 130966, "start": 1323.3600000000001, "end": 1324.68, "text": " Right, the future state.", "tokens": [51050, 1779, 11, 264, 2027, 1785, 13, 51116], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14376241069729045, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796963346789705e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 130966, "start": 1324.92, "end": 1325.3200000000002, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51128, 7587, 13, 51148], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14376241069729045, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796963346789705e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 130966, "start": 1325.5800000000002, "end": 1325.78, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51161, 865, 13, 51171], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14376241069729045, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796963346789705e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 130966, "start": 1325.9, "end": 1328.44, "text": " If you take a wrong turn, it recalculates.", "tokens": [51177, 759, 291, 747, 257, 2085, 1261, 11, 309, 850, 304, 2444, 1024, 13, 51304], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14376241069729045, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796963346789705e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 130966, "start": 1328.72, "end": 1330.74, "text": " It applies pressure on you like the voice saying,", "tokens": [51318, 467, 13165, 3321, 322, 291, 411, 264, 3177, 1566, 11, 51419], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14376241069729045, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796963346789705e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 130966, "start": 1331.0600000000002, "end": 1335.3600000000001, "text": " make a U-turn to force your present state to align with the stored future target.", "tokens": [51435, 652, 257, 624, 12, 33886, 281, 3464, 428, 1974, 1785, 281, 7975, 365, 264, 12187, 2027, 3779, 13, 51650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14376241069729045, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796963346789705e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 133536, "start": 1335.36, "end": 1340.4799999999998, "text": " The GPS analogy works perfectly because it highlights the goal-directed nature of the computation.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 19462, 21663, 1985, 6239, 570, 309, 14254, 264, 3387, 12, 44868, 292, 3687, 295, 264, 24903, 13, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1534615889839504, "compression_ratio": 1.6941176470588235, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171558449989965e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 133536, "start": 1341.12, "end": 1343.52, "text": " So now we arrive at the third type of boundary,", "tokens": [50653, 407, 586, 321, 8881, 412, 264, 2636, 2010, 295, 12866, 11, 50773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1534615889839504, "compression_ratio": 1.6941176470588235, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171558449989965e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 133536, "start": 1344.6399999999999, "end": 1348.74, "text": " the diachronic exclusion, or RSVP-style boundary.", "tokens": [50829, 264, 1026, 608, 10011, 33049, 11, 420, 25855, 53, 47, 12, 15014, 12866, 13, 51034], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1534615889839504, "compression_ratio": 1.6941176470588235, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171558449989965e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 133536, "start": 1348.8999999999999, "end": 1349.8, "text": " RSVP-style.", "tokens": [51042, 25855, 53, 47, 12, 15014, 13, 51087], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1534615889839504, "compression_ratio": 1.6941176470588235, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171558449989965e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 133536, "start": 1349.9799999999998, "end": 1350.24, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51096, 1079, 13, 51109], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1534615889839504, "compression_ratio": 1.6941176470588235, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171558449989965e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 133536, "start": 1350.6999999999998, "end": 1354.4599999999998, "text": " Named after an admissibility theoretic account of irreversible computation.", "tokens": [51132, 426, 3475, 934, 364, 5910, 891, 2841, 14308, 299, 2696, 295, 16014, 840, 964, 24903, 13, 51320], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1534615889839504, "compression_ratio": 1.6941176470588235, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171558449989965e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 133536, "start": 1354.9199999999998, "end": 1358.0, "text": " While the first boundary looks at the present and the second looks at the future,", "tokens": [51343, 3987, 264, 700, 12866, 1542, 412, 264, 1974, 293, 264, 1150, 1542, 412, 264, 2027, 11, 51497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1534615889839504, "compression_ratio": 1.6941176470588235, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171558449989965e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 133536, "start": 1358.32, "end": 1360.9199999999998, "text": " this third boundary is evaluated against the past.", "tokens": [51513, 341, 2636, 12866, 307, 25509, 1970, 264, 1791, 13, 51643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1534615889839504, "compression_ratio": 1.6941176470588235, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171558449989965e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 133536, "start": 1361.08, "end": 1361.6599999999999, "text": " The past.", "tokens": [51651, 440, 1791, 13, 51680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1534615889839504, "compression_ratio": 1.6941176470588235, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171558449989965e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 136166, "start": 1361.66, "end": 1366.42, "text": " It is a historical record of permanent refusal or permanent exclusion of options.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 257, 8584, 2136, 295, 10996, 48948, 420, 10996, 33049, 295, 3956, 13, 50603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1589434867681459, "compression_ratio": 1.7147651006711409, "no_speech_prob": 1.5432403618897972e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 136166, "start": 1366.5400000000002, "end": 1366.76, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50609, 1033, 13, 50620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1589434867681459, "compression_ratio": 1.7147651006711409, "no_speech_prob": 1.5432403618897972e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 136166, "start": 1367.14, "end": 1368.5, "text": " We can bring the bouncer back for this one.", "tokens": [50639, 492, 393, 1565, 264, 272, 14296, 646, 337, 341, 472, 13, 50707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1589434867681459, "compression_ratio": 1.7147651006711409, "no_speech_prob": 1.5432403618897972e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 136166, "start": 1368.5600000000002, "end": 1369.5400000000002, "text": " Yes, the third bouncer.", "tokens": [50710, 1079, 11, 264, 2636, 272, 14296, 13, 50759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1589434867681459, "compression_ratio": 1.7147651006711409, "no_speech_prob": 1.5432403618897972e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 136166, "start": 1369.96, "end": 1374.18, "text": " The diachronic bouncer is the guy who checks the permanent ban list from 10 years ago.", "tokens": [50780, 440, 1026, 608, 10011, 272, 14296, 307, 264, 2146, 567, 13834, 264, 10996, 5643, 1329, 490, 1266, 924, 2057, 13, 50991], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1589434867681459, "compression_ratio": 1.7147651006711409, "no_speech_prob": 1.5432403618897972e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 136166, "start": 1374.66, "end": 1376.88, "text": " It doesn't matter if your ID is perfect today.", "tokens": [51015, 467, 1177, 380, 1871, 498, 428, 7348, 307, 2176, 965, 13, 51126], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1589434867681459, "compression_ratio": 1.7147651006711409, "no_speech_prob": 1.5432403618897972e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 136166, "start": 1377.18, "end": 1380.96, "text": " It doesn't matter if you promise to behave perfectly in the future and buy bottle service.", "tokens": [51141, 467, 1177, 380, 1871, 498, 291, 6228, 281, 15158, 6239, 294, 264, 2027, 293, 2256, 7817, 2643, 13, 51330], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1589434867681459, "compression_ratio": 1.7147651006711409, "no_speech_prob": 1.5432403618897972e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 136166, "start": 1381.44, "end": 1383.4, "text": " You threw a glass at the bartender in 2016,", "tokens": [51354, 509, 11918, 257, 4276, 412, 264, 44768, 3216, 294, 6549, 11, 51452], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1589434867681459, "compression_ratio": 1.7147651006711409, "no_speech_prob": 1.5432403618897972e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 136166, "start": 1383.88, "end": 1388.38, "text": " and therefore your option to enter this club is permanently deleted from the universe.", "tokens": [51476, 293, 4412, 428, 3614, 281, 3242, 341, 6482, 307, 24042, 22981, 490, 264, 6445, 13, 51701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1589434867681459, "compression_ratio": 1.7147651006711409, "no_speech_prob": 1.5432403618897972e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 138838, "start": 1388.38, "end": 1389.1000000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50401], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18743433032119483, "compression_ratio": 1.6423357664233578, "no_speech_prob": 1.623477611026325e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 138838, "start": 1389.64, "end": 1393.8600000000001, "text": " Or, to put a finer mathematical point on it, it's a constitutive exclusion.", "tokens": [50428, 1610, 11, 281, 829, 257, 39130, 18894, 935, 322, 309, 11, 309, 311, 257, 23079, 17254, 33049, 13, 50639], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18743433032119483, "compression_ratio": 1.6423357664233578, "no_speech_prob": 1.623477611026325e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 138838, "start": 1394.7, "end": 1399.5600000000002, "text": " In a complex system, a refused option doesn't just become mathematically unlikely.", "tokens": [50681, 682, 257, 3997, 1185, 11, 257, 14654, 3614, 1177, 380, 445, 1813, 44003, 17518, 13, 50924], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18743433032119483, "compression_ratio": 1.6423357664233578, "no_speech_prob": 1.623477611026325e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 138838, "start": 1400.0200000000002, "end": 1403.2, "text": " It is removed from the system's permissible future entirely.", "tokens": [50947, 467, 307, 7261, 490, 264, 1185, 311, 4784, 41073, 2027, 7696, 13, 51106], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18743433032119483, "compression_ratio": 1.6423357664233578, "no_speech_prob": 1.623477611026325e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 138838, "start": 1403.6200000000001, "end": 1405.7800000000002, "text": " It is a hard wall built by history.", "tokens": [51127, 467, 307, 257, 1152, 2929, 3094, 538, 2503, 13, 51235], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18743433032119483, "compression_ratio": 1.6423357664233578, "no_speech_prob": 1.623477611026325e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 138838, "start": 1406.14, "end": 1406.3400000000001, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51253, 1033, 13, 51263], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18743433032119483, "compression_ratio": 1.6423357664233578, "no_speech_prob": 1.623477611026325e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 138838, "start": 1406.46, "end": 1408.0400000000002, "text": " So we have these three distinct boundaries.", "tokens": [51269, 407, 321, 362, 613, 1045, 10644, 13180, 13, 51348], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18743433032119483, "compression_ratio": 1.6423357664233578, "no_speech_prob": 1.623477611026325e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 138838, "start": 1408.5800000000002, "end": 1412.14, "text": " Present tense screens, future tense targets, and past tense exclusions.", "tokens": [51375, 33253, 18760, 11171, 11, 2027, 18760, 12911, 11, 293, 1791, 18760, 15085, 626, 13, 51553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18743433032119483, "compression_ratio": 1.6423357664233578, "no_speech_prob": 1.623477611026325e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 138838, "start": 1412.3400000000001, "end": 1415.38, "text": " And the text includes a formal mathematical proof, theorem 3.5.", "tokens": [51563, 400, 264, 2487, 5974, 257, 9860, 18894, 8177, 11, 20904, 805, 13, 20, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18743433032119483, "compression_ratio": 1.6423357664233578, "no_speech_prob": 1.623477611026325e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 141538, "start": 1415.38, "end": 1421.98, "text": " Yes, theorem 3.5 proves that these three boundaries absolutely cannot be collapsed into one generic concept.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 11, 20904, 805, 13, 20, 25019, 300, 613, 1045, 13180, 3122, 2644, 312, 24578, 666, 472, 19577, 3410, 13, 50695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1731605711437407, "compression_ratio": 1.7047970479704797, "no_speech_prob": 2.1842670901162098e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 141538, "start": 1422.6000000000001, "end": 1427.44, "text": " This feels like a profound warning to engineers and economists, or anyone designing a complex system.", "tokens": [50726, 639, 3417, 411, 257, 14382, 9164, 281, 11955, 293, 32431, 11, 420, 2878, 14685, 257, 3997, 1185, 13, 50968], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1731605711437407, "compression_ratio": 1.7047970479704797, "no_speech_prob": 2.1842670901162098e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 141538, "start": 1427.8000000000002, "end": 1428.2800000000002, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [50986, 467, 307, 13, 51010], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1731605711437407, "compression_ratio": 1.7047970479704797, "no_speech_prob": 2.1842670901162098e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 141538, "start": 1428.94, "end": 1436.7800000000002, "text": " The theorem proves that if you mix a present tense screen, the synchronic boundary, with a permanent deletion of an option,", "tokens": [51043, 440, 20904, 25019, 300, 498, 291, 2890, 257, 1974, 18760, 2568, 11, 264, 5451, 339, 10011, 12866, 11, 365, 257, 10996, 1103, 302, 313, 295, 364, 3614, 11, 51435], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1731605711437407, "compression_ratio": 1.7047970479704797, "no_speech_prob": 2.1842670901162098e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 141538, "start": 1437.64, "end": 1442.2800000000002, "text": " the diachronic boundary, without changing your underlying math to account for the difference,", "tokens": [51478, 264, 1026, 608, 10011, 12866, 11, 1553, 4473, 428, 14217, 5221, 281, 2696, 337, 264, 2649, 11, 51710], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1731605711437407, "compression_ratio": 1.7047970479704797, "no_speech_prob": 2.1842670901162098e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 141538, "start": 1442.68, "end": 1444.42, "text": " the entire system crashes.", "tokens": [51730, 264, 2302, 1185, 28642, 13, 51817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1731605711437407, "compression_ratio": 1.7047970479704797, "no_speech_prob": 2.1842670901162098e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 144442, "start": 1444.42, "end": 1447.6000000000001, "text": " I really want to understand the mechanics of this crash.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 534, 528, 281, 1223, 264, 12939, 295, 341, 8252, 13, 50524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15677107297457182, "compression_ratio": 1.5301724137931034, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827766173039716e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 144442, "start": 1448.16, "end": 1451.3000000000002, "text": " Walk me through the exact moment the system breaks down.", "tokens": [50552, 10818, 385, 807, 264, 1900, 1623, 264, 1185, 9857, 760, 13, 50709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15677107297457182, "compression_ratio": 1.5301724137931034, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827766173039716e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 144442, "start": 1451.7, "end": 1453.6200000000001, "text": " Let's say I'm an engineer, I've got my system running.", "tokens": [50729, 961, 311, 584, 286, 478, 364, 11403, 11, 286, 600, 658, 452, 1185, 2614, 13, 50825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15677107297457182, "compression_ratio": 1.5301724137931034, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827766173039716e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 144442, "start": 1453.94, "end": 1457.96, "text": " Why does treating these boundaries the same cause a failure?", "tokens": [50841, 1545, 775, 15083, 613, 13180, 264, 912, 3082, 257, 7763, 30, 51042], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15677107297457182, "compression_ratio": 1.5301724137931034, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827766173039716e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 144442, "start": 1458.3400000000001, "end": 1459.8400000000001, "text": " Let's walk through it step by step.", "tokens": [51061, 961, 311, 1792, 807, 309, 1823, 538, 1823, 13, 51136], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15677107297457182, "compression_ratio": 1.5301724137931034, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827766173039716e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 144442, "start": 1460.6000000000001, "end": 1465.8600000000001, "text": " Remember that a synchronic process minimizes discrepancy based only on the present state.", "tokens": [51174, 5459, 300, 257, 5451, 339, 10011, 1399, 4464, 5660, 2983, 265, 6040, 1344, 2361, 787, 322, 264, 1974, 1785, 13, 51437], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15677107297457182, "compression_ratio": 1.5301724137931034, "no_speech_prob": 1.7827766173039716e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 146586, "start": 1465.86, "end": 1470.26, "text": " It is constantly adjusting to find the optimum path forward right now.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 6460, 23559, 281, 915, 264, 39326, 3100, 2128, 558, 586, 13, 50585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14931232898266283, "compression_ratio": 1.5495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 2.035553583329408e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 146586, "start": 1470.32, "end": 1470.4799999999998, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50588, 1779, 13, 50596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14931232898266283, "compression_ratio": 1.5495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 2.035553583329408e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 146586, "start": 1470.76, "end": 1471.52, "text": " It has no memory.", "tokens": [50610, 467, 575, 572, 4675, 13, 50648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14931232898266283, "compression_ratio": 1.5495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 2.035553583329408e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 146586, "start": 1471.6799999999998, "end": 1472.3, "text": " It has no memory.", "tokens": [50656, 467, 575, 572, 4675, 13, 50687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14931232898266283, "compression_ratio": 1.5495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 2.035553583329408e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 146586, "start": 1472.4799999999998, "end": 1480.3799999999999, "text": " Now imagine it is moving toward an optimal choice, but suddenly the diachronic boundary permanently deletes that choice because of a historical exclusion rule.", "tokens": [50696, 823, 3811, 309, 307, 2684, 7361, 364, 16252, 3922, 11, 457, 5800, 264, 1026, 608, 10011, 12866, 24042, 1103, 37996, 300, 3922, 570, 295, 257, 8584, 33049, 4978, 13, 51091], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14931232898266283, "compression_ratio": 1.5495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 2.035553583329408e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 146586, "start": 1480.4799999999998, "end": 1482.0, "text": " The door just gets slammed in its face.", "tokens": [51096, 440, 2853, 445, 2170, 50196, 294, 1080, 1851, 13, 51172], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14931232898266283, "compression_ratio": 1.5495049504950495, "no_speech_prob": 2.035553583329408e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 148200, "start": 1482.0, "end": 1488.6, "text": " Yes, but because the synchronic math has no memory variable, it has no way to understand why its optimum just vanished.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 11, 457, 570, 264, 5451, 339, 10011, 5221, 575, 572, 4675, 7006, 11, 309, 575, 572, 636, 281, 1223, 983, 1080, 39326, 445, 37518, 13, 50695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14301829154674822, "compression_ratio": 1.3732394366197183, "no_speech_prob": 1.658494413851741e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 148200, "start": 1488.86, "end": 1491.9, "text": " It just sees that the present state suddenly doesn't make sense.", "tokens": [50708, 467, 445, 8194, 300, 264, 1974, 1785, 5800, 1177, 380, 652, 2020, 13, 50860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14301829154674822, "compression_ratio": 1.3732394366197183, "no_speech_prob": 1.658494413851741e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 148200, "start": 1492.0, "end": 1492.5, "text": " Oh, I see.", "tokens": [50865, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 50890], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14301829154674822, "compression_ratio": 1.3732394366197183, "no_speech_prob": 1.658494413851741e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 149250, "start": 1492.5, "end": 1502.18, "text": " So it will try to recalculate based on a new present, but it will keep bumping into this invisible historical wall that it lacks the vocabulary to comprehend.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 309, 486, 853, 281, 850, 304, 2444, 473, 2361, 322, 257, 777, 1974, 11, 457, 309, 486, 1066, 9961, 278, 666, 341, 14603, 8584, 2929, 300, 309, 31132, 264, 19864, 281, 38183, 13, 50849], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1523125129833556, "compression_ratio": 1.361842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 2.192805615905402e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 149250, "start": 1502.5, "end": 1503.52, "text": " It gets stuck in a loop.", "tokens": [50865, 467, 2170, 5541, 294, 257, 6367, 13, 50916], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1523125129833556, "compression_ratio": 1.361842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 2.192805615905402e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 149250, "start": 1503.86, "end": 1504.8, "text": " A total crash.", "tokens": [50933, 316, 3217, 8252, 13, 50980], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1523125129833556, "compression_ratio": 1.361842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 2.192805615905402e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 149250, "start": 1505.04, "end": 1505.46, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50992, 7587, 13, 51013], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1523125129833556, "compression_ratio": 1.361842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 2.192805615905402e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 150546, "start": 1505.46, "end": 1514.44, "text": " If an engineer assumes all boundaries are just generic walls and treats them as interchangeable variables in an equation, they'll create massive bookkeeping errors.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 364, 11403, 37808, 439, 13180, 366, 445, 19577, 7920, 293, 19566, 552, 382, 30358, 712, 9102, 294, 364, 5367, 11, 436, 603, 1884, 5994, 1446, 25769, 13603, 13, 50814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1557285371890738, "compression_ratio": 1.691588785046729, "no_speech_prob": 1.416032655715549e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 150546, "start": 1514.82, "end": 1519.3, "text": " You cannot treat a historical ban list the same way you treat a live present tense sensor.", "tokens": [50833, 509, 2644, 2387, 257, 8584, 5643, 1329, 264, 912, 636, 291, 2387, 257, 1621, 1974, 18760, 10200, 13, 51057], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1557285371890738, "compression_ratio": 1.691588785046729, "no_speech_prob": 1.416032655715549e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 150546, "start": 1519.54, "end": 1523.16, "text": " The math will literally tear itself apart trying to reconcile them.", "tokens": [51069, 440, 5221, 486, 3736, 12556, 2564, 4936, 1382, 281, 41059, 552, 13, 51250], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1557285371890738, "compression_ratio": 1.691588785046729, "no_speech_prob": 1.416032655715549e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 150546, "start": 1523.26, "end": 1525.26, "text": " That makes so much sense when you lay it out like that.", "tokens": [51255, 663, 1669, 370, 709, 2020, 562, 291, 2360, 309, 484, 411, 300, 13, 51355], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1557285371890738, "compression_ratio": 1.691588785046729, "no_speech_prob": 1.416032655715549e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 150546, "start": 1525.32, "end": 1525.44, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51358, 865, 13, 51364], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1557285371890738, "compression_ratio": 1.691588785046729, "no_speech_prob": 1.416032655715549e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 150546, "start": 1525.78, "end": 1532.52, "text": " Okay, so we've established that these boundaries on a spherical shell are active, complex, and temporally distinct.", "tokens": [51381, 1033, 11, 370, 321, 600, 7545, 300, 613, 13180, 322, 257, 37300, 8720, 366, 4967, 11, 3997, 11, 293, 8219, 379, 10644, 13, 51718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1557285371890738, "compression_ratio": 1.691588785046729, "no_speech_prob": 1.416032655715549e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 150546, "start": 1532.8, "end": 1535.24, "text": " They're doing intense concupational work.", "tokens": [51732, 814, 434, 884, 9447, 1588, 1010, 1478, 589, 13, 51854], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1557285371890738, "compression_ratio": 1.691588785046729, "no_speech_prob": 1.416032655715549e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 153546, "start": 1535.46, "end": 1543.6200000000001, "text": " But how do we actually measure the physical or informational tension of things moving across these boundaries or sliding along them?", "tokens": [50365, 583, 577, 360, 321, 767, 3481, 264, 4001, 420, 49391, 8980, 295, 721, 2684, 2108, 613, 13180, 420, 21169, 2051, 552, 30, 50773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10491496060801818, "compression_ratio": 1.6932907348242812, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956250213998823e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 153546, "start": 1543.88, "end": 1548.22, "text": " For that, the author introduces a tool from classical differential equations called the Laplacian.", "tokens": [50786, 1171, 300, 11, 264, 3793, 31472, 257, 2290, 490, 13735, 15756, 11787, 1219, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 13, 51003], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10491496060801818, "compression_ratio": 1.6932907348242812, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956250213998823e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 153546, "start": 1548.3, "end": 1555.42, "text": " Now, I always thought the Laplacian was just some incredibly scary physics equation you use to solve heat flow or wave propagation.", "tokens": [51007, 823, 11, 286, 1009, 1194, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 390, 445, 512, 6252, 6958, 10649, 5367, 291, 764, 281, 5039, 3738, 3095, 420, 5772, 38377, 13, 51363], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10491496060801818, "compression_ratio": 1.6932907348242812, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956250213998823e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 153546, "start": 1556.08, "end": 1559.22, "text": " You know, something you sweat over in a graduate thermodynamics class.", "tokens": [51396, 509, 458, 11, 746, 291, 11872, 670, 294, 257, 8080, 8810, 35483, 1508, 13, 51553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10491496060801818, "compression_ratio": 1.6932907348242812, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956250213998823e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 153546, "start": 1559.22, "end": 1564.92, "text": " It is used for those things, certainly, but the author reframes it entirely for this framework.", "tokens": [51553, 467, 307, 1143, 337, 729, 721, 11, 3297, 11, 457, 264, 3793, 13334, 1632, 309, 7696, 337, 341, 8388, 13, 51838], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10491496060801818, "compression_ratio": 1.6932907348242812, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956250213998823e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 156546, "start": 1565.46, "end": 1574.22, "text": " We are asked to view the Laplacian not as a solver for specific physics problems, but as a universal incompatibility detector.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 366, 2351, 281, 1910, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 406, 382, 257, 1404, 331, 337, 2685, 10649, 2740, 11, 457, 382, 257, 11455, 40393, 267, 2841, 25712, 13, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13976833918323256, "compression_ratio": 1.5515463917525774, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011275200984333e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 156546, "start": 1574.42, "end": 1576.2, "text": " An incompatibility detector.", "tokens": [50813, 1107, 40393, 267, 2841, 25712, 13, 50902], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13976833918323256, "compression_ratio": 1.5515463917525774, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011275200984333e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 156546, "start": 1576.3, "end": 1577.72, "text": " I really latched onto this framing.", "tokens": [50907, 286, 534, 287, 24102, 3911, 341, 28971, 13, 50978], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13976833918323256, "compression_ratio": 1.5515463917525774, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011275200984333e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 156546, "start": 1578.3, "end": 1583.68, "text": " The text says it measures how much a specific point disagrees with the average of its immediate surroundings.", "tokens": [51007, 440, 2487, 1619, 309, 8000, 577, 709, 257, 2685, 935, 10414, 4856, 365, 264, 4274, 295, 1080, 11629, 25314, 13, 51276], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13976833918323256, "compression_ratio": 1.5515463917525774, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011275200984333e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 158368, "start": 1583.68, "end": 1585.1000000000001, "text": " Think of it mathematically.", "tokens": [50365, 6557, 295, 309, 44003, 13, 50436], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16669621418431863, "compression_ratio": 1.6715686274509804, "no_speech_prob": 1.942335398422146e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 158368, "start": 1585.64, "end": 1594.52, "text": " If you evaluate the Laplacian at a specific point on a grid and the result is a positive number, it means that point is a local trough compared to its neighbors.", "tokens": [50463, 759, 291, 13059, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 412, 257, 2685, 935, 322, 257, 10748, 293, 264, 1874, 307, 257, 3353, 1230, 11, 309, 1355, 300, 935, 307, 257, 2654, 504, 581, 5347, 281, 1080, 12512, 13, 50907], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16669621418431863, "compression_ratio": 1.6715686274509804, "no_speech_prob": 1.942335398422146e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 158368, "start": 1594.76, "end": 1596.44, "text": " Like it's lower than the average around it.", "tokens": [50919, 1743, 309, 311, 3126, 813, 264, 4274, 926, 309, 13, 51003], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16669621418431863, "compression_ratio": 1.6715686274509804, "no_speech_prob": 1.942335398422146e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 158368, "start": 1596.44, "end": 1596.72, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51003, 1079, 13, 51017], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16669621418431863, "compression_ratio": 1.6715686274509804, "no_speech_prob": 1.942335398422146e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 158368, "start": 1597.26, "end": 1600.3200000000002, "text": " And if the result is a negative number, it's a local peak.", "tokens": [51044, 400, 498, 264, 1874, 307, 257, 3671, 1230, 11, 309, 311, 257, 2654, 10651, 13, 51197], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16669621418431863, "compression_ratio": 1.6715686274509804, "no_speech_prob": 1.942335398422146e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 158368, "start": 1600.44, "end": 1601.8400000000001, "text": " It's higher than the average.", "tokens": [51203, 467, 311, 2946, 813, 264, 4274, 13, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16669621418431863, "compression_ratio": 1.6715686274509804, "no_speech_prob": 1.942335398422146e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 158368, "start": 1601.94, "end": 1602.5800000000002, "text": " If it's zero.", "tokens": [51278, 759, 309, 311, 4018, 13, 51310], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16669621418431863, "compression_ratio": 1.6715686274509804, "no_speech_prob": 1.942335398422146e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 160258, "start": 1602.58, "end": 1607.3999999999999, "text": " If the Laplacian is zero, it means that point perfectly matches the average of its neighborhood.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 307, 4018, 11, 309, 1355, 300, 935, 6239, 10676, 264, 4274, 295, 1080, 7630, 13, 50606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10853771851441571, "compression_ratio": 1.5637065637065637, "no_speech_prob": 1.579692648391584e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 160258, "start": 1607.84, "end": 1609.3799999999999, "text": " There is no tension at all.", "tokens": [50628, 821, 307, 572, 8980, 412, 439, 13, 50705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10853771851441571, "compression_ratio": 1.5637065637065637, "no_speech_prob": 1.579692648391584e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 160258, "start": 1609.54, "end": 1618.1799999999998, "text": " So if I can use a human analogy again, if I walk into a room full of people wearing black tuxedos and I am wearing a bright neon pink suit,", "tokens": [50713, 407, 498, 286, 393, 764, 257, 1952, 21663, 797, 11, 498, 286, 1792, 666, 257, 1808, 1577, 295, 561, 4769, 2211, 256, 2449, 292, 329, 293, 286, 669, 4769, 257, 4730, 30820, 7022, 5722, 11, 51145], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10853771851441571, "compression_ratio": 1.5637065637065637, "no_speech_prob": 1.579692648391584e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 160258, "start": 1619.08, "end": 1623.96, "text": " the Laplacian evaluated at my location is essentially the math screaming, you don't fit in.", "tokens": [51190, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 25509, 412, 452, 4914, 307, 4476, 264, 5221, 12636, 11, 291, 500, 380, 3318, 294, 13, 51434], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10853771851441571, "compression_ratio": 1.5637065637065637, "no_speech_prob": 1.579692648391584e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 160258, "start": 1624.1599999999999, "end": 1626.78, "text": " You are a massive local peak of incompatibility.", "tokens": [51444, 509, 366, 257, 5994, 2654, 10651, 295, 40393, 267, 2841, 13, 51575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10853771851441571, "compression_ratio": 1.5637065637065637, "no_speech_prob": 1.579692648391584e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 162678, "start": 1626.78, "end": 1634.8, "text": " That's a perfect visualization of local mismatch, but here is the critical part that connects this back to the geometry of the sphere.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 311, 257, 2176, 25801, 295, 2654, 23220, 852, 11, 457, 510, 307, 264, 4924, 644, 300, 16967, 341, 646, 281, 264, 18426, 295, 264, 16687, 13, 50766], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11851599298674485, "compression_ratio": 1.7025089605734767, "no_speech_prob": 1.2208132725219367e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 162678, "start": 1635.34, "end": 1640.7, "text": " The author proves that the Laplacian splits perfectly into two distinct mathematical terms.", "tokens": [50793, 440, 3793, 25019, 300, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 37741, 6239, 666, 732, 10644, 18894, 2115, 13, 51061], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11851599298674485, "compression_ratio": 1.7025089605734767, "no_speech_prob": 1.2208132725219367e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 162678, "start": 1640.8999999999999, "end": 1641.3, "text": " Oh, right.", "tokens": [51071, 876, 11, 558, 13, 51091], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11851599298674485, "compression_ratio": 1.7025089605734767, "no_speech_prob": 1.2208132725219367e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 162678, "start": 1641.44, "end": 1645.82, "text": " One term detects radial incompatibility tension across levels or depth.", "tokens": [51098, 1485, 1433, 5531, 82, 38783, 40393, 267, 2841, 8980, 2108, 4358, 420, 7161, 13, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11851599298674485, "compression_ratio": 1.7025089605734767, "no_speech_prob": 1.2208132725219367e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 162678, "start": 1646.24, "end": 1650.58, "text": " The other term detects angular incompatibility tension within a single shell.", "tokens": [51338, 440, 661, 1433, 5531, 82, 24413, 40393, 267, 2841, 8980, 1951, 257, 2167, 8720, 13, 51555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11851599298674485, "compression_ratio": 1.7025089605734767, "no_speech_prob": 1.2208132725219367e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 162678, "start": 1650.74, "end": 1652.1, "text": " Wait, let me sit with that for a second.", "tokens": [51563, 3802, 11, 718, 385, 1394, 365, 300, 337, 257, 1150, 13, 51631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11851599298674485, "compression_ratio": 1.7025089605734767, "no_speech_prob": 1.2208132725219367e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 162678, "start": 1652.56, "end": 1655.04, "text": " The math can actually tell why I don't fit in.", "tokens": [51654, 440, 5221, 393, 767, 980, 983, 286, 500, 380, 3318, 294, 13, 51778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11851599298674485, "compression_ratio": 1.7025089605734767, "no_speech_prob": 1.2208132725219367e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 165504, "start": 1655.04, "end": 1662.02, "text": " It can distinguish if I don't fit in because I'm on the wrong hierarchical level versus not fitting in with my peers on the exact same level.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 393, 20206, 498, 286, 500, 380, 3318, 294, 570, 286, 478, 322, 264, 2085, 35250, 804, 1496, 5717, 406, 15669, 294, 365, 452, 16739, 322, 264, 1900, 912, 1496, 13, 50714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0713600292801857, "compression_ratio": 1.6739811912225706, "no_speech_prob": 1.3612854333350244e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 165504, "start": 1662.1399999999999, "end": 1665.36, "text": " That is the absolute beauty of the radial angular split.", "tokens": [50720, 663, 307, 264, 8236, 6643, 295, 264, 38783, 24413, 7472, 13, 50881], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0713600292801857, "compression_ratio": 1.6739811912225706, "no_speech_prob": 1.3612854333350244e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 165504, "start": 1665.56, "end": 1674.1399999999999, "text": " And the text applies this directly to physical fields, the RSVP field theory, which tracks scalar, vector, and entropy fields.", "tokens": [50891, 400, 264, 2487, 13165, 341, 3838, 281, 4001, 7909, 11, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 2519, 5261, 11, 597, 10218, 39684, 11, 8062, 11, 293, 30867, 7909, 13, 51320], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0713600292801857, "compression_ratio": 1.6739811912225706, "no_speech_prob": 1.3612854333350244e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 165504, "start": 1674.28, "end": 1675.1, "text": " Okay, let's look at that.", "tokens": [51327, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 574, 412, 300, 13, 51368], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0713600292801857, "compression_ratio": 1.6739811912225706, "no_speech_prob": 1.3612854333350244e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 165504, "start": 1675.22, "end": 1680.42, "text": " When you look at the gradient penalties in these fields through this split Laplacian, things get very clear.", "tokens": [51374, 1133, 291, 574, 412, 264, 16235, 35389, 294, 613, 7909, 807, 341, 7472, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 11, 721, 483, 588, 1850, 13, 51634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0713600292801857, "compression_ratio": 1.6739811912225706, "no_speech_prob": 1.3612854333350244e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 165504, "start": 1680.8999999999999, "end": 1684.36, "text": " Take the vector transport field, which describes how things flow or move.", "tokens": [51658, 3664, 264, 8062, 5495, 2519, 11, 597, 15626, 577, 721, 3095, 420, 1286, 13, 51831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0713600292801857, "compression_ratio": 1.6739811912225706, "no_speech_prob": 1.3612854333350244e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 168436, "start": 1684.36, "end": 1685.24, "text": " Like wind or water.", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 2468, 420, 1281, 13, 50409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15248312733390115, "compression_ratio": 1.5110132158590308, "no_speech_prob": 1.92791702741113e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 168436, "start": 1685.52, "end": 1686.0, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50423, 7587, 13, 50447], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15248312733390115, "compression_ratio": 1.5110132158590308, "no_speech_prob": 1.92791702741113e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 168436, "start": 1686.6599999999999, "end": 1694.6399999999999, "text": " The text points out that its vorticity, its curl, or its tendency to rotate like a whirlpool is intrinsically purely angular.", "tokens": [50480, 440, 2487, 2793, 484, 300, 1080, 371, 477, 44198, 11, 1080, 22591, 11, 420, 1080, 18187, 281, 13121, 411, 257, 35706, 17374, 307, 28621, 984, 17491, 24413, 13, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15248312733390115, "compression_ratio": 1.5110132158590308, "no_speech_prob": 1.92791702741113e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 168436, "start": 1695.12, "end": 1697.7199999999998, "text": " It penalizes rotation within a shell directly.", "tokens": [50903, 467, 13661, 5660, 12447, 1951, 257, 8720, 3838, 13, 51033], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15248312733390115, "compression_ratio": 1.5110132158590308, "no_speech_prob": 1.92791702741113e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 168436, "start": 1698.4399999999998, "end": 1703.6399999999999, "text": " Radial transport, which is moving straight out from the center like a ray of light, has no curl whatsoever.", "tokens": [51069, 9654, 831, 5495, 11, 597, 307, 2684, 2997, 484, 490, 264, 3056, 411, 257, 18592, 295, 1442, 11, 575, 572, 22591, 17076, 13, 51329], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15248312733390115, "compression_ratio": 1.5110132158590308, "no_speech_prob": 1.92791702741113e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 168436, "start": 1703.8799999999999, "end": 1705.1999999999998, "text": " And what about the entropy field?", "tokens": [51341, 400, 437, 466, 264, 30867, 2519, 30, 51407], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15248312733390115, "compression_ratio": 1.5110132158590308, "no_speech_prob": 1.92791702741113e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 170520, "start": 1705.2, "end": 1709.1200000000001, "text": " Because entropy is usually described as disorder, just things falling apart.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 30867, 307, 2673, 7619, 382, 13399, 11, 445, 721, 7440, 4936, 13, 50561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1852137605908891, "compression_ratio": 1.5482233502538072, "no_speech_prob": 1.5041993258607667e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 170520, "start": 1709.28, "end": 1711.82, "text": " But the text seems to give it a dual role here.", "tokens": [50569, 583, 264, 2487, 2544, 281, 976, 309, 257, 11848, 3090, 510, 13, 50696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1852137605908891, "compression_ratio": 1.5482233502538072, "no_speech_prob": 1.5041993258607667e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 170520, "start": 1712.16, "end": 1719.42, "text": " We usually think of entropy as this unstoppable force always increasing globally, slowly making a mess of the universe.", "tokens": [50713, 492, 2673, 519, 295, 30867, 382, 341, 48261, 3464, 1009, 5662, 18958, 11, 5692, 1455, 257, 2082, 295, 264, 6445, 13, 51076], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1852137605908891, "compression_ratio": 1.5482233502538072, "no_speech_prob": 1.5041993258607667e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 170520, "start": 1719.6000000000001, "end": 1722.4, "text": " But locally, entropy can decrease.", "tokens": [51085, 583, 16143, 11, 30867, 393, 11514, 13, 51225], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1852137605908891, "compression_ratio": 1.5482233502538072, "no_speech_prob": 1.5041993258607667e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 170520, "start": 1722.54, "end": 1723.3600000000001, "text": " Right, like life forming.", "tokens": [51232, 1779, 11, 411, 993, 15745, 13, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1852137605908891, "compression_ratio": 1.5482233502538072, "no_speech_prob": 1.5041993258607667e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 172336, "start": 1723.36, "end": 1723.8799999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1387143006195893, "compression_ratio": 1.5532994923857868, "no_speech_prob": 1.330048701383979e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 172336, "start": 1724.08, "end": 1728.06, "text": " A system can build local coherence, like a crystal forming or a cell organizing.", "tokens": [50401, 316, 1185, 393, 1322, 2654, 26528, 655, 11, 411, 257, 13662, 15745, 420, 257, 2815, 17608, 13, 50600], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1387143006195893, "compression_ratio": 1.5532994923857868, "no_speech_prob": 1.330048701383979e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 172336, "start": 1728.6399999999999, "end": 1732.3999999999999, "text": " But the Laplacian tells us exactly how it is building that coherence.", "tokens": [50629, 583, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 5112, 505, 2293, 577, 309, 307, 2390, 300, 26528, 655, 13, 50817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1387143006195893, "compression_ratio": 1.5532994923857868, "no_speech_prob": 1.330048701383979e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 172336, "start": 1732.76, "end": 1735.58, "text": " Is it organizing across levels a radial reduction in entropy?", "tokens": [50835, 1119, 309, 17608, 2108, 4358, 257, 38783, 11004, 294, 30867, 30, 50976], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1387143006195893, "compression_ratio": 1.5532994923857868, "no_speech_prob": 1.330048701383979e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 172336, "start": 1735.8799999999999, "end": 1740.3, "text": " Or is it creating highly organized patches within a single level an angular reduction?", "tokens": [50991, 1610, 307, 309, 4084, 5405, 9983, 26531, 1951, 257, 2167, 1496, 364, 24413, 11004, 30, 51212], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1387143006195893, "compression_ratio": 1.5532994923857868, "no_speech_prob": 1.330048701383979e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 174030, "start": 1740.3, "end": 1745.4199999999998, "text": " So the split Laplacian gives us the exact mathematical breakdown of where the tension is being resolved.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 264, 7472, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 2709, 505, 264, 1900, 18894, 18188, 295, 689, 264, 8980, 307, 885, 20772, 13, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14024078051249186, "compression_ratio": 1.5836065573770493, "no_speech_prob": 1.7901823686633511e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 174030, "start": 1745.56, "end": 1745.7, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50628, 1079, 13, 50635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14024078051249186, "compression_ratio": 1.5836065573770493, "no_speech_prob": 1.7901823686633511e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 174030, "start": 1745.78, "end": 1750.26, "text": " The text also talks about something called harmonic diagonalization in this section.", "tokens": [50639, 440, 2487, 611, 6686, 466, 746, 1219, 32270, 21539, 2144, 294, 341, 3541, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14024078051249186, "compression_ratio": 1.5836065573770493, "no_speech_prob": 1.7901823686633511e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 174030, "start": 1750.6599999999999, "end": 1758.8799999999999, "text": " It says the math penalizes fine, high-frequency angular structure far more severely than broad, low-frequency structure.", "tokens": [50883, 467, 1619, 264, 5221, 13661, 5660, 2489, 11, 1090, 12, 19325, 48154, 24413, 3877, 1400, 544, 26271, 813, 4152, 11, 2295, 12, 19325, 48154, 3877, 13, 51294], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14024078051249186, "compression_ratio": 1.5836065573770493, "no_speech_prob": 1.7901823686633511e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 174030, "start": 1759.44, "end": 1761.1, "text": " I read that sentence three times.", "tokens": [51322, 286, 1401, 300, 8174, 1045, 1413, 13, 51405], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14024078051249186, "compression_ratio": 1.5836065573770493, "no_speech_prob": 1.7901823686633511e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 174030, "start": 1761.6599999999999, "end": 1762.8799999999999, "text": " What does it actually mean in practice?", "tokens": [51433, 708, 775, 309, 767, 914, 294, 3124, 30, 51494], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14024078051249186, "compression_ratio": 1.5836065573770493, "no_speech_prob": 1.7901823686633511e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 174030, "start": 1763.08, "end": 1764.1599999999999, "text": " Let's visualize it.", "tokens": [51504, 961, 311, 23273, 309, 13, 51558], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14024078051249186, "compression_ratio": 1.5836065573770493, "no_speech_prob": 1.7901823686633511e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 174030, "start": 1764.6, "end": 1768.0, "text": " Imagine you're given a blank white sphere and a can of black paint.", "tokens": [51580, 11739, 291, 434, 2212, 257, 8247, 2418, 16687, 293, 257, 393, 295, 2211, 4225, 13, 51750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14024078051249186, "compression_ratio": 1.5836065573770493, "no_speech_prob": 1.7901823686633511e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 174030, "start": 1768.32, "end": 1768.56, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51766, 1033, 13, 51778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14024078051249186, "compression_ratio": 1.5836065573770493, "no_speech_prob": 1.7901823686633511e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 176856, "start": 1768.56, "end": 1777.1399999999999, "text": " If you paint exactly half of the sphere black and leave the other half white, that is a broad, low-frequency angular structure.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 4225, 2293, 1922, 295, 264, 16687, 2211, 293, 1856, 264, 661, 1922, 2418, 11, 300, 307, 257, 4152, 11, 2295, 12, 19325, 48154, 24413, 3877, 13, 50794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11502757498888465, "compression_ratio": 1.7324414715719063, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310961049355698e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 176856, "start": 1777.6399999999999, "end": 1781.1799999999998, "text": " The transition between the two colors happens only once along the equator.", "tokens": [50819, 440, 6034, 1296, 264, 732, 4577, 2314, 787, 1564, 2051, 264, 45544, 13, 50996], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11502757498888465, "compression_ratio": 1.7324414715719063, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310961049355698e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 176856, "start": 1781.8, "end": 1784.44, "text": " The Laplacian measures the tension at that single border.", "tokens": [51027, 440, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 8000, 264, 8980, 412, 300, 2167, 7838, 13, 51159], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11502757498888465, "compression_ratio": 1.7324414715719063, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310961049355698e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 176856, "start": 1784.58, "end": 1785.1, "text": " That makes sense.", "tokens": [51166, 663, 1669, 2020, 13, 51192], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11502757498888465, "compression_ratio": 1.7324414715719063, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310961049355698e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 176856, "start": 1785.32, "end": 1792.82, "text": " Now imagine instead of halves, you try to paint a highly intricate checkerboard pattern on the sphere with a million tiny black and white squares.", "tokens": [51203, 823, 3811, 2602, 295, 38490, 11, 291, 853, 281, 4225, 257, 5405, 38015, 1520, 260, 3787, 5102, 322, 264, 16687, 365, 257, 2459, 5870, 2211, 293, 2418, 19368, 13, 51578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11502757498888465, "compression_ratio": 1.7324414715719063, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310961049355698e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 176856, "start": 1793.1, "end": 1794.2, "text": " That sounds exhausting.", "tokens": [51592, 663, 3263, 34076, 13, 51647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11502757498888465, "compression_ratio": 1.7324414715719063, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310961049355698e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 176856, "start": 1794.58, "end": 1795.1599999999999, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [51666, 467, 307, 13, 51695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11502757498888465, "compression_ratio": 1.7324414715719063, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310961049355698e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 176856, "start": 1795.1599999999999, "end": 1798.1599999999999, "text": " And mathematically, that is high-frequency angular structure.", "tokens": [51695, 400, 44003, 11, 300, 307, 1090, 12, 19325, 48154, 24413, 3877, 13, 51845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11502757498888465, "compression_ratio": 1.7324414715719063, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310961049355698e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 179856, "start": 1798.56, "end": 1806.22, "text": " The Laplacian, our incompatibility detector, registers massive amounts of tension at every single border between every single one of those tiny squares.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 11, 527, 40393, 267, 2841, 25712, 11, 38351, 5994, 11663, 295, 8980, 412, 633, 2167, 7838, 1296, 633, 2167, 472, 295, 729, 5870, 19368, 13, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09565321992083294, "compression_ratio": 1.3471074380165289, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279196736635916e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 179856, "start": 1806.3799999999999, "end": 1806.9199999999998, "text": " Oh, I see.", "tokens": [50756, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 50783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09565321992083294, "compression_ratio": 1.3471074380165289, "no_speech_prob": 1.7279196736635916e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 180692, "start": 1806.92, "end": 1816.64, "text": " The math intrinsically penalizes complex, highly detailed angular patterns far more heavily than broad, simple ones because it detects vastly more local mismatch.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 5221, 28621, 984, 13661, 5660, 3997, 11, 5405, 9942, 24413, 8294, 1400, 544, 10950, 813, 4152, 11, 2199, 2306, 570, 309, 5531, 82, 41426, 544, 2654, 23220, 852, 13, 50851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0713911807095563, "compression_ratio": 1.4736842105263157, "no_speech_prob": 1.2445940545530165e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 180692, "start": 1817.3600000000001, "end": 1821.3400000000001, "text": " Maintaining that checkerboard requires a lot more energy than maintaining the two halves.", "tokens": [50887, 376, 5114, 3686, 300, 1520, 260, 3787, 7029, 257, 688, 544, 2281, 813, 14916, 264, 732, 38490, 13, 51086], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0713911807095563, "compression_ratio": 1.4736842105263157, "no_speech_prob": 1.2445940545530165e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 182134, "start": 1821.34, "end": 1833.4599999999998, "text": " Okay, so when the Laplacian detects all this mismatch, when it registers my neon pink suit in the room of tuxedos, or the million borders on the checkerboard, how does the system naturally respond?", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 370, 562, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 5531, 82, 439, 341, 23220, 852, 11, 562, 309, 38351, 452, 30820, 7022, 5722, 294, 264, 1808, 295, 256, 2449, 292, 329, 11, 420, 264, 2459, 16287, 322, 264, 1520, 260, 3787, 11, 577, 775, 264, 1185, 8195, 4196, 30, 50971], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1292566955089569, "compression_ratio": 1.5398230088495575, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610584656530757e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 182134, "start": 1833.6799999999998, "end": 1836.12, "text": " It doesn't just sit there in a state of high tension forever, right?", "tokens": [50982, 467, 1177, 380, 445, 1394, 456, 294, 257, 1785, 295, 1090, 8980, 5680, 11, 558, 30, 51104], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1292566955089569, "compression_ratio": 1.5398230088495575, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610584656530757e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 182134, "start": 1836.12, "end": 1837.5, "text": " Yeah, it tries to fix it.", "tokens": [51104, 865, 11, 309, 9898, 281, 3191, 309, 13, 51173], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1292566955089569, "compression_ratio": 1.5398230088495575, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610584656530757e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 182134, "start": 1837.6799999999998, "end": 1840.26, "text": " As the old saying goes, nature of horror is a gradient.", "tokens": [51182, 1018, 264, 1331, 1566, 1709, 11, 3687, 295, 11501, 307, 257, 16235, 13, 51311], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1292566955089569, "compression_ratio": 1.5398230088495575, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610584656530757e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 184026, "start": 1840.26, "end": 1843.64, "text": " This brings us to the geometric theory of repair.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 33246, 5261, 295, 10535, 13, 50534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18133388095431857, "compression_ratio": 1.60352422907489, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325104687532009e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 184026, "start": 1844.4, "end": 1847.44, "text": " This might be the most beautiful and poetic part of the deep drive for me.", "tokens": [50572, 639, 1062, 312, 264, 881, 2238, 293, 41080, 644, 295, 264, 2452, 3332, 337, 385, 13, 50724], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18133388095431857, "compression_ratio": 1.60352422907489, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325104687532009e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 184026, "start": 1847.96, "end": 1849.82, "text": " The author defines repair mathematically.", "tokens": [50750, 440, 3793, 23122, 10535, 44003, 13, 50843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18133388095431857, "compression_ratio": 1.60352422907489, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325104687532009e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 184026, "start": 1850.3, "end": 1852.08, "text": " It isn't just a biological concept.", "tokens": [50867, 467, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 13910, 3410, 13, 50956], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18133388095431857, "compression_ratio": 1.60352422907489, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325104687532009e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 184026, "start": 1852.3, "end": 1855.04, "text": " It is literally gradient descent on local mismatch.", "tokens": [50967, 467, 307, 3736, 16235, 23475, 322, 2654, 23220, 852, 13, 51104], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18133388095431857, "compression_ratio": 1.60352422907489, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325104687532009e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 184026, "start": 1855.12, "end": 1855.34, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51108, 1079, 13, 51119], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18133388095431857, "compression_ratio": 1.60352422907489, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325104687532009e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 184026, "start": 1855.7, "end": 1861.24, "text": " The system naturally moves in the direction that most reduces the Laplacian's signal of incompatibility.", "tokens": [51137, 440, 1185, 8195, 6067, 294, 264, 3513, 300, 881, 18081, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 311, 6358, 295, 40393, 267, 2841, 13, 51414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18133388095431857, "compression_ratio": 1.60352422907489, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325104687532009e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 186124, "start": 1861.24, "end": 1866.22, "text": " So the text identifies two fundamental opposing forces at work in this process.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 264, 2487, 34597, 732, 8088, 27890, 5874, 412, 589, 294, 341, 1399, 13, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1802178733369224, "compression_ratio": 1.7413127413127414, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610491415143923e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 186124, "start": 1866.66, "end": 1867.78, "text": " First is the Lamphrodine.", "tokens": [50636, 2386, 307, 264, 18825, 950, 11452, 533, 13, 50692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1802178733369224, "compression_ratio": 1.7413127413127414, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610491415143923e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 186124, "start": 1868.08, "end": 1870.0, "text": " The Lamphrodine represents the repair pressure.", "tokens": [50707, 440, 18825, 950, 11452, 533, 8855, 264, 10535, 3321, 13, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1802178733369224, "compression_ratio": 1.7413127413127414, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610491415143923e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 186124, "start": 1870.64, "end": 1875.42, "text": " It is the dynamic force that forces the relaxation and smoothing of gradients.", "tokens": [50835, 467, 307, 264, 8546, 3464, 300, 5874, 264, 30315, 293, 899, 6259, 571, 295, 2771, 2448, 13, 51074], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1802178733369224, "compression_ratio": 1.7413127413127414, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610491415143923e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 186124, "start": 1875.76, "end": 1877.66, "text": " It wants to erase the tension.", "tokens": [51091, 467, 2738, 281, 23525, 264, 8980, 13, 51186], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1802178733369224, "compression_ratio": 1.7413127413127414, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610491415143923e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 186124, "start": 1878.18, "end": 1880.0, "text": " It wants to blend everything together peacefully.", "tokens": [51212, 467, 2738, 281, 10628, 1203, 1214, 36485, 13, 51303], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1802178733369224, "compression_ratio": 1.7413127413127414, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610491415143923e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 186124, "start": 1880.2, "end": 1883.28, "text": " It wants me to change into a tuxedo so I match the room.", "tokens": [51313, 467, 2738, 385, 281, 1319, 666, 257, 256, 2449, 26351, 370, 286, 2995, 264, 1808, 13, 51467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1802178733369224, "compression_ratio": 1.7413127413127414, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610491415143923e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 186124, "start": 1883.34, "end": 1883.84, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51470, 7587, 13, 51495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1802178733369224, "compression_ratio": 1.7413127413127414, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610491415143923e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 186124, "start": 1884.44, "end": 1887.92, "text": " But consider what happens if the Lamphrodine went completely unchecked.", "tokens": [51525, 583, 1949, 437, 2314, 498, 264, 18825, 950, 11452, 533, 1437, 2584, 46672, 292, 13, 51699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1802178733369224, "compression_ratio": 1.7413127413127414, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610491415143923e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 188792, "start": 1887.92, "end": 1894.3400000000001, "text": " If repair pressure was the only force in the universe, it would smooth away all distinguishing structure.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 10535, 3321, 390, 264, 787, 3464, 294, 264, 6445, 11, 309, 576, 5508, 1314, 439, 11365, 3807, 3877, 13, 50686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14113332692859243, "compression_ratio": 1.6953125, "no_speech_prob": 1.875908933399173e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 188792, "start": 1894.96, "end": 1901.64, "text": " Every feature, every boundary, every distinct element would dissolve into a featureless, uniform, gray void.", "tokens": [50717, 2048, 4111, 11, 633, 12866, 11, 633, 10644, 4478, 576, 30150, 666, 257, 4111, 1832, 11, 9452, 11, 10855, 22009, 13, 51051], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14113332692859243, "compression_ratio": 1.6953125, "no_speech_prob": 1.875908933399173e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 188792, "start": 1901.8200000000002, "end": 1903.54, "text": " Everything would just be perfectly average.", "tokens": [51060, 5471, 576, 445, 312, 6239, 4274, 13, 51146], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14113332692859243, "compression_ratio": 1.6953125, "no_speech_prob": 1.875908933399173e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 188792, "start": 1903.7, "end": 1903.92, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51154, 1779, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14113332692859243, "compression_ratio": 1.6953125, "no_speech_prob": 1.875908933399173e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 188792, "start": 1904.28, "end": 1906.52, "text": " So opposing the Lamphrodine is the Lamphron.", "tokens": [51183, 407, 27890, 264, 18825, 950, 11452, 533, 307, 264, 18825, 950, 2044, 13, 51295], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14113332692859243, "compression_ratio": 1.6953125, "no_speech_prob": 1.875908933399173e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 188792, "start": 1906.64, "end": 1907.8600000000001, "text": " The structural stabilizer.", "tokens": [51301, 440, 15067, 11652, 6545, 13, 51362], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14113332692859243, "compression_ratio": 1.6953125, "no_speech_prob": 1.875908933399173e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 188792, "start": 1908.04, "end": 1908.4, "text": " Correct.", "tokens": [51371, 12753, 13, 51389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14113332692859243, "compression_ratio": 1.6953125, "no_speech_prob": 1.875908933399173e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 188792, "start": 1908.8200000000002, "end": 1913.38, "text": " The Lamphron is the tendency that allows coherent configurations like distinct objects,", "tokens": [51410, 440, 18825, 950, 2044, 307, 264, 18187, 300, 4045, 36239, 31493, 411, 10644, 6565, 11, 51638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14113332692859243, "compression_ratio": 1.6953125, "no_speech_prob": 1.875908933399173e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 191338, "start": 1913.38, "end": 1918.5400000000002, "text": " biological cells, or distinct states of information to persist despite the pressure to blend in.", "tokens": [50365, 13910, 5438, 11, 420, 10644, 4368, 295, 1589, 281, 13233, 7228, 264, 3321, 281, 10628, 294, 13, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11859561121741007, "compression_ratio": 1.577092511013216, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179254759539965e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 191338, "start": 1918.7800000000002, "end": 1920.22, "text": " So it's this constant push and pull.", "tokens": [50635, 407, 309, 311, 341, 5754, 2944, 293, 2235, 13, 50707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11859561121741007, "compression_ratio": 1.577092511013216, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179254759539965e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 191338, "start": 1920.5600000000002, "end": 1923.42, "text": " The duality between these two is critical for existence.", "tokens": [50724, 440, 11848, 507, 1296, 613, 732, 307, 4924, 337, 9123, 13, 50867], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11859561121741007, "compression_ratio": 1.577092511013216, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179254759539965e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 191338, "start": 1924.0, "end": 1926.2600000000002, "text": " Too much Lamphrodine and you get a featureless void.", "tokens": [50896, 11395, 709, 18825, 950, 11452, 533, 293, 291, 483, 257, 4111, 1832, 22009, 13, 51009], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11859561121741007, "compression_ratio": 1.577092511013216, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179254759539965e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 191338, "start": 1926.8200000000002, "end": 1933.42, "text": " Too much Lamphron and the system becomes entirely rigid, frozen, and incapable of adapting or healing from damage.", "tokens": [51037, 11395, 709, 18825, 950, 2044, 293, 264, 1185, 3643, 7696, 22195, 11, 12496, 11, 293, 44174, 295, 34942, 420, 9745, 490, 4344, 13, 51367], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11859561121741007, "compression_ratio": 1.577092511013216, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179254759539965e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 193342, "start": 1933.42, "end": 1940.7, "text": " So repair is this constant, agonizing, beautiful battle between smoothing things out and holding on to structure.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 10535, 307, 341, 5754, 11, 623, 266, 3319, 11, 2238, 4635, 1296, 899, 6259, 571, 721, 484, 293, 5061, 322, 281, 3877, 13, 50729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14049022953684737, "compression_ratio": 1.5732758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362216486223713e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 193342, "start": 1941.0600000000002, "end": 1946.78, "text": " But the text introduces a mathematical theorem here called the curvature defect, which just blew my mind.", "tokens": [50747, 583, 264, 2487, 31472, 257, 18894, 20904, 510, 1219, 264, 37638, 16445, 11, 597, 445, 19075, 452, 1575, 13, 51033], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14049022953684737, "compression_ratio": 1.5732758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362216486223713e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 193342, "start": 1947.1200000000001, "end": 1950.5600000000002, "text": " Because the math proves that perfect repair is actually impossible.", "tokens": [51050, 1436, 264, 5221, 25019, 300, 2176, 10535, 307, 767, 6243, 13, 51222], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14049022953684737, "compression_ratio": 1.5732758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362216486223713e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 193342, "start": 1950.8200000000002, "end": 1953.1200000000001, "text": " This is a fundamental geometric law.", "tokens": [51235, 639, 307, 257, 8088, 33246, 2101, 13, 51350], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14049022953684737, "compression_ratio": 1.5732758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362216486223713e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 193342, "start": 1953.68, "end": 1956.6000000000001, "text": " A repair process redistributes mismatch.", "tokens": [51378, 316, 10535, 1399, 36198, 2024, 1819, 23220, 852, 13, 51524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14049022953684737, "compression_ratio": 1.5732758620689655, "no_speech_prob": 1.6362216486223713e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 195660, "start": 1956.6, "end": 1958.4399999999998, "text": " It doesn't always eliminate it perfectly.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1177, 380, 1009, 13819, 309, 6239, 13, 50457], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1177851909727562, "compression_ratio": 1.6266233766233766, "no_speech_prob": 2.125688947779425e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 195660, "start": 1959.06, "end": 1967.9199999999998, "text": " Because a closed shell, like the surface of a sphere, inherently has positive curvature, you are mathematically forced to have some residual tension.", "tokens": [50488, 1436, 257, 5395, 8720, 11, 411, 264, 3753, 295, 257, 16687, 11, 27993, 575, 3353, 37638, 11, 291, 366, 44003, 7579, 281, 362, 512, 27980, 8980, 13, 50931], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1177851909727562, "compression_ratio": 1.6266233766233766, "no_speech_prob": 2.125688947779425e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 195660, "start": 1968.12, "end": 1970.36, "text": " I think you mentioned the Harry Ball theorem for this.", "tokens": [50941, 286, 519, 291, 2835, 264, 9378, 10744, 20904, 337, 341, 13, 51053], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1177851909727562, "compression_ratio": 1.6266233766233766, "no_speech_prob": 2.125688947779425e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 195660, "start": 1970.5, "end": 1970.76, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51060, 1079, 13, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1177851909727562, "compression_ratio": 1.6266233766233766, "no_speech_prob": 2.125688947779425e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 195660, "start": 1971.0, "end": 1971.74, "text": " Have you ever heard of it?", "tokens": [51085, 3560, 291, 1562, 2198, 295, 309, 30, 51122], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1177851909727562, "compression_ratio": 1.6266233766233766, "no_speech_prob": 2.125688947779425e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 195660, "start": 1971.86, "end": 1974.1999999999998, "text": " I have, but remind me how it works in this context.", "tokens": [51128, 286, 362, 11, 457, 4160, 385, 577, 309, 1985, 294, 341, 4319, 13, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1177851909727562, "compression_ratio": 1.6266233766233766, "no_speech_prob": 2.125688947779425e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 195660, "start": 1974.32, "end": 1982.3799999999999, "text": " It's a theorem in algebraic topology that states you cannot comb a Harry Ball flat without leaving at least one cowlick or tuft of hair sticking up.", "tokens": [51251, 467, 311, 257, 20904, 294, 21989, 299, 1192, 1793, 300, 4368, 291, 2644, 2512, 257, 9378, 10744, 4962, 1553, 5012, 412, 1935, 472, 8408, 75, 618, 420, 2604, 844, 295, 2578, 13465, 493, 13, 51654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1177851909727562, "compression_ratio": 1.6266233766233766, "no_speech_prob": 2.125688947779425e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 195660, "start": 1982.48, "end": 1983.32, "text": " You just can't do it.", "tokens": [51659, 509, 445, 393, 380, 360, 309, 13, 51701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1177851909727562, "compression_ratio": 1.6266233766233766, "no_speech_prob": 2.125688947779425e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 198332, "start": 1983.32, "end": 1989.1, "text": " The geometry of a closed, curved surface dictates that you cannot smooth everything out perfectly.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 18426, 295, 257, 5395, 11, 24991, 3753, 12569, 1024, 300, 291, 2644, 5508, 1203, 484, 6239, 13, 50654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0937546123157848, "compression_ratio": 1.7304964539007093, "no_speech_prob": 1.3780125044521307e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 198332, "start": 1989.78, "end": 1995.34, "text": " Some quantity of angular distinguishing power, some tension, will always be lost or compressed into a defect.", "tokens": [50688, 2188, 11275, 295, 24413, 11365, 3807, 1347, 11, 512, 8980, 11, 486, 1009, 312, 2731, 420, 30353, 666, 257, 16445, 13, 50966], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0937546123157848, "compression_ratio": 1.7304964539007093, "no_speech_prob": 1.3780125044521307e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 198332, "start": 1995.5, "end": 2004.0, "text": " So if we pull back and ask what this all means, it means perfect repair is literally a geometric impossibility on a closed surface.", "tokens": [50974, 407, 498, 321, 2235, 646, 293, 1029, 437, 341, 439, 1355, 11, 309, 1355, 2176, 10535, 307, 3736, 257, 33246, 38802, 2841, 322, 257, 5395, 3753, 13, 51399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0937546123157848, "compression_ratio": 1.7304964539007093, "no_speech_prob": 1.3780125044521307e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 198332, "start": 2004.52, "end": 2011.24, "text": " You can move the tension around, you can sweep it out of the rug, you can push it to the edges, but you cannot erase it completely from the system.", "tokens": [51425, 509, 393, 1286, 264, 8980, 926, 11, 291, 393, 22169, 309, 484, 295, 264, 18329, 11, 291, 393, 2944, 309, 281, 264, 8819, 11, 457, 291, 2644, 23525, 309, 2584, 490, 264, 1185, 13, 51761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0937546123157848, "compression_ratio": 1.7304964539007093, "no_speech_prob": 1.3780125044521307e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 201124, "start": 2011.24, "end": 2019.52, "text": " Exactly. And if we connect this to the bigger picture, it has profound implications for things like biological healing or even societal repair.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 400, 498, 321, 1745, 341, 281, 264, 3801, 3036, 11, 309, 575, 14382, 16602, 337, 721, 411, 13910, 9745, 420, 754, 33472, 10535, 13, 50779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10116248517423063, "compression_ratio": 1.5245098039215685, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492072464624474e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 201124, "start": 2020.24, "end": 2024.8, "text": " Think about a city filling a pothole or a body healing a wound.", "tokens": [50815, 6557, 466, 257, 2307, 10623, 257, 280, 900, 4812, 420, 257, 1772, 9745, 257, 10999, 13, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10116248517423063, "compression_ratio": 1.5245098039215685, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492072464624474e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 201124, "start": 2025.56, "end": 2031.38, "text": " A process can be functionally adequate. It heals the cut. It fixes the road. It stabilizes the economy.", "tokens": [51081, 316, 1399, 393, 312, 2445, 379, 20927, 13, 467, 45653, 264, 1723, 13, 467, 32539, 264, 3060, 13, 467, 11652, 5660, 264, 5010, 13, 51372], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10116248517423063, "compression_ratio": 1.5245098039215685, "no_speech_prob": 1.6492072464624474e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 203138, "start": 2031.38, "end": 2036.74, "text": " The mismatch is pushed below a critical threshold so the system can keep running.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 23220, 852, 307, 9152, 2507, 257, 4924, 14678, 370, 264, 1185, 393, 1066, 2614, 13, 50633], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1529363275884272, "compression_ratio": 1.6528925619834711, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045789913779474e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 203138, "start": 2037.24, "end": 2039.3600000000001, "text": " But it might not be architecturally transparent.", "tokens": [50658, 583, 309, 1062, 406, 312, 6331, 6512, 12737, 13, 50764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1529363275884272, "compression_ratio": 1.6528925619834711, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045789913779474e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 203138, "start": 2039.5400000000002, "end": 2041.24, "text": " What does that mean, architecturally transparent?", "tokens": [50773, 708, 775, 300, 914, 11, 6331, 6512, 12737, 30, 50858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1529363275884272, "compression_ratio": 1.6528925619834711, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045789913779474e-12}, {"id": 545, "seek": 203138, "start": 2041.4, "end": 2048.82, "text": " It means we still might not fully understand the exact cellular mechanism or the exact bureaucratic pathway that did the smoothing.", "tokens": [50866, 467, 1355, 321, 920, 1062, 406, 4498, 1223, 264, 1900, 29267, 7513, 420, 264, 1900, 26360, 25198, 18590, 300, 630, 264, 899, 6259, 571, 13, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1529363275884272, "compression_ratio": 1.6528925619834711, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045789913779474e-12}, {"id": 546, "seek": 203138, "start": 2049.26, "end": 2053.3, "text": " And more importantly, the fundamental tension hasn't been eradicated.", "tokens": [51259, 400, 544, 8906, 11, 264, 8088, 8980, 6132, 380, 668, 33078, 3587, 13, 51461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1529363275884272, "compression_ratio": 1.6528925619834711, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045789913779474e-12}, {"id": 547, "seek": 203138, "start": 2053.52, "end": 2054.06, "text": " It's just hidden.", "tokens": [51472, 467, 311, 445, 7633, 13, 51499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1529363275884272, "compression_ratio": 1.6528925619834711, "no_speech_prob": 1.6045789913779474e-12}, {"id": 548, "seek": 205406, "start": 2054.06, "end": 2060.72, "text": " It's been localized into scar tissue or smeared so thinly across the geometry of the system that we can't see it anymore.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 668, 44574, 666, 10569, 12404, 420, 41818, 1642, 370, 47337, 2108, 264, 18426, 295, 264, 1185, 300, 321, 393, 380, 536, 309, 3602, 13, 50698], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0920730891980623, "compression_ratio": 1.5826446280991735, "no_speech_prob": 1.6165692916236818e-12}, {"id": 549, "seek": 205406, "start": 2060.98, "end": 2063.68, "text": " But geometrically, the tension is still there.", "tokens": [50711, 583, 12956, 81, 984, 11, 264, 8980, 307, 920, 456, 13, 50846], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0920730891980623, "compression_ratio": 1.5826446280991735, "no_speech_prob": 1.6165692916236818e-12}, {"id": 550, "seek": 205406, "start": 2063.96, "end": 2068.6, "text": " Okay, let's take a deep breath here because we are about to make a massive conceptual leap.", "tokens": [50860, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 747, 257, 2452, 6045, 510, 570, 321, 366, 466, 281, 652, 257, 5994, 24106, 19438, 13, 51092], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0920730891980623, "compression_ratio": 1.5826446280991735, "no_speech_prob": 1.6165692916236818e-12}, {"id": 551, "seek": 205406, "start": 2068.7, "end": 2069.34, "text": " Yes, we are.", "tokens": [51097, 1079, 11, 321, 366, 13, 51129], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0920730891980623, "compression_ratio": 1.5826446280991735, "no_speech_prob": 1.6165692916236818e-12}, {"id": 552, "seek": 205406, "start": 2069.88, "end": 2076.0, "text": " Up until now, we've been talking about physical fields, biological tissue, planetary shells, tangible things.", "tokens": [51156, 5858, 1826, 586, 11, 321, 600, 668, 1417, 466, 4001, 7909, 11, 13910, 12404, 11, 35788, 22523, 11, 27094, 721, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0920730891980623, "compression_ratio": 1.5826446280991735, "no_speech_prob": 1.6165692916236818e-12}, {"id": 553, "seek": 207600, "start": 2076.0, "end": 2088.28, "text": " But the author takes this exact same spherical math, the radial progression, the angular boundaries, the Laplacian tension, and applies it to a space that has no physical reality at all.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 3793, 2516, 341, 1900, 912, 37300, 5221, 11, 264, 38783, 18733, 11, 264, 24413, 13180, 11, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 8980, 11, 293, 13165, 309, 281, 257, 1901, 300, 575, 572, 4001, 4103, 412, 439, 13, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12373384423212173, "compression_ratio": 1.6654804270462633, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234823815158839e-12}, {"id": 554, "seek": 207600, "start": 2088.7, "end": 2091.46, "text": " We move from physical space to possibility space.", "tokens": [51000, 492, 1286, 490, 4001, 1901, 281, 7959, 1901, 13, 51138], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12373384423212173, "compression_ratio": 1.6654804270462633, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234823815158839e-12}, {"id": 555, "seek": 207600, "start": 2091.86, "end": 2097.98, "text": " The text examines a theoretical framework called SPHERPOP, which is a computational calculus for state spaces.", "tokens": [51158, 440, 2487, 1139, 1652, 257, 20864, 8388, 1219, 8420, 39, 1598, 47, 12059, 11, 597, 307, 257, 28270, 33400, 337, 1785, 7673, 13, 51464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12373384423212173, "compression_ratio": 1.6654804270462633, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234823815158839e-12}, {"id": 556, "seek": 207600, "start": 2098.12, "end": 2098.66, "text": " Think spaces.", "tokens": [51471, 6557, 7673, 13, 51498], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12373384423212173, "compression_ratio": 1.6654804270462633, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234823815158839e-12}, {"id": 557, "seek": 207600, "start": 2098.96, "end": 2099.18, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51513, 1779, 13, 51524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12373384423212173, "compression_ratio": 1.6654804270462633, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234823815158839e-12}, {"id": 558, "seek": 207600, "start": 2099.46, "end": 2103.08, "text": " It maps out possibilities, human decisions, and computational histories.", "tokens": [51538, 467, 11317, 484, 12178, 11, 1952, 5327, 11, 293, 28270, 30631, 13, 51719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12373384423212173, "compression_ratio": 1.6654804270462633, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234823815158839e-12}, {"id": 559, "seek": 207600, "start": 2103.54, "end": 2104.64, "text": " It is completely abstract.", "tokens": [51742, 467, 307, 2584, 12649, 13, 51797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12373384423212173, "compression_ratio": 1.6654804270462633, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234823815158839e-12}, {"id": 560, "seek": 210464, "start": 2104.64, "end": 2111.24, "text": " There is no physical planet, no gravity, no distance, yet it perfectly matches the spherical decomposition we've been discussing.", "tokens": [50365, 821, 307, 572, 4001, 5054, 11, 572, 12110, 11, 572, 4560, 11, 1939, 309, 6239, 10676, 264, 37300, 48356, 321, 600, 668, 10850, 13, 50695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13956426280413486, "compression_ratio": 1.6417445482866044, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112797503175293e-12}, {"id": 561, "seek": 210464, "start": 2111.56, "end": 2112.68, "text": " It's computing without a planet.", "tokens": [50711, 467, 311, 15866, 1553, 257, 5054, 13, 50767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13956426280413486, "compression_ratio": 1.6417445482866044, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112797503175293e-12}, {"id": 562, "seek": 210464, "start": 2113.18, "end": 2115.9, "text": " In SPHERPOP, the radial coordinate isn't distance anymore.", "tokens": [50792, 682, 8420, 39, 1598, 47, 12059, 11, 264, 38783, 15670, 1943, 380, 4560, 3602, 13, 50928], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13956426280413486, "compression_ratio": 1.6417445482866044, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112797503175293e-12}, {"id": 563, "seek": 210464, "start": 2116.06, "end": 2116.68, "text": " It's called POP.", "tokens": [50936, 467, 311, 1219, 430, 12059, 13, 50967], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13956426280413486, "compression_ratio": 1.6417445482866044, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112797503175293e-12}, {"id": 564, "seek": 210464, "start": 2117.2, "end": 2120.3399999999997, "text": " And POP represents the irreversible record of choices made.", "tokens": [50993, 400, 430, 12059, 8855, 264, 16014, 840, 964, 2136, 295, 7994, 1027, 13, 51150], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13956426280413486, "compression_ratio": 1.6417445482866044, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112797503175293e-12}, {"id": 565, "seek": 210464, "start": 2120.6, "end": 2123.52, "text": " Making a permanent commitment consumes the option space.", "tokens": [51163, 14595, 257, 10996, 8371, 48823, 264, 3614, 1901, 13, 51309], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13956426280413486, "compression_ratio": 1.6417445482866044, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112797503175293e-12}, {"id": 566, "seek": 210464, "start": 2124.16, "end": 2125.8599999999997, "text": " Think about the conservation of possibility.", "tokens": [51341, 6557, 466, 264, 16185, 295, 7959, 13, 51426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13956426280413486, "compression_ratio": 1.6417445482866044, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112797503175293e-12}, {"id": 567, "seek": 210464, "start": 2126.3399999999997, "end": 2133.3199999999997, "text": " When you begin a complex computation, or even just begin your life as a young person, you have a vast space of options.", "tokens": [51450, 1133, 291, 1841, 257, 3997, 24903, 11, 420, 754, 445, 1841, 428, 993, 382, 257, 2037, 954, 11, 291, 362, 257, 8369, 1901, 295, 3956, 13, 51799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13956426280413486, "compression_ratio": 1.6417445482866044, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112797503175293e-12}, {"id": 568, "seek": 210464, "start": 2133.8199999999997, "end": 2134.12, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51824, 1779, 13, 51839], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13956426280413486, "compression_ratio": 1.6417445482866044, "no_speech_prob": 1.8112797503175293e-12}, {"id": 569, "seek": 213412, "start": 2134.12, "end": 2141.7799999999997, "text": " When you make a permanent commitment, a POP, you convert potential into recorded history.", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 291, 652, 257, 10996, 8371, 11, 257, 430, 12059, 11, 291, 7620, 3995, 666, 8287, 2503, 13, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13251113891601562, "compression_ratio": 1.4673913043478262, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609805336004977e-12}, {"id": 570, "seek": 213412, "start": 2142.98, "end": 2150.8199999999997, "text": " Radius, in this abstract computational space, is a measure of how much of your initial option space has been consumed.", "tokens": [50808, 9654, 4872, 11, 294, 341, 12649, 28270, 1901, 11, 307, 257, 3481, 295, 577, 709, 295, 428, 5883, 3614, 1901, 575, 668, 21226, 13, 51200], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13251113891601562, "compression_ratio": 1.4673913043478262, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609805336004977e-12}, {"id": 571, "seek": 213412, "start": 2151.2, "end": 2154.68, "text": " You are moving outward radially across levels of realization.", "tokens": [51219, 509, 366, 2684, 26914, 2843, 2270, 2108, 4358, 295, 25138, 13, 51393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13251113891601562, "compression_ratio": 1.4673913043478262, "no_speech_prob": 1.4609805336004977e-12}, {"id": 572, "seek": 215468, "start": 2154.68, "end": 2158.8999999999996, "text": " The analogy that came to mind for this was reading a choose-your-own-adventure book.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 21663, 300, 1361, 281, 1575, 337, 341, 390, 3760, 257, 2826, 12, 23093, 12, 648, 12, 345, 2475, 540, 1446, 13, 50576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16349345347920402, "compression_ratio": 1.618320610687023, "no_speech_prob": 1.9276349180058494e-12}, {"id": 573, "seek": 215468, "start": 2158.98, "end": 2160.2599999999998, "text": " Oh, I so love those.", "tokens": [50580, 876, 11, 286, 370, 959, 729, 13, 50644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16349345347920402, "compression_ratio": 1.618320610687023, "no_speech_prob": 1.9276349180058494e-12}, {"id": 574, "seek": 215468, "start": 2160.2999999999997, "end": 2160.62, "text": " Me too.", "tokens": [50646, 1923, 886, 13, 50662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16349345347920402, "compression_ratio": 1.618320610687023, "no_speech_prob": 1.9276349180058494e-12}, {"id": 575, "seek": 215468, "start": 2161.14, "end": 2164.44, "text": " And moving your finger down the page, reading the different choices.", "tokens": [50688, 400, 2684, 428, 5984, 760, 264, 3028, 11, 3760, 264, 819, 7994, 13, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16349345347920402, "compression_ratio": 1.618320610687023, "no_speech_prob": 1.9276349180058494e-12}, {"id": 576, "seek": 215468, "start": 2164.8999999999996, "end": 2167.04, "text": " If you want to open the door, go to page 12.", "tokens": [50876, 759, 291, 528, 281, 1269, 264, 2853, 11, 352, 281, 3028, 2272, 13, 50983], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16349345347920402, "compression_ratio": 1.618320610687023, "no_speech_prob": 1.9276349180058494e-12}, {"id": 577, "seek": 215468, "start": 2167.3199999999997, "end": 2170.7799999999997, "text": " If you want to fight the goblin, go to age 42 up and that is angular movement.", "tokens": [50997, 759, 291, 528, 281, 2092, 264, 20489, 5045, 11, 352, 281, 3205, 14034, 493, 293, 300, 307, 24413, 3963, 13, 51170], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16349345347920402, "compression_ratio": 1.618320610687023, "no_speech_prob": 1.9276349180058494e-12}, {"id": 578, "seek": 215468, "start": 2171.2799999999997, "end": 2175.2599999999998, "text": " You are just reorganizing options in your head, evaluating them laterally.", "tokens": [51195, 509, 366, 445, 41203, 3319, 3956, 294, 428, 1378, 11, 27479, 552, 1780, 379, 13, 51394], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16349345347920402, "compression_ratio": 1.618320610687023, "no_speech_prob": 1.9276349180058494e-12}, {"id": 579, "seek": 215468, "start": 2175.3799999999997, "end": 2176.74, "text": " You aren't actually consuming them.", "tokens": [51400, 509, 3212, 380, 767, 19867, 552, 13, 51468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16349345347920402, "compression_ratio": 1.618320610687023, "no_speech_prob": 1.9276349180058494e-12}, {"id": 580, "seek": 215468, "start": 2176.7999999999997, "end": 2176.94, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51471, 1779, 13, 51478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16349345347920402, "compression_ratio": 1.618320610687023, "no_speech_prob": 1.9276349180058494e-12}, {"id": 581, "seek": 217694, "start": 2176.94, "end": 2178.2400000000002, "text": " You're just exploring the shell.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 434, 445, 12736, 264, 8720, 13, 50430], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18573118078297582, "compression_ratio": 1.3733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.803406924662243e-12}, {"id": 582, "seek": 217694, "start": 2178.36, "end": 2183.18, "text": " But the moment you actually physically flip the page to 42, that is a radial move.", "tokens": [50436, 583, 264, 1623, 291, 767, 9762, 7929, 264, 3028, 281, 14034, 11, 300, 307, 257, 38783, 1286, 13, 50677], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18573118078297582, "compression_ratio": 1.3733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.803406924662243e-12}, {"id": 583, "seek": 217694, "start": 2183.44, "end": 2185.88, "text": " You've consumed potential and made a reality.", "tokens": [50690, 509, 600, 21226, 3995, 293, 1027, 257, 4103, 13, 50812], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18573118078297582, "compression_ratio": 1.3733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.803406924662243e-12}, {"id": 584, "seek": 217694, "start": 2186.02, "end": 2186.78, "text": " You've popped the bubble.", "tokens": [50819, 509, 600, 21545, 264, 12212, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18573118078297582, "compression_ratio": 1.3733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.803406924662243e-12}, {"id": 585, "seek": 217694, "start": 2187.0, "end": 2187.7200000000003, "text": " You can't go back.", "tokens": [50868, 509, 393, 380, 352, 646, 13, 50904], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18573118078297582, "compression_ratio": 1.3733333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.803406924662243e-12}, {"id": 586, "seek": 218772, "start": 2187.72, "end": 2192.74, "text": " That analogy holds up incredibly well, and the angular coordinates in SpherePop are handled", "tokens": [50365, 663, 21663, 9190, 493, 6252, 731, 11, 293, 264, 24413, 21056, 294, 318, 6605, 38677, 366, 18033, 50616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14805911520253057, "compression_ratio": 1.592982456140351, "no_speech_prob": 1.8829460560199074e-12}, {"id": 587, "seek": 218772, "start": 2192.74, "end": 2196.66, "text": " by three specific operators called Refuse, Bind, and Collapse.", "tokens": [50616, 538, 1045, 2685, 19077, 1219, 16957, 438, 11, 363, 471, 11, 293, 4586, 11145, 13, 50812], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14805911520253057, "compression_ratio": 1.592982456140351, "no_speech_prob": 1.8829460560199074e-12}, {"id": 588, "seek": 218772, "start": 2196.74, "end": 2199.2599999999998, "text": " And these reorganize the options without consuming them.", "tokens": [50816, 400, 613, 41203, 1125, 264, 3956, 1553, 19867, 552, 13, 50942], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14805911520253057, "compression_ratio": 1.592982456140351, "no_speech_prob": 1.8829460560199074e-12}, {"id": 589, "seek": 218772, "start": 2199.58, "end": 2200.18, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50958, 7587, 13, 50988], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14805911520253057, "compression_ratio": 1.592982456140351, "no_speech_prob": 1.8829460560199074e-12}, {"id": 590, "seek": 218772, "start": 2200.52, "end": 2204.4199999999996, "text": " And they map perfectly onto the three boundary types we discussed earlier.", "tokens": [51005, 400, 436, 4471, 6239, 3911, 264, 1045, 12866, 3467, 321, 7152, 3071, 13, 51200], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14805911520253057, "compression_ratio": 1.592982456140351, "no_speech_prob": 1.8829460560199074e-12}, {"id": 591, "seek": 218772, "start": 2204.4399999999996, "end": 2205.4199999999996, "text": " Oh, this is so cool.", "tokens": [51201, 876, 11, 341, 307, 370, 1627, 13, 51250], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14805911520253057, "compression_ratio": 1.592982456140351, "no_speech_prob": 1.8829460560199074e-12}, {"id": 592, "seek": 218772, "start": 2205.48, "end": 2206.4199999999996, "text": " Let's trace that mapping.", "tokens": [51253, 961, 311, 13508, 300, 18350, 13, 51300], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14805911520253057, "compression_ratio": 1.592982456140351, "no_speech_prob": 1.8829460560199074e-12}, {"id": 593, "seek": 218772, "start": 2206.68, "end": 2209.62, "text": " The Refuse operator permanently excludes an option.", "tokens": [51313, 440, 16957, 438, 12973, 24042, 16269, 279, 364, 3614, 13, 51460], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14805911520253057, "compression_ratio": 1.592982456140351, "no_speech_prob": 1.8829460560199074e-12}, {"id": 594, "seek": 218772, "start": 2210.08, "end": 2213.7599999999998, "text": " That maps directly to your RSVP-style diachronic exclusion.", "tokens": [51483, 663, 11317, 3838, 281, 428, 25855, 53, 47, 12, 15014, 1026, 608, 10011, 33049, 13, 51667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14805911520253057, "compression_ratio": 1.592982456140351, "no_speech_prob": 1.8829460560199074e-12}, {"id": 595, "seek": 221376, "start": 2213.76, "end": 2218.0400000000004, "text": " It alters the angular landscape by placing a permanent wall.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 419, 1559, 264, 24413, 9661, 538, 17221, 257, 10996, 2929, 13, 50579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15888880145165227, "compression_ratio": 1.5528169014084507, "no_speech_prob": 1.377838164742795e-12}, {"id": 596, "seek": 221376, "start": 2218.5400000000004, "end": 2220.32, "text": " You can't go to page 12 ever again.", "tokens": [50604, 509, 393, 380, 352, 281, 3028, 2272, 1562, 797, 13, 50693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15888880145165227, "compression_ratio": 1.5528169014084507, "no_speech_prob": 1.377838164742795e-12}, {"id": 597, "seek": 221376, "start": 2220.5400000000004, "end": 2220.6200000000003, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50704, 1779, 13, 50708], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15888880145165227, "compression_ratio": 1.5528169014084507, "no_speech_prob": 1.377838164742795e-12}, {"id": 598, "seek": 221376, "start": 2220.7400000000002, "end": 2222.0, "text": " The bouncer with the ban list.", "tokens": [50714, 440, 272, 14296, 365, 264, 5643, 1329, 13, 50777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15888880145165227, "compression_ratio": 1.5528169014084507, "no_speech_prob": 1.377838164742795e-12}, {"id": 599, "seek": 221376, "start": 2222.1200000000003, "end": 2222.4, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50783, 1079, 13, 50797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15888880145165227, "compression_ratio": 1.5528169014084507, "no_speech_prob": 1.377838164742795e-12}, {"id": 600, "seek": 221376, "start": 2223.1200000000003, "end": 2226.8, "text": " The Bind operator creates a constraint for a future evaluation.", "tokens": [50833, 440, 363, 471, 12973, 7829, 257, 25534, 337, 257, 2027, 13344, 13, 51017], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15888880145165227, "compression_ratio": 1.5528169014084507, "no_speech_prob": 1.377838164742795e-12}, {"id": 601, "seek": 221376, "start": 2227.2200000000003, "end": 2229.5400000000004, "text": " That is your Levin-style stored target.", "tokens": [51038, 663, 307, 428, 1456, 4796, 12, 15014, 12187, 3779, 13, 51154], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15888880145165227, "compression_ratio": 1.5528169014084507, "no_speech_prob": 1.377838164742795e-12}, {"id": 602, "seek": 221376, "start": 2230.1000000000004, "end": 2235.34, "text": " It sets a condition that future choices must meet, exactly like the GPS recalculating.", "tokens": [51182, 467, 6352, 257, 4188, 300, 2027, 7994, 1633, 1677, 11, 2293, 411, 264, 19462, 850, 304, 2444, 990, 13, 51444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15888880145165227, "compression_ratio": 1.5528169014084507, "no_speech_prob": 1.377838164742795e-12}, {"id": 603, "seek": 221376, "start": 2235.6200000000003, "end": 2237.3, "text": " And what about the synchronic screen?", "tokens": [51458, 400, 437, 466, 264, 5451, 339, 10011, 2568, 30, 51542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15888880145165227, "compression_ratio": 1.5528169014084507, "no_speech_prob": 1.377838164742795e-12}, {"id": 604, "seek": 221376, "start": 2237.6600000000003, "end": 2242.0600000000004, "text": " The SpherePop bubble itself acts as the Friston-style synchronic screen.", "tokens": [51560, 440, 318, 6605, 38677, 12212, 2564, 10672, 382, 264, 1526, 47345, 12, 15014, 5451, 339, 10011, 2568, 13, 51780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15888880145165227, "compression_ratio": 1.5528169014084507, "no_speech_prob": 1.377838164742795e-12}, {"id": 605, "seek": 224206, "start": 2242.06, "end": 2246.2999999999997, "text": " The text says a computational bubble hides its internal calculations.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2487, 1619, 257, 28270, 12212, 35953, 1080, 6920, 20448, 13, 50577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16396379063272068, "compression_ratio": 1.6345514950166113, "no_speech_prob": 1.6878877852691265e-12}, {"id": 606, "seek": 224206, "start": 2246.74, "end": 2250.88, "text": " Only the final, popped result propagates outward to the rest of the system.", "tokens": [50599, 5686, 264, 2572, 11, 21545, 1874, 12425, 1024, 26914, 281, 264, 1472, 295, 264, 1185, 13, 50806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16396379063272068, "compression_ratio": 1.6345514950166113, "no_speech_prob": 1.6878877852691265e-12}, {"id": 607, "seek": 224206, "start": 2251.06, "end": 2254.84, "text": " It perfectly screens the present internal state from the external world,", "tokens": [50815, 467, 6239, 11171, 264, 1974, 6920, 1785, 490, 264, 8320, 1002, 11, 51004], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16396379063272068, "compression_ratio": 1.6345514950166113, "no_speech_prob": 1.6878877852691265e-12}, {"id": 608, "seek": 224206, "start": 2255.0, "end": 2256.04, "text": " just like the Markov blanket.", "tokens": [51012, 445, 411, 264, 3934, 5179, 17907, 13, 51064], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16396379063272068, "compression_ratio": 1.6345514950166113, "no_speech_prob": 1.6878877852691265e-12}, {"id": 609, "seek": 224206, "start": 2256.2999999999997, "end": 2256.68, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51077, 7587, 13, 51096], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16396379063272068, "compression_ratio": 1.6345514950166113, "no_speech_prob": 1.6878877852691265e-12}, {"id": 610, "seek": 224206, "start": 2257.2, "end": 2259.08, "text": " And then there is the collapse operator,", "tokens": [51122, 400, 550, 456, 307, 264, 15584, 12973, 11, 51216], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16396379063272068, "compression_ratio": 1.6345514950166113, "no_speech_prob": 1.6878877852691265e-12}, {"id": 611, "seek": 224206, "start": 2259.2599999999998, "end": 2262.7799999999997, "text": " which might be the most philosophically dense part of the SpherePop framework.", "tokens": [51225, 597, 1062, 312, 264, 881, 14529, 984, 18011, 644, 295, 264, 318, 6605, 38677, 8388, 13, 51401], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16396379063272068, "compression_ratio": 1.6345514950166113, "no_speech_prob": 1.6878877852691265e-12}, {"id": 612, "seek": 224206, "start": 2262.94, "end": 2263.5, "text": " Lay it on me.", "tokens": [51409, 20084, 309, 322, 385, 13, 51437], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16396379063272068, "compression_ratio": 1.6345514950166113, "no_speech_prob": 1.6878877852691265e-12}, {"id": 613, "seek": 224206, "start": 2263.64, "end": 2266.2799999999997, "text": " Collapse operators determine what counts as the same history.", "tokens": [51444, 4586, 11145, 19077, 6997, 437, 14893, 382, 264, 912, 2503, 13, 51576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16396379063272068, "compression_ratio": 1.6345514950166113, "no_speech_prob": 1.6878877852691265e-12}, {"id": 614, "seek": 224206, "start": 2266.48, "end": 2268.16, "text": " They dictate the equivalence relation.", "tokens": [51586, 814, 36071, 264, 9052, 655, 9721, 13, 51670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16396379063272068, "compression_ratio": 1.6345514950166113, "no_speech_prob": 1.6878877852691265e-12}, {"id": 615, "seek": 226816, "start": 2268.16, "end": 2268.68, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1671424354474569, "compression_ratio": 1.5492957746478873, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485497641814285e-12}, {"id": 616, "seek": 226816, "start": 2268.8599999999997, "end": 2271.46, "text": " Because if I flip to page 42 and you flip to page 42,", "tokens": [50400, 1436, 498, 286, 7929, 281, 3028, 14034, 293, 291, 7929, 281, 3028, 14034, 11, 50530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1671424354474569, "compression_ratio": 1.5492957746478873, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485497641814285e-12}, {"id": 617, "seek": 226816, "start": 2271.66, "end": 2273.14, "text": " did we have the exact same adventure?", "tokens": [50540, 630, 321, 362, 264, 1900, 912, 9868, 30, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1671424354474569, "compression_ratio": 1.5492957746478873, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485497641814285e-12}, {"id": 618, "seek": 226816, "start": 2273.42, "end": 2275.54, "text": " It depends on how we choose to collapse the history.", "tokens": [50628, 467, 5946, 322, 577, 321, 2826, 281, 15584, 264, 2503, 13, 50734], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1671424354474569, "compression_ratio": 1.5492957746478873, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485497641814285e-12}, {"id": 619, "seek": 226816, "start": 2275.8999999999996, "end": 2278.04, "text": " Maybe I got to page 42 by fighting the goblin,", "tokens": [50752, 2704, 286, 658, 281, 3028, 14034, 538, 5237, 264, 20489, 5045, 11, 50859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1671424354474569, "compression_ratio": 1.5492957746478873, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485497641814285e-12}, {"id": 620, "seek": 226816, "start": 2278.22, "end": 2280.2599999999998, "text": " and you got there by sneaking past it.", "tokens": [50868, 293, 291, 658, 456, 538, 48525, 1791, 309, 13, 50970], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1671424354474569, "compression_ratio": 1.5492957746478873, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485497641814285e-12}, {"id": 621, "seek": 226816, "start": 2280.7599999999998, "end": 2282.2999999999997, "text": " Are we in the same state?", "tokens": [50995, 2014, 321, 294, 264, 912, 1785, 30, 51072], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1671424354474569, "compression_ratio": 1.5492957746478873, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485497641814285e-12}, {"id": 622, "seek": 226816, "start": 2282.7799999999997, "end": 2286.64, "text": " The text posits what it calls the axiom of contextual equivalence.", "tokens": [51096, 440, 2487, 1366, 1208, 437, 309, 5498, 264, 6360, 72, 298, 295, 35526, 9052, 655, 13, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1671424354474569, "compression_ratio": 1.5492957746478873, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485497641814285e-12}, {"id": 623, "seek": 228664, "start": 2286.64, "end": 2291.08, "text": " There is no ultimate objective truth of equivalence in computation.", "tokens": [50365, 821, 307, 572, 9705, 10024, 3494, 295, 9052, 655, 294, 24903, 13, 50587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18797162499758277, "compression_ratio": 1.5338645418326693, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013953180350372e-12}, {"id": 624, "seek": 228664, "start": 2291.8199999999997, "end": 2296.54, "text": " Whether two histories are game the same depends entirely on which collapse operator you,", "tokens": [50624, 8503, 732, 30631, 366, 1216, 264, 912, 5946, 7696, 322, 597, 15584, 12973, 291, 11, 50860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18797162499758277, "compression_ratio": 1.5338645418326693, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013953180350372e-12}, {"id": 625, "seek": 228664, "start": 2296.8599999999997, "end": 2298.74, "text": " the observer, choose to apply.", "tokens": [50876, 264, 27878, 11, 2826, 281, 3079, 13, 50970], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18797162499758277, "compression_ratio": 1.5338645418326693, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013953180350372e-12}, {"id": 626, "seek": 228664, "start": 2299.02, "end": 2299.8599999999997, "text": " So it's subjective.", "tokens": [50984, 407, 309, 311, 25972, 13, 51026], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18797162499758277, "compression_ratio": 1.5338645418326693, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013953180350372e-12}, {"id": 627, "seek": 228664, "start": 2300.42, "end": 2300.9, "text": " Contextual.", "tokens": [51054, 4839, 3828, 901, 13, 51078], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18797162499758277, "compression_ratio": 1.5338645418326693, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013953180350372e-12}, {"id": 628, "seek": 228664, "start": 2301.2999999999997, "end": 2303.58, "text": " Do you only care about the terminal value,", "tokens": [51098, 1144, 291, 787, 1127, 466, 264, 14709, 2158, 11, 51212], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18797162499758277, "compression_ratio": 1.5338645418326693, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013953180350372e-12}, {"id": 629, "seek": 228664, "start": 2303.74, "end": 2305.7, "text": " the fact that we both ended up on page 42?", "tokens": [51220, 264, 1186, 300, 321, 1293, 4590, 493, 322, 3028, 14034, 30, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18797162499758277, "compression_ratio": 1.5338645418326693, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013953180350372e-12}, {"id": 630, "seek": 228664, "start": 2306.2799999999997, "end": 2308.52, "text": " Or do you care about the full provenance,", "tokens": [51347, 1610, 360, 291, 1127, 466, 264, 1577, 12785, 719, 11, 51459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18797162499758277, "compression_ratio": 1.5338645418326693, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013953180350372e-12}, {"id": 631, "seek": 228664, "start": 2308.62, "end": 2310.3799999999997, "text": " every single step taken to get there?", "tokens": [51464, 633, 2167, 1823, 2726, 281, 483, 456, 30, 51552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18797162499758277, "compression_ratio": 1.5338645418326693, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013953180350372e-12}, {"id": 632, "seek": 231038, "start": 2310.38, "end": 2312.7400000000002, "text": " If we zoom out and look at what this implies,", "tokens": [50365, 759, 321, 8863, 484, 293, 574, 412, 437, 341, 18779, 11, 50483], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820996105670929, "compression_ratio": 1.6331168831168832, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782055787754267e-12}, {"id": 633, "seek": 231038, "start": 2313.32, "end": 2316.6800000000003, "text": " this proves that the sphere isn't just a physical shape we see with our eyes,", "tokens": [50512, 341, 25019, 300, 264, 16687, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 4001, 3909, 321, 536, 365, 527, 2575, 11, 50680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820996105670929, "compression_ratio": 1.6331168831168832, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782055787754267e-12}, {"id": 634, "seek": 231038, "start": 2316.88, "end": 2318.54, "text": " like a baseball or a planet.", "tokens": [50690, 411, 257, 14323, 420, 257, 5054, 13, 50773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820996105670929, "compression_ratio": 1.6331168831168832, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782055787754267e-12}, {"id": 635, "seek": 231038, "start": 2318.82, "end": 2323.36, "text": " It is the fundamental mathematical geometry of irreversible commitment.", "tokens": [50787, 467, 307, 264, 8088, 18894, 18426, 295, 16014, 840, 964, 8371, 13, 51014], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820996105670929, "compression_ratio": 1.6331168831168832, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782055787754267e-12}, {"id": 636, "seek": 231038, "start": 2323.36, "end": 2325.6, "text": " That is a heavy concept to walk around with.", "tokens": [51014, 663, 307, 257, 4676, 3410, 281, 1792, 926, 365, 13, 51126], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820996105670929, "compression_ratio": 1.6331168831168832, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782055787754267e-12}, {"id": 637, "seek": 231038, "start": 2325.76, "end": 2328.86, "text": " Every choice you make is radially consuming your sphere of potential.", "tokens": [51134, 2048, 3922, 291, 652, 307, 2843, 2270, 19867, 428, 16687, 295, 3995, 13, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820996105670929, "compression_ratio": 1.6331168831168832, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782055787754267e-12}, {"id": 638, "seek": 231038, "start": 2329.34, "end": 2329.94, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [51313, 467, 534, 307, 13, 51343], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820996105670929, "compression_ratio": 1.6331168831168832, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782055787754267e-12}, {"id": 639, "seek": 231038, "start": 2330.04, "end": 2330.1800000000003, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51348, 865, 13, 51355], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820996105670929, "compression_ratio": 1.6331168831168832, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782055787754267e-12}, {"id": 640, "seek": 231038, "start": 2330.34, "end": 2332.8, "text": " And it sets up the climax of the monograph.", "tokens": [51363, 400, 309, 6352, 493, 264, 41329, 295, 264, 1108, 3108, 13, 51486], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820996105670929, "compression_ratio": 1.6331168831168832, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782055787754267e-12}, {"id": 641, "seek": 231038, "start": 2333.1600000000003, "end": 2336.42, "text": " Because if choosing how we collapse our history", "tokens": [51504, 1436, 498, 10875, 577, 321, 15584, 527, 2503, 51667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820996105670929, "compression_ratio": 1.6331168831168832, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782055787754267e-12}, {"id": 642, "seek": 231038, "start": 2336.42, "end": 2339.2400000000002, "text": " determines what we can distinguish from each other,", "tokens": [51667, 24799, 437, 321, 393, 20206, 490, 1184, 661, 11, 51808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1820996105670929, "compression_ratio": 1.6331168831168832, "no_speech_prob": 1.4782055787754267e-12}, {"id": 643, "seek": 233924, "start": 2339.24, "end": 2344.06, "text": " how do we geometrically measure this distinguishability?", "tokens": [50365, 577, 360, 321, 12956, 81, 984, 3481, 341, 20206, 2310, 30, 50606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17593818599894895, "compression_ratio": 1.7167235494880546, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779848352131086e-12}, {"id": 644, "seek": 233924, "start": 2344.22, "end": 2345.8199999999997, "text": " Prepare yourself if you're listening to this,", "tokens": [50614, 29689, 1803, 498, 291, 434, 4764, 281, 341, 11, 50694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17593818599894895, "compression_ratio": 1.7167235494880546, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779848352131086e-12}, {"id": 645, "seek": 233924, "start": 2345.8799999999997, "end": 2349.58, "text": " because here is where the sphere stops being a metaphor entirely.", "tokens": [50697, 570, 510, 307, 689, 264, 16687, 10094, 885, 257, 19157, 7696, 13, 50882], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17593818599894895, "compression_ratio": 1.7167235494880546, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779848352131086e-12}, {"id": 646, "seek": 233924, "start": 2349.7, "end": 2351.9599999999996, "text": " The author drops an absolute mic drop.", "tokens": [50888, 440, 3793, 11438, 364, 8236, 3123, 3270, 13, 51001], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17593818599894895, "compression_ratio": 1.7167235494880546, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779848352131086e-12}, {"id": 647, "seek": 233924, "start": 2352.04, "end": 2352.8999999999996, "text": " That's a whole mic drop.", "tokens": [51005, 663, 311, 257, 1379, 3123, 3270, 13, 51048], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17593818599894895, "compression_ratio": 1.7167235494880546, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779848352131086e-12}, {"id": 648, "seek": 233924, "start": 2352.9799999999996, "end": 2355.9399999999996, "text": " The text utilizes tools from information geometry,", "tokens": [51052, 440, 2487, 4976, 5660, 3873, 490, 1589, 18426, 11, 51200], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17593818599894895, "compression_ratio": 1.7167235494880546, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779848352131086e-12}, {"id": 649, "seek": 233924, "start": 2356.5, "end": 2359.08, "text": " specifically something called the Jensen-Shannon divergence", "tokens": [51228, 4682, 746, 1219, 264, 508, 32934, 12, 7774, 16138, 47387, 51357], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17593818599894895, "compression_ratio": 1.7167235494880546, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779848352131086e-12}, {"id": 650, "seek": 233924, "start": 2359.08, "end": 2360.9399999999996, "text": " and the Fisher information metric,", "tokens": [51357, 293, 264, 26676, 1589, 20678, 11, 51450], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17593818599894895, "compression_ratio": 1.7167235494880546, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779848352131086e-12}, {"id": 651, "seek": 233924, "start": 2361.16, "end": 2364.4199999999996, "text": " to measure distinguishability between statistical outcomes.", "tokens": [51461, 281, 3481, 20206, 2310, 1296, 22820, 10070, 13, 51624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17593818599894895, "compression_ratio": 1.7167235494880546, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779848352131086e-12}, {"id": 652, "seek": 233924, "start": 2364.7599999999998, "end": 2365.04, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51641, 1033, 13, 51655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17593818599894895, "compression_ratio": 1.7167235494880546, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779848352131086e-12}, {"id": 653, "seek": 233924, "start": 2365.04, "end": 2368.66, "text": " And it proves that for a finite categorical outcome space,", "tokens": [51655, 400, 309, 25019, 300, 337, 257, 19362, 19250, 804, 9700, 1901, 11, 51836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17593818599894895, "compression_ratio": 1.7167235494880546, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779848352131086e-12}, {"id": 654, "seek": 236866, "start": 2368.66, "end": 2370.6, "text": " it's like a set of distinct probabilities,", "tokens": [50365, 309, 311, 411, 257, 992, 295, 10644, 33783, 11, 50462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2118824634355368, "compression_ratio": 1.5178571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.5519385906589966e-12}, {"id": 655, "seek": 236866, "start": 2371.3399999999997, "end": 2375.14, "text": " the statistical manifold is isometric to the positive orthant of a sphere.", "tokens": [50499, 264, 22820, 47138, 307, 307, 29470, 281, 264, 3353, 19052, 394, 295, 257, 16687, 13, 50689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2118824634355368, "compression_ratio": 1.5178571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.5519385906589966e-12}, {"id": 656, "seek": 236866, "start": 2375.24, "end": 2375.3999999999996, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50694, 1033, 13, 50702], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2118824634355368, "compression_ratio": 1.5178571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.5519385906589966e-12}, {"id": 657, "seek": 236866, "start": 2375.5, "end": 2377.5, "text": " You just threw a lot of heavy statistical words at me.", "tokens": [50707, 509, 445, 11918, 257, 688, 295, 4676, 22820, 2283, 412, 385, 13, 50807], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2118824634355368, "compression_ratio": 1.5178571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.5519385906589966e-12}, {"id": 658, "seek": 236866, "start": 2377.8199999999997, "end": 2380.54, "text": " Jensen-Shannon, Fisher, positive orthant.", "tokens": [50823, 508, 32934, 12, 7774, 16138, 11, 26676, 11, 3353, 19052, 394, 13, 50959], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2118824634355368, "compression_ratio": 1.5178571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.5519385906589966e-12}, {"id": 659, "seek": 236866, "start": 2381.14, "end": 2382.64, "text": " Break that down for me because I'm lost.", "tokens": [50989, 16925, 300, 760, 337, 385, 570, 286, 478, 2731, 13, 51064], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2118824634355368, "compression_ratio": 1.5178571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.5519385906589966e-12}, {"id": 660, "seek": 236866, "start": 2382.7799999999997, "end": 2383.56, "text": " Let's translate it.", "tokens": [51071, 961, 311, 13799, 309, 13, 51110], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2118824634355368, "compression_ratio": 1.5178571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.5519385906589966e-12}, {"id": 661, "seek": 236866, "start": 2383.94, "end": 2387.72, "text": " Imagine an outcome space, let's say, rolling a loaded die.", "tokens": [51129, 11739, 364, 9700, 1901, 11, 718, 311, 584, 11, 9439, 257, 13210, 978, 13, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2118824634355368, "compression_ratio": 1.5178571428571428, "no_speech_prob": 1.5519385906589966e-12}, {"id": 662, "seek": 238772, "start": 2387.72, "end": 2392.22, "text": " You have six categorical outcomes and each has a specific probability of happening.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 362, 2309, 19250, 804, 10070, 293, 1184, 575, 257, 2685, 8482, 295, 2737, 13, 50590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17069235513376635, "compression_ratio": 1.6150627615062763, "no_speech_prob": 1.3142721503114907e-12}, {"id": 663, "seek": 238772, "start": 2392.62, "end": 2396.8199999999997, "text": " If you want to mathematically measure how different one set of probabilities is", "tokens": [50610, 759, 291, 528, 281, 44003, 3481, 577, 819, 472, 992, 295, 33783, 307, 50820], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17069235513376635, "compression_ratio": 1.6150627615062763, "no_speech_prob": 1.3142721503114907e-12}, {"id": 664, "seek": 238772, "start": 2396.8199999999997, "end": 2399.3599999999997, "text": " from another set, how distinguishable they are,", "tokens": [50820, 490, 1071, 992, 11, 577, 20206, 712, 436, 366, 11, 50947], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17069235513376635, "compression_ratio": 1.6150627615062763, "no_speech_prob": 1.3142721503114907e-12}, {"id": 665, "seek": 238772, "start": 2399.68, "end": 2401.66, "text": " you use the Fisher information metric.", "tokens": [50963, 291, 764, 264, 26676, 1589, 20678, 13, 51062], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17069235513376635, "compression_ratio": 1.6150627615062763, "no_speech_prob": 1.3142721503114907e-12}, {"id": 666, "seek": 238772, "start": 2402.2599999999998, "end": 2407.52, "text": " Now, when mathematicians map out all those possible probabilities into a geometric space,", "tokens": [51092, 823, 11, 562, 32811, 2567, 4471, 484, 439, 729, 1944, 33783, 666, 257, 33246, 1901, 11, 51355], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17069235513376635, "compression_ratio": 1.6150627615062763, "no_speech_prob": 1.3142721503114907e-12}, {"id": 667, "seek": 238772, "start": 2407.7599999999998, "end": 2409.3599999999997, "text": " they find something astonishing.", "tokens": [51367, 436, 915, 746, 35264, 13, 51447], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17069235513376635, "compression_ratio": 1.6150627615062763, "no_speech_prob": 1.3142721503114907e-12}, {"id": 668, "seek": 238772, "start": 2409.62, "end": 2410.12, "text": " What's that?", "tokens": [51460, 708, 311, 300, 30, 51485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17069235513376635, "compression_ratio": 1.6150627615062763, "no_speech_prob": 1.3142721503114907e-12}, {"id": 669, "seek": 241012, "start": 2410.12, "end": 2413.72, "text": " The shape of that space is perfectly isometric,", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3909, 295, 300, 1901, 307, 6239, 307, 29470, 11, 50545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1777799496283898, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.2639263550703883e-12}, {"id": 670, "seek": 241012, "start": 2414.3599999999997, "end": 2418.16, "text": " meaning it has the exact same geometric properties as a sphere,", "tokens": [50577, 3620, 309, 575, 264, 1900, 912, 33246, 7221, 382, 257, 16687, 11, 50767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1777799496283898, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.2639263550703883e-12}, {"id": 671, "seek": 241012, "start": 2418.64, "end": 2420.8399999999997, "text": " specifically the positive orthant,", "tokens": [50791, 4682, 264, 3353, 19052, 394, 11, 50901], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1777799496283898, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.2639263550703883e-12}, {"id": 672, "seek": 241012, "start": 2420.96, "end": 2423.64, "text": " which just means you are looking at the corner of the sphere", "tokens": [50907, 597, 445, 1355, 291, 366, 1237, 412, 264, 4538, 295, 264, 16687, 51041], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1777799496283898, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.2639263550703883e-12}, {"id": 673, "seek": 241012, "start": 2423.64, "end": 2425.88, "text": " where all coordinates are positive numbers", "tokens": [51041, 689, 439, 21056, 366, 3353, 3547, 51153], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1777799496283898, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.2639263550703883e-12}, {"id": 674, "seek": 241012, "start": 2425.88, "end": 2427.96, "text": " because you can't have a negative probability.", "tokens": [51153, 570, 291, 393, 380, 362, 257, 3671, 8482, 13, 51257], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1777799496283898, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.2639263550703883e-12}, {"id": 675, "seek": 241012, "start": 2428.1, "end": 2429.1, "text": " Wait, let me get this straight.", "tokens": [51264, 3802, 11, 718, 385, 483, 341, 2997, 13, 51314], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1777799496283898, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.2639263550703883e-12}, {"id": 676, "seek": 241012, "start": 2429.2799999999997, "end": 2432.18, "text": " We started this deep dive by saying coordinates aren't real.", "tokens": [51323, 492, 1409, 341, 2452, 9192, 538, 1566, 21056, 3212, 380, 957, 13, 51468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1777799496283898, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.2639263550703883e-12}, {"id": 677, "seek": 241012, "start": 2432.7799999999997, "end": 2434.18, "text": " They are just interfaces.", "tokens": [51498, 814, 366, 445, 28416, 13, 51568], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1777799496283898, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.2639263550703883e-12}, {"id": 678, "seek": 241012, "start": 2434.5, "end": 2434.7799999999997, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51584, 1779, 13, 51598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1777799496283898, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.2639263550703883e-12}, {"id": 679, "seek": 243478, "start": 2434.78, "end": 2436.76, "text": " The Cartesian grid, the polar angles,", "tokens": [50365, 440, 22478, 42434, 10748, 11, 264, 12367, 14708, 11, 50464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15456482569376628, "compression_ratio": 1.7509433962264151, "no_speech_prob": 1.6047702446411738e-12}, {"id": 680, "seek": 243478, "start": 2436.86, "end": 2439.96, "text": " they're just arbitrary labels we put on reality to make math easier.", "tokens": [50469, 436, 434, 445, 23211, 16949, 321, 829, 322, 4103, 281, 652, 5221, 3571, 13, 50624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15456482569376628, "compression_ratio": 1.7509433962264151, "no_speech_prob": 1.6047702446411738e-12}, {"id": 681, "seek": 243478, "start": 2440.1600000000003, "end": 2440.4, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50634, 1779, 13, 50646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15456482569376628, "compression_ratio": 1.7509433962264151, "no_speech_prob": 1.6047702446411738e-12}, {"id": 682, "seek": 243478, "start": 2440.7000000000003, "end": 2443.6400000000003, "text": " But you're telling me that when it comes to raw probability,", "tokens": [50661, 583, 291, 434, 3585, 385, 300, 562, 309, 1487, 281, 8936, 8482, 11, 50808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15456482569376628, "compression_ratio": 1.7509433962264151, "no_speech_prob": 1.6047702446411738e-12}, {"id": 683, "seek": 243478, "start": 2444.1200000000003, "end": 2447.98, "text": " when it comes to the pure ability to distinguish one piece of data from another,", "tokens": [50832, 562, 309, 1487, 281, 264, 6075, 3485, 281, 20206, 472, 2522, 295, 1412, 490, 1071, 11, 51025], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15456482569376628, "compression_ratio": 1.7509433962264151, "no_speech_prob": 1.6047702446411738e-12}, {"id": 684, "seek": 243478, "start": 2448.3, "end": 2451.0, "text": " the sphere isn't an interface.", "tokens": [51041, 264, 16687, 1943, 380, 364, 9226, 13, 51176], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15456482569376628, "compression_ratio": 1.7509433962264151, "no_speech_prob": 1.6047702446411738e-12}, {"id": 685, "seek": 243478, "start": 2451.3, "end": 2452.1000000000004, "text": " It's not an interface.", "tokens": [51191, 467, 311, 406, 364, 9226, 13, 51231], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15456482569376628, "compression_ratio": 1.7509433962264151, "no_speech_prob": 1.6047702446411738e-12}, {"id": 686, "seek": 243478, "start": 2452.1000000000004, "end": 2454.6000000000004, "text": " It's the actual literal shape of statistics.", "tokens": [51231, 467, 311, 264, 3539, 20411, 3909, 295, 12523, 13, 51356], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15456482569376628, "compression_ratio": 1.7509433962264151, "no_speech_prob": 1.6047702446411738e-12}, {"id": 687, "seek": 243478, "start": 2454.9, "end": 2458.46, "text": " That is the inescapable conclusion of the mathematics.", "tokens": [51371, 663, 307, 264, 294, 279, 9485, 712, 10063, 295, 264, 18666, 13, 51549], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15456482569376628, "compression_ratio": 1.7509433962264151, "no_speech_prob": 1.6047702446411738e-12}, {"id": 688, "seek": 243478, "start": 2458.94, "end": 2462.0600000000004, "text": " The theory space of probability literally is a sphere.", "tokens": [51573, 440, 5261, 1901, 295, 8482, 3736, 307, 257, 16687, 13, 51729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15456482569376628, "compression_ratio": 1.7509433962264151, "no_speech_prob": 1.6047702446411738e-12}, {"id": 689, "seek": 246206, "start": 2462.06, "end": 2467.18, "text": " The Fisher information metric pulls back perfectly into the round metric of a sphere.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 26676, 1589, 20678, 16982, 646, 6239, 666, 264, 3098, 20678, 295, 257, 16687, 13, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18357237558516246, "compression_ratio": 1.627831715210356, "no_speech_prob": 1.567411998804058e-12}, {"id": 690, "seek": 246206, "start": 2467.32, "end": 2468.2599999999998, "text": " It's not an analogy.", "tokens": [50628, 467, 311, 406, 364, 21663, 13, 50675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18357237558516246, "compression_ratio": 1.627831715210356, "no_speech_prob": 1.567411998804058e-12}, {"id": 691, "seek": 246206, "start": 2468.48, "end": 2469.54, "text": " It's not a convenient chart.", "tokens": [50686, 467, 311, 406, 257, 10851, 6927, 13, 50739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18357237558516246, "compression_ratio": 1.627831715210356, "no_speech_prob": 1.567411998804058e-12}, {"id": 692, "seek": 246206, "start": 2469.68, "end": 2470.88, "text": " It is an identity.", "tokens": [50746, 467, 307, 364, 6575, 13, 50806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18357237558516246, "compression_ratio": 1.627831715210356, "no_speech_prob": 1.567411998804058e-12}, {"id": 693, "seek": 246206, "start": 2471.2799999999997, "end": 2472.22, "text": " That is staggering.", "tokens": [50826, 663, 307, 42974, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18357237558516246, "compression_ratio": 1.627831715210356, "no_speech_prob": 1.567411998804058e-12}, {"id": 694, "seek": 246206, "start": 2472.44, "end": 2474.84, "text": " This shape of probability is curved.", "tokens": [50884, 639, 3909, 295, 8482, 307, 24991, 13, 51004], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18357237558516246, "compression_ratio": 1.627831715210356, "no_speech_prob": 1.567411998804058e-12}, {"id": 695, "seek": 246206, "start": 2475.08, "end": 2479.2599999999998, "text": " And because it's curved, we run into that curvature defect we talked about earlier, right?", "tokens": [51016, 400, 570, 309, 311, 24991, 11, 321, 1190, 666, 300, 37638, 16445, 321, 2825, 466, 3071, 11, 558, 30, 51225], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18357237558516246, "compression_ratio": 1.627831715210356, "no_speech_prob": 1.567411998804058e-12}, {"id": 696, "seek": 246206, "start": 2479.32, "end": 2480.12, "text": " The Harry-Bowell theorem.", "tokens": [51228, 440, 9378, 12, 33, 305, 898, 20904, 13, 51268], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18357237558516246, "compression_ratio": 1.627831715210356, "no_speech_prob": 1.567411998804058e-12}, {"id": 697, "seek": 246206, "start": 2480.34, "end": 2480.62, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51279, 1079, 13, 51293], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18357237558516246, "compression_ratio": 1.627831715210356, "no_speech_prob": 1.567411998804058e-12}, {"id": 698, "seek": 246206, "start": 2481.06, "end": 2483.46, "text": " And here it takes on a terrifying meaning,", "tokens": [51315, 400, 510, 309, 2516, 322, 257, 18106, 3620, 11, 51435], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18357237558516246, "compression_ratio": 1.627831715210356, "no_speech_prob": 1.567411998804058e-12}, {"id": 699, "seek": 246206, "start": 2483.7, "end": 2486.62, "text": " especially for fields like data science and artificial intelligence.", "tokens": [51447, 2318, 337, 7909, 411, 1412, 3497, 293, 11677, 7599, 13, 51593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18357237558516246, "compression_ratio": 1.627831715210356, "no_speech_prob": 1.567411998804058e-12}, {"id": 700, "seek": 246206, "start": 2487.42, "end": 2490.32, "text": " Positive sectional curvature on this statistical manifold", "tokens": [51633, 46326, 3541, 304, 37638, 322, 341, 22820, 47138, 51778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18357237558516246, "compression_ratio": 1.627831715210356, "no_speech_prob": 1.567411998804058e-12}, {"id": 701, "seek": 249032, "start": 2490.32, "end": 2494.2400000000002, "text": " means that nearby theories, or nearby data points, pull together.", "tokens": [50365, 1355, 300, 11184, 13667, 11, 420, 11184, 1412, 2793, 11, 2235, 1214, 13, 50561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21692005638937348, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.2202592452117966e-12}, {"id": 702, "seek": 249032, "start": 2494.44, "end": 2494.92, "text": " Pull together.", "tokens": [50571, 15074, 1214, 13, 50595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21692005638937348, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.2202592452117966e-12}, {"id": 703, "seek": 249032, "start": 2495.04, "end": 2495.2400000000002, "text": " How?", "tokens": [50601, 1012, 30, 50611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21692005638937348, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.2202592452117966e-12}, {"id": 704, "seek": 249032, "start": 2495.38, "end": 2496.96, "text": " Because the space is curved inward,", "tokens": [50618, 1436, 264, 1901, 307, 24991, 29876, 11, 50697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21692005638937348, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.2202592452117966e-12}, {"id": 705, "seek": 249032, "start": 2497.26, "end": 2499.54, "text": " lines that start out parallel eventually intersect,", "tokens": [50712, 3876, 300, 722, 484, 8952, 4728, 27815, 11, 50826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21692005638937348, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.2202592452117966e-12}, {"id": 706, "seek": 249032, "start": 2499.82, "end": 2501.88, "text": " like longitude lines hitting the North Pole.", "tokens": [50840, 411, 938, 4377, 3876, 8850, 264, 4067, 34212, 13, 50943], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21692005638937348, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.2202592452117966e-12}, {"id": 707, "seek": 249032, "start": 2502.04, "end": 2503.44, "text": " They collapse into each other.", "tokens": [50951, 814, 15584, 666, 1184, 661, 13, 51021], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21692005638937348, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.2202592452117966e-12}, {"id": 708, "seek": 249032, "start": 2503.78, "end": 2508.2000000000003, "text": " They become observationally indistinguishable faster than their actual parameters suggest.", "tokens": [51038, 814, 1813, 14816, 379, 1016, 468, 7050, 742, 712, 4663, 813, 641, 3539, 9834, 3402, 13, 51259], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21692005638937348, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.2202592452117966e-12}, {"id": 709, "seek": 249032, "start": 2508.46, "end": 2508.84, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [51272, 3153, 13, 51291], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21692005638937348, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.2202592452117966e-12}, {"id": 710, "seek": 249032, "start": 2508.96, "end": 2513.44, "text": " Curvature in probability space is the literal geometry of overfitting.", "tokens": [51297, 7907, 85, 1503, 294, 8482, 1901, 307, 264, 20411, 18426, 295, 670, 69, 2414, 13, 51521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21692005638937348, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.2202592452117966e-12}, {"id": 711, "seek": 251344, "start": 2513.44, "end": 2517.12, "text": " And the text introduces the concept of harmonic truncation here.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 2487, 31472, 264, 3410, 295, 32270, 504, 409, 46252, 510, 13, 50549], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16756817418285924, "compression_ratio": 1.6173285198555956, "no_speech_prob": 1.7727956689445046e-12}, {"id": 712, "seek": 251344, "start": 2517.4, "end": 2519.78, "text": " It says, if you have a complex data set,", "tokens": [50563, 467, 1619, 11, 498, 291, 362, 257, 3997, 1412, 992, 11, 50682], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16756817418285924, "compression_ratio": 1.6173285198555956, "no_speech_prob": 1.7727956689445046e-12}, {"id": 713, "seek": 251344, "start": 2519.82, "end": 2522.7000000000003, "text": " it's like a complex high-frequency angular pattern on the sphere.", "tokens": [50684, 309, 311, 411, 257, 3997, 1090, 12, 19325, 48154, 24413, 5102, 322, 264, 16687, 13, 50828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16756817418285924, "compression_ratio": 1.6173285198555956, "no_speech_prob": 1.7727956689445046e-12}, {"id": 714, "seek": 251344, "start": 2522.94, "end": 2525.64, "text": " The millions of tiny black and white squares we talked about.", "tokens": [50840, 440, 6803, 295, 5870, 2211, 293, 2418, 19368, 321, 2825, 466, 13, 50975], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16756817418285924, "compression_ratio": 1.6173285198555956, "no_speech_prob": 1.7727956689445046e-12}, {"id": 715, "seek": 251344, "start": 2525.86, "end": 2525.92, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50986, 1779, 13, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16756817418285924, "compression_ratio": 1.6173285198555956, "no_speech_prob": 1.7727956689445046e-12}, {"id": 716, "seek": 251344, "start": 2526.12, "end": 2527.5, "text": " If you truncate that data,", "tokens": [50999, 759, 291, 504, 409, 66, 473, 300, 1412, 11, 51068], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16756817418285924, "compression_ratio": 1.6173285198555956, "no_speech_prob": 1.7727956689445046e-12}, {"id": 717, "seek": 251344, "start": 2527.7400000000002, "end": 2530.88, "text": " if you shorten the description to save space on a hard drive,", "tokens": [51080, 498, 291, 39632, 264, 3855, 281, 3155, 1901, 322, 257, 1152, 3332, 11, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16756817418285924, "compression_ratio": 1.6173285198555956, "no_speech_prob": 1.7727956689445046e-12}, {"id": 718, "seek": 251344, "start": 2530.92, "end": 2534.66, "text": " or if an AI compresses it into a smaller formula,", "tokens": [51239, 420, 498, 364, 7318, 14778, 279, 309, 666, 257, 4356, 8513, 11, 51426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16756817418285924, "compression_ratio": 1.6173285198555956, "no_speech_prob": 1.7727956689445046e-12}, {"id": 719, "seek": 251344, "start": 2535.38, "end": 2538.78, "text": " you are mathematically guaranteed to create a reconstruction defect.", "tokens": [51462, 291, 366, 44003, 18031, 281, 1884, 257, 31565, 16445, 13, 51632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16756817418285924, "compression_ratio": 1.6173285198555956, "no_speech_prob": 1.7727956689445046e-12}, {"id": 720, "seek": 253878, "start": 2538.78, "end": 2541.86, "text": " The author calls this the compression fallacy.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3793, 5498, 341, 264, 19355, 2100, 2551, 13, 50519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13194419597757273, "compression_ratio": 1.6431095406360423, "no_speech_prob": 2.16338492259327e-12}, {"id": 721, "seek": 253878, "start": 2542.6200000000003, "end": 2545.1800000000003, "text": " There is a deeply held belief in tech right now", "tokens": [50557, 821, 307, 257, 8760, 5167, 7107, 294, 7553, 558, 586, 50685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13194419597757273, "compression_ratio": 1.6431095406360423, "no_speech_prob": 2.16338492259327e-12}, {"id": 722, "seek": 253878, "start": 2545.1800000000003, "end": 2548.6600000000003, "text": " that if an AI can summarize a massive data set", "tokens": [50685, 300, 498, 364, 7318, 393, 20858, 257, 5994, 1412, 992, 50859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13194419597757273, "compression_ratio": 1.6431095406360423, "no_speech_prob": 2.16338492259327e-12}, {"id": 723, "seek": 253878, "start": 2548.6600000000003, "end": 2552.28, "text": " into a neat, short, little mathematical representation,", "tokens": [50859, 666, 257, 10654, 11, 2099, 11, 707, 18894, 10290, 11, 51040], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13194419597757273, "compression_ratio": 1.6431095406360423, "no_speech_prob": 2.16338492259327e-12}, {"id": 724, "seek": 253878, "start": 2552.6200000000003, "end": 2554.42, "text": " it has somehow understood it.", "tokens": [51057, 309, 575, 6063, 7320, 309, 13, 51147], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13194419597757273, "compression_ratio": 1.6431095406360423, "no_speech_prob": 2.16338492259327e-12}, {"id": 725, "seek": 253878, "start": 2554.46, "end": 2554.6200000000003, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51149, 865, 13, 51157], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13194419597757273, "compression_ratio": 1.6431095406360423, "no_speech_prob": 2.16338492259327e-12}, {"id": 726, "seek": 253878, "start": 2554.76, "end": 2556.4, "text": " That's the whole pitch for AI right now.", "tokens": [51164, 663, 311, 264, 1379, 7293, 337, 7318, 558, 586, 13, 51246], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13194419597757273, "compression_ratio": 1.6431095406360423, "no_speech_prob": 2.16338492259327e-12}, {"id": 727, "seek": 253878, "start": 2556.52, "end": 2559.2000000000003, "text": " But the geometry proves that just because you can compress it", "tokens": [51252, 583, 264, 18426, 25019, 300, 445, 570, 291, 393, 14778, 309, 51386], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13194419597757273, "compression_ratio": 1.6431095406360423, "no_speech_prob": 2.16338492259327e-12}, {"id": 728, "seek": 253878, "start": 2559.2000000000003, "end": 2562.9, "text": " does not mean you have preserved the distinguishing power of the original data.", "tokens": [51386, 775, 406, 914, 291, 362, 22242, 264, 11365, 3807, 1347, 295, 264, 3380, 1412, 13, 51571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13194419597757273, "compression_ratio": 1.6431095406360423, "no_speech_prob": 2.16338492259327e-12}, {"id": 729, "seek": 253878, "start": 2563.2000000000003, "end": 2564.94, "text": " Because shortness is not understanding.", "tokens": [51586, 1436, 2099, 1287, 307, 406, 3701, 13, 51673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13194419597757273, "compression_ratio": 1.6431095406360423, "no_speech_prob": 2.16338492259327e-12}, {"id": 730, "seek": 253878, "start": 2565.32, "end": 2565.7400000000002, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51692, 7587, 13, 51713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13194419597757273, "compression_ratio": 1.6431095406360423, "no_speech_prob": 2.16338492259327e-12}, {"id": 731, "seek": 256574, "start": 2565.74, "end": 2568.4799999999996, "text": " When you truncate the spherical harmonics,", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 291, 504, 409, 66, 473, 264, 37300, 14750, 1167, 11, 50502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20520408267066592, "compression_ratio": 1.6380597014925373, "no_speech_prob": 2.2019244066973087e-12}, {"id": 732, "seek": 256574, "start": 2568.8999999999996, "end": 2571.3199999999997, "text": " you throw away the high-frequency angular structure.", "tokens": [50523, 291, 3507, 1314, 264, 1090, 12, 19325, 48154, 24413, 3877, 13, 50644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20520408267066592, "compression_ratio": 1.6380597014925373, "no_speech_prob": 2.2019244066973087e-12}, {"id": 733, "seek": 256574, "start": 2571.72, "end": 2575.4799999999996, "text": " You lose the ability to distinguish between fine, nuanced details.", "tokens": [50664, 509, 3624, 264, 3485, 281, 20206, 1296, 2489, 11, 45115, 4365, 13, 50852], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20520408267066592, "compression_ratio": 1.6380597014925373, "no_speech_prob": 2.2019244066973087e-12}, {"id": 734, "seek": 256574, "start": 2575.9799999999996, "end": 2578.4199999999996, "text": " And because the space is positively curved,", "tokens": [50877, 400, 570, 264, 1901, 307, 25795, 24991, 11, 50999], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20520408267066592, "compression_ratio": 1.6380597014925373, "no_speech_prob": 2.2019244066973087e-12}, {"id": 735, "seek": 256574, "start": 2578.7599999999998, "end": 2580.58, "text": " those nearby points pull together.", "tokens": [51016, 729, 11184, 2793, 2235, 1214, 13, 51107], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20520408267066592, "compression_ratio": 1.6380597014925373, "no_speech_prob": 2.2019244066973087e-12}, {"id": 736, "seek": 256574, "start": 2580.7799999999997, "end": 2582.4799999999996, "text": " The details just blend into each other.", "tokens": [51117, 440, 4365, 445, 10628, 666, 1184, 661, 13, 51202], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20520408267066592, "compression_ratio": 1.6380597014925373, "no_speech_prob": 2.2019244066973087e-12}, {"id": 737, "seek": 256574, "start": 2582.7, "end": 2585.66, "text": " That lost distinguishability is gone forever.", "tokens": [51213, 663, 2731, 20206, 2310, 307, 2780, 5680, 13, 51361], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20520408267066592, "compression_ratio": 1.6380597014925373, "no_speech_prob": 2.2019244066973087e-12}, {"id": 738, "seek": 256574, "start": 2585.9599999999996, "end": 2586.62, "text": " It collapses.", "tokens": [51376, 467, 48765, 13, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20520408267066592, "compression_ratio": 1.6380597014925373, "no_speech_prob": 2.2019244066973087e-12}, {"id": 739, "seek": 256574, "start": 2587.04, "end": 2590.4599999999996, "text": " You cannot reverse engineer or reconstruct the true,", "tokens": [51430, 509, 2644, 9943, 11403, 420, 31499, 264, 2074, 11, 51601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20520408267066592, "compression_ratio": 1.6380597014925373, "no_speech_prob": 2.2019244066973087e-12}, {"id": 740, "seek": 256574, "start": 2590.9199999999996, "end": 2593.5, "text": " complex history from the compressed summary.", "tokens": [51624, 3997, 2503, 490, 264, 30353, 12691, 13, 51753], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20520408267066592, "compression_ratio": 1.6380597014925373, "no_speech_prob": 2.2019244066973087e-12}, {"id": 741, "seek": 259350, "start": 2593.5, "end": 2596.16, "text": " The uniqueness is permanently destroyed.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 48294, 307, 24042, 8937, 13, 50498], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16934210794013843, "compression_ratio": 1.6487455197132617, "no_speech_prob": 2.125693718268984e-12}, {"id": 742, "seek": 259350, "start": 2596.66, "end": 2597.98, "text": " So every time we compress data,", "tokens": [50523, 407, 633, 565, 321, 14778, 1412, 11, 50589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16934210794013843, "compression_ratio": 1.6487455197132617, "no_speech_prob": 2.125693718268984e-12}, {"id": 743, "seek": 259350, "start": 2598.34, "end": 2601.44, "text": " every time an algorithm simplifies a complex pattern of human behavior", "tokens": [50607, 633, 565, 364, 9284, 6883, 11221, 257, 3997, 5102, 295, 1952, 5223, 50762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16934210794013843, "compression_ratio": 1.6487455197132617, "no_speech_prob": 2.125693718268984e-12}, {"id": 744, "seek": 259350, "start": 2601.44, "end": 2604.22, "text": " into, like, a targeted ad profile,", "tokens": [50762, 666, 11, 411, 11, 257, 15045, 614, 7964, 11, 50901], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16934210794013843, "compression_ratio": 1.6487455197132617, "no_speech_prob": 2.125693718268984e-12}, {"id": 745, "seek": 259350, "start": 2604.88, "end": 2608.68, "text": " it is literally forcing our high-frequency angular reality", "tokens": [50934, 309, 307, 3736, 19030, 527, 1090, 12, 19325, 48154, 24413, 4103, 51124], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16934210794013843, "compression_ratio": 1.6487455197132617, "no_speech_prob": 2.125693718268984e-12}, {"id": 746, "seek": 259350, "start": 2608.68, "end": 2610.76, "text": " into a lower-resolution shell.", "tokens": [51124, 666, 257, 3126, 12, 495, 3386, 8720, 13, 51228], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16934210794013843, "compression_ratio": 1.6487455197132617, "no_speech_prob": 2.125693718268984e-12}, {"id": 747, "seek": 259350, "start": 2611.42, "end": 2613.92, "text": " And uniqueness is irreversibly destroyed", "tokens": [51261, 400, 48294, 307, 16014, 840, 3545, 8937, 51386], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16934210794013843, "compression_ratio": 1.6487455197132617, "no_speech_prob": 2.125693718268984e-12}, {"id": 748, "seek": 259350, "start": 2613.92, "end": 2615.76, "text": " by the curvature of the math itself.", "tokens": [51386, 538, 264, 37638, 295, 264, 5221, 2564, 13, 51478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16934210794013843, "compression_ratio": 1.6487455197132617, "no_speech_prob": 2.125693718268984e-12}, {"id": 749, "seek": 259350, "start": 2615.98, "end": 2618.64, "text": " It is a grim, unavoidable mathematical truth.", "tokens": [51489, 467, 307, 257, 36010, 11, 36541, 17079, 712, 18894, 3494, 13, 51622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16934210794013843, "compression_ratio": 1.6487455197132617, "no_speech_prob": 2.125693718268984e-12}, {"id": 750, "seek": 259350, "start": 2618.94, "end": 2621.96, "text": " It forces us to reckon with the limits of our computational models.", "tokens": [51637, 467, 5874, 505, 281, 29548, 365, 264, 10406, 295, 527, 28270, 5245, 13, 51788], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16934210794013843, "compression_ratio": 1.6487455197132617, "no_speech_prob": 2.125693718268984e-12}, {"id": 751, "seek": 262196, "start": 2621.96, "end": 2623.36, "text": " That is incredibly dark.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 6252, 2877, 13, 50435], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14106880905281785, "compression_ratio": 1.686131386861314, "no_speech_prob": 2.0442575583701217e-12}, {"id": 752, "seek": 262196, "start": 2623.56, "end": 2626.14, "text": " But, okay, to prove that this incredibly abstract,", "tokens": [50445, 583, 11, 1392, 11, 281, 7081, 300, 341, 6252, 12649, 11, 50574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14106880905281785, "compression_ratio": 1.686131386861314, "no_speech_prob": 2.0442575583701217e-12}, {"id": 753, "seek": 262196, "start": 2626.38, "end": 2629.46, "text": " high-level theoretical framework actually matters in the physical world,", "tokens": [50586, 1090, 12, 12418, 20864, 8388, 767, 7001, 294, 264, 4001, 1002, 11, 50740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14106880905281785, "compression_ratio": 1.686131386861314, "no_speech_prob": 2.0442575583701217e-12}, {"id": 754, "seek": 262196, "start": 2629.86, "end": 2632.66, "text": " the author brings it all crashing down to Earth in the final section.", "tokens": [50760, 264, 3793, 5607, 309, 439, 26900, 760, 281, 4755, 294, 264, 2572, 3541, 13, 50900], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14106880905281785, "compression_ratio": 1.686131386861314, "no_speech_prob": 2.0442575583701217e-12}, {"id": 755, "seek": 262196, "start": 2633.06, "end": 2633.98, "text": " Literally down to Earth.", "tokens": [50920, 23768, 760, 281, 4755, 13, 50966], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14106880905281785, "compression_ratio": 1.686131386861314, "no_speech_prob": 2.0442575583701217e-12}, {"id": 756, "seek": 262196, "start": 2634.12, "end": 2635.7, "text": " Dirt, steel, and concrete.", "tokens": [50973, 413, 2498, 11, 8269, 11, 293, 9859, 13, 51052], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14106880905281785, "compression_ratio": 1.686131386861314, "no_speech_prob": 2.0442575583701217e-12}, {"id": 757, "seek": 262196, "start": 2635.9, "end": 2636.08, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51062, 1079, 13, 51071], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14106880905281785, "compression_ratio": 1.686131386861314, "no_speech_prob": 2.0442575583701217e-12}, {"id": 758, "seek": 262196, "start": 2636.2, "end": 2639.38, "text": " The text applies all of these spherical insights to planetary engineering,", "tokens": [51077, 440, 2487, 13165, 439, 295, 613, 37300, 14310, 281, 35788, 7043, 11, 51236], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14106880905281785, "compression_ratio": 1.686131386861314, "no_speech_prob": 2.0442575583701217e-12}, {"id": 759, "seek": 262196, "start": 2639.52, "end": 2642.78, "text": " specifically through a model called the Orthodromic Infrastructure Blueprint.", "tokens": [51243, 4682, 807, 257, 2316, 1219, 264, 27554, 378, 4397, 299, 38425, 2885, 2177, 29017, 13, 51406], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14106880905281785, "compression_ratio": 1.686131386861314, "no_speech_prob": 2.0442575583701217e-12}, {"id": 760, "seek": 262196, "start": 2642.94, "end": 2643.84, "text": " Orthodromic Infrastructure.", "tokens": [51414, 27554, 378, 4397, 299, 38425, 2885, 13, 51459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14106880905281785, "compression_ratio": 1.686131386861314, "no_speech_prob": 2.0442575583701217e-12}, {"id": 761, "seek": 262196, "start": 2643.92, "end": 2644.1, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51463, 1033, 13, 51472], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14106880905281785, "compression_ratio": 1.686131386861314, "no_speech_prob": 2.0442575583701217e-12}, {"id": 762, "seek": 264410, "start": 2644.1, "end": 2648.5, "text": " This is an architectural blueprint for organizing planetary-scale infrastructure.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 364, 26621, 35868, 337, 17608, 35788, 12, 20033, 6896, 13, 50585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14882539266563324, "compression_ratio": 1.5222672064777327, "no_speech_prob": 2.0362884555619187e-12}, {"id": 763, "seek": 264410, "start": 2649.12, "end": 2653.8199999999997, "text": " Think global energy grids, water pipelines, or high-speed transit networks.", "tokens": [50616, 6557, 4338, 2281, 677, 3742, 11, 1281, 40168, 11, 420, 1090, 12, 22746, 17976, 9590, 13, 50851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14882539266563324, "compression_ratio": 1.5222672064777327, "no_speech_prob": 2.0362884555619187e-12}, {"id": 764, "seek": 264410, "start": 2653.98, "end": 2656.2799999999997, "text": " And it maps perfectly onto everything we've just discussed.", "tokens": [50859, 400, 309, 11317, 6239, 3911, 1203, 321, 600, 445, 7152, 13, 50974], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14882539266563324, "compression_ratio": 1.5222672064777327, "no_speech_prob": 2.0362884555619187e-12}, {"id": 765, "seek": 264410, "start": 2656.8199999999997, "end": 2659.66, "text": " The blueprint restricts engineering to a single reference,", "tokens": [51001, 440, 35868, 7694, 82, 7043, 281, 257, 2167, 6408, 11, 51143], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14882539266563324, "compression_ratio": 1.5222672064777327, "no_speech_prob": 2.0362884555619187e-12}, {"id": 766, "seek": 264410, "start": 2659.96, "end": 2661.2, "text": " shell the surface of the planet.", "tokens": [51158, 8720, 264, 3753, 295, 264, 5054, 13, 51220], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14882539266563324, "compression_ratio": 1.5222672064777327, "no_speech_prob": 2.0362884555619187e-12}, {"id": 767, "seek": 264410, "start": 2661.62, "end": 2665.42, "text": " So in our spherical math, the radial coordinate is suddenly fixed.", "tokens": [51241, 407, 294, 527, 37300, 5221, 11, 264, 38783, 15670, 307, 5800, 6806, 13, 51431], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14882539266563324, "compression_ratio": 1.5222672064777327, "no_speech_prob": 2.0362884555619187e-12}, {"id": 768, "seek": 266542, "start": 2665.42, "end": 2669.78, "text": " By fixing the radius, the blueprint entirely suppresses the radial dimension", "tokens": [50365, 3146, 19442, 264, 15845, 11, 264, 35868, 7696, 26835, 279, 264, 38783, 10139, 50583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.122467041015625, "compression_ratio": 1.646643109540636, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077911350707464e-12}, {"id": 769, "seek": 266542, "start": 2669.78, "end": 2672.16, "text": " from the primary geometric layout of the planet.", "tokens": [50583, 490, 264, 6194, 33246, 13333, 295, 264, 5054, 13, 50702], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.122467041015625, "compression_ratio": 1.646643109540636, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077911350707464e-12}, {"id": 770, "seek": 266542, "start": 2672.58, "end": 2674.76, "text": " But it reinterprets it brilliantly.", "tokens": [50723, 583, 309, 319, 5106, 3712, 1373, 309, 8695, 42580, 13, 50832], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.122467041015625, "compression_ratio": 1.646643109540636, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077911350707464e-12}, {"id": 771, "seek": 266542, "start": 2675.56, "end": 2679.1800000000003, "text": " The radial dimension becomes the axis of technological substitution.", "tokens": [50872, 440, 38783, 10139, 3643, 264, 10298, 295, 18439, 35827, 13, 51053], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.122467041015625, "compression_ratio": 1.646643109540636, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077911350707464e-12}, {"id": 772, "seek": 266542, "start": 2679.82, "end": 2681.86, "text": " Walk me through what that looks like in a real city.", "tokens": [51085, 10818, 385, 807, 437, 300, 1542, 411, 294, 257, 957, 2307, 13, 51187], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.122467041015625, "compression_ratio": 1.646643109540636, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077911350707464e-12}, {"id": 773, "seek": 266542, "start": 2682.08, "end": 2684.32, "text": " Imagine a specific coordinate on the Earth.", "tokens": [51198, 11739, 257, 2685, 15670, 322, 264, 4755, 13, 51310], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.122467041015625, "compression_ratio": 1.646643109540636, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077911350707464e-12}, {"id": 774, "seek": 266542, "start": 2684.86, "end": 2689.44, "text": " The exact depth or height of the transit infrastructure at that spot can change over time.", "tokens": [51337, 440, 1900, 7161, 420, 6681, 295, 264, 17976, 6896, 412, 300, 4008, 393, 1319, 670, 565, 13, 51566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.122467041015625, "compression_ratio": 1.646643109540636, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077911350707464e-12}, {"id": 775, "seek": 266542, "start": 2690.08, "end": 2692.76, "text": " Today, it might be a surface-level train track.", "tokens": [51598, 2692, 11, 309, 1062, 312, 257, 3753, 12, 12418, 3847, 2837, 13, 51732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.122467041015625, "compression_ratio": 1.646643109540636, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077911350707464e-12}, {"id": 776, "seek": 269276, "start": 2692.76, "end": 2697.0600000000004, "text": " In 50 years, technology improves, and it becomes an underground hyperloop.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 2625, 924, 11, 2899, 24771, 11, 293, 309, 3643, 364, 14977, 9848, 46623, 13, 50580], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1465807278951009, "compression_ratio": 1.6199376947040498, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354736997129196e-12}, {"id": 777, "seek": 269276, "start": 2697.1400000000003, "end": 2699.92, "text": " Or in 100 years, it's an elevated magnetic tube in the sky.", "tokens": [50584, 1610, 294, 2319, 924, 11, 309, 311, 364, 23457, 12688, 9917, 294, 264, 5443, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1465807278951009, "compression_ratio": 1.6199376947040498, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354736997129196e-12}, {"id": 778, "seek": 269276, "start": 2699.98, "end": 2700.34, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50726, 7587, 13, 50744], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1465807278951009, "compression_ratio": 1.6199376947040498, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354736997129196e-12}, {"id": 779, "seek": 269276, "start": 2701.0, "end": 2704.6400000000003, "text": " The specific technology substitutes it moves radially up and down across levels,", "tokens": [50777, 440, 2685, 2899, 26441, 1819, 309, 6067, 2843, 2270, 493, 293, 760, 2108, 4358, 11, 50959], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1465807278951009, "compression_ratio": 1.6199376947040498, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354736997129196e-12}, {"id": 780, "seek": 269276, "start": 2704.88, "end": 2708.2200000000003, "text": " but the angular position on the planet remains absolutely constant.", "tokens": [50971, 457, 264, 24413, 2535, 322, 264, 5054, 7023, 3122, 5754, 13, 51138], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1465807278951009, "compression_ratio": 1.6199376947040498, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354736997129196e-12}, {"id": 781, "seek": 269276, "start": 2708.6600000000003, "end": 2712.5800000000004, "text": " And that angular dimension is the permanent identity of the infrastructure.", "tokens": [51160, 400, 300, 24413, 10139, 307, 264, 10996, 6575, 295, 264, 6896, 13, 51356], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1465807278951009, "compression_ratio": 1.6199376947040498, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354736997129196e-12}, {"id": 782, "seek": 269276, "start": 2713.42, "end": 2716.6600000000003, "text": " The blueprint relies on great circles, or orthodromes.", "tokens": [51398, 440, 35868, 30910, 322, 869, 13040, 11, 420, 19052, 378, 4397, 279, 13, 51560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1465807278951009, "compression_ratio": 1.6199376947040498, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354736997129196e-12}, {"id": 783, "seek": 269276, "start": 2717.28, "end": 2721.6600000000003, "text": " These are the straightest possible lines you can draw wrapped around a sphere, like the equator.", "tokens": [51591, 1981, 366, 264, 2997, 377, 1944, 3876, 291, 393, 2642, 14226, 926, 257, 16687, 11, 411, 264, 45544, 13, 51810], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1465807278951009, "compression_ratio": 1.6199376947040498, "no_speech_prob": 1.9354736997129196e-12}, {"id": 784, "seek": 272166, "start": 2721.66, "end": 2726.66, "text": " The Great Circle Corridor remains the constant intergenerational address.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3769, 29381, 3925, 8558, 284, 7023, 264, 5754, 728, 21848, 1478, 2985, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1480559576125372, "compression_ratio": 1.5845070422535212, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656437935666737e-12}, {"id": 785, "seek": 272166, "start": 2727.3799999999997, "end": 2731.52, "text": " It is the permanent target, regardless of what technology is running through it.", "tokens": [50651, 467, 307, 264, 10996, 3779, 11, 10060, 295, 437, 2899, 307, 2614, 807, 309, 13, 50858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1480559576125372, "compression_ratio": 1.5845070422535212, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656437935666737e-12}, {"id": 786, "seek": 272166, "start": 2731.56, "end": 2735.1, "text": " Which brings our three boundaries back into play in the physical world.", "tokens": [50860, 3013, 5607, 527, 1045, 13180, 646, 666, 862, 294, 264, 4001, 1002, 13, 51037], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1480559576125372, "compression_ratio": 1.5845070422535212, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656437935666737e-12}, {"id": 787, "seek": 272166, "start": 2735.58, "end": 2738.6, "text": " The blueprint explicitly uses all three.", "tokens": [51061, 440, 35868, 20803, 4960, 439, 1045, 13, 51212], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1480559576125372, "compression_ratio": 1.5845070422535212, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656437935666737e-12}, {"id": 788, "seek": 272166, "start": 2739.04, "end": 2740.96, "text": " First, Voronoi cells.", "tokens": [51234, 2386, 11, 12231, 266, 4869, 5438, 13, 51330], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1480559576125372, "compression_ratio": 1.5845070422535212, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656437935666737e-12}, {"id": 789, "seek": 272166, "start": 2741.04, "end": 2741.6, "text": " What are those again?", "tokens": [51334, 708, 366, 729, 797, 30, 51362], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1480559576125372, "compression_ratio": 1.5845070422535212, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656437935666737e-12}, {"id": 790, "seek": 272166, "start": 2741.94, "end": 2745.92, "text": " They're geometric regions where every point is closest to a specific center.", "tokens": [51379, 814, 434, 33246, 10682, 689, 633, 935, 307, 13699, 281, 257, 2685, 3056, 13, 51578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1480559576125372, "compression_ratio": 1.5845070422535212, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656437935666737e-12}, {"id": 791, "seek": 272166, "start": 2746.44, "end": 2749.3399999999997, "text": " These act as the synchronic screens for service distribution.", "tokens": [51604, 1981, 605, 382, 264, 5451, 339, 10011, 11171, 337, 2643, 7316, 13, 51749], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1480559576125372, "compression_ratio": 1.5845070422535212, "no_speech_prob": 1.9656437935666737e-12}, {"id": 792, "seek": 274934, "start": 2749.34, "end": 2754.98, "text": " They divide up the map dynamically based on present-day needs, like where the population currently lives.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 9845, 493, 264, 4471, 43492, 2361, 322, 1974, 12, 810, 2203, 11, 411, 689, 264, 4415, 4362, 2909, 13, 50647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13764958838893943, "compression_ratio": 1.471698113207547, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612969901310225e-12}, {"id": 793, "seek": 274934, "start": 2755.1800000000003, "end": 2756.04, "text": " Okay, present tense.", "tokens": [50657, 1033, 11, 1974, 18760, 13, 50700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13764958838893943, "compression_ratio": 1.471698113207547, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612969901310225e-12}, {"id": 794, "seek": 274934, "start": 2756.44, "end": 2761.2400000000002, "text": " And the Great Circle Corridors themselves act as the stored targets, the Levin-style boundaries.", "tokens": [50720, 400, 264, 3769, 29381, 3925, 8558, 830, 2969, 605, 382, 264, 12187, 12911, 11, 264, 1456, 4796, 12, 15014, 13180, 13, 50960], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13764958838893943, "compression_ratio": 1.471698113207547, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612969901310225e-12}, {"id": 795, "seek": 274934, "start": 2761.46, "end": 2761.84, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50971, 1079, 13, 50990], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13764958838893943, "compression_ratio": 1.471698113207547, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612969901310225e-12}, {"id": 796, "seek": 274934, "start": 2762.02, "end": 2767.08, "text": " They are the ideal, mathematically perfect routes reserved for future construction.", "tokens": [50999, 814, 366, 264, 7157, 11, 44003, 2176, 18242, 24819, 337, 2027, 6435, 13, 51252], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13764958838893943, "compression_ratio": 1.471698113207547, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612969901310225e-12}, {"id": 797, "seek": 276708, "start": 2767.08, "end": 2771.2999999999997, "text": " They act like the GPS, constantly pulling development toward the ideal line.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 605, 411, 264, 19462, 11, 6460, 8407, 3250, 7361, 264, 7157, 1622, 13, 50576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12626618398746975, "compression_ratio": 1.5363636363636364, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144818550973717e-12}, {"id": 798, "seek": 276708, "start": 2771.2999999999997, "end": 2783.2599999999998, "text": " And then the hard ecological exclusions, the massive mountain ranges you can't drill through, the protected wildlife reserves you refuse to pave over, those act as the diachronic exclusions.", "tokens": [50576, 400, 550, 264, 1152, 31054, 15085, 626, 11, 264, 5994, 6937, 22526, 291, 393, 380, 11392, 807, 11, 264, 10594, 19199, 27483, 291, 16791, 281, 28870, 670, 11, 729, 605, 382, 264, 1026, 608, 10011, 15085, 626, 13, 51174], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12626618398746975, "compression_ratio": 1.5363636363636364, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144818550973717e-12}, {"id": 799, "seek": 276708, "start": 2783.52, "end": 2788.06, "text": " They are permanent historical records of what is absolutely forbidden.", "tokens": [51187, 814, 366, 10996, 8584, 7724, 295, 437, 307, 3122, 25990, 13, 51414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12626618398746975, "compression_ratio": 1.5363636363636364, "no_speech_prob": 1.7144818550973717e-12}, {"id": 800, "seek": 278806, "start": 2788.06, "end": 2792.18, "text": " And here we see the physical manifestation of the Laplacian tension we talked about.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 510, 321, 536, 264, 4001, 29550, 295, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 8980, 321, 2825, 466, 13, 50571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10985295396102102, "compression_ratio": 1.604878048780488, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236295077506901e-12}, {"id": 801, "seek": 278806, "start": 2792.62, "end": 2797.54, "text": " The Great Circle represents the idealized math, the perfect frictionless commute.", "tokens": [50593, 440, 3769, 29381, 8855, 264, 7157, 1602, 5221, 11, 264, 2176, 17710, 1832, 36750, 13, 50839], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10985295396102102, "compression_ratio": 1.604878048780488, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236295077506901e-12}, {"id": 802, "seek": 278806, "start": 2798.18, "end": 2804.84, "text": " But the actual physical terrain represents the physical cost density, the mountains, the rivers, the bedrock.", "tokens": [50871, 583, 264, 3539, 4001, 17674, 8855, 264, 4001, 2063, 10305, 11, 264, 10233, 11, 264, 18361, 11, 264, 2901, 17799, 13, 51204], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10985295396102102, "compression_ratio": 1.604878048780488, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236295077506901e-12}, {"id": 803, "seek": 278806, "start": 2804.92, "end": 2807.64, "text": " The math wants to go straight, but reality is messy.", "tokens": [51208, 440, 5221, 2738, 281, 352, 2997, 11, 457, 4103, 307, 16191, 13, 51344], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10985295396102102, "compression_ratio": 1.604878048780488, "no_speech_prob": 1.6236295077506901e-12}, {"id": 804, "seek": 280764, "start": 2807.64, "end": 2813.22, "text": " So the pipeline, or the train track, deviates from the perfect Great Circle where the physical terrain demands it.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 264, 15517, 11, 420, 264, 3847, 2837, 11, 31219, 1024, 490, 264, 2176, 3769, 29381, 689, 264, 4001, 17674, 15107, 309, 13, 50644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09971391001055317, "compression_ratio": 1.7224489795918367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947646628087676e-12}, {"id": 805, "seek": 280764, "start": 2813.72, "end": 2819.7999999999997, "text": " But without the mathematical ideal of the Great Circle acting as a baseline, we wouldn't even know how to measure our deviation.", "tokens": [50669, 583, 1553, 264, 18894, 7157, 295, 264, 3769, 29381, 6577, 382, 257, 20518, 11, 321, 2759, 380, 754, 458, 577, 281, 3481, 527, 25163, 13, 50973], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09971391001055317, "compression_ratio": 1.7224489795918367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947646628087676e-12}, {"id": 806, "seek": 280764, "start": 2820.08, "end": 2823.22, "text": " We wouldn't know how inefficient our physical route actually is.", "tokens": [50987, 492, 2759, 380, 458, 577, 43495, 527, 4001, 7955, 767, 307, 13, 51144], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09971391001055317, "compression_ratio": 1.7224489795918367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947646628087676e-12}, {"id": 807, "seek": 280764, "start": 2823.72, "end": 2830.02, "text": " The Laplacian measures the exact incompatibility between the ideal angular route and the jagged physical reality.", "tokens": [51169, 440, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 8000, 264, 1900, 40393, 267, 2841, 1296, 264, 7157, 24413, 7955, 293, 264, 6368, 3004, 4001, 4103, 13, 51484], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09971391001055317, "compression_ratio": 1.7224489795918367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6947646628087676e-12}, {"id": 808, "seek": 283002, "start": 2830.02, "end": 2833.16, "text": " And the author explicitly reiterates the warning from earlier.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 3793, 20803, 25211, 1024, 264, 9164, 490, 3071, 13, 50522], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.142458252679734, "compression_ratio": 1.568904593639576, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271461616643943e-12}, {"id": 809, "seek": 283002, "start": 2834.0, "end": 2837.64, "text": " The system crash of Theorem 3.5, they call it Pareto transparency.", "tokens": [50564, 440, 1185, 8252, 295, 440, 37956, 805, 13, 20, 11, 436, 818, 309, 31189, 1353, 17131, 13, 50746], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.142458252679734, "compression_ratio": 1.568904593639576, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271461616643943e-12}, {"id": 810, "seek": 283002, "start": 2838.04, "end": 2840.2, "text": " You cannot mix up your boundaries when building a planet.", "tokens": [50766, 509, 2644, 2890, 493, 428, 13180, 562, 2390, 257, 5054, 13, 50874], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.142458252679734, "compression_ratio": 1.568904593639576, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271461616643943e-12}, {"id": 811, "seek": 283002, "start": 2840.4, "end": 2847.0, "text": " You cannot treat a hard ecological exclusion, a diachronic boundary, like a flexible cost term.", "tokens": [50884, 509, 2644, 2387, 257, 1152, 31054, 33049, 11, 257, 1026, 608, 10011, 12866, 11, 411, 257, 11358, 2063, 1433, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.142458252679734, "compression_ratio": 1.568904593639576, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271461616643943e-12}, {"id": 812, "seek": 283002, "start": 2847.6, "end": 2855.14, "text": " If a city planner looks at a protected mountain range and says, well, it's not permanently banned, it will just cost a billion dollars more to drill through it,", "tokens": [51244, 759, 257, 2307, 31268, 1542, 412, 257, 10594, 6937, 3613, 293, 1619, 11, 731, 11, 309, 311, 406, 24042, 19564, 11, 309, 486, 445, 2063, 257, 5218, 3808, 544, 281, 11392, 807, 309, 11, 51621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.142458252679734, "compression_ratio": 1.568904593639576, "no_speech_prob": 1.4271461616643943e-12}, {"id": 813, "seek": 285514, "start": 2855.14, "end": 2861.5, "text": " they are treating a permanent historical ban as a present-day synchronic cost variable.", "tokens": [50365, 436, 366, 15083, 257, 10996, 8584, 5643, 382, 257, 1974, 12, 810, 5451, 339, 10011, 2063, 7006, 13, 50683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12284336266694246, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6751756232169512e-12}, {"id": 814, "seek": 285514, "start": 2861.9, "end": 2863.04, "text": " And what happens if they do that?", "tokens": [50703, 400, 437, 2314, 498, 436, 360, 300, 30, 50760], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12284336266694246, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6751756232169512e-12}, {"id": 815, "seek": 285514, "start": 2863.3599999999997, "end": 2871.3199999999997, "text": " If you do that, the intergenerational stability of the infrastructure collapses, the math breaks, the blueprint fails,", "tokens": [50776, 759, 291, 360, 300, 11, 264, 728, 21848, 1478, 11826, 295, 264, 6896, 48765, 11, 264, 5221, 9857, 11, 264, 35868, 18199, 11, 51174], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12284336266694246, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6751756232169512e-12}, {"id": 816, "seek": 285514, "start": 2871.56, "end": 2876.62, "text": " because you have allowed temporary present-day money to erase a permanent structural limit.", "tokens": [51186, 570, 291, 362, 4350, 13413, 1974, 12, 810, 1460, 281, 23525, 257, 10996, 15067, 4948, 13, 51439], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12284336266694246, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6751756232169512e-12}, {"id": 817, "seek": 285514, "start": 2876.8399999999997, "end": 2881.56, "text": " Wow. Okay, let's take a step back and look at the massive journey we've just been on.", "tokens": [51450, 3153, 13, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 747, 257, 1823, 646, 293, 574, 412, 264, 5994, 4671, 321, 600, 445, 668, 322, 13, 51686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12284336266694246, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6751756232169512e-12}, {"id": 818, "seek": 285514, "start": 2881.62, "end": 2882.68, "text": " It's been quite a ride.", "tokens": [51689, 467, 311, 668, 1596, 257, 5077, 13, 51742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12284336266694246, "compression_ratio": 1.625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6751756232169512e-12}, {"id": 819, "seek": 288268, "start": 2882.68, "end": 2891.08, "text": " We started by shattering the illusion of the Cartesian graph, realizing that the coordinates we trust are just interfaces, just stickers on a blank space.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 1409, 538, 402, 14849, 264, 18854, 295, 264, 22478, 42434, 4295, 11, 16734, 300, 264, 21056, 321, 3361, 366, 445, 28416, 11, 445, 21019, 322, 257, 8247, 1901, 13, 50785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12063310713995071, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 2.254135897036824e-12}, {"id": 820, "seek": 288268, "start": 2891.3399999999997, "end": 2898.74, "text": " We discovered the universal radial-angular split of the sphere, where radius is depth across levels and angle is lateral organization.", "tokens": [50798, 492, 6941, 264, 11455, 38783, 12, 656, 1040, 7472, 295, 264, 16687, 11, 689, 15845, 307, 7161, 2108, 4358, 293, 5802, 307, 25128, 4475, 13, 51168], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12063310713995071, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 2.254135897036824e-12}, {"id": 821, "seek": 288268, "start": 2899.0, "end": 2903.96, "text": " And we tracked the Laplacian's mathematical cries of incompatibility when things don't fit in.", "tokens": [51181, 400, 321, 31703, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 311, 18894, 29206, 295, 40393, 267, 2841, 562, 721, 500, 380, 3318, 294, 13, 51429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12063310713995071, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 2.254135897036824e-12}, {"id": 822, "seek": 288268, "start": 2904.3199999999997, "end": 2904.66, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51447, 1079, 13, 51464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12063310713995071, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 2.254135897036824e-12}, {"id": 823, "seek": 288268, "start": 2905.2999999999997, "end": 2910.5, "text": " We witnessed how repair dynamics violently battle to stabilize structure against the void.", "tokens": [51496, 492, 21519, 577, 10535, 15679, 46728, 4635, 281, 31870, 3877, 1970, 264, 22009, 13, 51756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12063310713995071, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 2.254135897036824e-12}, {"id": 824, "seek": 291050, "start": 2910.5, "end": 2919.88, "text": " We mapped the pure, abstract stateses of human decisions, found the literal, undeniable spherical geometry of probability and AI compression.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 33318, 264, 6075, 11, 12649, 4368, 279, 295, 1952, 5327, 11, 1352, 264, 20411, 11, 674, 268, 9364, 37300, 18426, 295, 8482, 293, 7318, 19355, 13, 50834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14155348793405, "compression_ratio": 1.4316939890710383, "no_speech_prob": 1.74856309986815e-12}, {"id": 825, "seek": 291050, "start": 2920.16, "end": 2924.56, "text": " And finally, we used it all to lay out a planetary high-speed rail network.", "tokens": [50848, 400, 2721, 11, 321, 1143, 309, 439, 281, 2360, 484, 257, 35788, 1090, 12, 22746, 8765, 3209, 13, 51068], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14155348793405, "compression_ratio": 1.4316939890710383, "no_speech_prob": 1.74856309986815e-12}, {"id": 826, "seek": 291050, "start": 2924.64, "end": 2926.68, "text": " It is a breathtaking synthesis of knowledge.", "tokens": [51072, 467, 307, 257, 48393, 30252, 295, 3601, 13, 51174], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14155348793405, "compression_ratio": 1.4316939890710383, "no_speech_prob": 1.74856309986815e-12}, {"id": 827, "seek": 292668, "start": 2926.68, "end": 2940.74, "text": " The author has demonstrated that the universe, whether it's made of physical matter, bioelectric regenerating tissue, abstract computational history, or pure statistical probability, is bound by the exact same underlying geometric infrastructure.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3793, 575, 18772, 300, 264, 6445, 11, 1968, 309, 311, 1027, 295, 4001, 1871, 11, 12198, 33243, 26358, 990, 12404, 11, 12649, 28270, 2503, 11, 420, 6075, 22820, 8482, 11, 307, 5472, 538, 264, 1900, 912, 14217, 33246, 6896, 13, 51068], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09766681570755809, "compression_ratio": 1.5228426395939085, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368639520729754e-12}, {"id": 828, "seek": 292668, "start": 2941.12, "end": 2943.6, "text": " It really unites everything under one geometric roof.", "tokens": [51087, 467, 534, 517, 3324, 1203, 833, 472, 33246, 8418, 13, 51211], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09766681570755809, "compression_ratio": 1.5228426395939085, "no_speech_prob": 1.5368639520729754e-12}, {"id": 829, "seek": 294360, "start": 2943.6, "end": 2948.36, "text": " But the author leaves us with one final, mind-bending thought in the concluding chapter on generalization.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 3793, 5510, 505, 365, 472, 2572, 11, 1575, 12, 65, 2029, 1194, 294, 264, 9312, 278, 7187, 322, 2674, 2144, 13, 50603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11571326563435216, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.7901935359457277e-12}, {"id": 830, "seek": 294360, "start": 2948.7799999999997, "end": 2950.7599999999998, "text": " And I want to leave you, the listener, with this.", "tokens": [50624, 400, 286, 528, 281, 1856, 291, 11, 264, 31569, 11, 365, 341, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11571326563435216, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.7901935359457277e-12}, {"id": 831, "seek": 294360, "start": 2951.04, "end": 2957.6, "text": " The mathematics of the sphere, the Laplacian incompatibility detector, the radial-angular split, all of it works flawlessly.", "tokens": [50737, 440, 18666, 295, 264, 16687, 11, 264, 2369, 564, 326, 952, 40393, 267, 2841, 25712, 11, 264, 38783, 12, 656, 1040, 7472, 11, 439, 295, 309, 1985, 13717, 12048, 13, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11571326563435216, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.7901935359457277e-12}, {"id": 832, "seek": 294360, "start": 2958.44, "end": 2961.18, "text": " It is rigorous, it is proven, and it governs reality.", "tokens": [51107, 467, 307, 29882, 11, 309, 307, 12785, 11, 293, 309, 1980, 82, 4103, 13, 51244], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11571326563435216, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.7901935359457277e-12}, {"id": 833, "seek": 294360, "start": 2961.52, "end": 2963.36, "text": " But the math never selects the origin.", "tokens": [51261, 583, 264, 5221, 1128, 3048, 82, 264, 4957, 13, 51353], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11571326563435216, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.7901935359457277e-12}, {"id": 834, "seek": 294360, "start": 2963.68, "end": 2966.1, "text": " The math cannot tell you where the center of the sphere is.", "tokens": [51369, 440, 5221, 2644, 980, 291, 689, 264, 3056, 295, 264, 16687, 307, 13, 51490], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11571326563435216, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.7901935359457277e-12}, {"id": 835, "seek": 294360, "start": 2966.6, "end": 2968.04, "text": " The center is completely arbitrary.", "tokens": [51515, 440, 3056, 307, 2584, 23211, 13, 51587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11571326563435216, "compression_ratio": 1.6785714285714286, "no_speech_prob": 1.7901935359457277e-12}, {"id": 836, "seek": 296804, "start": 2968.04, "end": 2974.56, "text": " It was chosen by the observer based on their specific task, their specific bias, or their specific goal.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 390, 8614, 538, 264, 27878, 2361, 322, 641, 2685, 5633, 11, 641, 2685, 12577, 11, 420, 641, 2685, 3387, 13, 50691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10174366246874088, "compression_ratio": 1.6857142857142857, "no_speech_prob": 2.1253606513615964e-12}, {"id": 837, "seek": 296804, "start": 2974.7599999999998, "end": 2978.58, "text": " The geometry is absolute, but the origin is an entirely human choice.", "tokens": [50701, 440, 18426, 307, 8236, 11, 457, 264, 4957, 307, 364, 7696, 1952, 3922, 13, 50892], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10174366246874088, "compression_ratio": 1.6857142857142857, "no_speech_prob": 2.1253606513615964e-12}, {"id": 838, "seek": 296804, "start": 2978.68, "end": 2979.1, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50897, 7587, 13, 50918], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10174366246874088, "compression_ratio": 1.6857142857142857, "no_speech_prob": 2.1253606513615964e-12}, {"id": 839, "seek": 296804, "start": 2979.44, "end": 2993.62, "text": " So, as you go out into the world today and you look at all the beautifully logical, perfectly mapped systems and models we use to define our reality, economic models, political maps, algorithmic feeds, social hierarchies, ask yourself this.", "tokens": [50935, 407, 11, 382, 291, 352, 484, 666, 264, 1002, 965, 293, 291, 574, 412, 439, 264, 16525, 14978, 11, 6239, 33318, 3652, 293, 5245, 321, 764, 281, 6964, 527, 4103, 11, 4836, 5245, 11, 3905, 11317, 11, 9284, 299, 23712, 11, 2093, 35250, 530, 11, 1029, 1803, 341, 13, 51644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10174366246874088, "compression_ratio": 1.6857142857142857, "no_speech_prob": 2.1253606513615964e-12}, {"id": 840, "seek": 296804, "start": 2994.18, "end": 2996.36, "text": " The math running that system might be flawless.", "tokens": [51672, 440, 5221, 2614, 300, 1185, 1062, 312, 45693, 13, 51781], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10174366246874088, "compression_ratio": 1.6857142857142857, "no_speech_prob": 2.1253606513615964e-12}, {"id": 841, "seek": 299636, "start": 2996.36, "end": 2998.58, "text": " But who got to choose the center?", "tokens": [50365, 583, 567, 658, 281, 2826, 264, 3056, 30, 50476], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17382631440093552, "compression_ratio": 1.439153439153439, "no_speech_prob": 2.219187941049361e-12}, {"id": 842, "seek": 299636, "start": 2999.1200000000003, "end": 3001.52, "text": " And what gets pushed to the edges because of that choice?", "tokens": [50503, 400, 437, 2170, 9152, 281, 264, 8819, 570, 295, 300, 3922, 30, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17382631440093552, "compression_ratio": 1.439153439153439, "no_speech_prob": 2.219187941049361e-12}, {"id": 843, "seek": 299636, "start": 3002.1800000000003, "end": 3003.94, "text": " Question the interfaces you take for granted.", "tokens": [50656, 14464, 264, 28416, 291, 747, 337, 12344, 13, 50744], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17382631440093552, "compression_ratio": 1.439153439153439, "no_speech_prob": 2.219187941049361e-12}, {"id": 844, "seek": 299636, "start": 3004.4, "end": 3006.92, "text": " Thank you for joining us on this deep dive into the source material.", "tokens": [50767, 1044, 291, 337, 5549, 505, 322, 341, 2452, 9192, 666, 264, 4009, 2527, 13, 50893], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17382631440093552, "compression_ratio": 1.439153439153439, "no_speech_prob": 2.219187941049361e-12}, {"id": 845, "seek": 299636, "start": 3007.2400000000002, "end": 3010.1800000000003, "text": " We'll be back next time with more paradigm-shifting explorations.", "tokens": [50909, 492, 603, 312, 646, 958, 565, 365, 544, 24709, 12, 2716, 10106, 24765, 763, 13, 51056], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17382631440093552, "compression_ratio": 1.439153439153439, "n